Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nOutpatient with primary DSM- IV OCD\nCompletion of a 14-week open label trial of one the following SRI\'s: fluoxetine 80 mg/day, paroxetine 60 mg/day, fluvoxamine 300 mg/day, clomipramine 250 mg/day, sertraline 200 mg/day, citalopram 60 mg/day, escitalopram 30 mg/day and demonstrating a non or partial responses to SRI treatment (CGI-I of 3 or 4, Y-BOCS reduction of < 35%)\nStable (8 wks or longer) concurrent medications including benzodiazepines, sedative hypnotics, antipsychotics, and antidepressants.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nAny other primary DSM-IV diagnosis; DSM-IV criteria for body dysmorphic disorder, bipolar affective disorder, schizophrenia, psychotic disorder, current alcohol/substance abuse.\nA previous adequate trial of topiramate\nComorbid major depressive disorder diagnosis which predates OCD diagnosis\nCognitive behavioural therapy or additional psychotherapy in past four months\nAllergy or hypersensitivity to topiramate\nBMI < 20\nHistory of kidney stones\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nOutpatient [AND] with primary DSM- IV OCD\nCompletion of a 14-week open label trial of one the following SRI\'s: fluoxetine 80 mg/day, [OR] paroxetine 60 mg/day, [OR] fluvoxamine 300 mg/day, [OR] clomipramine 250 mg/day, [OR] sertraline 200 mg/day, [OR] citalopram 60 mg/day, [OR] escitalopram 30 mg/day [AND] and demonstrating a [NOT] non [OR] or partial responses to SRI treatment (CGI-I of 3 or 4, Y-BOCS reduction of < 35%)\nStable (8 wks or longer) concurrent medications including benzodiazepines, [OR] sedative hypnotics, [OR] antipsychotics, [OR] and antidepressants.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nAny other primary DSM-IV diagnosis; DSM-IV criteria for body dysmorphic disorder, [OR] bipolar affective disorder, [OR] schizophrenia, [OR] psychotic disorder, current alcohol/ [OR] substance abuse.\nA previous adequate trial of topiramate\nComorbid major depressive disorder diagnosis which predates OCD diagnosis\nCognitive behavioural therapy [OR] or additional psychotherapy in past four months\nAllergy [OR] or hypersensitivity to topiramate\nBMI < 20\nHistory of kidney stones<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Outpatient [AND] with primary DSM- IV OCD
Completion of a 14-week open label trial of one the following SRI's: fluoxetine 80 mg/day, [OR] paroxetine 60 mg/day, [OR] fluvoxamine 300 mg/day, [OR] clomipramine 250 mg/day, [OR] sertraline 200 mg/day, [OR] citalopram 60 mg/day, [OR] escitalopram 30 mg/day [AND] and demonstrating a [NOT] non [OR] or partial responses to SRI treatment (CGI-I of 3 or 4, Y-BOCS reduction of < 35%)
Stable (8 wks or longer) concurrent medications including benzodiazepines, [OR] sedative hypnotics, [OR] antipsychotics, [OR] and antidepressants.

Exclusion Criteria:
Any other primary DSM-IV diagnosis; DSM-IV criteria for body dysmorphic disorder, [OR] bipolar affective disorder, [OR] schizophrenia, [OR] psychotic disorder, current alcohol/ [OR] substance abuse.
A previous adequate trial of topiramate
Comorbid major depressive disorder diagnosis which predates OCD diagnosis
Cognitive behavioural therapy [OR] or additional psychotherapy in past four months
Allergy [OR] or hypersensitivity to topiramate
BMI < 20
History of kidney stones
