Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nThe treating physician has chosen Ventavis as a suitable long-term treatment for the patient \nPatient with primary pulmonary hypertension (i.e. Idiopathic Pulmonary Arterial Hypertension or Familial Pulmonary Arterial Hypertension) and classified as NYHA functional class III (NYHA = New York Heart Association) \nNo prior treatment with Ventavis or other active treatments for primary pulmonary hypertension within 6 weeks of date of study inclusion (unless otherwise advised by Bayer Schering Pharma) \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nAny condition that prevents participation in the study, including pregnancy and other contraindications for Ventavis treatment (as listed in the current Ventavis Summary of Product Characteristics and patient package insert)       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nThe treating physician has chosen Ventavis as a suitable long-term treatment for the patient \nPatient with primary pulmonary hypertension (i.e. Idiopathic Pulmonary Arterial Hypertension [OR] or Familial Pulmonary Arterial Hypertension) [AND] and classified as NYHA functional class III (NYHA = New York Heart Association) \n [NOT] No prior treatment with Ventavis [OR] or other active treatments for primary pulmonary hypertension within 6 weeks of date of study inclusion (unless otherwise advised by Bayer Schering Pharma) \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nAny condition that [NOT] prevents participation in the study, including pregnancy [OR] and other contraindications for Ventavis treatment (as listed in the current Ventavis Summary of Product Characteristics and patient package insert)<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
The treating physician has chosen Ventavis as a suitable long-term treatment for the patient 
Patient with primary pulmonary hypertension (i.e. Idiopathic Pulmonary Arterial Hypertension [OR] or Familial Pulmonary Arterial Hypertension) [AND] and classified as NYHA functional class III (NYHA = New York Heart Association) 
 [NOT] No prior treatment with Ventavis [OR] or other active treatments for primary pulmonary hypertension within 6 weeks of date of study inclusion (unless otherwise advised by Bayer Schering Pharma) 

Exclusion Criteria:
Any condition that [NOT] prevents participation in the study, including pregnancy [OR] and other contraindications for Ventavis treatment (as listed in the current Ventavis Summary of Product Characteristics and patient package insert)
