Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nGenerally healthy, postmenopausal woman who seeks treatment for hot flushes. \nMeets 1 of the following: At least 12 months of spontaneous amenorrhea; At least 6 months of spontaneous amenorrhea with serum follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH) levels > 40 mIU/mL; At least 6 weeks postsurgical bilateral oophorectomy (with or without hysterectomy). Hysterectomized without bilateral oophorectomy and with serum FSH levels >40 mIU/mL. \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nHistory of a seizure disorder other than a single childhood febrile seizure. \nHistory or presence of clinically important hepatic or renal disease or other medical disease. \nPresence or recent history of major depressive disorder, bipolar disorder, psychotic disorder, or generalized anxiety disorder requiring therapy.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nGenerally healthy, postmenopausal woman [AND] who seeks treatment for hot flushes. \nMeets 1 of the following: At least 12 months of spontaneous amenorrhea; At least 6 months of spontaneous amenorrhea [AND] with serum follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH) levels > 40 mIU/mL; At least 6 weeks postsurgical bilateral oophorectomy (with [OR] or [NOT] without hysterectomy). Hysterectomized [NOT] without bilateral oophorectomy [AND] and with serum FSH levels >40 mIU/mL. \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nHistory of a seizure disorder other than a single childhood febrile seizure. \nHistory [OR] or presence of clinically important hepatic [OR] or renal disease [OR] or other medical disease. \nPresence [OR] or recent history of major depressive disorder, [OR] bipolar disorder, [OR] psychotic disorder, [OR] or generalized anxiety disorder requiring therapy.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Generally healthy, postmenopausal woman [AND] who seeks treatment for hot flushes. 
Meets 1 of the following: At least 12 months of spontaneous amenorrhea; At least 6 months of spontaneous amenorrhea [AND] with serum follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH) levels > 40 mIU/mL; At least 6 weeks postsurgical bilateral oophorectomy (with [OR] or [NOT] without hysterectomy). Hysterectomized [NOT] without bilateral oophorectomy [AND] and with serum FSH levels >40 mIU/mL. 

Exclusion Criteria:
History of a seizure disorder other than a single childhood febrile seizure. 
History [OR] or presence of clinically important hepatic [OR] or renal disease [OR] or other medical disease. 
Presence [OR] or recent history of major depressive disorder, [OR] bipolar disorder, [OR] psychotic disorder, [OR] or generalized anxiety disorder requiring therapy.
