Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nWomen must be postmenopausal (i.e.12 months without menstrual period), or surgically sterile, i.e. women of child bearing potential are not allowed to be included into the study. In cases of doubt a pregnancy test should be performed. (NB -post menopausal women currently receiving hormone replacement are permissible) \nAcute myocardial infarction < 12 h defined as: \n1. Angina or equivalent symptoms > 20 min and \n2. ST elevation in 2 contiguous ECG leads (= 2 mm precordial lead, = 1 mm limb lead). This ECG recording serves as baseline ECG, i.e. ECG I. \nPlanned primary percutaneous coronary intervention \nThe subject has given written informed, dated consent to participate in the study \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nSubjects not able to give informed consent \nLeft Bundle Branch Block \nThrombolytic therapy within 24 hours before randomization \nOral anticoagulation with International Normalized Ratio (INR) > 2 \nKnown platelets < 100.000/µl or known hemorrhagic diathesis \nStroke or Transient Ischemic Attack (TIA) within the past 6 months or any permanent residual neurological defect \nEvidence of an active gastrointestinal or urogenital bleeding \nMajor surgery within 6 weeks \nHistory of allergic reaction to abciximab or eptifibatide or any component used in the study (including contrast media) \nKnown severe renal (creatinine clearance <30ml/min) or hepatic insufficiency as well as Alanine transaminase (ALT)/aspartate transaminase (AST) elevations = 3xUpper limit normal (ULN); isolated AST-elevation is not considered an exclusion criteria from study participation \nSevere concomitant disease with life expectation < 1 year \nSubject has participated in any study using an investigational drug or device within 30 days or within 5 half-lives of the investigational drug (whichever is longer) of entry into this study. \nSubjects who will be inaccessible due to geographic or social factors during treatment or follow-up \nIn France, a subject is neither affiliated with nor a beneficiary of a social security category.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nWomen must be postmenopausal (i.e.12 months [NOT] without menstrual period), [OR] or surgically sterile, i.e. women [NOT] of child bearing potential are [NOT] not allowed to be included into the study. In cases of doubt a pregnancy test should be performed. (NB -post menopausal women currently receiving hormone replacement are permissible) \nAcute myocardial infarction < 12 h defined as: \n1. Angina [OR] or equivalent symptoms > 20 min [AND] and \n2. ST elevation in 2 contiguous ECG leads (= 2 mm precordial lead, = 1 mm limb lead). This ECG recording serves as baseline ECG, i.e. ECG I. \nPlanned primary percutaneous coronary intervention \nThe subject has given written informed, dated consent to participate in the study \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nSubjects [NOT] not able to give informed consent \nLeft Bundle Branch Block \nThrombolytic therapy within 24 hours before randomization \nOral anticoagulation [AND] with International Normalized Ratio (INR) > 2 \nKnown platelets < 100.000/µl [OR] or known hemorrhagic diathesis \nStroke [OR] or Transient Ischemic Attack (TIA) within the past 6 months [OR] or any permanent residual neurological defect \nEvidence of an active gastrointestinal [OR] or urogenital bleeding \nMajor surgery within 6 weeks \nHistory of allergic reaction to abciximab [OR] or eptifibatide [OR] or any component used in the study (including contrast media) \nKnown severe renal (creatinine clearance <30ml/min) [OR] or hepatic insufficiency as well as Alanine transaminase (ALT)/ [OR] aspartate transaminase (AST) elevations = 3xUpper limit normal (ULN); isolated AST-elevation is [NOT] not considered an exclusion criteria from study participation \nSevere concomitant disease [AND] with life expectation < 1 year \nSubject has participated in any study using an investigational drug [OR] or device within 30 days [OR] or within 5 half-lives of the investigational drug (whichever is longer) of entry into this study. \nSubjects who will be inaccessible due to geographic [OR] or social factors during treatment [OR] or follow-up \nIn France, a subject is neither affiliated with nor a beneficiary of a social security category.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Women must be postmenopausal (i.e.12 months [NOT] without menstrual period), [OR] or surgically sterile, i.e. women [NOT] of child bearing potential are [NOT] not allowed to be included into the study. In cases of doubt a pregnancy test should be performed. (NB -post menopausal women currently receiving hormone replacement are permissible) 
Acute myocardial infarction < 12 h defined as: 
1. Angina [OR] or equivalent symptoms > 20 min [AND] and 
2. ST elevation in 2 contiguous ECG leads (= 2 mm precordial lead, = 1 mm limb lead). This ECG recording serves as baseline ECG, i.e. ECG I. 
Planned primary percutaneous coronary intervention 
The subject has given written informed, dated consent to participate in the study 

Exclusion Criteria:
Subjects [NOT] not able to give informed consent 
Left Bundle Branch Block 
Thrombolytic therapy within 24 hours before randomization 
Oral anticoagulation [AND] with International Normalized Ratio (INR) > 2 
Known platelets < 100.000/µl [OR] or known hemorrhagic diathesis 
Stroke [OR] or Transient Ischemic Attack (TIA) within the past 6 months [OR] or any permanent residual neurological defect 
Evidence of an active gastrointestinal [OR] or urogenital bleeding 
Major surgery within 6 weeks 
History of allergic reaction to abciximab [OR] or eptifibatide [OR] or any component used in the study (including contrast media) 
Known severe renal (creatinine clearance <30ml/min) [OR] or hepatic insufficiency as well as Alanine transaminase (ALT)/ [OR] aspartate transaminase (AST) elevations = 3xUpper limit normal (ULN); isolated AST-elevation is [NOT] not considered an exclusion criteria from study participation 
Severe concomitant disease [AND] with life expectation < 1 year 
Subject has participated in any study using an investigational drug [OR] or device within 30 days [OR] or within 5 half-lives of the investigational drug (whichever is longer) of entry into this study. 
Subjects who will be inaccessible due to geographic [OR] or social factors during treatment [OR] or follow-up 
In France, a subject is neither affiliated with nor a beneficiary of a social security category.
