adio-allergosorbent test (RAST) to grass [OR] and/or ragweed pollen \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nOngoing allergen immunotherapy \nupper respiratory tract infection \nPregnancy \nClinical history of lactose-intolerance [OR] or allergies to cow-milk<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Clinical diagnosis of allergic rhinitis based on sneeze attacks, [OR] runny/ [OR] blocked/ [OR] itchy nose [NOT] in the [NOT] absence of a common cold during the previous 12 months. 
History of positive skin prick test [OR] or blood radio-allergosorbent test (RAST) to grass [OR] and/or ragweed pollen 

Exclusion Criteria:
Ongoing allergen immunotherapy 
upper respiratory tract infection 
Pregnancy 
Clinical history of lactose-intolerance [OR] or allergies to cow-milk
