Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAmbulatory status (outpatient) at time of consent \nAge 10-55 years \nClinical diagnosis of Autism Spectrum Disorder \nIQ greater than or equal to 70 \nScore greater than 8 on Children\'s Yale-Brown Obsessive Compulsive Scale \nFree of psychoactive medication for at least: one month for fluoxetine; two weeks for other SSRIs and neuroleptics; and five days for stimulants prior to MRI scanning [excepting stable doses (greater than three months duration) of anticonvulsant medication for seizure disorder] \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nAge less than 10 years or greater than 55 years, at time of consent \nEstimated IQ < 70 \nUncontrolled epilepsy (seizure within 6 months prior to consent) \n4. Presence of medical conditions that might interfere with participation, or where participation would be contraindicated \nHistory of neurological injury: head trauma, poorly-controlled seizure disorder (seizure within the preceding six months), stroke, prior neurosurgery, or under the care of a neurologist or neurosurgeon as determined by interview \nHistory of claustrophobia \nImplanted or irremovable metal in the body (including certain tattoos and permanent make-up) \nCurrent pregnancy (as verified by testing prior to both initial dose administration of citalopram or placebo and prior to magnetic resonance imaging) due to the risk that may be associated with SSRI treatment and magnetic resonance imaging on fetal health \nMedical contraindications to SSRI therapy as determined by history (including induction of mania or hypomania during SSRI therapy, or known drug allergy) \nConcomitant medication that would interfere with study participation \nPrior history of citalopram treatment failure at appropriate doses and duration \nPrior history of treatment failure to two previous SSRI trials at appropriate doses and duration \nOngoing need for psychoactive medication other than study medication [excepting stable doses (greater than three months duration) of anticonvulsant medication for seizure disorder, or diphenhydramine (Benadryl®)for sleep]       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAmbulatory status (outpatient) at time of consent \nAge 10-55 years \nClinical diagnosis of Autism Spectrum Disorder \nIQ greater than or equal to 70 \nScore greater than 8 on Children\'s Yale-Brown Obsessive Compulsive Scale \n[NOT] Free of psychoactive medication for at least: one month for fluoxetine; two weeks for other SSRIs [OR] and neuroleptics; [OR] and five days for stimulants prior to MRI scanning [excepting stable doses (greater than three months duration) of anticonvulsant medication for seizure disorder] \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nAge less than 10 years [OR] or greater than 55 years, at time of consent \nEstimated IQ < 70 \nUncontrolled epilepsy (seizure within 6 months prior to consent) \n4. Presence of medical conditions that might interfere with participation, [OR] or where participation would be contraindicated \nHistory of neurological injury: head trauma, poorly-controlled seizure disorder (seizure within the preceding six months), stroke, prior neurosurgery, [OR] or under the care of a neurologist [OR] or neurosurgeon as determined by interview \nHistory of claustrophobia \nImplanted [OR] or irremovable metal in the body (including certain tattoos [OR] and permanent make-up) \nCurrent pregnancy (as verified by testing prior to both initial dose administration of citalopram [OR] or placebo and prior to magnetic resonance imaging) due to the risk that may be associated with SSRI treatment [OR] and magnetic resonance imaging on fetal health \nMedical contraindications to SSRI therapy as determined by history (including induction of mania [OR] or hypomania during SSRI therapy, [OR] or known drug allergy) \nConcomitant medication that would interfere with study participation \nPrior history of citalopram treatment failure at appropriate doses and duration \nPrior history of treatment failure to two previous SSRI trials at appropriate doses and duration \nOngoing need for psychoactive medication other than study medication [excepting stable doses (greater than three months duration) of anticonvulsant medication for seizure disorder, [OR] or diphenhydramine (Benadryl®)for sleep]<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Ambulatory status (outpatient) at time of consent 
Age 10-55 years 
Clinical diagnosis of Autism Spectrum Disorder 
IQ greater than or equal to 70 
Score greater than 8 on Children's Yale-Brown Obsessive Compulsive Scale 
[NOT] Free of psychoactive medication for at least: one month for fluoxetine; two weeks for other SSRIs [OR] and neuroleptics; [OR] and five days for stimulants prior to MRI scanning [excepting stable doses (greater than three months duration) of anticonvulsant medication for seizure disorder] 

Exclusion Criteria:
Age less than 10 years [OR] or greater than 55 years, at time of consent 
Estimated IQ < 70 
Uncontrolled epilepsy (seizure within 6 months prior to consent) 
4. Presence of medical conditions that might interfere with participation, [OR] or where participation would be contraindicated 
History of neurological injury: head trauma, poorly-controlled seizure disorder (seizure within the preceding six months), stroke, prior neurosurgery, [OR] or under the care of a neurologist [OR] or neurosurgeon as determined by interview 
History of claustrophobia 
Implanted [OR] or irremovable metal in the body (including certain tattoos [OR] and permanent make-up) 
Current pregnancy (as verified by testing prior to both initial dose administration of citalopram [OR] or placebo and prior to magnetic resonance imaging) due to the risk that may be associated with SSRI treatment [OR] and magnetic resonance imaging on fetal health 
Medical contraindications to SSRI therapy as determined by history (including induction of mania [OR] or hypomania during SSRI therapy, [OR] or known drug allergy) 
Concomitant medication that would interfere with study participation 
Prior history of citalopram treatment failure at appropriate doses and duration 
Prior history of treatment failure to two previous SSRI trials at appropriate doses and duration 
Ongoing need for psychoactive medication other than study medication [excepting stable doses (greater than three months duration) of anticonvulsant medication for seizure disorder, [OR] or diphenhydramine (Benadryl®)for sleep]
