Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\n1. Are referred to the Cachexia Clinic with involuntary weight loss of >5% of their premorbid weight within the previous 6 months. \n2. Are 18 years of age or older \n3. Have a Karnofsky performance score of 60 or higher. \n4. Can maintain oral food intake during the study \n5. Can understand the study procedures and can sign an informed consent form. \n6. Are not currently taking melatonin. \n7. Are taking megestrol acetate and continue to lose weight despite at least 2 weeks of therapy. \n8. Have a calculated creatinine clearance of >/= 60 cc/min. \n\nExclusion Criteria:\n1. Have dementia or delirium (as determined by the palliative care specialist) at study entry. \n2. Are pregnant \n3. Have been taking corticosteroids for longer than 48 hours. \n4. Have pulmonary edema, ascites or pitting edema on clinical examination. \n5. Are unable to walk. \n6. Have a history of serious adverse gastrointestinal events (i.e., bleeding or perforation),history of a coagulopathy or current anti-coagulant use. \n7. Have an ALT/AST>3x upper limit of normal. \n8. Patients on methotrexate. \n9. Patients taking melatonin receptor agonists (such as Rozerem® [ramelteon]).       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n1. Are referred to the Cachexia Clinic [AND] with involuntary weight loss of >5% of their premorbid weight within the previous 6 months. \n2. Are 18 years of age or older \n3. Have a Karnofsky performance score of 60 or higher. \n4. Can maintain oral food intake during the study \n5. Can understand the study procedures and can sign an informed consent form. \n6. Are [NOT] not currently taking melatonin. \n7. Are taking megestrol acetate [AND] and continue to lose weight [AND] despite at least 2 weeks of therapy. \n8. Have a calculated creatinine clearance of >/= 60 cc/min.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n1. Have dementia [OR] or delirium (as determined by the palliative care specialist) at study entry. \n2. Are pregnant \n3. Have been taking corticosteroids for longer than 48 hours. \n4. Have pulmonary edema, [OR] ascites [OR] or pitting edema on clinical examination. \n5. Are [NOT] unable to walk. \n6. Have a history of serious adverse gastrointestinal events (i.e., bleeding [OR] or perforation),history of a coagulopathy [OR] or current anti-coagulant use. \n7. Have an ALT/ [OR] AST>3x upper limit of normal. \n8. Patients on methotrexate. \n9. Patients taking melatonin receptor agonists (such as Rozerem® [ramelteon]).<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
1. Are referred to the Cachexia Clinic [AND] with involuntary weight loss of >5% of their premorbid weight within the previous 6 months. 
2. Are 18 years of age or older 
3. Have a Karnofsky performance score of 60 or higher. 
4. Can maintain oral food intake during the study 
5. Can understand the study procedures and can sign an informed consent form. 
6. Are [NOT] not currently taking melatonin. 
7. Are taking megestrol acetate [AND] and continue to lose weight [AND] despite at least 2 weeks of therapy. 
8. Have a calculated creatinine clearance of >/= 60 cc/min.

Exclusion Criteria:
1. Have dementia [OR] or delirium (as determined by the palliative care specialist) at study entry. 
2. Are pregnant 
3. Have been taking corticosteroids for longer than 48 hours. 
4. Have pulmonary edema, [OR] ascites [OR] or pitting edema on clinical examination. 
5. Are [NOT] unable to walk. 
6. Have a history of serious adverse gastrointestinal events (i.e., bleeding [OR] or perforation),history of a coagulopathy [OR] or current anti-coagulant use. 
7. Have an ALT/ [OR] AST>3x upper limit of normal. 
8. Patients on methotrexate. 
9. Patients taking melatonin receptor agonists (such as Rozerem® [ramelteon]).
