Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nSubjects aged 12-65. \nConfirmed idiopathic pulmonary hypertension, connective tissue disease associated pulmonary hypertension, congenital heart disease(with Eisenmenger syndrome) associated pulmonary hypertension. \nBaseline 6-minutes walking distance 150m-550m. \nWHO pulmonary hypertension function II-III with non-responder to calcium channel blockers. \nDocumented written informed consent. \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nThe other types of pulmonary hypertension. \nSubjects who refuse to subscribe written informed consents or can\'t cooperate with the trial well. \nSubjects with serious acute or chronic disease involved liver, kidney, and brain or have to use potent CYP3A4-inhibitor or nitrate to treat the underlying diseases. \nSubjects who are currently treated with sildenafil for PAH or taking sildenafil or tadalafil. \nOther contraindications in package insert.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nSubjects aged 12-65. \nConfirmed idiopathic pulmonary hypertension, [OR] connective tissue disease associated pulmonary hypertension, [OR] congenital heart disease(with Eisenmenger syndrome) associated pulmonary hypertension. \nBaseline 6-minutes walking distance 150m-550m. \nWHO pulmonary hypertension function II-III [AND] with [NOT] non-responder to calcium channel blockers. \nDocumented written informed consent. \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nThe other types of pulmonary hypertension. \n Subjects who refuse to subscribe written informed consents or can\'t cooperate with the trial well. \nSubjects with serious acute [OR] or chronic disease involved liver, [OR] kidney, [OR] and brain [OR] or have to use potent CYP3A4-inhibitor [OR] or nitrate to treat the underlying diseases. \nSubjects who are currently treated with sildenafil for PAH [OR] or taking sildenafil [OR] or tadalafil. \nOther contraindications in package insert.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Subjects aged 12-65. 
Confirmed idiopathic pulmonary hypertension, [OR] connective tissue disease associated pulmonary hypertension, [OR] congenital heart disease(with Eisenmenger syndrome) associated pulmonary hypertension. 
Baseline 6-minutes walking distance 150m-550m. 
WHO pulmonary hypertension function II-III [AND] with [NOT] non-responder to calcium channel blockers. 
Documented written informed consent. 

Exclusion Criteria:
The other types of pulmonary hypertension. 
 Subjects who refuse to subscribe written informed consents or can't cooperate with the trial well. 
Subjects with serious acute [OR] or chronic disease involved liver, [OR] kidney, [OR] and brain [OR] or have to use potent CYP3A4-inhibitor [OR] or nitrate to treat the underlying diseases. 
Subjects who are currently treated with sildenafil for PAH [OR] or taking sildenafil [OR] or tadalafil. 
Other contraindications in package insert.
