Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nHLA-A2 melanoma patients with : \neither loco-regional or lymph node metastasis \ntransit nodules not surgically resectable \nmeasurable cutaneous or visceral metastasis \nPatients\' tumor express Melan-A/MART-1 antigen. \nNo chemotherapy treatment (except for Deticene used before the first T cell clones infusion) or radiotherapy or immunotherapy in the last 4 weeks before infusion. \nNo other melanoma treatment during the protocol. \nLife expectancy should be greater than 6 months. \nGeneral state with Karnowsky greater than 80, ECOG = 0, 1 or 2. \nPatient should be negative for HIV and B and C hepatitis. \nBiological parameters at the beginning of the study: leucocytes ³ 2000 elements per mm3, hemoglobin ³ 10.5g/dl, platelets ³ 100 000 per mm3, phosphatases alcalines transaminases £ 1 time 1/2 compared to the normal. \nSigned informed consent \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nCardio-vascular pathologies, evoluting and uncontrolled, (severe HTA), cardiac deficiency, severe angor, severe arrhythmia. \nInfectious pathologies evoluting and requiring antibiotherapy. \nPatients HIV+. \nTransplanted patients or patients suffering from severe auto-immune disease. \nPsychiatric troubles that do not allow the protocol follow-up. \nPregnant or breast-feeding women. \nNo contraception.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nHLA-A2 melanoma patients with : \neither loco-regional [OR] or lymph node metastasis \ntransit nodules [NOT] not surgically resectable \nmeasurable cutaneous [OR] or visceral metastasis \nPatients\' tumor express Melan-A/ [OR] MART-1 antigen. \n [NOT] No chemotherapy treatment (except for Deticene used before the first T cell clones infusion) [OR] or radiotherapy [OR] or immunotherapy in the last 4 weeks before infusion. \n [NOT] No other melanoma treatment during the protocol. \nLife expectancy should be greater than 6 months. \nGeneral state with Karnowsky greater than 80, ECOG = 0, 1 or 2. \nPatient should be negative for HIV [OR] and B [OR] and C hepatitis. \nBiological parameters at the beginning of the study: leucocytes ³ 2000 elements per mm3, hemoglobin ³ 10.5g/dl, platelets ³ 100 000 per mm3, phosphatases alcalines transaminases £ 1 time 1/2 compared to the normal. \nSigned informed consent \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nCardio-vascular pathologies, evoluting [OR] and uncontrolled, (severe HTA), cardiac deficiency, severe angor, severe arrhythmia. \nInfectious pathologies evoluting [OR] and requiring antibiotherapy. \n Patients HIV+. \nTransplanted patients [OR] or patients suffering from severe auto-immune disease. \nPsychiatric troubles that do [NOT] not allow the protocol follow-up. \nPregnant [OR] or breast-feeding women. \n [NOT] No contraception.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
HLA-A2 melanoma patients with : 
either loco-regional [OR] or lymph node metastasis 
transit nodules [NOT] not surgically resectable 
measurable cutaneous [OR] or visceral metastasis 
Patients' tumor express Melan-A/ [OR] MART-1 antigen. 
 [NOT] No chemotherapy treatment (except for Deticene used before the first T cell clones infusion) [OR] or radiotherapy [OR] or immunotherapy in the last 4 weeks before infusion. 
 [NOT] No other melanoma treatment during the protocol. 
Life expectancy should be greater than 6 months. 
General state with Karnowsky greater than 80, ECOG = 0, 1 or 2. 
Patient should be negative for HIV [OR] and B [OR] and C hepatitis. 
Biological parameters at the beginning of the study: leucocytes ³ 2000 elements per mm3, hemoglobin ³ 10.5g/dl, platelets ³ 100 000 per mm3, phosphatases alcalines transaminases £ 1 time 1/2 compared to the normal. 
Signed informed consent 

Exclusion Criteria:
Cardio-vascular pathologies, evoluting [OR] and uncontrolled, (severe HTA), cardiac deficiency, severe angor, severe arrhythmia. 
Infectious pathologies evoluting [OR] and requiring antibiotherapy. 
 Patients HIV+. 
Transplanted patients [OR] or patients suffering from severe auto-immune disease. 
Psychiatric troubles that do [NOT] not allow the protocol follow-up. 
Pregnant [OR] or breast-feeding women. 
 [NOT] No contraception.
