Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nNon-smoking, or smoking no more than 10 cigarettes, or 2 cigars, or 2 pipes per day for at least 3 months prior to selection \nNormal weight as defined by a Body Mass Index (BMI, weight in kg divided by the square of height in meters) of 18.0 to 30.0 kg/m2, extremes included \nAble to comply with protocol requirements. Healthy on the basis of a medical evaluation that reveals the absence of any clinically relevant abnormality and includes a physical examination, medical history, electrocardiogram (ECG), vital signs, and the results of blood biochemistry, blood coagulation, and hematology tests and a urinalysis carried out at screening. \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nNo positive HIV 1 or HIV 2 test at screening \nno history of significant skin disease such as, but not limited to rash or eruptions, drug allergies, food allergy, dermatitis, eczema, psoriasis, or urticaria \nno history of allergy to drugs such as, but not limited to, sulphonamides and penicillins \nno previously demonstrated clinically significant allergy or hypersensitivity to any of the excipients of the investigational medication administered in this trial \nno female subject of childbearing potential without use of effective nonhormonal birth control methods, or not willing to continue practicing these birth control methods for at least 30 days after the end of the treatment period \nno positive pregnancy test or breast feeding at screening       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n[NOT] Non-smoking, [OR] or smoking [NOT] no more than 10 cigarettes, [OR] or 2 cigars, [OR] or 2 pipes per day for at least 3 months prior to selection \nNormal weight as defined by a Body Mass Index (BMI, weight in kg divided by the square of height in meters) of 18.0 to 30.0 kg/m2, extremes included \nAble to comply with protocol requirements. Healthy on the basis of a medical evaluation that reveals the [NOT] absence of any clinically relevant abnormality and includes a physical examination, medical history, electrocardiogram (ECG), vital signs, and the results of blood biochemistry, [OR] blood coagulation, [OR] and hematology tests and a urinalysis carried out at screening. \n\nExclusion Criteria:\n [NOT] No positive HIV 1 [OR] or HIV 2 test at screening \n [NOT] no history of significant skin disease such as, but not limited to rash [OR] or eruptions, drug allergies, [OR] food allergy, [OR] dermatitis, [OR] eczema, [OR] psoriasis, [OR] or urticaria \n [NOT] no history of allergy to drugs such as, but not limited to, sulphonamides [OR] and penicillins \n [NOT] no previously demonstrated clinically significant allergy [OR] or hypersensitivity to any of the excipients of the investigational medication administered in this trial \n [NOT] no female subject of childbearing potential [NOT] without use of effective [NOT] nonhormonal birth control methods, [OR] or [NOT] not willing to continue practicing these birth control methods for at least 30 days after the end of the treatment period \n [NOT] no positive pregnancy test [OR] or breast feeding at screening<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
[NOT] Non-smoking, [OR] or smoking [NOT] no more than 10 cigarettes, [OR] or 2 cigars, [OR] or 2 pipes per day for at least 3 months prior to selection 
Normal weight as defined by a Body Mass Index (BMI, weight in kg divided by the square of height in meters) of 18.0 to 30.0 kg/m2, extremes included 
Able to comply with protocol requirements. Healthy on the basis of a medical evaluation that reveals the [NOT] absence of any clinically relevant abnormality and includes a physical examination, medical history, electrocardiogram (ECG), vital signs, and the results of blood biochemistry, [OR] blood coagulation, [OR] and hematology tests and a urinalysis carried out at screening. 

Exclusion Criteria:
 [NOT] No positive HIV 1 [OR] or HIV 2 test at screening 
 [NOT] no history of significant skin disease such as, but not limited to rash [OR] or eruptions, drug allergies, [OR] food allergy, [OR] dermatitis, [OR] eczema, [OR] psoriasis, [OR] or urticaria 
 [NOT] no history of allergy to drugs such as, but not limited to, sulphonamides [OR] and penicillins 
 [NOT] no previously demonstrated clinically significant allergy [OR] or hypersensitivity to any of the excipients of the investigational medication administered in this trial 
 [NOT] no female subject of childbearing potential [NOT] without use of effective [NOT] nonhormonal birth control methods, [OR] or [NOT] not willing to continue practicing these birth control methods for at least 30 days after the end of the treatment period 
 [NOT] no positive pregnancy test [OR] or breast feeding at screening
