Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nHealthy adults 18-45 years of age \nNon-smoking \nNon-pregnant (post-menopausal, surgically sterile or using effective contraceptive measures) \nBody mass index (BMI) less than or equal to 32 \nMedically healthy on the basis of medical history and physical examination \nHemoglobin > or = to 11.5g/dL \nCompletion of the screening process within 28 days prior to dosing \nProvision of voluntary written informed consent \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nRecent participation (within 28 days) in other research studies \nRecent significant blood donation or plasma donation \nPregnant or lactating \nTest positive at screening for human immunodeficiency virus (HIV), hepatitis B surface antigen (HbsAg), or hepatitis C virus (HCV) \nRecent (2-year) history or evidence of alcoholism or drug abuse \nHistory or presence of significant cardiovascular, pulmonary, hepatic, gallbladder or biliary tract, renal, hematologic, gastrointestinal, endocrine, immunologic, dermatologic, neurologic, or psychiatric disease \nSubjects who have used any drugs or substances known to inhibit or induce cytochrome (CYP) P450 enzymes and/or P-glycoprotein (P-gp) within 28 days prior to the first dose and throughout the study \nDrug allergies to quinine sulfate or rosiglitazone       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nHealthy adults 18-45 years of age \n[NOT] Non-smoking \n [NOT] Non-pregnant (post-menopausal, surgically sterile [OR] or using effective contraceptive measures) \nBody mass index (BMI) less than or equal to 32 \nMedically healthy on the basis of medical history [AND] and physical examination \nHemoglobin > or = to 11.5g/dL \nCompletion of the screening process within 28 days prior to dosing \nProvision of voluntary written informed consent \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nRecent participation (within 28 days) in other research studies \nRecent significant blood donation [OR] or plasma donation \nPregnant [OR] or lactating \nTest positive at screening for human immunodeficiency virus (HIV), hepatitis B surface antigen (HbsAg), [OR] or hepatitis C virus (HCV) \nRecent (2-year) history [OR] or evidence of alcoholism [OR] or drug abuse \nHistory [OR] or presence of significant cardiovascular, [OR] pulmonary, [OR] hepatic, [OR] gallbladder [OR] or biliary tract, renal, [OR] hematologic, [OR] gastrointestinal, [OR] endocrine, [OR] immunologic, [OR] dermatologic, [OR] neurologic, [OR] or psychiatric disease \nSubjects who have used any drugs [OR] or substances known to inhibit [OR] or induce cytochrome (CYP) P450 enzymes [OR] and/or P-glycoprotein (P-gp) within 28 days prior to the first dose and throughout the study \nDrug allergies to quinine sulfate [OR] or rosiglitazone<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Healthy adults 18-45 years of age 
[NOT] Non-smoking 
 [NOT] Non-pregnant (post-menopausal, surgically sterile [OR] or using effective contraceptive measures) 
Body mass index (BMI) less than or equal to 32 
Medically healthy on the basis of medical history [AND] and physical examination 
Hemoglobin > or = to 11.5g/dL 
Completion of the screening process within 28 days prior to dosing 
Provision of voluntary written informed consent 

Exclusion Criteria:
Recent participation (within 28 days) in other research studies 
Recent significant blood donation [OR] or plasma donation 
Pregnant [OR] or lactating 
Test positive at screening for human immunodeficiency virus (HIV), hepatitis B surface antigen (HbsAg), [OR] or hepatitis C virus (HCV) 
Recent (2-year) history [OR] or evidence of alcoholism [OR] or drug abuse 
History [OR] or presence of significant cardiovascular, [OR] pulmonary, [OR] hepatic, [OR] gallbladder [OR] or biliary tract, renal, [OR] hematologic, [OR] gastrointestinal, [OR] endocrine, [OR] immunologic, [OR] dermatologic, [OR] neurologic, [OR] or psychiatric disease 
Subjects who have used any drugs [OR] or substances known to inhibit [OR] or induce cytochrome (CYP) P450 enzymes [OR] and/or P-glycoprotein (P-gp) within 28 days prior to the first dose and throughout the study 
Drug allergies to quinine sulfate [OR] or rosiglitazone
