Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nThe patient was on nonsteroid anti-inflammatory drug (NSAID) treatment on the day when consent was obtained, and requires the long-term continuous treatment even after treatment with the investigational drug is started. \nThe patient was confirmed to have a history of gastric ulcer or duodenal ulcer. \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nEndoscopically confirmed gastric and/or duodenal ulcers on Day 1. \nEndoscopically confirmed active upper gastrointestinal hemorrhage on Day 1. \nCurrent or past history of aspirin-induced asthma or hypersensitivity to NSAIDs. \nPast or planned surgery affecting gastric acid secretion. \nClinically significant hepatic or renal disorder. \nSerious cardiac dysfunction, hypertension, or hematological disorder.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nThe patient was on nonsteroid anti-inflammatory drug (NSAID) treatment on the day when consent was obtained, [AND] and requires the long-term continuous treatment even after treatment with the investigational drug is started. \nThe patient was confirmed to have a history of gastric ulcer [OR] or duodenal ulcer. \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nEndoscopically confirmed gastric [OR] and/or duodenal ulcers on Day 1. \nEndoscopically confirmed active upper gastrointestinal hemorrhage on Day 1. \nCurrent [OR] or past history of aspirin-induced asthma [OR] or hypersensitivity to NSAIDs. \nPast [OR] or planned surgery affecting gastric acid secretion. \nClinically significant hepatic [OR] or renal disorder. \nSerious cardiac dysfunction, [OR] hypertension, [OR] or hematological disorder.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
The patient was on nonsteroid anti-inflammatory drug (NSAID) treatment on the day when consent was obtained, [AND] and requires the long-term continuous treatment even after treatment with the investigational drug is started. 
The patient was confirmed to have a history of gastric ulcer [OR] or duodenal ulcer. 

Exclusion Criteria:
Endoscopically confirmed gastric [OR] and/or duodenal ulcers on Day 1. 
Endoscopically confirmed active upper gastrointestinal hemorrhage on Day 1. 
Current [OR] or past history of aspirin-induced asthma [OR] or hypersensitivity to NSAIDs. 
Past [OR] or planned surgery affecting gastric acid secretion. 
Clinically significant hepatic [OR] or renal disorder. 
Serious cardiac dysfunction, [OR] hypertension, [OR] or hematological disorder.
