Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAfter the investigator has taken the decision to use human insulin or insulin analogues to treat the subject, any type 2 diabetic previously inadequately controlled with two or more OADs is eligible for the study \nThe selection of the subjects will be at the discretion of the individual investigator \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nKnown or suspected allergy to trial product(s) or related products \nSubjects who are unlikely to comply with protocol requirements, e.g. uncooperative attitude, inability to return for the final visit \nSubjects who previously enrolled in this study \nFemales of childbearing potential who are pregnant, breast-feeding or intend to become pregnant or are not using adequate contraceptive methods \nThe receipt of any investigational product within 3 months prior to this trial       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAfter the investigator has taken the decision to use human insulin [OR] or insulin analogues to treat the subject, any type 2 diabetic previously inadequately controlled with two or more OADs is eligible for the study \nThe selection of the subjects will be at the discretion of the individual investigator \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nKnown [OR] or suspected allergy to trial product(s) [OR] or related products \nSubjects who are unlikely to comply with protocol requirements, e.g. uncooperative attitude, [NOT] inability to return for the final visit \nSubjects who previously enrolled in this study \nFemales [AND] of childbearing potential [AND] who are pregnant, [OR] breast-feeding [OR] or intend to become pregnant [OR] or are [NOT] not using adequate contraceptive methods \nThe receipt of any investigational product within 3 months prior to this trial<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
After the investigator has taken the decision to use human insulin [OR] or insulin analogues to treat the subject, any type 2 diabetic previously inadequately controlled with two or more OADs is eligible for the study 
The selection of the subjects will be at the discretion of the individual investigator 

Exclusion Criteria:
Known [OR] or suspected allergy to trial product(s) [OR] or related products 
Subjects who are unlikely to comply with protocol requirements, e.g. uncooperative attitude, [NOT] inability to return for the final visit 
Subjects who previously enrolled in this study 
Females [AND] of childbearing potential [AND] who are pregnant, [OR] breast-feeding [OR] or intend to become pregnant [OR] or are [NOT] not using adequate contraceptive methods 
The receipt of any investigational product within 3 months prior to this trial
