sting sphincter problems or evidence of extensive local disease in the pelvis.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n1. Patient is over 18 years old. \n2. Patient is scheduled for a [NOT] non-emergency procedure. \n3. Subject signs and dates a written informed consent form (ICF) and indicates an understanding of the study procedures. \n\nExclusion Criteria:\n1. Patient has an allergy to nickel. \n2. Patient has a diagnosis of bowel obstruction, [OR] bowel strangulation, [OR] peritonitis, [OR] bowel perforation, local [OR] or systemic infection, [OR] ischemic bowel, [OR] carcinomatosis [OR] or extensively spread inflammatory bowel disease. \n3. Patient is participating in another clinical trial which may affect this study\'s outcomes. \n4. Patient has been taking regular steroid medication. \n5. Patient has contraindications to general anesthesia. \n6. Patient has preexisting sphincter problems [OR] or evidence of extensive local disease in the pelvis.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
1. Patient is over 18 years old. 
2. Patient is scheduled for a [NOT] non-emergency procedure. 
3. Subject signs and dates a written informed consent form (ICF) and indicates an understanding of the study procedures. 

Exclusion Criteria:
1. Patient has an allergy to nickel. 
2. Patient has a diagnosis of bowel obstruction, [OR] bowel strangulation, [OR] peritonitis, [OR] bowel perforation, local [OR] or systemic infection, [OR] ischemic bowel, [OR] carcinomatosis [OR] or extensively spread inflammatory bowel disease. 
3. Patient is participating in another clinical trial which may affect this study's outcomes. 
4. Patient has been taking regular steroid medication. 
5. Patient has contraindications to general anesthesia. 
6. Patient has preexisting sphincter problems [OR] or evidence of extensive local disease in the pelvis.
