Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nMust have pathologically confirmed invasive adenocarcinoma or ductal carcinoma in situ of the breast. \nPatients must have undergone segmental mastectomy (i.e., lumpectomy). \nPatients must not have received prior radiation therapy to the breast. \nPatients must not have active local-regional disease prior to registration. \nPatients must not be pregnant because of the potential for fetal harm as a result of radiation treatment. Women of child-bearing age will be given a serum pregnancy test prior to study entry to ensure they are not pregnant. They will also be counseled on the importance of avoiding pregnancy and hormonal contraception while undergoing radiation therapy. \nPatients must not have a serious medical or psychiatric illness which prevents informed consent or compliance with treatment. \nAll patients must be informed of the investigational nature of this study and give written informed consent in accordance with institutional and federal guidelines. \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nVisible skin pathology, excessive freckles, or skin blemishes in the test area. \nHistory of skin disease or hypersensitivity and repeated contact allergies. \nSarcoma or squamous cell histology. \nMetastatic disease to the breast. \nCurrent tobacco use.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nMust have pathologically confirmed invasive adenocarcinoma [OR] or ductal carcinoma in situ of the breast. \nPatients must have undergone segmental mastectomy (i.e., lumpectomy). \nPatients must [NOT] not have received prior radiation therapy to the breast. \nPatients must [NOT] not have active local-regional disease prior to registration. \nPatients must [NOT] not be pregnant because of the potential for fetal harm as a result of radiation treatment. Women [AND] of child-bearing age will be given a serum pregnancy test prior to study entry to ensure they are [NOT] not pregnant. They will also be counseled on the importance of [NOT] avoiding pregnancy [AND] and hormonal contraception while undergoing radiation therapy. \nPatients must [NOT] not have a serious medical [OR] or psychiatric illness which [NOT] prevents informed consent or compliance with treatment. \nAll patients must be informed of the investigational nature of this study and give written informed consent in accordance with institutional and federal guidelines. \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nVisible skin pathology, excessive freckles, [OR] or skin blemishes in the test area. \nHistory of skin disease [OR] or hypersensitivity and repeated contact allergies. \nSarcoma [OR] or squamous cell histology. \nMetastatic disease to the breast. \nCurrent tobacco use.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Must have pathologically confirmed invasive adenocarcinoma [OR] or ductal carcinoma in situ of the breast. 
Patients must have undergone segmental mastectomy (i.e., lumpectomy). 
Patients must [NOT] not have received prior radiation therapy to the breast. 
Patients must [NOT] not have active local-regional disease prior to registration. 
Patients must [NOT] not be pregnant because of the potential for fetal harm as a result of radiation treatment. Women [AND] of child-bearing age will be given a serum pregnancy test prior to study entry to ensure they are [NOT] not pregnant. They will also be counseled on the importance of [NOT] avoiding pregnancy [AND] and hormonal contraception while undergoing radiation therapy. 
Patients must [NOT] not have a serious medical [OR] or psychiatric illness which [NOT] prevents informed consent or compliance with treatment. 
All patients must be informed of the investigational nature of this study and give written informed consent in accordance with institutional and federal guidelines. 

Exclusion Criteria:
Visible skin pathology, excessive freckles, [OR] or skin blemishes in the test area. 
History of skin disease [OR] or hypersensitivity and repeated contact allergies. 
Sarcoma [OR] or squamous cell histology. 
Metastatic disease to the breast. 
Current tobacco use.
