Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAdults (18 and older) with physiologically confirmed SA or mild-moderate asthma and followed by an asthma specialist for at least 6 months. \nMust agree to have regular clinic visits (minimum 3-4 per year for SA, 1-2 for mild-moderate asthma). \nMust have good compliance with medications Patients with asthma and COPD. \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nMalignancy and other significant medical conditions that will impact follow up within this program. \nThose less than 18 years of age. \nConcomitant interstitial lung disease, sarcoidosis, other significant lung disease. \nThose who have had a transplant. \nSignificant travel with work. \nUnable to make appointments (every three to six months over 2 years). \nThose residing in another country or planned absence for more than one month.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAdults (18 and older) [AND] with physiologically confirmed SA [OR] or mild-moderate asthma [AND] and followed by an asthma specialist for at least 6 months. \nMust agree to have regular clinic visits (minimum 3-4 per year for SA, 1-2 for mild-moderate asthma). \nMust have good compliance with medications Patients with asthma [OR] and COPD. \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nMalignancy [OR] and other significant medical conditions that will impact follow up within this program. \nThose less than 18 years of age. \nConcomitant interstitial lung disease, [OR] sarcoidosis, other significant lung disease. \n Those who have had a transplant. \nSignificant travel with work. \n[NOT] Unable to make appointments (every three to six months over 2 years). \nThose residing in another country [OR] or planned absence for more than one month.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Adults (18 and older) [AND] with physiologically confirmed SA [OR] or mild-moderate asthma [AND] and followed by an asthma specialist for at least 6 months. 
Must agree to have regular clinic visits (minimum 3-4 per year for SA, 1-2 for mild-moderate asthma). 
Must have good compliance with medications Patients with asthma [OR] and COPD. 

Exclusion Criteria:
Malignancy [OR] and other significant medical conditions that will impact follow up within this program. 
Those less than 18 years of age. 
Concomitant interstitial lung disease, [OR] sarcoidosis, other significant lung disease. 
 Those who have had a transplant. 
Significant travel with work. 
[NOT] Unable to make appointments (every three to six months over 2 years). 
Those residing in another country [OR] or planned absence for more than one month.
