Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nLiver cirrhosis\nAge between 18 and 70 years\nEsophageal varices with high bleeding risk: more than F2 and red color sign\nNo previous history of upper gastrointestinal bleeding\nNo previous history of endoscopic, radiologic, or surgical therapy for varices or ascites\nDo not take beta-blocker, ACE inhibitor, or nitrate\nChild-Pugh score <12\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPatients with systolic blood pressure <100 mmHg or basal heart rate <60/min\nPortal vein thrombosis\nUncontrolled ascites or hepatic encephalopathy\nSevere coagulation disorder: prothrombin time <40% (or INR >1.7) or platelet count <30,000/mm3\nMedium or large sized gastric or duodenal varices\nCoexisting malignancy\nSevere cardiovascular disorder, renal failure, peritonitis, sepsis\nSevere erosive esophagitis, severe esophageal stricture, active gastric or duodenal ulcer\nContraindication to beta-blocker\nPregnancy\nRefusal to give consent to participate in the trial\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nLiver cirrhosis\nAge between 18 and 70 years\nEsophageal varices [AND] with high bleeding risk: more than F2 [AND] and red color sign\n [NOT] No previous history of upper gastrointestinal bleeding\n [NOT] No previous history of endoscopic, [OR] radiologic, [OR] or surgical therapy for varices [OR] or ascites\nDo [NOT] not take beta-blocker, [OR] ACE inhibitor, [OR] or nitrate\nChild-Pugh score <12\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPatients with systolic blood pressure <100 mmHg [OR] or basal heart rate <60/min\nPortal vein thrombosis\nUncontrolled ascites [OR] or hepatic encephalopathy\nSevere coagulation disorder: prothrombin time <40% [OR] (or INR >1.7) or platelet count <30,000/mm3\n Medium [OR] or large sized gastric [OR] or duodenal varices\nCoexisting malignancy\nSevere cardiovascular disorder, [OR] renal failure, [OR] peritonitis, [OR] sepsis\nSevere erosive esophagitis, severe esophageal stricture, active gastric [OR] or duodenal ulcer\nContraindication to beta-blocker\nPregnancy\nRefusal to give consent to participate in the trial<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Liver cirrhosis
Age between 18 and 70 years
Esophageal varices [AND] with high bleeding risk: more than F2 [AND] and red color sign
 [NOT] No previous history of upper gastrointestinal bleeding
 [NOT] No previous history of endoscopic, [OR] radiologic, [OR] or surgical therapy for varices [OR] or ascites
Do [NOT] not take beta-blocker, [OR] ACE inhibitor, [OR] or nitrate
Child-Pugh score <12

Exclusion Criteria:
Patients with systolic blood pressure <100 mmHg [OR] or basal heart rate <60/min
Portal vein thrombosis
Uncontrolled ascites [OR] or hepatic encephalopathy
Severe coagulation disorder: prothrombin time <40% [OR] (or INR >1.7) or platelet count <30,000/mm3
 Medium [OR] or large sized gastric [OR] or duodenal varices
Coexisting malignancy
Severe cardiovascular disorder, [OR] renal failure, [OR] peritonitis, [OR] sepsis
Severe erosive esophagitis, severe esophageal stricture, active gastric [OR] or duodenal ulcer
Contraindication to beta-blocker
Pregnancy
Refusal to give consent to participate in the trial
