 \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAble to give fully informed consent in writing \nMales [OR] or females aged >/= 50 years \n[NOT] No significant disease [OR] or drug use \n [NOT] Absence of any sign of dementia/ [OR] cognitive impairment in neuropsychological examinationsPatients for brain imaging: \nPatient and designee capable of giving fully informed consent in writing \nPatient fulfils DSM-IV [AND] and NINCDS-ADRA criteria for probable Alzheimers disease \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nCurrent unstable medical condition (e.g. unstable angina, [OR] myocardial infarction [OR] or coronary revascularization in the preceding 12 months, cardiac failure, [OR] chronic renal failure, [OR] chronic hepatic disease, [OR] severe pulmonary disease, [OR] blood disorders, [OR] poorly controlled diabetes, [OR] chronic infection)<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Able to give fully informed consent in writing 
Males [OR] or females aged >/= 50 years 
[NOT] No significant disease [OR] or drug use 
 [NOT] Absence of any sign of dementia/ [OR] cognitive impairment in neuropsychological examinationsPatients for brain imaging: 
Patient and designee capable of giving fully informed consent in writing 
Patient fulfils DSM-IV [AND] and NINCDS-ADRA criteria for probable Alzheimers disease 

Exclusion Criteria:
Current unstable medical condition (e.g. unstable angina, [OR] myocardial infarction [OR] or coronary revascularization in the preceding 12 months, cardiac failure, [OR] chronic renal failure, [OR] chronic hepatic disease, [OR] severe pulmonary disease, [OR] blood disorders, [OR] poorly controlled diabetes, [OR] chronic infection)
