Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\n1. HIV infection with plasma and CSF HIV RNA concentrations (using Roche Amplicor assay) > 1,000 copies/ mL (available after baseline LP). \n2. Off antiretroviral therapy (ART) for > 6 weeks before the study and no plans to begin treatment for the study duration. (The decision of whether or not a subject takes antiretroviral therapy will be made by the subject in consultation with his/her primary care provider prior to screening for this study.) \n3. Predicted adherence to the medication. \n4. Capable of providing informed consent. \n5. > 18 years old \n6. CD4 cell counts >150 cells/μL (though likely most, if not all, will be >250 cells/μL). \n7. When available, subjects will be screened for stability of blood CD4 and HIV RNA levels. \n\nExclusion Criteria:\n1. Taking a tetracycline within 6 months or history of adverse reaction to minocycline or another tetracycline. \n2. Enhanced risk from lumbar puncture, including documented or suspected cerebral mass lesion predisposing to brain herniation or bleeding diathesis. \n3. Pregnancy or expectation of pregnancy during the study. \n4. Active opportunistic infection or active neurological disease that might confound evaluation. \n5. ADC Stage > 1. \n6. Hemoglobin < 10 Gms/dL. \n7. BUN or creatine above the normal limits. \n8. Taking other drugs known to reduce the metabolism of minocycline and thus increase the probability of toxicity.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n1. HIV infection [AND] with plasma [AND] and CSF HIV RNA concentrations (using Roche Amplicor assay) > 1,000 copies/ mL (available after baseline LP). \n2. [NOT] Off antiretroviral therapy (ART) for > 6 weeks before the study [AND] and [NOT] no plans to begin treatment for the study duration. (The decision of whether or not a subject takes antiretroviral therapy will be made by the subject in consultation with his/her primary care provider prior to screening for this study.) \n3. Predicted adherence to the medication. \n4. Capable of providing informed consent. \n5. > 18 years old \n6. CD4 cell counts >150 cells/μL (though likely most, if not all, will be >250 cells/μL). \n7. When available, subjects will be screened for stability of blood CD4 [AND] and HIV RNA levels. \n\nExclusion Criteria:\n1. Taking a tetracycline within 6 months [OR] or history of adverse reaction to minocycline [OR] or another tetracycline. \n2. Enhanced risk from lumbar puncture, including documented [OR] or suspected cerebral mass lesion predisposing to brain herniation [OR] or bleeding diathesis. \n3. Pregnancy [OR] or expectation of pregnancy during the study. \n4. Active opportunistic infection [OR] or active neurological disease that might confound evaluation. \n5. ADC Stage > 1. \n6. Hemoglobin < 10 Gms/dL. \n7. BUN [OR] or creatine above the normal limits. \n8. Taking other drugs known to reduce the metabolism of minocycline [AND] and thus increase the probability of toxicity.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
1. HIV infection [AND] with plasma [AND] and CSF HIV RNA concentrations (using Roche Amplicor assay) > 1,000 copies/ mL (available after baseline LP). 
2. [NOT] Off antiretroviral therapy (ART) for > 6 weeks before the study [AND] and [NOT] no plans to begin treatment for the study duration. (The decision of whether or not a subject takes antiretroviral therapy will be made by the subject in consultation with his/her primary care provider prior to screening for this study.) 
3. Predicted adherence to the medication. 
4. Capable of providing informed consent. 
5. > 18 years old 
6. CD4 cell counts >150 cells/μL (though likely most, if not all, will be >250 cells/μL). 
7. When available, subjects will be screened for stability of blood CD4 [AND] and HIV RNA levels. 

Exclusion Criteria:
1. Taking a tetracycline within 6 months [OR] or history of adverse reaction to minocycline [OR] or another tetracycline. 
2. Enhanced risk from lumbar puncture, including documented [OR] or suspected cerebral mass lesion predisposing to brain herniation [OR] or bleeding diathesis. 
3. Pregnancy [OR] or expectation of pregnancy during the study. 
4. Active opportunistic infection [OR] or active neurological disease that might confound evaluation. 
5. ADC Stage > 1. 
6. Hemoglobin < 10 Gms/dL. 
7. BUN [OR] or creatine above the normal limits. 
8. Taking other drugs known to reduce the metabolism of minocycline [AND] and thus increase the probability of toxicity.
