File: NCT01116973 

Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_full/NCT01116973.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nSubject\'s ability to lay in a supine position with their hands at their sides during CVP measurements \nA consent form signed by the patient or patient\'s representative \nSubjects that are age 18-90 \nSubjects that have an indwelling CICC and are transitioning to a PICC for long-term IV access \nCICC placed in the internal jugular vein or subclavian vein position \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nInability to obtain consent \nSubjects under 18 years of age \nNon-English speaking subjects \nSubjects that are unable to lay flat due to pulmonary complications, increased intracranial pressure (ICP), or unstable spinal cord injuries \nSubjects with known cardiac abnormalities (atrial septal defects or ventricular septal defects, severe tricuspid valve disease, severe pulmonary hypertension, Ejection fraction < 15%) \nPrisoners \nSubjects with known upper extremity deep vein thromboses (subclavian or distal) \nSubjects with non-functional CICC or PICC distal ports \nSubjects with femoral CICCs \nPregnant women       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nSubject\'s ability to lay in a supine position [AND] with their hands at their sides during CVP measurements \nA consent form signed by the patient or patient\'s representative \nSubjects that are age 18-90 \nSubjects that have an indwelling CICC [AND] and are transitioning to a PICC for long-term IV access \nCICC placed in the internal jugular vein [OR] or subclavian vein position \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nInability to obtain consent \nSubjects under 18 years of age \nNon-English speaking subjects \nSubjects that are [NOT] unable to lay flat due to pulmonary complications, [OR] increased intracranial pressure (ICP), [OR] or unstable spinal cord injuries \nSubjects with known cardiac abnormalities (atrial septal defects [OR] or ventricular septal defects, severe tricuspid valve disease, severe pulmonary hypertension, [OR] Ejection fraction < 15%) \nPrisoners \nSubjects with known upper extremity deep vein thromboses (subclavian [OR] or distal) \nSubjects with [NOT] non-functional CICC [OR] or PICC distal ports \nSubjects with femoral CICCs \nPregnant women<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Subject's ability to lay in a supine position [AND] with their hands at their sides during CVP measurements 
A consent form signed by the patient or patient's representative 
Subjects that are age 18-90 
Subjects that have an indwelling CICC [AND] and are transitioning to a PICC for long-term IV access 
CICC placed in the internal jugular vein [OR] or subclavian vein position 

Exclusion Criteria:
Inability to obtain consent 
Subjects under 18 years of age 
Non-English speaking subjects 
Subjects that are [NOT] unable to lay flat due to pulmonary complications, [OR] increased intracranial pressure (ICP), [OR] or unstable spinal cord injuries 
Subjects with known cardiac abnormalities (atrial septal defects [OR] or ventricular septal defects, severe tricuspid valve disease, severe pulmonary hypertension, [OR] Ejection fraction < 15%) 
Prisoners 
Subjects with known upper extremity deep vein thromboses (subclavian [OR] or distal) 
Subjects with [NOT] non-functional CICC [OR] or PICC distal ports 
Subjects with femoral CICCs 
Pregnant women
