Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients of familial cases of POF : \nFemale subjects between 16 and 40 years or women older than 40 years with a cessation of ovarian function before the age of 40 years with increased levels of FSH \nPrimary or secondary amenorrhea for more than three months with LH and FSH> 30mUI/ml \nNo cases of fragile X syndrome in the family or blepharophimosis syndrome \nAt least two cases in the family \nOrigin Caucasian \nPatient signing the consent form for at least the blood sample \nPatient with Social Security \nPopulation Index related topics : \nThe presence of cycles until the age of 40 years with proven fertility, at least one child \nAmenorrhea and FSH> 30mUI/ml according to the criteria of the index subject \nMen of the family of index case \nPopulation control : \nWomen of Caucasian origin \nWomen who had regular cycles until at least age 40 and at least one child \nLack of land autoimmune (no history of thyroid disease or diabetes type 1) \nWoman signing the consent form for at least the blood sample \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nBlood donation of more than 450ml in the previous three months. \nSubject with an abnormal karyotype in favor of Turner syndrome or having a premutation of the FMR1 gene or a syndromic form \nSubject exclusion period in another study without direct individual benefit \nSubject refusing to sign the consent form       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients of familial cases of POF : \nFemale subjects between 16 and 40 years [OR] or women older than 40 years [AND] with a cessation of ovarian function before the age of 40 years [AND] with increased levels of FSH \nPrimary [OR] or secondary amenorrhea  for more than three months [AND] with LH [AND] and FSH> 30mUI/ml \n [NOT] No cases of fragile X syndrome in the family [OR] or blepharophimosis syndrome \nAt least two cases in the family \nOrigin Caucasian \nPatient signing the consent form for at least the blood sample \nPatient with Social Security \nPopulation Index related topics : \nThe presence of cycles until the age of 40 years [AND] with proven fertility, at least one child \nAmenorrhea [AND] and FSH> 30mUI/ml according to the criteria of the index subject \nMen of the family of index case \nPopulation control : \nWomen of Caucasian origin \nWomen [AND] who had regular cycles until at least age 40 [AND] and at least one child \n [NOT] Lack of land autoimmune ([NOT] no history of thyroid disease [OR] or diabetes type 1) \nWoman signing the consent form for at least the blood sample \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nBlood donation of more than 450ml in the previous three months. \nSubject with an abnormal karyotype in favor of Turner syndrome [OR] or having a premutation of the FMR1 gene [OR] or a syndromic form\nSubject exclusion period in another study [NOT] without direct individual benefit\nSubject refusing to sign the consent form<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Patients of familial cases of POF : 
Female subjects between 16 and 40 years [OR] or women older than 40 years [AND] with a cessation of ovarian function before the age of 40 years [AND] with increased levels of FSH 
Primary [OR] or secondary amenorrhea  for more than three months [AND] with LH [AND] and FSH> 30mUI/ml 
 [NOT] No cases of fragile X syndrome in the family [OR] or blepharophimosis syndrome 
At least two cases in the family 
Origin Caucasian 
Patient signing the consent form for at least the blood sample 
Patient with Social Security 
Population Index related topics : 
The presence of cycles until the age of 40 years [AND] with proven fertility, at least one child 
Amenorrhea [AND] and FSH> 30mUI/ml according to the criteria of the index subject 
Men of the family of index case 
Population control : 
Women of Caucasian origin 
Women [AND] who had regular cycles until at least age 40 [AND] and at least one child 
 [NOT] Lack of land autoimmune ([NOT] no history of thyroid disease [OR] or diabetes type 1) 
Woman signing the consent form for at least the blood sample 

Exclusion Criteria:
Blood donation of more than 450ml in the previous three months. 
Subject with an abnormal karyotype in favor of Turner syndrome [OR] or having a premutation of the FMR1 gene [OR] or a syndromic form
Subject exclusion period in another study [NOT] without direct individual benefit
Subject refusing to sign the consent form
