Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\n1. Age: 18-75 years old, no limitation in gender; \n2. Left ventricular ejection fraction (LVEF) ≤ 40% (ECHO); \n3. Patients with chronic heart failure (NYHA class II or III); \n4. In the past one month, the clinical condition (including history, clinical symptoms and signs) was relatively stable; \n5. Patients on standard treatment of chronic heart failure at the target dose or maximum tolerance dose for over 1 month,or unchanged dose in last 1 month; \n6. Understand and sign the informed consent form; \n\nExclusion Criteria:\n1. Atrial fibrillation; \n2. Subject underwent cardiac pacemaker treatment; \n3. Subject underwent metal graft treatment; \n4. Claustrophobia; \n5. Acute myocardial infarction, cardiac ischemia indicated by 6-minute walk test, hypertrophic cardiomyopathy, constrictive pericarditis, significant valve disease or congenital heart disease, severe pulmonary hypertension; \n6. Ischemic heart failure without the revascularization or undergone the revascularization within last 6 months; \n7. Subject underwent cardiac surgery or cerebrovascular events within the previous six months; \n8. Subjects who plan to have cardiac transplantation; \n9. Severe hepatic and renal insufficiency (serum creatinine>2.0 mg /dl, AST or ALT is five times higher than the upper limit of normal range); \n10. Subject needs mechanical ventilation; \n11. Systolic blood pressure < 90mmHg, or > 160mmHg; \n12. Chronic heart failure complicated with acute hemodynamic disturbance or acute decompensation within last 1 month; \n13. Mobitz Type II or III° atrial ventricular block，severe ventricular arrhythmia (polymorphic and frequent premature ventricular beats, frequent non-sustained ventricular tachycardia); \n14. Serum potassium<3.2mmol/L, or>5.5mmol/L; \n15. Female subject is pregnant or plan to become pregnant \n16. Childbearing-aged female subject who is unmarried or dose not bear child; \n17. Subject with life expectancy less than 6 months as assessed by investigators; \n18. Subject participated in any other clinical trial within the previous three months; \n19. Subject with previous history of tumor, or current tumor patient, or subject with pre-cancerous disease manifested by pathological examination (such as ductal carcinoma in situ or cervical epithelial dysplasia) \n20. Examinations (physical examination, X-ray examination, type-B ultrasonic detection or other methods) reveal that the subject has malignant mass, gland hyperplasia or adenoma with endocrine activity, or impact on heart, or endocrine function (such as pheochromocytoma, thyroid enlargement); \n21. The Investigator deemed for whatever reason that the subject is not likely to complete the study or comply with the study procedures (due to administration or any other reason).       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n 1. Age: 18-75 years old, [NOT] no limitation in gender; \n 2. Left ventricular ejection fraction (LVEF) ≤ 40% (ECHO); \n 3. Patients with chronic heart failure (NYHA class II or III); \n 4. In the past one month, the clinical condition (including history, clinical symptoms and signs) was relatively stable; \n 5. Patients on standard treatment of chronic heart failure at the target dose [OR] or maximum tolerance dose for over 1 month, [OR] or unchanged dose in last 1 month; \n 6. Understand and sign the informed consent form; \n\nExclusion Criteria:\n 1. Atrial fibrillation; \n 2. Subject underwent cardiac pacemaker treatment; \n 3. Subject underwent metal graft treatment; \n 4. Claustrophobia; \n 5. Acute myocardial infarction, [OR] cardiac ischemia indicated by 6-minute walk test, [OR] hypertrophic cardiomyopathy, [OR] constrictive pericarditis, significant valve disease [OR] or congenital heart disease, severe pulmonary hypertension; \n 6. Ischemic heart failure [NOT] without the revascularization [OR] or undergone the revascularization within last 6 months; \n 7. Subject underwent cardiac surgery [OR] or cerebrovascular events within the previous six months; \n 8. Subjects who plan to have cardiac transplantation; \n 9. Severe hepatic [OR] and renal insufficiency (serum creatinine>2.0 mg /dl, AST [OR] or ALT is five times higher than the upper limit of normal range); \n 10. Subject needs mechanical ventilation; \n 11. Systolic blood pressure < 90mmHg, [OR] or > 160mmHg; \n 12. Chronic heart failure complicated with acute hemodynamic disturbance [OR] or acute decompensation within last 1 month; \n 13. Mobitz Type II or III° atrial ventricular block，severe ventricular arrhythmia (polymorphic [OR] and frequent premature ventricular beats, frequent [NOT] non-sustained ventricular tachycardia); \n 14. Serum potassium<3.2mmol/L, [OR] or>5.5mmol/L; \n 15. Female subject is pregnant [OR] or plan to become pregnant \n 16. Childbearing-aged female subject [AND] who is unmarried [OR] or dose [NOT] not bear child; \n 17. Subject with life expectancy less than 6 months as assessed by investigators; \n 18. Subject participated in any other clinical trial within the previous three months; \n 19. Subject with previous history of tumor, [OR] or current tumor patient, [OR] or subject with pre-cancerous disease manifested by pathological examination (such as ductal carcinoma in situ [OR] or cervical epithelial dysplasia) \n 20. Examinations (physical examination, [OR] X-ray examination, [OR] type-B ultrasonic detection [OR] or other methods) reveal that the subject has malignant mass, [OR] gland hyperplasia [OR] or adenoma with endocrine activity, [OR] or impact on heart, [OR] or endocrine function (such as pheochromocytoma, [OR] thyroid enlargement); \n 21. The Investigator deemed for whatever reason that the subject is [NOT] not likely to complete the study [OR] or comply with the study procedures (due to administration [OR] or any other reason).<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
 1. Age: 18-75 years old, [NOT] no limitation in gender; 
 2. Left ventricular ejection fraction (LVEF) ≤ 40% (ECHO); 
 3. Patients with chronic heart failure (NYHA class II or III); 
 4. In the past one month, the clinical condition (including history, clinical symptoms and signs) was relatively stable; 
 5. Patients on standard treatment of chronic heart failure at the target dose [OR] or maximum tolerance dose for over 1 month, [OR] or unchanged dose in last 1 month; 
 6. Understand and sign the informed consent form; 

Exclusion Criteria:
 1. Atrial fibrillation; 
 2. Subject underwent cardiac pacemaker treatment; 
 3. Subject underwent metal graft treatment; 
 4. Claustrophobia; 
 5. Acute myocardial infarction, [OR] cardiac ischemia indicated by 6-minute walk test, [OR] hypertrophic cardiomyopathy, [OR] constrictive pericarditis, significant valve disease [OR] or congenital heart disease, severe pulmonary hypertension; 
 6. Ischemic heart failure [NOT] without the revascularization [OR] or undergone the revascularization within last 6 months; 
 7. Subject underwent cardiac surgery [OR] or cerebrovascular events within the previous six months; 
 8. Subjects who plan to have cardiac transplantation; 
 9. Severe hepatic [OR] and renal insufficiency (serum creatinine>2.0 mg /dl, AST [OR] or ALT is five times higher than the upper limit of normal range); 
 10. Subject needs mechanical ventilation; 
 11. Systolic blood pressure < 90mmHg, [OR] or > 160mmHg; 
 12. Chronic heart failure complicated with acute hemodynamic disturbance [OR] or acute decompensation within last 1 month; 
 13. Mobitz Type II or III° atrial ventricular block，severe ventricular arrhythmia (polymorphic [OR] and frequent premature ventricular beats, frequent [NOT] non-sustained ventricular tachycardia); 
 14. Serum potassium<3.2mmol/L, [OR] or>5.5mmol/L; 
 15. Female subject is pregnant [OR] or plan to become pregnant 
 16. Childbearing-aged female subject [AND] who is unmarried [OR] or dose [NOT] not bear child; 
 17. Subject with life expectancy less than 6 months as assessed by investigators; 
 18. Subject participated in any other clinical trial within the previous three months; 
 19. Subject with previous history of tumor, [OR] or current tumor patient, [OR] or subject with pre-cancerous disease manifested by pathological examination (such as ductal carcinoma in situ [OR] or cervical epithelial dysplasia) 
 20. Examinations (physical examination, [OR] X-ray examination, [OR] type-B ultrasonic detection [OR] or other methods) reveal that the subject has malignant mass, [OR] gland hyperplasia [OR] or adenoma with endocrine activity, [OR] or impact on heart, [OR] or endocrine function (such as pheochromocytoma, [OR] thyroid enlargement); 
 21. The Investigator deemed for whatever reason that the subject is [NOT] not likely to complete the study [OR] or comply with the study procedures (due to administration [OR] or any other reason).
