rsensitivity to any of the components of the formulations used in the study.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatient is indicated to have an ocular refractive surgery performed (myopia, [OR] astigmatism, [OR] hypermetropy) by the Lasik method. \nPatient presents a normal eye fundus. \nPatient has intraocular pressure (IOP) ≤ 20 mmHg. \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nSurgery [OR] and/or previous ocular pathology (presence of scar/ [OR] change in the cornea, [OR] glaucoma, [OR] retinopathies, etc.). \nPatient has diabetes [OR] or is immunodepressed. \nAny systemic infection during the study. \nSigns [OR] and/or symptoms of ocular inflammation/ [OR] infection (bacterial, [OR] viral, [OR] fungal, caused by Chlamydia, [OR] by Mycobacterium, [OR] Acanthamoeba [OR] or of allergic etiology). \nHave used any systemic [OR] or topical antibiotics for ocular infection in the previous 14 days. \nPatient has known hypersensitivity to any of the components of the formulations used in the study.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Patient is indicated to have an ocular refractive surgery performed (myopia, [OR] astigmatism, [OR] hypermetropy) by the Lasik method. 
Patient presents a normal eye fundus. 
Patient has intraocular pressure (IOP) ≤ 20 mmHg. 

Exclusion Criteria:
Surgery [OR] and/or previous ocular pathology (presence of scar/ [OR] change in the cornea, [OR] glaucoma, [OR] retinopathies, etc.). 
Patient has diabetes [OR] or is immunodepressed. 
