sification. \nPatients who exceed minimal physical activity recommendations from the US Surgeon General\'s Report: Accumulation of 30 minutes or more of moderate physical activity on most days of the week. \nMorbidly obese with BMI ≥ 40       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPost menopausal women [AND] with a history of estrogen positive breast cancer [AND] who are receiving aromatase inhibitors for at least one month. \nPatients must complain of mild [OR] to moderate arthralgia.\nAbility to understand and sign informed consent.\nPatients meet criteria for low [OR] to moderate risk for moderate exercise based on the ACSM guidelines.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nInability to comply with study requirements.\nMetastatic breast cancer.\nPatients with orthopedic [OR] or neuromuscular disorders that [NOT] preclude participation in exercise.\nRheumatoid arthritis.\nHistory of MI, [OR] angina [OR] or congestive heart failure.\nPregnant [OR] or lactating females.\nPatients that are high risk for moderate exercise based on ACSM risk classification.\nPatients who exceed minimal physical activity recommendations from the US Surgeon General\'s Report: Accumulation of 30 minutes or more of moderate physical activity on most days of the week.\nMorbidly obese [AND] with BMI ≥ 40<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Post menopausal women [AND] with a history of estrogen positive breast cancer [AND] who are receiving aromatase inhibitors for at least one month. 
Patients must complain of mild [OR] to moderate arthralgia.
Ability to understand and sign informed consent.
Patients meet criteria for low [OR] to moderate risk for moderate exercise based on the ACSM guidelines.

Exclusion Criteria:
Inability to comply with study requirements.
Metastatic breast cancer.
Patients with orthopedic [OR] or neuromuscular disorders that [NOT] preclude participation in exercise.
Rheumatoid arthritis.
History of MI, [OR] angina [OR] or congestive heart failure.
Pregnant [OR] or lactating females.
Patients that are high risk for moderate exercise based on ACSM risk classification.
Patients who exceed minimal physical activity recommendations from the US Surgeon General's Report: Accumulation of 30 minutes or more of moderate physical activity on most days of the week.
Morbidly obese [AND] with BMI ≥ 40
