Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nInformed consent obtained prior to any screening procedure \nCaucasian male or female patient \nAt least 18 years of age \nWeight at least 45 kg \nPatient with moderate or severe chronic atopic dermatitis \nGood general health ascertained by medical history, physical examination and laboratory determinations, showing no signs of clinically significant findings, except chronic atopic dermatitis \nNegative pregnancy test (premenopausal female patient) at screening and use of adequate contraceptive measures (both male and female patients) throughout the study and 30 days after the last cis-UCA dose \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nHistory of other significant skin disease, or skin manifestations of allergic illness or other dermatologic condition, except chronic moderate or severe atopic dermatitis, that would interfere with the trial assessments or compromise the patient\'s safety according to the opinion of the Investigator \nPresent symptoms of other skin diseases, except chronic atopic dermatitis, that could disturb the study assessment and evaluation of the skin \nCurrent use of any active systemic medication for chronic atopic dermatitis within one month \nCurrent use of active topical medication in the planned investigational area for chronic atopic dermatitis within two weeks \nHistory of a sunny holiday, UV-light therapy or solarium use within one month before beginning of study treatments, or planning such during the study or within 7 days after the study \nAllergy to cis-UCA, or any constituents of the placebo emulsion cream or any constituents of Protopic® ointment \nHistory of any skin-related cancer \nCongenital or acquired immunodeficiency or ongoing therapy that cause immunosuppression \nEarlier participation in a clinical study performed with cis-UCA \nAny clinically significant laboratory test result \nSuspected current drug or alcohol abuse \nClinically significant illness during the 4 weeks prior to the first dose administration \nAny other condition that in the opinion of the Investigator would interfere with the evaluation of the study results or constitute a health hazard for the patient \nUnwillingness or doubtful capacity to comply with the protocol \nDoubtful availability to complete the study       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nInformed consent obtained prior to any screening procedure \nCaucasian male [OR] or female patient \nAt least 18 years of age \nWeight at least 45 kg \nPatient with moderate [OR] or severe chronic atopic dermatitis \nGood general health ascertained by medical history, [OR] physical examination [OR] and laboratory determinations, showing [NOT] no signs of clinically significant findings, except chronic atopic dermatitis \nNegative pregnancy test [OR] (premenopausal female patient) at screening [AND] and use of adequate contraceptive measures (both male [OR] and female patients) throughout the study [AND] and 30 days after the last cis-UCA dose \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nHistory of other significant skin disease, [OR] or skin manifestations of allergic illness [OR] or other dermatologic condition, except chronic moderate [OR] or severe atopic dermatitis, that would interfere with the trial assessments [OR] or compromise the patient\'s safety according to the opinion of the Investigator \nPresent symptoms of other skin diseases, except chronic atopic dermatitis, that could disturb the study assessment [OR] and evaluation of the skin \nCurrent use of any active systemic medication [OR] for chronic atopic dermatitis within one month \nCurrent use of active topical medication [OR] in the planned investigational area for chronic atopic dermatitis within two weeks \nHistory of a sunny holiday, [OR] UV-light therapy [OR] or solarium use within one month before beginning of study treatments, [OR] or planning such during the study [OR] or within 7 days after the study \nAllergy to cis-UCA, [OR] or any constituents of the placebo emulsion cream [OR] or any constituents of Protopic® ointment \nHistory of any skin-related cancer \nCongenital [OR] or acquired immunodeficiency [OR] or ongoing therapy that cause immunosuppression \nEarlier participation in a clinical study performed with cis-UCA \nAny clinically significant laboratory test result \nSuspected current drug [OR] or alcohol abuse \nClinically significant illness during the 4 weeks prior to the first dose administration \nAny other condition that in the opinion of the Investigator would interfere with the evaluation of the study results [OR] or constitute a health hazard for the patient \nUnwillingness [OR] or doubtful capacity to comply with the protocol \nDoubtful availability to complete the study<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Informed consent obtained prior to any screening procedure 
Caucasian male [OR] or female patient 
At least 18 years of age 
Weight at least 45 kg 
Patient with moderate [OR] or severe chronic atopic dermatitis 
Good general health ascertained by medical history, [OR] physical examination [OR] and laboratory determinations, showing [NOT] no signs of clinically significant findings, except chronic atopic dermatitis 
Negative pregnancy test [OR] (premenopausal female patient) at screening [AND] and use of adequate contraceptive measures (both male [OR] and female patients) throughout the study [AND] and 30 days after the last cis-UCA dose 

Exclusion Criteria:
History of other significant skin disease, [OR] or skin manifestations of allergic illness [OR] or other dermatologic condition, except chronic moderate [OR] or severe atopic dermatitis, that would interfere with the trial assessments [OR] or compromise the patient's safety according to the opinion of the Investigator 
Present symptoms of other skin diseases, except chronic atopic dermatitis, that could disturb the study assessment [OR] and evaluation of the skin 
Current use of any active systemic medication [OR] for chronic atopic dermatitis within one month 
Current use of active topical medication [OR] in the planned investigational area for chronic atopic dermatitis within two weeks 
History of a sunny holiday, [OR] UV-light therapy [OR] or solarium use within one month before beginning of study treatments, [OR] or planning such during the study [OR] or within 7 days after the study 
Allergy to cis-UCA, [OR] or any constituents of the placebo emulsion cream [OR] or any constituents of Protopic® ointment 
History of any skin-related cancer 
Congenital [OR] or acquired immunodeficiency [OR] or ongoing therapy that cause immunosuppression 
Earlier participation in a clinical study performed with cis-UCA 
Any clinically significant laboratory test result 
Suspected current drug [OR] or alcohol abuse 
Clinically significant illness during the 4 weeks prior to the first dose administration 
Any other condition that in the opinion of the Investigator would interfere with the evaluation of the study results [OR] or constitute a health hazard for the patient 
Unwillingness [OR] or doubtful capacity to comply with the protocol 
Doubtful availability to complete the study
