Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients with functional dyspepsia that fulfill Rome III criteria with inadequate relief of dyspeptic symptoms\nAge >18\nProvision of written consent\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPresence of organic pathology identified by upper endoscopy or other investigations\nPresence of sliding hiatus hernia as defined by flap valve grade IV disruption of morphology at gastro-esophageal junction\nConcurrent medications that affect gastrointestinal motility\nPresence of acid reflux or heartburn symptoms of more than twice a month\nHistory of gastric surgery\nH. pylori infection\nUse of PPI or NSAID in the past 4 weeks\nPregnancy\nKnown hypersensitivity to PPI\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients with functional dyspepsia that fulfill Rome III criteria [AND] with inadequate relief of dyspeptic symptoms\nAge >18\nProvision of written consent\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPresence of organic pathology identified by upper endoscopy [OR] or other investigations\nPresence of sliding hiatus hernia as defined by flap valve grade IV disruption of morphology at gastro-esophageal junction\nConcurrent medications that affect gastrointestinal motility\n Presence of acid reflux [OR] or heartburn symptoms of more than twice a month\nHistory of gastric surgery\nH. pylori infection\nUse of PPI [OR] or NSAID in the past 4 weeks\nPregnancy\nKnown hypersensitivity to PPI<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Patients with functional dyspepsia that fulfill Rome III criteria [AND] with inadequate relief of dyspeptic symptoms
Age >18
Provision of written consent

Exclusion Criteria:
Presence of organic pathology identified by upper endoscopy [OR] or other investigations
Presence of sliding hiatus hernia as defined by flap valve grade IV disruption of morphology at gastro-esophageal junction
Concurrent medications that affect gastrointestinal motility
 Presence of acid reflux [OR] or heartburn symptoms of more than twice a month
History of gastric surgery
H. pylori infection
Use of PPI [OR] or NSAID in the past 4 weeks
Pregnancy
Known hypersensitivity to PPI
