Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nCervical spine injury with functional loss in the upper extremity\nGreater than 4 months out from C-spine injury\nStable motor recovery\nMedically stable\nInternational Classification for Surgery of the Hand in Tetraplegia of 0-5 at 6 months\nGrade 0 finger/thumb extension at 6 months\nSubjects fluent in English or when not fluent, an appropriate translator is present\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nUnstable patient\nJoint contracture\nSpasticity\nLoss of function is expected to be improved by reliable tendon transfer, tenodesis or arthrodesis that is available\nEvidence of recovering finger/thumb extension at 4-6 months\nGreater than 12 months from spinal cord injury\nSubject not fluent in English or an appropriate translator not available\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nCervical spine injury [AND] with functional loss in the upper extremity\nGreater than 4 months out from C-spine injury\nStable motor recovery\nMedically stable\nInternational Classification for Surgery of the Hand in Tetraplegia of 0-5 at 6 months\nGrade 0 finger/ [OR] thumb extension at 6 months\nSubjects fluent in English or when not fluent, an appropriate translator is present\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nUnstable patient\nJoint contracture\nSpasticity\nLoss of function is expected to be improved by reliable tendon transfer, [OR] tenodesis [OR] or arthrodesis that is available\nEvidence of recovering finger/ [OR] thumb extension at 4-6 months\nGreater than 12 months from spinal cord injury\nSubject [NOT] not fluent in English or an appropriate translator [NOT] not available<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Cervical spine injury [AND] with functional loss in the upper extremity
Greater than 4 months out from C-spine injury
Stable motor recovery
Medically stable
International Classification for Surgery of the Hand in Tetraplegia of 0-5 at 6 months
Grade 0 finger/ [OR] thumb extension at 6 months
Subjects fluent in English or when not fluent, an appropriate translator is present

Exclusion Criteria:
Unstable patient
Joint contracture
Spasticity
Loss of function is expected to be improved by reliable tendon transfer, [OR] tenodesis [OR] or arthrodesis that is available
Evidence of recovering finger/ [OR] thumb extension at 4-6 months
Greater than 12 months from spinal cord injury
Subject [NOT] not fluent in English or an appropriate translator [NOT] not available
