cle activity \nAny diagnosed cardiovascular, pulmonary, neurological, and/ or orthopedic conditions that would interfere with subject participation       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nweigh more than 200 lbs \nare high level ambulators corresponding to levels E to F of the Special Interest Group of Amputee Medicine (SIGAM) mobility grade \nhave the ability to follow multi-step commands. \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nscore level D on the SIGAM mobility grade \nhave experienced 1 or more falls in the last month before the study \nhave a residual limb length which does [NOT] not allow for seven inches clearance of bracket attachment for the PowerFoot \nthe residual limb must be stable in volume ([NOT] no change in socket [OR] or socket padding in last 6 months) [AND] and [NOT] without pain that [NOT] limits function \nthe sound-side (contralateral) lower extremity must be [NOT] free of impediments that affect gait, [OR] range of motion, [OR] or limb muscle activity \nAny diagnosed cardiovascular, [OR] pulmonary, [OR] neurological, [OR] and/ or orthopedic conditions that would interfere with subject participation<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
weigh more than 200 lbs 
are high level ambulators corresponding to levels E to F of the Special Interest Group of Amputee Medicine (SIGAM) mobility grade 
have the ability to follow multi-step commands. 

Exclusion Criteria:
score level D on the SIGAM mobility grade 
have experienced 1 or more falls in the last month before the study 
have a residual limb length which does [NOT] not allow for seven inches clearance of bracket attachment for the PowerFoot 
the residual limb must be stable in volume ([NOT] no change in socket [OR] or socket padding in last 6 months) [AND] and [NOT] without pain that [NOT] limits function 
the sound-side (contralateral) lower extremity must be [NOT] free of impediments that affect gait, [OR] range of motion, [OR] or limb muscle activity 
Any diagnosed cardiovascular, [OR] pulmonary, [OR] neurological, [OR] and/ or orthopedic conditions that would interfere with subject participation
