Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients must be more than 18 years of age and referred for coronary angiography\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPlan for diagnostic-only coronary angiography\nOn colchicine chronically\nHistory of intolerance to colchicine\nGlomerular filtration rate <30mL/minute or on dialysis\nActive malignancy or infection\nHistory of myelodysplasia\nHigh-dose statin load <24 hours prior to procedure\nUse of oral steroids or non-steroidal anti-inflammatory agents other than aspirin within 72 hours or 3 times the agent\'s half-life (whichever is longer)\nUse of strong CYP3A4/P-glycoprotein inhibitors (specifically ritonavir, ketoconazole, clarithromycin, cyclosporine, diltiazem and verapamil)\nUnable to consent\nParticipating in a competing study\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients must be more than 18 years of age [AND] and referred for coronary angiography\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPlan for diagnostic-only coronary angiography\nOn colchicine chronically\nHistory of intolerance to colchicine\nGlomerular filtration rate <30mL/minute [OR] or on dialysis\nActive malignancy [OR] or infection\nHistory of myelodysplasia\nHigh-dose statin load <24 hours prior to procedure\nUse of oral steroids [OR] or non-steroidal anti-inflammatory agents other than aspirin within 72 hours [OR] or 3 times the agent\'s half-life (whichever is longer)\nUse of strong CYP3A4/ [OR] P-glycoprotein inhibitors (specifically ritonavir, [OR] ketoconazole, [OR] clarithromycin, [OR] cyclosporine, [OR] diltiazem [OR] and verapamil)\nUnable to consent\nParticipating in a competing study<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Patients must be more than 18 years of age [AND] and referred for coronary angiography

Exclusion Criteria:
Plan for diagnostic-only coronary angiography
On colchicine chronically
History of intolerance to colchicine
Glomerular filtration rate <30mL/minute [OR] or on dialysis
Active malignancy [OR] or infection
History of myelodysplasia
High-dose statin load <24 hours prior to procedure
Use of oral steroids [OR] or non-steroidal anti-inflammatory agents other than aspirin within 72 hours [OR] or 3 times the agent's half-life (whichever is longer)
Use of strong CYP3A4/ [OR] P-glycoprotein inhibitors (specifically ritonavir, [OR] ketoconazole, [OR] clarithromycin, [OR] cyclosporine, [OR] diltiazem [OR] and verapamil)
Unable to consent
Participating in a competing study
