Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nHealthy male volunteers, 18 to 45 years of age, inclusive. Healthy status is defined by absence of evidence of any active or chronic disease following a detailed medical and surgical history, a complete physical examination including vital signs, 12-lead ECG, hematology, blood chemistry, serology and urinalysis \nBody mass index (BMI) 18 to 30 kg/m2 inclusive \nMale subjects (whether surgically sterilized or not) with female partners of child-bearing potential must use two forms of contraception, one of which must be a barrier method, for the duration of the study and for 77 days after the last dose \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nHistory or presence of any clinically significant disease or disorder \nAny condition or disease that would render the subject unsuitable for the study, place the subject at undue risk or interfere with the ability of the subject to complete the study in the opinion of the investigator \nHistory of clinically significant hypersensitivity or allergic drug reactions \nAny suspicion or history of alcohol abuse and/or consumption of other drugs of abuse \nRegular smoker (> 5 cigarettes, > 1 pipeful or > 1 cigar per day) \nPositive for hepatitis B, hepatitis C or HIV infection \nDietary restrictions that would prohibit the consumption of standardized meals \nParticipation in an investigational drug or device study within 90 days prior to screening, as calculated from the follow-up from the previous study       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nHealthy male volunteers, 18 to 45 years of age, inclusive. Healthy status is defined by [NOT] absence of evidence of any active [OR] or chronic disease following a detailed medical [OR] and surgical history, a complete physical examination including vital signs, 12-lead ECG, [OR] hematology, [OR] blood chemistry, [OR] serology [OR] and urinalysis \nBody mass index (BMI) 18 to 30 kg/m2 inclusive \nMale subjects (whether surgically sterilized [OR] or [NOT] not) [AND] with female partners [AND] of child-bearing potential must use two forms of contraception, one of which must be a barrier method, for the duration of the study [AND] and for 77 days after the last dose \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nHistory [OR] or presence of any clinically significant disease [OR] or disorder \nAny condition [OR] or disease that would render the subject unsuitable for the study, place the subject at undue risk [OR] or interfere with the ability of the subject to complete the study in the opinion of the investigator \nHistory of clinically significant hypersensitivity [OR] or allergic drug reactions \n Any suspicion [OR] or history of alcohol abuse [OR] and/or consumption of other drugs of abuse \nRegular smoker (> 5 cigarettes, > 1 pipeful [OR] or > 1 cigar per day) \nPositive for hepatitis B, [OR] hepatitis C [OR] or HIV infection \nDietary restrictions that would [NOT] prohibit the consumption of standardized meals \nParticipation in an investigational drug [OR] or device study within 90 days prior to screening, as calculated from the follow-up from the previous study<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Healthy male volunteers, 18 to 45 years of age, inclusive. Healthy status is defined by [NOT] absence of evidence of any active [OR] or chronic disease following a detailed medical [OR] and surgical history, a complete physical examination including vital signs, 12-lead ECG, [OR] hematology, [OR] blood chemistry, [OR] serology [OR] and urinalysis 
Body mass index (BMI) 18 to 30 kg/m2 inclusive 
Male subjects (whether surgically sterilized [OR] or [NOT] not) [AND] with female partners [AND] of child-bearing potential must use two forms of contraception, one of which must be a barrier method, for the duration of the study [AND] and for 77 days after the last dose 

Exclusion Criteria:
History [OR] or presence of any clinically significant disease [OR] or disorder 
Any condition [OR] or disease that would render the subject unsuitable for the study, place the subject at undue risk [OR] or interfere with the ability of the subject to complete the study in the opinion of the investigator 
History of clinically significant hypersensitivity [OR] or allergic drug reactions 
 Any suspicion [OR] or history of alcohol abuse [OR] and/or consumption of other drugs of abuse 
Regular smoker (> 5 cigarettes, > 1 pipeful [OR] or > 1 cigar per day) 
Positive for hepatitis B, [OR] hepatitis C [OR] or HIV infection 
Dietary restrictions that would [NOT] prohibit the consumption of standardized meals 
Participation in an investigational drug [OR] or device study within 90 days prior to screening, as calculated from the follow-up from the previous study
