Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\n18 years or older\nChest radiograph showing new opacities.\nCough\nProduction of sputum\nTemp >38,0 °C or <36,0 °C\nAudible abnormalities by chest examination compatible with pneumonia\nLeukocytosis (>10.000 cells/mm3), leftward shift (>10%) or leucopenia (<4000 cells/mm3)\nC-reactive protein > 15 mg/l (three fold higher than the upper limit of normal)\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nImmunocompromised patients:\nPatients with a known congenital or acquired immunodeficiency.\nPatients who received chemotherapy less than 6 weeks ago.\nPatients who received corticosteroids in the last 6 weeks.\nPatients who received immunosuppressive medication in the last 6 weeks (e.g. cyclosporin, cyclophosphamide, azathioprine).\nPatients with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease who are on systemic corticosteroids.\nPatients who require intensive care unit treatment.\nPatients with tropical worm infection.\nPatients with dexamethasone intolerance.\nPregnant and breastfeeding women.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n18 years or older\nChest radiograph showing new opacities.\nCough\nProduction of sputum\nTemp >38,0 °C [OR] or <36,0 °C\nAudible abnormalities by chest examination compatible with pneumonia\nLeukocytosis (>10.000 cells/mm3), leftward shift (>10%) [OR] or leucopenia (<4000 cells/mm3)\nC-reactive protein > 15 mg/l (three fold higher than the upper limit of normal)\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nImmunocompromised patients:\nPatients with a known congenital [OR] or acquired immunodeficiency.\nPatients who received chemotherapy less than 6 weeks ago.\n Patients who received corticosteroids in the last 6 weeks.\n Patients who received immunosuppressive medication in the last 6 weeks (e.g. cyclosporin, [OR] cyclophosphamide, [OR] azathioprine).\n Patients with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease [AND] [AND] who are on systemic corticosteroids.\n Patients who require intensive care unit treatment.\n Patients with tropical worm infection.\n Patients with dexamethasone intolerance.\nPregnant [OR] and breastfeeding women.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
18 years or older
Chest radiograph showing new opacities.
Cough
Production of sputum
Temp >38,0 °C [OR] or <36,0 °C
Audible abnormalities by chest examination compatible with pneumonia
Leukocytosis (>10.000 cells/mm3), leftward shift (>10%) [OR] or leucopenia (<4000 cells/mm3)
C-reactive protein > 15 mg/l (three fold higher than the upper limit of normal)

Exclusion Criteria:
Immunocompromised patients:
Patients with a known congenital [OR] or acquired immunodeficiency.
Patients who received chemotherapy less than 6 weeks ago.
 Patients who received corticosteroids in the last 6 weeks.
 Patients who received immunosuppressive medication in the last 6 weeks (e.g. cyclosporin, [OR] cyclophosphamide, [OR] azathioprine).
 Patients with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease [AND] [AND] who are on systemic corticosteroids.
 Patients who require intensive care unit treatment.
 Patients with tropical worm infection.
 Patients with dexamethasone intolerance.
Pregnant [OR] and breastfeeding women.
