Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nmajor elective gastrointestinal, gynecological, prostate or bladder surgery patients who are = 60 years old.\nthe surgery is laparoscopic surgery and is expected to last for = 2 hours under general anesthesia and the patient will stay in hospital for at least 7 days after surgery.\nlack of serious hearing and vision impairment and be able to read so that neurobehavioral tests can be performed.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPatients are not expected to be alive for longer than 3 months.\nMini-mental State Examination (MMSE) [18] score = 23.\nhistory of dementia, psychiatric illness or any diseases of central nervous system.\ncurrent use of sedatives or antidepressant.\nalcoholism and drug dependence.\npatients previously included in this study (for patients who have second intra-abdominal surgery during the study period).\ndifficult to follow up or patients with poor compliance.\nuncontrolled hypertension (> 180/100 mmHg)\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nmajor elective gastrointestinal, [OR] gynecological, [OR] prostate [OR] or bladder surgery patients [AND] who are = 60 years old.\nthe surgery is laparoscopic surgery [AND] and is expected to last for = 2 hours under general anesthesia [AND] and the patient will stay in hospital for at least 7 days after surgery.\n[NOT] lack of serious hearing [AND] and vision impairment [AND] and be able to read so that neurobehavioral tests can be performed.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPatients are [NOT] not expected to be alive for longer than 3 months.\nMini-mental State Examination (MMSE) [18] score = 23.\nhistory of dementia, [OR] psychiatric illness [OR] or any diseases of central nervous system.\ncurrent use of sedatives [OR] or antidepressant.\nalcoholism [OR] and drug dependence.\npatients previously included in this study (for patients who have second intra-abdominal surgery during the study period).\ndifficult to follow up or patients with poor compliance.\nuncontrolled hypertension (> 180/100 mmHg)<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
major elective gastrointestinal, [OR] gynecological, [OR] prostate [OR] or bladder surgery patients [AND] who are = 60 years old.
the surgery is laparoscopic surgery [AND] and is expected to last for = 2 hours under general anesthesia [AND] and the patient will stay in hospital for at least 7 days after surgery.
[NOT] lack of serious hearing [AND] and vision impairment [AND] and be able to read so that neurobehavioral tests can be performed.

Exclusion Criteria:
Patients are [NOT] not expected to be alive for longer than 3 months.
Mini-mental State Examination (MMSE) [18] score = 23.
history of dementia, [OR] psychiatric illness [OR] or any diseases of central nervous system.
current use of sedatives [OR] or antidepressant.
alcoholism [OR] and drug dependence.
patients previously included in this study (for patients who have second intra-abdominal surgery during the study period).
difficult to follow up or patients with poor compliance.
uncontrolled hypertension (> 180/100 mmHg)
