Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nHistologic or cytologic diagnosis of stage IIIB/IV NSCLC \nECOG PS: 0,1 \nUnidimensional or bi-dimensional measurable disease \nReceive prior treatment including first-line platinum-based chemotherapy, standard second-line chemotherapy and 1 EGF/EGFR inhibitor \nEvidence of disease progression \nLife expectancy >12 weeks \nNeutrophils > 1.5 109/l, Platelets > 100 109/l, Hemoglobin > 9g/dl, Total bilirubin < 1.5 UNL, AST (SGOT) and ALT (SGPT) < 2.5 UNL, Alkaline phosphatases < 5 UNL, Creatinine < 1 UNL \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPre-existing hemoptysis of a severity > grade 3 by NCI CTCAE criteria within 4 weeks prior to study entry \nUncontrolled hypertension \nCHF, angina or arrhythmias \nLVEF < 1 UNL \nExisting a second malignancy within 5 years \nInfected with HIV       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nHistologic [OR] or cytologic diagnosis of stage IIIB/ [OR] IV NSCLC \nECOG PS: 0,1 \nUnidimensional [OR] or bi-dimensional measurable disease \nReceive prior treatment including first-line platinum-based chemotherapy, standard second-line chemotherapy [AND] and 1 EGF/ [OR] EGFR inhibitor \nEvidence of disease progression \nLife expectancy >12 weeks \nNeutrophils > 1.5 109/l, Platelets > 100 109/l, Hemoglobin > 9g/dl, Total bilirubin < 1.5 UNL, AST (SGOT) [AND] and ALT (SGPT) < 2.5 UNL, Alkaline phosphatases < 5 UNL, Creatinine < 1 UNL \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPre-existing hemoptysis [AND] of a severity > grade 3 by NCI CTCAE criteria within 4 weeks prior to study entry \nUncontrolled hypertension \nCHF, [OR] angina [OR] or arrhythmias \nLVEF < 1 UNL \nExisting a second malignancy within 5 years \nInfected with HIV       \n<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Histologic [OR] or cytologic diagnosis of stage IIIB/ [OR] IV NSCLC 
ECOG PS: 0,1 
Unidimensional [OR] or bi-dimensional measurable disease 
Receive prior treatment including first-line platinum-based chemotherapy, standard second-line chemotherapy [AND] and 1 EGF/ [OR] EGFR inhibitor 
Evidence of disease progression 
Life expectancy >12 weeks 
Neutrophils > 1.5 109/l, Platelets > 100 109/l, Hemoglobin > 9g/dl, Total bilirubin < 1.5 UNL, AST (SGOT) [AND] and ALT (SGPT) < 2.5 UNL, Alkaline phosphatases < 5 UNL, Creatinine < 1 UNL 

Exclusion Criteria:
Pre-existing hemoptysis [AND] of a severity > grade 3 by NCI CTCAE criteria within 4 weeks prior to study entry 
Uncontrolled hypertension 
CHF, [OR] angina [OR] or arrhythmias 
LVEF < 1 UNL 
Existing a second malignancy within 5 years 
Infected with HIV       

