Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients with a confirmed diagnosis of: \n1. Stage 4 colon cancer either s/p metastasectomy or post-initial chemotherapy or maintenance "standard of care", either involving 5-fluorouracil/leucovorin (5-FU/LV) alone or continual bevacizumab alone. Patients in maintenance cohort must have had 2 consecutive CT scans showing stable disease and not be experiencing significant prior treatment-related toxicity above Grade 1. \n2. Pancreas cancer, either s/p resection and adjuvant chemotherapy or locally advanced pancreas cancer s/p chemotherapy and radiation. Initial chemotherapy or radiation therapy may have been stopped between 2 weeks and 2 months prior to study start, and patients must have recovered from prior treatment related toxicity to grade 1 or less. \nPrior surgery, including tumor resection or metastasectomy must have been performed at least 4 weeks prior to study enrollment. \nNo concomitant anti-cancer treatment is allowed \nAge >/= 18 years \nPerformance status of 0-1 \nAdequate hepatic, bone marrow, and renal function \nPartial thromboplastin time (PTT) must be </= 1.5 x upper normal limit of institution\'s normal range and INR (International Normalized Ratio) < 1.5. \nLife expectancy >/= 4 months for maintenance cohorts and >/= 6 months for adjuvant cohorts \nWomen of childbearing potential must have a negative serum pregnancy test within 14 days prior to initiation of treatment and must not be lactating. \nSubject is capable of understanding and complying with protocol demands and able to sign and date the informed consent \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nWomen of child-bearing potential, who are biologically able to conceive, not employing two forms of highly effective contraception or who are pregnant. \nWomen who are breast-feeding \nFertile males unwilling to use contraception \nPatients with brain metastases or any history of brain metastases \nPatients who have undergone major surgery (e.g., intra-thoracic, -abdominal, or -pelvic) </= 4 weeks prior to starting study treatment or who have not recovered from such therapy \nPatients with a history of pulmonary embolism, or untreated deep vein thrombosis within the past 6 months \nImpairment of gastrointestinal (GI) function or GI disease that may significantly alter the absorption of dovitinib \nThe subject has had another active malignancy within the past 5 years except for cervical cancer in situ, in situ carcinoma of the bladder or non-melanoma carcinoma of the skin. \nPatients who have received the last administration of an anticancer therapy including chemotherapy, immunotherapy, hormonal therapy and monoclonal antibodies </= 2 weeks prior to starting the study drug, or who have not recovered from the side effects of such therapy \nCirrhosis, chronic active hepatitis or chronic persistent hepatitis \nPatients who are currently receiving prasugrel \nNo concurrent use of isoniazid, labetolol, trovafloxacin, tolcapone, and felbamate \nNo concurrent use of other investigational drugs or antineoplastic therapies. \nPatients with impaired cardiac function or clinically significant cardiac diseases.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients with a confirmed diagnosis of: \n1. Stage 4 colon cancer either s/p metastasectomy [OR] or post-initial chemotherapy [OR] or maintenance "standard of care", either involving 5-fluorouracil/ [OR] leucovorin (5-FU/ [OR] LV) alone [OR] or continual bevacizumab alone. Patients in maintenance cohort must have had 2 consecutive CT scans showing stable disease [AND] and [NOT] not be experiencing significant prior treatment-related toxicity above Grade 1. \n2. Pancreas cancer, either s/p resection [OR] and adjuvant chemotherapy [OR] or locally advanced pancreas cancer s/p chemotherapy [OR] and radiation. Initial chemotherapy [OR] or radiation therapy may have been [NOT] stopped between 2 weeks and 2 months prior to study start, and patients must have recovered from prior treatment related toxicity to grade 1 or less. \nPrior surgery, including tumor resection [OR] or metastasectomy must have been performed at least 4 weeks prior to study enrollment. \n[NOT] No concomitant anti-cancer treatment is allowed \nAge >/= 18 years \nPerformance status of 0-1 \nAdequate hepatic, [OR] bone marrow, [OR] and renal function \nPartial thromboplastin time (PTT) must be </= 1.5 x upper normal limit of institution\'s normal range and INR (International Normalized Ratio) < 1.5. \nLife expectancy >/= 4 months for maintenance cohorts and >/= 6 months for adjuvant cohorts \nWomen [AND] of childbearing potential must have a negative serum pregnancy test within 14 days prior to initiation of treatment [AND] and must [NOT] not be lactating. \nSubject is capable of understanding and complying with protocol demands and able to sign and date the informed consent \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nWomen [AND] of child-bearing potential, [AND] who are biologically able to conceive, [NOT] not employing two forms of highly effective contraception [OR] or who are pregnant. \nWomen [AND] who are breast-feeding \nFertile males unwilling to use contraception \nPatients with brain metastases [OR] or any history of brain metastases \nPatients who have undergone major surgery (e.g., intra-thoracic, [OR] -abdominal, [OR] or -pelvic) </= 4 weeks prior to starting study treatment [OR] or who have [NOT] not recovered from such therapy \nPatients with a history of pulmonary embolism, [OR] or [NOT] untreated deep vein thrombosis within the past 6 months \nImpairment of gastrointestinal (GI) function [OR] or GI disease that may significantly alter the absorption of dovitinib \nThe subject has had another active malignancy within the past 5 years except for cervical cancer in situ, in situ carcinoma of the bladder [OR] or [NOT] non-melanoma carcinoma of the skin. \nPatients who have received the last administration of an anticancer therapy including chemotherapy, [OR] immunotherapy, [OR] hormonal therapy [OR] and monoclonal antibodies </= 2 weeks prior to starting the study drug, [OR] or who have [NOT] not recovered from the side effects of such therapy \nCirrhosis, chronic active hepatitis [OR] or chronic persistent hepatitis \nPatients who are currently receiving prasugrel \n [NOT] No concurrent use of isoniazid, [OR] labetolol, [OR] trovafloxacin, [OR] tolcapone, [OR] and felbamate \n [NOT] No concurrent use of other investigational drugs [OR] or antineoplastic therapies. \nPatients with impaired cardiac function [OR] or clinically significant cardiac diseases.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Patients with a confirmed diagnosis of: 
1. Stage 4 colon cancer either s/p metastasectomy [OR] or post-initial chemotherapy [OR] or maintenance "standard of care", either involving 5-fluorouracil/ [OR] leucovorin (5-FU/ [OR] LV) alone [OR] or continual bevacizumab alone. Patients in maintenance cohort must have had 2 consecutive CT scans showing stable disease [AND] and [NOT] not be experiencing significant prior treatment-related toxicity above Grade 1. 
2. Pancreas cancer, either s/p resection [OR] and adjuvant chemotherapy [OR] or locally advanced pancreas cancer s/p chemotherapy [OR] and radiation. Initial chemotherapy [OR] or radiation therapy may have been [NOT] stopped between 2 weeks and 2 months prior to study start, and patients must have recovered from prior treatment related toxicity to grade 1 or less. 
Prior surgery, including tumor resection [OR] or metastasectomy must have been performed at least 4 weeks prior to study enrollment. 
[NOT] No concomitant anti-cancer treatment is allowed 
Age >/= 18 years 
Performance status of 0-1 
Adequate hepatic, [OR] bone marrow, [OR] and renal function 
Partial thromboplastin time (PTT) must be </= 1.5 x upper normal limit of institution's normal range and INR (International Normalized Ratio) < 1.5. 
Life expectancy >/= 4 months for maintenance cohorts and >/= 6 months for adjuvant cohorts 
Women [AND] of childbearing potential must have a negative serum pregnancy test within 14 days prior to initiation of treatment [AND] and must [NOT] not be lactating. 
Subject is capable of understanding and complying with protocol demands and able to sign and date the informed consent 

Exclusion Criteria:
Women [AND] of child-bearing potential, [AND] who are biologically able to conceive, [NOT] not employing two forms of highly effective contraception [OR] or who are pregnant. 
Women [AND] who are breast-feeding 
Fertile males unwilling to use contraception 
Patients with brain metastases [OR] or any history of brain metastases 
Patients who have undergone major surgery (e.g., intra-thoracic, [OR] -abdominal, [OR] or -pelvic) </= 4 weeks prior to starting study treatment [OR] or who have [NOT] not recovered from such therapy 
Patients with a history of pulmonary embolism, [OR] or [NOT] untreated deep vein thrombosis within the past 6 months 
Impairment of gastrointestinal (GI) function [OR] or GI disease that may significantly alter the absorption of dovitinib 
The subject has had another active malignancy within the past 5 years except for cervical cancer in situ, in situ carcinoma of the bladder [OR] or [NOT] non-melanoma carcinoma of the skin. 
Patients who have received the last administration of an anticancer therapy including chemotherapy, [OR] immunotherapy, [OR] hormonal therapy [OR] and monoclonal antibodies </= 2 weeks prior to starting the study drug, [OR] or who have [NOT] not recovered from the side effects of such therapy 
Cirrhosis, chronic active hepatitis [OR] or chronic persistent hepatitis 
Patients who are currently receiving prasugrel 
 [NOT] No concurrent use of isoniazid, [OR] labetolol, [OR] trovafloxacin, [OR] tolcapone, [OR] and felbamate 
 [NOT] No concurrent use of other investigational drugs [OR] or antineoplastic therapies. 
Patients with impaired cardiac function [OR] or clinically significant cardiac diseases.
