Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nCases (with a history of TBI): \n1. Ages 50-95 years \n2. History of traumatic brain injury of sufficient severity to have resulted in medical attention (ascertained via the Ohio State University TBI Identification Questionnaire—OSU TBI-ID, and based on DoD/VA criteria) \n3. Residence in AFRH-Washington D.C. or the Veterans Home of California-Yountville \n4. MMSE score ≥ 20 \n5. Capacity to provide consent to participate in research (assessment made by study physician) \n6. Ability to read and write English \nControls (without a history of TBI): \n1. Ages 50-95 years \n2. No history of traumatic brain injury of sufficient severity to have resulted in medical attention (ascertained via the Ohio State University TBI Identification Questionnaire—OSU TBI-ID) \n3. Residence in AFRH-Washington or the Veterans Home of California-Yountville \n4. MMSE score ≥ 20 \n5. Capacity to provide consent or assent to participate in research \n6. Ability to read and write English - \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nCases (with a history of TBI): \n1. History of penetrating brain injury \n2. History of disabling neurological or psychiatric condition such as epilepsy (besides posttraumatic epilepsy), multiple sclerosis, cortical stroke, hypoxic-ischemic encephalopathy, encephalitis, or schizophrenia \nControls (without a history of TBI): \nHistory of disabling neurological or psychiatric condition such as epilepsy, multiple sclerosis, cortical stroke, hypoxic-ischemic encephalopathy, encephalitis, or schizophrenia       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nCases (with a history of TBI): \n1. Ages 50-95 years \n2. History of traumatic brain injury of sufficient severity to have resulted in medical attention (ascertained via the Ohio State University TBI Identification Questionnaire—OSU TBI-ID, and based on DoD/VA criteria) \n3. Residence in AFRH-Washington D.C. [OR] or the Veterans Home of California-Yountville \n4. MMSE score ≥ 20 \n5. Capacity to provide consent to participate in research (assessment made by study physician) \n6. Ability to read and write English \nControls (without a history of TBI): \n1. Ages 50-95 years \n2. [NOT] No history of traumatic brain injury of sufficient severity to have resulted in medical attention (ascertained via the Ohio State University TBI Identification Questionnaire—OSU TBI-ID) \n3. Residence in AFRH-Washington [OR] or the Veterans Home of California-Yountville \n4. MMSE score ≥ 20 \n5. Capacity to provide consent or assent to participate in research \n6. Ability to read and write English - \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nCases (with a history of TBI): \n1. History of penetrating brain injury \n2. History of disabling neurological [OR] or psychiatric condition such as epilepsy (besides posttraumatic epilepsy), multiple sclerosis, [OR] cortical stroke, [OR] hypoxic-ischemic encephalopathy, [OR] encephalitis, [OR] or schizophrenia \nControls (without a history of TBI): \nHistory of disabling neurological [OR] or psychiatric condition such as epilepsy, [OR] multiple sclerosis, [OR] cortical stroke, [OR] hypoxic-ischemic encephalopathy, [OR] encephalitis, [OR] or schizophrenia<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Cases (with a history of TBI): 
1. Ages 50-95 years 
2. History of traumatic brain injury of sufficient severity to have resulted in medical attention (ascertained via the Ohio State University TBI Identification Questionnaire—OSU TBI-ID, and based on DoD/VA criteria) 
3. Residence in AFRH-Washington D.C. [OR] or the Veterans Home of California-Yountville 
4. MMSE score ≥ 20 
5. Capacity to provide consent to participate in research (assessment made by study physician) 
6. Ability to read and write English 
Controls (without a history of TBI): 
1. Ages 50-95 years 
2. [NOT] No history of traumatic brain injury of sufficient severity to have resulted in medical attention (ascertained via the Ohio State University TBI Identification Questionnaire—OSU TBI-ID) 
3. Residence in AFRH-Washington [OR] or the Veterans Home of California-Yountville 
4. MMSE score ≥ 20 
5. Capacity to provide consent or assent to participate in research 
6. Ability to read and write English - 

Exclusion Criteria:
Cases (with a history of TBI): 
1. History of penetrating brain injury 
2. History of disabling neurological [OR] or psychiatric condition such as epilepsy (besides posttraumatic epilepsy), multiple sclerosis, [OR] cortical stroke, [OR] hypoxic-ischemic encephalopathy, [OR] encephalitis, [OR] or schizophrenia 
Controls (without a history of TBI): 
History of disabling neurological [OR] or psychiatric condition such as epilepsy, [OR] multiple sclerosis, [OR] cortical stroke, [OR] hypoxic-ischemic encephalopathy, [OR] encephalitis, [OR] or schizophrenia
