Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAged at least 18 years \nThe presence of a solid, malignant tumour, excluding lymphoma, that is resistance to standard therapies or for which no standard therapies exist \nThe presence of at least one lesion that can be accurately assessed at baseline by Computerised Tomography (CT), Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI) or plain X-ray and is suitable for repeated assessment \nEstimated life expectancy of more than 12 weeks \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nClinically significant abnormalities of glucose metabolism \nSpinal cord compression or brain metastases unless asymptomatic, treated and stable (not requiring steroids) \nEvidence of severe or uncontrolled systemic diseases, including active bleeding diatheses or active infections including hepatitis B, C and Human Immunodeficiency Virus (HIV) \nEvidence of clinically significant cardiac abnormalities, uncontrolled hypotension, left ventricular ejection fraction below the lower limit of normal for the site or experience of significant cardiac interventional procedures \nA bad reaction to AZD5363 or any drugs similar to it in structure or class       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAged at least 18 years \nThe presence of a solid, [OR] malignant tumour, [OR] excluding lymphoma, [AND] that is resistance to standard therapies [OR] or for which [NOT] no standard therapies exist \nThe presence of at least one lesion that can be accurately assessed at baseline by Computerised Tomography (CT), [OR] Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI) [OR] or plain X-ray [AND] and is suitable for repeated assessment \nEstimated life expectancy of more than 12 weeks \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nClinically significant abnormalities of glucose metabolism \nSpinal cord compression [OR] or brain metastases unless asymptomatic, treated [AND] and stable ([NOT] not requiring steroids) \nEvidence of severe [OR] or uncontrolled systemic diseases, including active bleeding diatheses [OR] or active infections including hepatitis B, [OR] C [OR] and Human Immunodeficiency Virus (HIV) \nEvidence of clinically significant cardiac abnormalities, uncontrolled hypotension, [OR] left ventricular ejection fraction below the lower limit of normal for the site [OR] or experience of significant cardiac interventional procedures \nA bad reaction to AZD5363 [OR] or any drugs similar to it in structure [OR] or class<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Aged at least 18 years 
The presence of a solid, [OR] malignant tumour, [OR] excluding lymphoma, [AND] that is resistance to standard therapies [OR] or for which [NOT] no standard therapies exist 
The presence of at least one lesion that can be accurately assessed at baseline by Computerised Tomography (CT), [OR] Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI) [OR] or plain X-ray [AND] and is suitable for repeated assessment 
Estimated life expectancy of more than 12 weeks 

Exclusion Criteria:
Clinically significant abnormalities of glucose metabolism 
Spinal cord compression [OR] or brain metastases unless asymptomatic, treated [AND] and stable ([NOT] not requiring steroids) 
Evidence of severe [OR] or uncontrolled systemic diseases, including active bleeding diatheses [OR] or active infections including hepatitis B, [OR] C [OR] and Human Immunodeficiency Virus (HIV) 
Evidence of clinically significant cardiac abnormalities, uncontrolled hypotension, [OR] left ventricular ejection fraction below the lower limit of normal for the site [OR] or experience of significant cardiac interventional procedures 
A bad reaction to AZD5363 [OR] or any drugs similar to it in structure [OR] or class
