Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAge : from 20 to 90 y/o.\nHBsAg-positive for more than 6 months and HBV DNA < 2000 IU/ml (Subgroup 1)or HBsAg-negative but anti-HBc positive with HBV DNA < 2000 IU/ml (Subgroup 2).\nInflammatory arthritis patients who plan to treat with biological agents, including Humira or Enbrel or Simponi or Orencia or Mabthera or Actemra; as first line biologic treatment is indicated.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nHCV, HIV, or HDV coinfection.\nHCC or other malignancy within 3 years.\nDecompensated liver cirrhosis (CTP score = 7).\nUremia patients under hemodialysis or continuous ambulatory peritoneal dialysis or patients with Ccr < 50 mL/min\nPregnant or breastfeeding women.\nWomen of child-bearing potential (WOCBP) who are unwilling or unable to use an acceptable method of contraception to avoid pregnancy throughout the study and for up to 4 weeks after the last dose of study drug.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAge : from 20 to 90 y/o.\nHBsAg-positive for more than 6 months [AND] and HBV DNA < 2000 IU/ml (Subgroup 1) [OR] or HBsAg- [NOT] negative [AND] but anti-HBc positive [AND] with HBV DNA < 2000 IU/ml (Subgroup 2).\nInflammatory arthritis patients [AND] who plan to treat with biological agents, including Humira [OR] or Enbrel [OR] or Simponi [OR] or Orencia [OR] or Mabthera [OR] or Actemra; as first line biologic treatment is indicated.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nHCV, [OR] HIV, [OR] or HDV coinfection.\nHCC [OR] or other malignancy within 3 years.\nDecompensated liver cirrhosis (CTP score = 7).\nUremia patients under hemodialysis [OR] or continuous ambulatory peritoneal dialysis [OR] or patients with Ccr < 50 mL/min\nPregnant [OR] or breastfeeding women.\nWomen [AND] of child-bearing potential (WOCBP) [AND] who are unwilling [OR] or [NOT] unable to use an acceptable method of contraception to [NOT] avoid pregnancy throughout the study [AND] and for up to 4 weeks after the last dose of study drug.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Age : from 20 to 90 y/o.
HBsAg-positive for more than 6 months [AND] and HBV DNA < 2000 IU/ml (Subgroup 1) [OR] or HBsAg- [NOT] negative [AND] but anti-HBc positive [AND] with HBV DNA < 2000 IU/ml (Subgroup 2).
Inflammatory arthritis patients [AND] who plan to treat with biological agents, including Humira [OR] or Enbrel [OR] or Simponi [OR] or Orencia [OR] or Mabthera [OR] or Actemra; as first line biologic treatment is indicated.

Exclusion Criteria:
HCV, [OR] HIV, [OR] or HDV coinfection.
HCC [OR] or other malignancy within 3 years.
Decompensated liver cirrhosis (CTP score = 7).
Uremia patients under hemodialysis [OR] or continuous ambulatory peritoneal dialysis [OR] or patients with Ccr < 50 mL/min
Pregnant [OR] or breastfeeding women.
Women [AND] of child-bearing potential (WOCBP) [AND] who are unwilling [OR] or [NOT] unable to use an acceptable method of contraception to [NOT] avoid pregnancy throughout the study [AND] and for up to 4 weeks after the last dose of study drug.
