Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients with chronic heart failure of New York Heart Association Class II or III, a left ventricular ejection fraction of = 40% for patients in NYHA class II or = 45% for patients in NYHA class III, a hemoglobin level at the screening visit between 9.5-13.5 g/dl, and iron deficiency, which is defined as serum ferritin level < 100µg/l or between 100 and 299 µg/l, when transferring saturation is < 20%.\nAge =18 years\nObtained informed consent\nStable pharmacological therapy during the last 4 weeks (with the exception of diuretics)\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nHemochromatosis, iron overload, defined as TSAT > 45%\nKnown hypersensitivity to Ferinject®.\nKnown active infection, CRP>20 mg/L, clinically significant bleeding, active malignancy.\nChronic liver disease and/or screening alanine transaminase (ALT) or aspartate transaminase (AST) above three times the upper limit of the normal range.\nImmunosuppressive therapy or renal dialysis (current or planned within the next 6 months).\nHistory of erythropoietin, i. v. or oral iron therapy, and blood transfusion in previous 12 weeks and/or such therapy planned within the next 6 months.\nUnstable angina pectoris as judged by the investigator, clinically significant uncorrected valvular disease or left ventricular outflow obstruction, obstructive cardiomyopathy, poorly controlled fast atrial fibrillation or flutter, poorly controlled symptomatic brady- or tachyarrhythmias.\nAcute myocardial infarction or acute coronary syndrome, transient ischemic attack or stroke within the last 3 months.\nCoronary-artery bypass graft, percutaneous intervention (e.g. cardiac, cerebrovascular, aortic; diagnostic catheters are allowed) or major surgery, including thoracic and cardiac surgery, within the last 3 months.\nParticipation in a CHF training program.\nKnown HIV/AIDS.\nInability to fully comprehend and/or perform study procedures in the investigator\'s opinion.\nVitamin B12 and/or serum folate deficiency according to the laboratory (re-screening is possible after substitution therapy).\nPregnancy or lactation.\nParticipation in another clinical trial within previous 30 days and/or anticipated participation in another trial during this study.\nAnticoagulation\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients with chronic heart failure of New York Heart Association Class II or III, a left ventricular ejection fraction of = 40% [AND] for patients in NYHA class II [OR] or = 45% [AND] for patients in NYHA class III, a hemoglobin level at the screening visit between 9.5-13.5 g/dl, [AND] and iron deficiency, which is defined as serum ferritin level < 100µg/l [OR] or between 100 and 299 µg/l, when transferring saturation is < 20%.\nAge =18 years\nObtained informed consent\nStable pharmacological therapy during the last 4 weeks (with the exception of diuretics)\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nHemochromatosis, [OR] iron overload, defined as TSAT > 45%\n Known hypersensitivity to Ferinject®.\nKnown active infection, [OR] CRP>20 mg/L, clinically significant bleeding, active malignancy.\nChronic liver disease [OR] and/or screening alanine transaminase (ALT) [OR] or aspartate transaminase (AST) above three times the upper limit of the normal range.\nImmunosuppressive therapy [OR] or renal dialysis (current [OR] or planned within the next 6 months).\n History of erythropoietin, [OR] i. v. [OR] or oral iron therapy, [AND] and blood transfusion in previous 12 weeks [OR] and/or such therapy planned within the next 6 months.\nUnstable angina pectoris as judged by the investigator, clinically significant uncorrected valvular disease [OR] or left ventricular outflow obstruction, [OR] obstructive cardiomyopathy, [OR] poorly controlled fast atrial fibrillation [OR] or flutter, poorly controlled symptomatic brady- [OR] or tachyarrhythmias.\nAcute myocardial infarction [OR] or acute coronary syndrome, [OR] transient ischemic attack [OR] or stroke within the last 3 months.\nCoronary-artery bypass graft, [OR] percutaneous intervention (e.g. cardiac, [OR] cerebrovascular, [OR] aortic; diagnostic catheters are allowed) or major surgery, including thoracic [OR] and cardiac surgery, within the last 3 months.\nParticipation in a CHF training program.\nKnown HIV/AIDS.\nInability to fully comprehend and/or perform study procedures in the investigator\'s opinion.\nVitamin B12 [OR] and/or serum folate deficiency according to the laboratory (re-screening is possible after substitution therapy).\nPregnancy [OR] or lactation.\nParticipation in another clinical trial within previous 30 days [OR] and/or anticipated participation in another trial during this study.\nAnticoagulation<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Patients with chronic heart failure of New York Heart Association Class II or III, a left ventricular ejection fraction of = 40% [AND] for patients in NYHA class II [OR] or = 45% [AND] for patients in NYHA class III, a hemoglobin level at the screening visit between 9.5-13.5 g/dl, [AND] and iron deficiency, which is defined as serum ferritin level < 100µg/l [OR] or between 100 and 299 µg/l, when transferring saturation is < 20%.
Age =18 years
Obtained informed consent
Stable pharmacological therapy during the last 4 weeks (with the exception of diuretics)

Exclusion Criteria:
Hemochromatosis, [OR] iron overload, defined as TSAT > 45%
 Known hypersensitivity to Ferinject®.
Known active infection, [OR] CRP>20 mg/L, clinically significant bleeding, active malignancy.
Chronic liver disease [OR] and/or screening alanine transaminase (ALT) [OR] or aspartate transaminase (AST) above three times the upper limit of the normal range.
Immunosuppressive therapy [OR] or renal dialysis (current [OR] or planned within the next 6 months).
 History of erythropoietin, [OR] i. v. [OR] or oral iron therapy, [AND] and blood transfusion in previous 12 weeks [OR] and/or such therapy planned within the next 6 months.
Unstable angina pectoris as judged by the investigator, clinically significant uncorrected valvular disease [OR] or left ventricular outflow obstruction, [OR] obstructive cardiomyopathy, [OR] poorly controlled fast atrial fibrillation [OR] or flutter, poorly controlled symptomatic brady- [OR] or tachyarrhythmias.
Acute myocardial infarction [OR] or acute coronary syndrome, [OR] transient ischemic attack [OR] or stroke within the last 3 months.
Coronary-artery bypass graft, [OR] percutaneous intervention (e.g. cardiac, [OR] cerebrovascular, [OR] aortic; diagnostic catheters are allowed) or major surgery, including thoracic [OR] and cardiac surgery, within the last 3 months.
Participation in a CHF training program.
Known HIV/AIDS.
Inability to fully comprehend and/or perform study procedures in the investigator's opinion.
Vitamin B12 [OR] and/or serum folate deficiency according to the laboratory (re-screening is possible after substitution therapy).
Pregnancy [OR] or lactation.
Participation in another clinical trial within previous 30 days [OR] and/or anticipated participation in another trial during this study.
Anticoagulation
