Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\n=18 years old, men or post-menopausal women (women with no periods for 12 months or more, or those who have had a surgical menopause)\nTreated hypertensive patients with an average daytime ambulatory blood pressure measurement (ABPM) <150/95mmHg on stable doses of one or more antihypertensive medication (at least one of which should be; an ACE inhibitor, angiotensin receptor blocker or diuretic) for 3 months, or untreated hypertensive patients with an average daytime ABPM =135/85 but <150/95.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nHistory of ischaemic heart disease, cardiac failure, cerebrovascular disease, liver impairment (ALT/AST>50IU/L) or stage 3-5 chronic kidney disease.\nHistory of overdose or suicidal ideation\nPatients weighing <55kgs.\nPatients with chronic pain requiring treatment, with a known allergy to paracetamol, or concomitant use of non-steroidal anti-inflammatories, oral anticoagulants or corticosteroids.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n=18 years old, men [OR] or post-menopausal women ([women] [AND] [NOT] with [NOT] no periods for 12 months or more, [OR] or those who have had a surgical menopause)\nTreated hypertensive patients with an average daytime ambulatory blood pressure measurement (ABPM) <150/95mmHg on stable doses of one or more antihypertensive medication (at least one of which should be; an ACE inhibitor, [OR] angiotensin receptor blocker [OR] or diuretic) for 3 months, [OR] or [NOT] untreated hypertensive patients with an average daytime ABPM =135/85 [AND] but <150/95.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nHistory of ischaemic heart disease, [OR] cardiac failure, [OR] cerebrovascular disease, [OR] liver impairment (ALT/ [OR] AST>50IU/L) or stage 3-5 chronic kidney disease.\nHistory of overdose [OR] or suicidal ideation\nPatients weighing <55kgs.\nPatients with chronic pain requiring treatment, [AND] with a known allergy to paracetamol, [OR] or concomitant use of non-steroidal anti-inflammatories, [OR] oral anticoagulants [OR] or corticosteroids.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
=18 years old, men [OR] or post-menopausal women ([women] [AND] [NOT] with [NOT] no periods for 12 months or more, [OR] or those who have had a surgical menopause)
Treated hypertensive patients with an average daytime ambulatory blood pressure measurement (ABPM) <150/95mmHg on stable doses of one or more antihypertensive medication (at least one of which should be; an ACE inhibitor, [OR] angiotensin receptor blocker [OR] or diuretic) for 3 months, [OR] or [NOT] untreated hypertensive patients with an average daytime ABPM =135/85 [AND] but <150/95.

Exclusion Criteria:
History of ischaemic heart disease, [OR] cardiac failure, [OR] cerebrovascular disease, [OR] liver impairment (ALT/ [OR] AST>50IU/L) or stage 3-5 chronic kidney disease.
History of overdose [OR] or suicidal ideation
Patients weighing <55kgs.
Patients with chronic pain requiring treatment, [AND] with a known allergy to paracetamol, [OR] or concomitant use of non-steroidal anti-inflammatories, [OR] oral anticoagulants [OR] or corticosteroids.
