Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\ncolorectal cancer above to 12 cm from the anal verge\nunresectable synchronous metastases\nno contraindications for chemotherapy\nabsence of peritoneal carcinomatosis, central nervous system o bone metastasis.\nperformance status ECOG = 2 (Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group)\nuncontrolled concomitant medical conditions that may compromise to chemotherapy\nsignificant symptomatic cardiac disease\nnot pregnancy or breastfeeding\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nCases of rectal tumours below 12cm from anal verge, or locally advanced tumours invading blood vessels, nerves or bone.\nMultiple bone metastasis or central nervous system metastasis\nOther neoplastic disease in the 5 previous years, except squamous or basal cell skin carcinoma or cervical "in situ" carcinoma\nSignificant heart disease (chronic congestive heart failure, symptomatic coronary disease) or myocardial infarction in the previous 6 months\nPeripheral neuropathy\nPatients who do not give informed consent\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\ncolorectal cancer above to 12 cm from the anal verge\nunresectable synchronous metastases\n [NOT] no contraindications for chemotherapy\n [NOT] absence of peritoneal carcinomatosis, [OR] central nervous system [OR] o bone metastasis.\nperformance status ECOG = 2 (Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group)\nuncontrolled concomitant medical conditions that may compromise to chemotherapy\nsignificant symptomatic cardiac disease\n [NOT] not pregnancy [OR] or breastfeeding\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nCases of rectal tumours below 12cm from anal verge, [OR] or locally advanced tumours invading blood vessels, [OR] nerves [OR] or bone.\nMultiple bone metastasis [OR] or central nervous system metastasis\n Other neoplastic disease in the 5 previous years, except squamous [OR] or basal cell skin carcinoma [OR] or cervical "in situ" carcinoma\n Significant heart disease (chronic congestive heart failure, symptomatic coronary disease) [OR] or myocardial infarction in the previous 6 months\n Peripheral neuropathy\n Patients who do not give informed consent<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
colorectal cancer above to 12 cm from the anal verge
unresectable synchronous metastases
 [NOT] no contraindications for chemotherapy
 [NOT] absence of peritoneal carcinomatosis, [OR] central nervous system [OR] o bone metastasis.
performance status ECOG = 2 (Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group)
uncontrolled concomitant medical conditions that may compromise to chemotherapy
significant symptomatic cardiac disease
 [NOT] not pregnancy [OR] or breastfeeding

Exclusion Criteria:
Cases of rectal tumours below 12cm from anal verge, [OR] or locally advanced tumours invading blood vessels, [OR] nerves [OR] or bone.
Multiple bone metastasis [OR] or central nervous system metastasis
 Other neoplastic disease in the 5 previous years, except squamous [OR] or basal cell skin carcinoma [OR] or cervical "in situ" carcinoma
 Significant heart disease (chronic congestive heart failure, symptomatic coronary disease) [OR] or myocardial infarction in the previous 6 months
 Peripheral neuropathy
 Patients who do not give informed consent
