Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nType 2 Diabetes\nHypertension\nEstimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) > 30 ml/min\nUse of Ace Inh and ARB for control of blood pressure who are willing to be placed on alternate drug(s) in the washout period for blood pressure control\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPregnancy\nPatients with chronic kidney disease stage with eGFR < 30 ml/min (CKD stage IV and V)\nNephrotic range proteinuria (urinary protein > 3.5 gm/day)\nHistory or renal transplantation\nHistory of multiple myeloma\nKnown history of hypersensitivity reaction or intolerability to Ace Inh or ARB.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nType 2 Diabetes\nHypertension\nEstimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) > 30 ml/min\nUse of Ace Inh [OR] and ARB for control of blood pressure [AND] who are willing to be placed on alternate drug(s) in the washout period for blood pressure control\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPregnancy\nPatients with chronic kidney disease stage [AND] with eGFR < 30 ml/min (CKD stage IV and V)\nNephrotic range proteinuria (urinary protein > 3.5 gm/day)\nHistory or renal transplantation\nHistory of multiple myeloma\nKnown history of hypersensitivity reaction [OR] or intolerability to Ace Inh [OR] or ARB.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Type 2 Diabetes
Hypertension
Estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) > 30 ml/min
Use of Ace Inh [OR] and ARB for control of blood pressure [AND] who are willing to be placed on alternate drug(s) in the washout period for blood pressure control

Exclusion Criteria:
Pregnancy
Patients with chronic kidney disease stage [AND] with eGFR < 30 ml/min (CKD stage IV and V)
Nephrotic range proteinuria (urinary protein > 3.5 gm/day)
History or renal transplantation
History of multiple myeloma
Known history of hypersensitivity reaction [OR] or intolerability to Ace Inh [OR] or ARB.
