Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAdults (= 18 years of age) with World Health Organization Group 2 Pulmonary Hypertension (Mean pulmonary artery pressure = 25 mmHg and pulmonary capillary wedge pressure = 15 mmHg)\nNew York Heart Association class II-IV symptoms\nLeft ventricular ejection fraction (LVEF) = 45%\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nOther causes of heart failure other than diastolic dysfunction, such as restrictive cardiomyopathy or infiltrative cardiomyopathy\nWomen who are pregnant or nursing\nLiver cirrhosis,\nPrimary valvular disease\nAcute coronary syndrome\nCauses of PH other than that of heart failure, such as: chronic thromboembolic PH, sickle-cell disease, or sarcoidosis\nSevere bradycardia or greater than 1st degree heart block\nDecompensated heart failure\nCurrent use of a third generation beta-blocker (nebivolol, carvedilol, or labetalol) or high dose of any beta-blockers (greater than 100 mg daily of metoprolol, or equivalent)\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAdults (= 18 years of age) [AND] with World Health Organization Group 2 Pulmonary Hypertension (Mean pulmonary artery pressure = 25 mmHg [AND] and pulmonary capillary wedge pressure = 15 mmHg)\nNew York Heart Association class II-IV symptoms\nLeft ventricular ejection fraction (LVEF) = 45%\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nOther causes of heart failure other than diastolic dysfunction, such as restrictive cardiomyopathy [OR] or infiltrative cardiomyopathy\nWomen [AND] who are pregnant [OR] or nursing\nLiver cirrhosis,\nPrimary valvular disease\nAcute coronary syndrome\nCauses of PH other than that of heart failure, such as: chronic thromboembolic PH, [OR] sickle-cell disease, [OR] or sarcoidosis\nSevere bradycardia [OR] or greater than 1st degree heart block\n Decompensated heart failure\nCurrent use of a third generation beta-blocker (nebivolol, [OR] carvedilol, [OR] or labetalol) [OR] or high dose of any beta-blockers (greater than 100 mg daily of metoprolol, [OR] or equivalent)<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Adults (= 18 years of age) [AND] with World Health Organization Group 2 Pulmonary Hypertension (Mean pulmonary artery pressure = 25 mmHg [AND] and pulmonary capillary wedge pressure = 15 mmHg)
New York Heart Association class II-IV symptoms
Left ventricular ejection fraction (LVEF) = 45%

Exclusion Criteria:
Other causes of heart failure other than diastolic dysfunction, such as restrictive cardiomyopathy [OR] or infiltrative cardiomyopathy
Women [AND] who are pregnant [OR] or nursing
Liver cirrhosis,
Primary valvular disease
Acute coronary syndrome
Causes of PH other than that of heart failure, such as: chronic thromboembolic PH, [OR] sickle-cell disease, [OR] or sarcoidosis
Severe bradycardia [OR] or greater than 1st degree heart block
 Decompensated heart failure
Current use of a third generation beta-blocker (nebivolol, [OR] carvedilol, [OR] or labetalol) [OR] or high dose of any beta-blockers (greater than 100 mg daily of metoprolol, [OR] or equivalent)
