Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nChildren 7-17 with moderate to severe pain requiring around the clock treatment with an opioid analgesic.\nBe an experienced opioid user, defined as any subject treated with opioid therapy, equivalent or equal to >20 mg per day of morphine, for a period of 3 consecutive days immediately prior to first day of dosing.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nColumbia-Suicide Severity Rating Scale (C-SSRS) for suicidal ideation and behavior in past year.\nHypersensitivity to morphine, naltrexone.\nA life expectancy (assessed by investigator) of less than 6 months or is no longer capable of taking medication orally.\nUndergone surgery within 3 days prior to the first day of dosing.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nChildren 7-17 [AND] with moderate [OR] to severe pain requiring around the clock treatment with an opioid analgesic.\nBe an experienced opioid user, defined as any subject treated with opioid therapy, equivalent or equal to >20 mg per day of morphine, for a period of 3 consecutive days immediately prior to first day of dosing.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nColumbia-Suicide Severity Rating Scale (C-SSRS) for suicidal ideation [OR] and behavior in past year.\nHypersensitivity to morphine, [OR] naltrexone.\nA life expectancy (assessed by investigator) of less than 6 months [OR] or is [NOT] no longer capable of taking medication orally.\nUndergone surgery within 3 days prior to the first day of dosing.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Children 7-17 [AND] with moderate [OR] to severe pain requiring around the clock treatment with an opioid analgesic.
Be an experienced opioid user, defined as any subject treated with opioid therapy, equivalent or equal to >20 mg per day of morphine, for a period of 3 consecutive days immediately prior to first day of dosing.

Exclusion Criteria:
Columbia-Suicide Severity Rating Scale (C-SSRS) for suicidal ideation [OR] and behavior in past year.
Hypersensitivity to morphine, [OR] naltrexone.
A life expectancy (assessed by investigator) of less than 6 months [OR] or is [NOT] no longer capable of taking medication orally.
Undergone surgery within 3 days prior to the first day of dosing.
