Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nNormotensive controls\nStage I (140-159/90-99 mmHg) untreated subjects with essential hypertension\nPatients with PA and stage I (140-159/90-99 mmHg) hypertension\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nCongestive heart failure or coronary artery disease\nBlood pressure averaging > 159/99 mmHg\nSerum creatinine > 1.5 mg/dL\nDiabetes mellitus or other systemic illness\nLeft ventricular hypertrophy by echocardiography or ECG\nPregnancy\nHypersensitivity to spironolactone, chlorthalidone, amlodipine, human recombinant insulin or Definity\nAny history of substance abuse (other than tobacco)\nHistory of gouty arthritis\nPatients with right-to-left, bi-directional, or transient right-to-left cardiac shunts\nHypersensitivity to perflutren, blood, blood products or albumin\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nNormotensive controls\nStage I (140-159/90-99 mmHg) [NOT] untreated subjects with essential hypertension\nPatients with PA [AND] and stage I (140-159/90-99 mmHg) hypertension\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nCongestive heart failure [OR] or coronary artery disease\nBlood pressure averaging > 159/99 mmHg\nSerum creatinine > 1.5 mg/dL\nDiabetes mellitus [OR] or other systemic illness\nLeft ventricular hypertrophy by echocardiography [OR] or ECG\nPregnancy\nHypersensitivity to spironolactone, [OR] chlorthalidone, [OR] amlodipine, human recombinant insulin [OR] or Definity\nAny history of substance abuse (other than tobacco)\nHistory of gouty arthritis\nPatients with right-to-left, [OR] bi-directional, [OR] or transient right-to-left cardiac shunts\nHypersensitivity to perflutren, blood, [OR] blood products [OR] or albumin<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Normotensive controls
Stage I (140-159/90-99 mmHg) [NOT] untreated subjects with essential hypertension
Patients with PA [AND] and stage I (140-159/90-99 mmHg) hypertension

Exclusion Criteria:
Congestive heart failure [OR] or coronary artery disease
Blood pressure averaging > 159/99 mmHg
Serum creatinine > 1.5 mg/dL
Diabetes mellitus [OR] or other systemic illness
Left ventricular hypertrophy by echocardiography [OR] or ECG
Pregnancy
Hypersensitivity to spironolactone, [OR] chlorthalidone, [OR] amlodipine, human recombinant insulin [OR] or Definity
Any history of substance abuse (other than tobacco)
History of gouty arthritis
Patients with right-to-left, [OR] bi-directional, [OR] or transient right-to-left cardiac shunts
Hypersensitivity to perflutren, blood, [OR] blood products [OR] or albumin
