Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\n18 years of age or older \nHistologically confirmed diagnosis of melanoma, breast cancer or gynecologic cancer at MSKCC \nHave one of the following disease histories: \nNewly-diagnosed or recurrent (local, regional, metastatic) malignant melanoma or breast cancer patients in whom SLN mapping is indicated \nResidual clinically or radiographically evident tumor, including primary cutaneous and mucosal melanomas \nPrior radiation therapy, chemotherapy, or surgery in patients requiring flap reconstruction in the head and neck region. \nNewly diagnosed patients with previous excisional biopsy. OR \nNewly-diagnosed gynecologic cancer patients in whom SLN mapping and surgical excision is indicated OR \nNormal baseline cardiac function based upon pre-operative evaluation \nAt the discretion of the operating surgeon, ANC>1000/mcl and platelets>100,000/mcl. \nAt the discretion of the operating surgeon, Bilirubin level of < 2.0 mg/dl in the absence of a history of Gilbert\'s disease (or pattern consistent with Gilbert\'s). \nFor melanoma patients, If patients have a history of malignancy other than melanoma, and other skin cancers in the past five years, their inclusion is up to the discretion of the physician. \nAll patients of childbearing and child-creating age must be using an acceptable form of birth control \nWomen who are pre-menopausal must have a negative serum pregnancy test \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nKnown pregnancy or breast-feeding. \nMedical illness unrelated to the tumor which in the opinion of the attending physician and principal investigator will preclude administration of the agent. This includes patients with uncontrolled infection, chronic renal insufficiency, myocardial infarction within the past 6 months, unstable angina, cardiac arrhythmias other than chronic atrial fibrillation and chronic active or persistent hepatitis, or New York Heart Association Classification III or IV heart disease.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n18 years of age or older \nHistologically confirmed diagnosis of melanoma, [OR] breast cancer [OR] or gynecologic cancer at MSKCC \nHave one of the following disease histories: \nNewly-diagnosed [OR] or recurrent (local, [OR] regional, [OR] metastatic) malignant melanoma [OR] or breast cancer patients in whom SLN mapping is indicated \nResidual clinically [OR] or radiographically evident tumor, including primary cutaneous [OR] and mucosal melanomas \nPrior radiation therapy, [OR] chemotherapy, [OR] or surgery in patients requiring flap reconstruction in the head [OR] and neck region. \nNewly diagnosed patients with previous excisional biopsy. [OR] OR \nNewly-diagnosed gynecologic cancer patients in whom SLN mapping [OR] and surgical excision is indicated [OR] OR \nNormal baseline cardiac function based upon pre-operative evaluation \nAt the discretion of the operating surgeon, ANC>1000/mcl [AND] and platelets>100,000/mcl. \nAt the discretion of the operating surgeon, Bilirubin level of < 2.0 mg/dl [AND] in the [NOT] absence of a history of Gilbert\'s disease [OR] (or pattern consistent with Gilbert\'s). \nFor melanoma patients, If patients have a history of malignancy other than melanoma, [OR] and other skin cancers in the past five years, their inclusion is up to the discretion of the physician. \nAll patients of childbearing [OR] and child-creating age must be using an acceptable form of birth control \nWomen [AND] who are pre-menopausal must have a negative serum pregnancy test \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nKnown pregnancy [OR] or breast-feeding. \nMedical illness unrelated to the tumor which in the opinion of the attending physician and principal investigator will [NOT] preclude administration of the agent. This includes patients with uncontrolled infection, chronic renal insufficiency, [OR] myocardial infarction within the past 6 months, unstable angina, [OR] cardiac arrhythmias other than chronic atrial fibrillation [OR] and chronic active [OR] or persistent hepatitis, [OR] or New York Heart Association Classification III or IV heart disease.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
18 years of age or older 
Histologically confirmed diagnosis of melanoma, [OR] breast cancer [OR] or gynecologic cancer at MSKCC 
Have one of the following disease histories: 
Newly-diagnosed [OR] or recurrent (local, [OR] regional, [OR] metastatic) malignant melanoma [OR] or breast cancer patients in whom SLN mapping is indicated 
Residual clinically [OR] or radiographically evident tumor, including primary cutaneous [OR] and mucosal melanomas 
Prior radiation therapy, [OR] chemotherapy, [OR] or surgery in patients requiring flap reconstruction in the head [OR] and neck region. 
Newly diagnosed patients with previous excisional biopsy. [OR] OR 
Newly-diagnosed gynecologic cancer patients in whom SLN mapping [OR] and surgical excision is indicated [OR] OR 
Normal baseline cardiac function based upon pre-operative evaluation 
At the discretion of the operating surgeon, ANC>1000/mcl [AND] and platelets>100,000/mcl. 
At the discretion of the operating surgeon, Bilirubin level of < 2.0 mg/dl [AND] in the [NOT] absence of a history of Gilbert's disease [OR] (or pattern consistent with Gilbert's). 
For melanoma patients, If patients have a history of malignancy other than melanoma, [OR] and other skin cancers in the past five years, their inclusion is up to the discretion of the physician. 
All patients of childbearing [OR] and child-creating age must be using an acceptable form of birth control 
Women [AND] who are pre-menopausal must have a negative serum pregnancy test 

Exclusion Criteria:
Known pregnancy [OR] or breast-feeding. 
Medical illness unrelated to the tumor which in the opinion of the attending physician and principal investigator will [NOT] preclude administration of the agent. This includes patients with uncontrolled infection, chronic renal insufficiency, [OR] myocardial infarction within the past 6 months, unstable angina, [OR] cardiac arrhythmias other than chronic atrial fibrillation [OR] and chronic active [OR] or persistent hepatitis, [OR] or New York Heart Association Classification III or IV heart disease.
