File: NCT02109081 

Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_full/NCT02109081.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\npatients = 70 years of age, undergoing a noncardiac surgical procedure under general anesthesia, with an anticipated duration of postoperative admission of at least 2 days.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n1) preoperative diagnosis of delirium or dementia; 2) MMSE score of = 20 out of 30 on preoperative testing (more than mild cognitive impairment) or delirium on preoperative CAM testing; 3) language barriers that would preclude testing; 4) preoperative steroid use within 3 days of surgery; or 5) anticipation of postoperative intubation.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\npatients = 70 years of age, undergoing a [NOT] noncardiac surgical procedure under general anesthesia, [AND] with an anticipated duration of postoperative admission of at least 2 days.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n 1) preoperative diagnosis of delirium [OR] or dementia; 2) MMSE score of = 20 out of 30 on preoperative testing (more than mild cognitive impairment) [OR] or delirium on preoperative CAM testing; 3) language barriers that would [NOT] preclude testing; 4) preoperative steroid use within 3 days of surgery; or 5) anticipation of postoperative intubation.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
patients = 70 years of age, undergoing a [NOT] noncardiac surgical procedure under general anesthesia, [AND] with an anticipated duration of postoperative admission of at least 2 days.

Exclusion Criteria:
 1) preoperative diagnosis of delirium [OR] or dementia; 2) MMSE score of = 20 out of 30 on preoperative testing (more than mild cognitive impairment) [OR] or delirium on preoperative CAM testing; 3) language barriers that would [NOT] preclude testing; 4) preoperative steroid use within 3 days of surgery; or 5) anticipation of postoperative intubation.
