Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAdult participants with low or intermediate-1 risk MDS\nNo previous treatment with hematopoietic growth factors within 3 months prior to screening\nSymptomatic anemia (hemoglobin <10 g/dL) as determined by investigator\nSerum erythropoietin <500 milliunits/milliliter (mU/mL) within 14 days prior to the first dose of study treatment\nRequire no red blood cell transfusion or dependent on <4 units within 8 weeks prior to screening\nClinically stable for at least 1 month prior to entry into the study\nFor female participants of childbearing potential and male participants with partners of childbearing potential, agreement (by participants and/or partner) to use highly effective form(s) of contraception\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nContraindications and/or known hypersensitivity to the active substance and/or any of the excipients of epoetin beta treatment\nPoorly controlled hypertension as assessed by the investigator\nHistory of Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) or high risk for AML\nAdministration of another investigational drug within 1 month before screening or planned during the study period\nPreviously documented evidence of Pure Red Cell Aplasia (PRCA)\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAdult participants [AND] with low [OR] or intermediate-1 risk MDS\n [NOT] No previous treatment with hematopoietic growth factors within 3 months prior to screening\nSymptomatic anemia (hemoglobin <10 g/dL) as determined by investigator\nSerum erythropoietin <500 milliunits/milliliter (mU/mL) within 14 days prior to the first dose of study treatment\nRequire [NOT] no red blood cell transfusion [OR] or dependent on <4 units within 8 weeks prior to screening\nClinically stable for at least 1 month prior to entry into the study\nFor female participants of childbearing potential [AND] and male participants [AND] with partners of childbearing potential, agreement (by participants and/or partner) to use highly effective form(s) of contraception\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nContraindications [OR] and/or known hypersensitivity to the active substance [OR] and/or any of the excipients of epoetin beta treatment\nPoorly controlled hypertension as assessed by the investigator\n History of Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) [OR] or high risk for AML\n Administration of another investigational drug within 1 month before screening [OR] or planned during the study period\nPreviously documented evidence of Pure Red Cell Aplasia (PRCA)<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Adult participants [AND] with low [OR] or intermediate-1 risk MDS
 [NOT] No previous treatment with hematopoietic growth factors within 3 months prior to screening
Symptomatic anemia (hemoglobin <10 g/dL) as determined by investigator
Serum erythropoietin <500 milliunits/milliliter (mU/mL) within 14 days prior to the first dose of study treatment
Require [NOT] no red blood cell transfusion [OR] or dependent on <4 units within 8 weeks prior to screening
Clinically stable for at least 1 month prior to entry into the study
For female participants of childbearing potential [AND] and male participants [AND] with partners of childbearing potential, agreement (by participants and/or partner) to use highly effective form(s) of contraception

Exclusion Criteria:
Contraindications [OR] and/or known hypersensitivity to the active substance [OR] and/or any of the excipients of epoetin beta treatment
Poorly controlled hypertension as assessed by the investigator
 History of Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) [OR] or high risk for AML
 Administration of another investigational drug within 1 month before screening [OR] or planned during the study period
Previously documented evidence of Pure Red Cell Aplasia (PRCA)
