Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients between 3 to 16 years of age undergoing adenotonsillectomy, with or without myringotomy or myringoplasty\nASA 1 & 2\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nKnown allergy or hypersensitivity reaction to dexmedetomidine\nOrgan dysfunction (renal/hepatic failure or leukemia)\nCardiac disease (congenital or acquired)\nAirway or thoracic malformation\nCerebral palsy\nHypotonia\nNeed for premedication\nCurrent/recent upper respiratory infection (within four weeks prior to the surgery)\nAsthma\nAllergy or intolerance to clonidine\nNon-English speaking parents/patients.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients between 3 to 16 years of age undergoing adenotonsillectomy, [AND] with or [NOT] without myringotomy [OR] or myringoplasty\nASA 1 & 2\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nKnown allergy [OR] or hypersensitivity reaction to dexmedetomidine\nOrgan dysfunction (renal/ [OR] hepatic failure [OR] or leukemia)\nCardiac disease (congenital [OR] or acquired)\nAirway [OR] or thoracic malformation\nCerebral palsy\nHypotonia\nNeed for premedication\nCurrent/ [OR] recent upper respiratory infection (within four weeks prior to the surgery)\nAsthma\nAllergy [OR] or intolerance to clonidine\n [NOT] Non-English speaking parents/ [OR] patients.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Patients between 3 to 16 years of age undergoing adenotonsillectomy, [AND] with or [NOT] without myringotomy [OR] or myringoplasty
ASA 1 & 2

Exclusion Criteria:
Known allergy [OR] or hypersensitivity reaction to dexmedetomidine
Organ dysfunction (renal/ [OR] hepatic failure [OR] or leukemia)
Cardiac disease (congenital [OR] or acquired)
Airway [OR] or thoracic malformation
Cerebral palsy
Hypotonia
Need for premedication
Current/ [OR] recent upper respiratory infection (within four weeks prior to the surgery)
Asthma
Allergy [OR] or intolerance to clonidine
 [NOT] Non-English speaking parents/ [OR] patients.
