Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAge between 20 and 80 years\nPatients undergoing percutaneous coronary intervention and need to take dual antiplatelet therapy continuously at least 12weeks\nModified Lanza Score grade 0-1 measured by upper gastrointestinal endoscopy\nmild gastrointestinal symptom\nCreatinen in blood = 3mg/dl\nBUN = 50mg/dl\nBirilubin = 3mg/dl\nAST and ALT = 80U/L\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPregnant or breast feeding\nHistory of Stomach or esophagus surgery\nPeptic ulcer or reflux esophagitis\nZollinger-Ellison syndrome or primary esophageal motility disorders\nMalignant tumor\nBleeding tendency or coagulopathy\nContraindication of ALBIS\nLong term use of aspirin or P2Y12 receptor antagonist within 1month\nPatients who tool medicine such as PPI, APA,H2blocker, Muscarine receptor antagonist, anti-gastic agent, antacid, anticaogulant, Bisphosphonate agents, Cytotoxic drug, NSAID, adrenal cortex hormone agents (topical treatment is allowed)\nTerminal patient\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAge between 20 and 80 years\nPatients undergoing percutaneous coronary intervention [AND] and need to take dual antiplatelet therapy continuously at least 12weeks\nModified Lanza Score grade 0-1 measured by upper gastrointestinal endoscopy\nmild gastrointestinal symptom\nCreatinen in blood = 3mg/dl\nBUN = 50mg/dl\n Birilubin = 3mg/dl\nAST [AND] and ALT = 80U/L\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPregnant [OR] or breast feeding\nHistory of Stomach [OR] or esophagus surgery\nPeptic ulcer [OR] or reflux esophagitis\nZollinger-Ellison syndrome [OR] or primary esophageal motility disorders\nMalignant tumor\nBleeding tendency [OR] or coagulopathy\nContraindication of ALBIS\nLong term use of aspirin [OR] or P2Y12 receptor antagonist within 1month\nPatients who tool medicine such as PPI, [OR] APA, [OR] H2blocker, [OR] Muscarine receptor antagonist, [OR] anti-gastic agent, [OR] antacid, [OR] anticaogulant, [OR] Bisphosphonate agents, [OR] Cytotoxic drug, [OR] NSAID, [OR] adrenal cortex hormone agents (topical treatment is allowed)\nTerminal patient<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Age between 20 and 80 years
Patients undergoing percutaneous coronary intervention [AND] and need to take dual antiplatelet therapy continuously at least 12weeks
Modified Lanza Score grade 0-1 measured by upper gastrointestinal endoscopy
mild gastrointestinal symptom
Creatinen in blood = 3mg/dl
BUN = 50mg/dl
 Birilubin = 3mg/dl
AST [AND] and ALT = 80U/L

Exclusion Criteria:
Pregnant [OR] or breast feeding
History of Stomach [OR] or esophagus surgery
Peptic ulcer [OR] or reflux esophagitis
Zollinger-Ellison syndrome [OR] or primary esophageal motility disorders
Malignant tumor
Bleeding tendency [OR] or coagulopathy
Contraindication of ALBIS
Long term use of aspirin [OR] or P2Y12 receptor antagonist within 1month
Patients who tool medicine such as PPI, [OR] APA, [OR] H2blocker, [OR] Muscarine receptor antagonist, [OR] anti-gastic agent, [OR] antacid, [OR] anticaogulant, [OR] Bisphosphonate agents, [OR] Cytotoxic drug, [OR] NSAID, [OR] adrenal cortex hormone agents (topical treatment is allowed)
Terminal patient
