File: NCT02251249 

Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_full/NCT02251249.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatient over 18 years weighing between 65 and 85 Kg\nReferred for STEMI within 6 hours from beginning of chest pain or stable coronary artery disease requiring a loading dose of Prasugrel or Ticagrelor according to the international recommendations.\nNo previous treatment with Clopidogrel, Prasugrel or Ticagrelor.\nPatient fasting for at least 6 hours.\nAffiliate or receiving a social security system.\nWritten informed consent.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nAllergy or contraindication to paracetamol, Prasugrel or Ticagrelor\nParacetamol ingestion in the previous 48 hours\nPatient treated with drugs supposed to alter gastric emptying times (calcium antagonists, Alimentary tract treatments, opioid analgesics, tricyclic antidepressants, antibiotics).\nConditions or pathologies supposed to alter gastric emptying times (Thyroid dysfunction, chronic renal failure, Parkinson\'s disease, scleroderma, amyloidosis, any gastrointestinal disease, any not cured malignancy, and any advanced psychiatric or neurological disease).\nPresence of vomiting\nCardiogenic shock, ventricular arrhythmia or resuscitated cardiac arrest\nHepatic insufficiency\nSevere respiratory disease\nPregnant or breastfeeding women\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatient over 18 years weighing between 65 and 85 Kg\nReferred for STEMI within 6 hours from beginning of chest pain [OR] or stable coronary artery disease requiring a loading dose of Prasugrel [OR] or Ticagrelor according to the international recommendations.\n [NOT] No previous treatment with Clopidogrel, [OR] Prasugrel [OR] or Ticagrelor.\nPatient fasting for at least 6 hours.\nAffiliate or receiving a social security system.\nWritten informed consent.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nAllergy [OR] or contraindication to paracetamol, [OR] Prasugrel [OR] or Ticagrelor\nParacetamol ingestion in the previous 48 hours\nPatient treated with drugs supposed to alter gastric emptying times (calcium antagonists, Alimentary tract treatments, [OR] opioid analgesics, [OR] tricyclic antidepressants, [OR] antibiotics).\nConditions [OR] or pathologies supposed to alter gastric emptying times (Thyroid dysfunction, chronic renal failure, [OR] Parkinson\'s disease, [OR] scleroderma, [OR] amyloidosis, any gastrointestinal disease, any [NOT] not cured malignancy, [OR] and any advanced psychiatric [OR] or neurological disease).\nPresence of vomiting\nCardiogenic shock, [OR] ventricular arrhythmia [OR] or resuscitated cardiac arrest\nHepatic insufficiency\nSevere respiratory disease\nPregnant [OR] or breastfeeding women<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Patient over 18 years weighing between 65 and 85 Kg
Referred for STEMI within 6 hours from beginning of chest pain [OR] or stable coronary artery disease requiring a loading dose of Prasugrel [OR] or Ticagrelor according to the international recommendations.
 [NOT] No previous treatment with Clopidogrel, [OR] Prasugrel [OR] or Ticagrelor.
Patient fasting for at least 6 hours.
Affiliate or receiving a social security system.
Written informed consent.

Exclusion Criteria:
Allergy [OR] or contraindication to paracetamol, [OR] Prasugrel [OR] or Ticagrelor
Paracetamol ingestion in the previous 48 hours
Patient treated with drugs supposed to alter gastric emptying times (calcium antagonists, Alimentary tract treatments, [OR] opioid analgesics, [OR] tricyclic antidepressants, [OR] antibiotics).
Conditions [OR] or pathologies supposed to alter gastric emptying times (Thyroid dysfunction, chronic renal failure, [OR] Parkinson's disease, [OR] scleroderma, [OR] amyloidosis, any gastrointestinal disease, any [NOT] not cured malignancy, [OR] and any advanced psychiatric [OR] or neurological disease).
Presence of vomiting
Cardiogenic shock, [OR] ventricular arrhythmia [OR] or resuscitated cardiac arrest
Hepatic insufficiency
Severe respiratory disease
Pregnant [OR] or breastfeeding women
