nBlood platelet count<100,000/L\nExpected life span<6-month\nSystematical inflammation\nMalignant cancer(s)\nTricuspid valve stenosis, Supra-pulmonary valve stenosis\nAllergic to studied drugs or metal materials.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nProvision of informed consent prior to any study specific procedures;\nMen [OR] and women 18 years and older;\n Group I PAH, defined as a mPAP=25mmHg, [AND] PCWP<15mmHg [AND] and PVR[The PVR =(mPAP- [AND] PCWP)/CO]>3.0 Woods unit.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPregnancy [OR] and breast feeding mother;\nEstimated life expectancy <12 months;\n Scheduled major surgery in the next 6 months;\n [NOT] Inability to follow the protocol and comply with follow-up requirements or any other reason that the investigator feels would place the patient at increased risk;\n Previous enrolment in this study [OR] or treatment with an investigational drug [OR] or device under another study protocol in the past 30 days.\nWHO group II, [OR] III, [OR] IV, [OR] V PH\n Severe Renal dysfunction (Ccr<30 ml/min)\n Blood platelet count<100,000/L\n Expected life span<6-month\n Systematical inflammation\n Malignant cancer(s)\n Tricuspid valve stenosis, [OR] Supra-pulmonary valve stenosis\n Allergic to studied drugs [OR] or metal materials.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Provision of informed consent prior to any study specific procedures;
Men [OR] and women 18 years and older;
 Group I PAH, defined as a mPAP=25mmHg, [AND] PCWP<15mmHg [AND] and PVR[The PVR =(mPAP- [AND] PCWP)/CO]>3.0 Woods unit.

Exclusion Criteria:
Pregnancy [OR] and breast feeding mother;
Estimated life expectancy <12 months;
 Scheduled major surgery in the next 6 months;
 [NOT] Inability to follow the protocol and comply with follow-up requirements or any other reason that the investigator feels would place the patient at increased risk;
 Previous enrolment in this study [OR] or treatment with an investigational drug [OR] or device under another study protocol in the past 30 days.
WHO group II, [OR] III, [OR] IV, [OR] V PH
 Severe Renal dysfunction (Ccr<30 ml/min)
