Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nDiagnosed epileptic patients of either sex with age between 10-19 yrs (<19yrs), coming to the medicine Out Patient /In Patient Departments and undergoing AED therapy for more than 6 months. \nEpileptics with high homocysteine levels i.e. > 10.9 µmol/L (Normal homocysteine levels are 4.3-9.9 µmol/L for male and 3.3-7.2 µmol/L for female adolescent and a high homocysteine concentration is deaned as at least 11.4 µmol/L for male and at least 10.4 µmol/L for female. Gender mean of high homocysteine concentration is 10.9 µmol/L) [5] \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPregnancy and lactation \nPatients with diabetes, Ischemic heart disease (IHD), stroke, malignancy and psychiatric diseases are excluded from study. \nThe patients receiving vitamin supplements or who had clinical evidence for an acute illness, renal dysfunction, thyroid dysfunction, chronic inflammatory diseases, inborn errors of homocysteine, cobalamin or folate metabolism, or any other condition known to interfere with homocysteine metabolism will be excluded \nPatients who are already involved in any other trial. \nPatients not willing to fill consent/ assent form are also excluded from study.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nDiagnosed epileptic patients of either sex [AND] with age between 10-19 yrs (<19yrs), coming to the medicine Out Patient /In Patient Departments [AND] and undergoing AED therapy for more than 6 months. \nEpileptics [AND] with high homocysteine levels i.e. > 10.9 µmol/L (Normal homocysteine levels are 4.3-9.9 µmol/L for male [AND] and 3.3-7.2 µmol/L for female adolescent [AND] and a high homocysteine concentration is deaned as at least 11.4 µmol/L for male [AND] and at least 10.4 µmol/L for female. Gender mean of high homocysteine concentration is 10.9 µmol/L) [5] \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPregnancy [AND] and lactation \nPatients with diabetes, [OR] Ischemic heart disease (IHD), [OR] stroke, [OR] malignancy [OR] and psychiatric diseases are [NOT] excluded from study. \nThe patients receiving vitamin supplements [OR] or who had clinical evidence for an acute illness, [OR] renal dysfunction, [OR] thyroid dysfunction, [OR] chronic inflammatory diseases, [OR] inborn errors of homocysteine, [OR] cobalamin [OR] or folate metabolism, [OR] or any other condition known to interfere with homocysteine metabolism will be [NOT] excluded \nPatients who are already involved in any other trial. \nPatients [NOT] not willing to fill consent/ assent form are also [NOT] excluded from study.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Diagnosed epileptic patients of either sex [AND] with age between 10-19 yrs (<19yrs), coming to the medicine Out Patient /In Patient Departments [AND] and undergoing AED therapy for more than 6 months. 
Epileptics [AND] with high homocysteine levels i.e. > 10.9 µmol/L (Normal homocysteine levels are 4.3-9.9 µmol/L for male [AND] and 3.3-7.2 µmol/L for female adolescent [AND] and a high homocysteine concentration is deaned as at least 11.4 µmol/L for male [AND] and at least 10.4 µmol/L for female. Gender mean of high homocysteine concentration is 10.9 µmol/L) [5] 

Exclusion Criteria:
Pregnancy [AND] and lactation 
Patients with diabetes, [OR] Ischemic heart disease (IHD), [OR] stroke, [OR] malignancy [OR] and psychiatric diseases are [NOT] excluded from study. 
The patients receiving vitamin supplements [OR] or who had clinical evidence for an acute illness, [OR] renal dysfunction, [OR] thyroid dysfunction, [OR] chronic inflammatory diseases, [OR] inborn errors of homocysteine, [OR] cobalamin [OR] or folate metabolism, [OR] or any other condition known to interfere with homocysteine metabolism will be [NOT] excluded 
Patients who are already involved in any other trial. 
Patients [NOT] not willing to fill consent/ assent form are also [NOT] excluded from study.
