, stroke, brain tumors, epilepsy, Parkinson\'s disease, or demyelinating diseases\nMRI contraindications\nAny physical or intellectual disability adversely affecting ability to complete assessments\nElectroconvulsive therapy in last 6 months\nUse of antidepressant medications or other psychotropic medications in the last 4 weeks (or the last 6 weeks for fluoxetine). Occasional use of benzodiazepines or non-benzodiazepine sedatives (such as zolpidem, eszopiclone, or zaleplon) during this period is allowable.\nA failed therapeutic trial of escitalopram in the current depressive episode (defined as at least 6 weeks of treatment at a daily dose of 10mg or higher)\nKnown allergy or hypersensitivity to escitalopram or bupropion\nCurrent or planned psychotherapy\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAge 60 years or older.\nCurrent diagnosis of major depressive disorder (DSM-IV-TR), single episode, [OR] recurrent [OR] or chronic, [NOT] without psychotic features, as detected by MINI [AND] and clinical exam.\nMinimum MADRS score = 15.\nMini-Mental State Exam = 24.\nFluent in English.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nCurrent [OR] or past diagnoses of other Axis I psychiatric disorders, except for generalized anxiety disorder (GAD) symptoms occurring during a depressive episode\nHistory of alcohol [OR] or drug dependence [OR] or abuse in the last three years\n History of developmental disorder [OR] or IQ score < 70\n Presence of acute suicidality\n Acute grief (< 1 month)\n Current [OR] or past psychosis\n Primary neurological disorder, including but not limited to dementia, [OR] stroke, [OR] brain tumors, [OR] epilepsy, [OR] Parkinson\'s disease, [OR] or demyelinating diseases\n MRI contraindications\n Any physical [OR] or intellectual disability adversely affecting ability to complete assessments\n Electroconvulsive therapy in last 6 months\n Use of antidepressant medications [OR] or other psychotropic medications in the last 4 weeks ([OR] or the last 6 weeks for fluoxetine). Occasional use of benzodiazepines [OR] or [NOT] non-benzodiazepine sedatives (such as zolpidem, [OR] eszopiclone, [OR] or zaleplon) during this period is allowable.\n A failed therapeutic trial of escitalopram in the current depressive episode (defined as at least 6 weeks of treatment at a daily dose of 10mg or higher)\n Known allergy [OR] or hypersensitivity to escitalopram [OR] or bupropion\nCurrent [OR] or planned psychotherapy<|eot_id|>']
