Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nInclusion Criteria Patients: Fulfilling the diagnostic criteria of schizophrenia or schizoaffective disorder according to ICD-10 (International Classification of Diseases version 10) or DSM-IV/V (Diagnostic and Statistical Manual version 4 /5), Age 18-45 years, Never treated with antipsychotic compounds or central nervous system (CNS) stimulants, Legally competent\nInclusion criteria controls: Matching patients on age (+/- 2 years), sex and parental socioeconomic status, Age 18-45 years, No psychiatric or physical disease.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nExclusion Criteria patients: Substance abuse on a daily basis during the last 3 month or patients fulfilling the criteria of ongoing substance abuse due to ICD-10/DSM-IV/V, Treatment with antidepressant during the last 30 days, Head injury with more than 5 minutes of unconsciousness, Patients involuntarily admitted or treated, Components of metal implanted by operation, Pacemaker, Pregnancy, Severe physical illness\nExclusion criteria controls: First degree relatives with psychiatric disease, Substance abuse during the last 3 month or positive screening of drugs in urine-sample, Head injury with more than 5 minutes of unconsciousness, Components of metal implanted by operation, Pacemaker, Pregnancy, Severe physical illness\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nInclusion Criteria Patients: Fulfilling the diagnostic criteria of schizophrenia [OR] or schizoaffective disorder according to ICD-10 (International Classification of Diseases version 10) [OR] or DSM-IV/V (Diagnostic and Statistical Manual version 4 /5), Age 18-45 years, [NOT] Never treated with antipsychotic compounds [OR] or central nervous system (CNS) stimulants, Legally competent\nInclusion criteria controls: Matching patients on age (+/- 2 years), sex and parental socioeconomic status, Age 18-45 years, [NOT] No psychiatric [OR] or physical disease.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nExclusion criteria patients: Substance abuse on a daily basis during the last 3 month [OR] or patients fulfilling the criteria of ongoing substance abuse due to ICD-10/ [OR] DSM-IV/V, Treatment with antidepressant during the last 30 days, Head injury [AND] with more than 5 minutes of unconsciousness, Patients involuntarily admitted [OR] or treated, Components of metal implanted by operation, [OR] Pacemaker, [OR] Pregnancy, [OR] Severe physical illness\nExclusion criteria controls: First degree relatives with psychiatric disease, Substance abuse during the last 3 month [OR] or positive screening of drugs in urine-sample, Head injury [AND] with more than 5 minutes of unconsciousness, Components of metal implanted by operation, [OR] Pacemaker, [OR] Pregnancy, [OR] Severe physical illness<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Inclusion Criteria Patients: Fulfilling the diagnostic criteria of schizophrenia [OR] or schizoaffective disorder according to ICD-10 (International Classification of Diseases version 10) [OR] or DSM-IV/V (Diagnostic and Statistical Manual version 4 /5), Age 18-45 years, [NOT] Never treated with antipsychotic compounds [OR] or central nervous system (CNS) stimulants, Legally competent
Inclusion criteria controls: Matching patients on age (+/- 2 years), sex and parental socioeconomic status, Age 18-45 years, [NOT] No psychiatric [OR] or physical disease.

Exclusion Criteria:
Exclusion criteria patients: Substance abuse on a daily basis during the last 3 month [OR] or patients fulfilling the criteria of ongoing substance abuse due to ICD-10/ [OR] DSM-IV/V, Treatment with antidepressant during the last 30 days, Head injury [AND] with more than 5 minutes of unconsciousness, Patients involuntarily admitted [OR] or treated, Components of metal implanted by operation, [OR] Pacemaker, [OR] Pregnancy, [OR] Severe physical illness
Exclusion criteria controls: First degree relatives with psychiatric disease, Substance abuse during the last 3 month [OR] or positive screening of drugs in urine-sample, Head injury [AND] with more than 5 minutes of unconsciousness, Components of metal implanted by operation, [OR] Pacemaker, [OR] Pregnancy, [OR] Severe physical illness
