Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nInfertile lean women with PCOS as defined by the Rotterdam criteria.\nCC resistance (defined as failure of ovulation after receiving 150 mg/day of CC for 5 consecutive days per cycle, for at least 3 consecutive cycles).\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nAge < 20 or > 35 years.\nBody mass index (BMI) < 18.5 kg/m2 or > 25 kg/m2.\nPresence of any infertility factor other than anovulatory PCOS.\nPrevious history of ovarian surgery or surgical removal of one ovary.\nPrevious exposure to cytotoxic drugs or pelvic irradiation.\nOral hypoglycemic or hormonal therapy either currently or in the preceding 3 months.\nMetabolic or hormonal abnormalities\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nInfertile lean women [AND] with PCOS as defined by the Rotterdam criteria.\nCC resistance (defined as [NOT] failure of ovulation after receiving 150 mg/day of CC for 5 consecutive days per cycle, for at least 3 consecutive cycles).\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nAge < 20 [OR] or > 35 years.\nBody mass index (BMI) < 18.5 kg/m2 [OR] or > 25 kg/m2.\nPresence of any infertility factor other than anovulatory PCOS.\nPrevious history of ovarian surgery [OR] or surgical removal of one ovary.\n Previous exposure to cytotoxic drugs [OR] or pelvic irradiation.\nOral hypoglycemic [OR] or hormonal therapy either currently [OR] or in the preceding 3 months.\nMetabolic [OR] or hormonal abnormalities<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Infertile lean women [AND] with PCOS as defined by the Rotterdam criteria.
CC resistance (defined as [NOT] failure of ovulation after receiving 150 mg/day of CC for 5 consecutive days per cycle, for at least 3 consecutive cycles).

Exclusion Criteria:
Age < 20 [OR] or > 35 years.
Body mass index (BMI) < 18.5 kg/m2 [OR] or > 25 kg/m2.
Presence of any infertility factor other than anovulatory PCOS.
Previous history of ovarian surgery [OR] or surgical removal of one ovary.
 Previous exposure to cytotoxic drugs [OR] or pelvic irradiation.
Oral hypoglycemic [OR] or hormonal therapy either currently [OR] or in the preceding 3 months.
Metabolic [OR] or hormonal abnormalities
