Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nSelf-identified African American\nSmokes = 1 cigarette per day (cpd)\nSmoke on = 25 days of the past 30 days\nFunctioning telephone\nInterested in quitting smoking\nInterested in taking 3 months of varenicline\nWilling to complete all study visits\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nRenal impairment\nEvidence or history of clinically significant allergic reactions to varenicline\nA cardiovascular event in the past month\nHistory of alcohol or drug dependence in the past year\nMajor depressive disorder in the last year requiring treatment\nHistory of panic disorder, psychosis, bipolar disorder, or eating disorders\nUse of tobacco products other than cigarettes in past 30 days\nUse of pharmacotherapy in the month prior to enrollment, including prior use of varenicline\nPregnant, contemplating getting pregnant, or breastfeeding\nPlans to move from Kansas City during the treatment and follow-up phase\nAnother household member enrolled in the study\nEvidence of current severe major depressive disorder or suicidal ideation\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nSelf-identified African American\nSmokes = 1 cigarette per day (cpd)\nSmoke on = 25 days of the past 30 days\nFunctioning telephone\nInterested in quitting smoking\nInterested in taking 3 months of varenicline\nWilling to complete all study visits\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nRenal impairment\nEvidence [OR] or history of clinically significant allergic reactions to varenicline\nA cardiovascular event in the past month\nHistory of alcohol [OR] or drug dependence in the past year\nMajor depressive disorder in the last year requiring treatment\nHistory of panic disorder, [OR] psychosis, [OR] bipolar disorder, [OR] or eating disorders\nUse of tobacco products other than cigarettes in past 30 days\n Use of pharmacotherapy in the month prior to enrollment, including prior use of varenicline\nPregnant, contemplating getting pregnant, [OR] or breastfeeding\nPlans to move from Kansas City during the treatment [AND] and follow-up phase\nAnother household member enrolled in the study\nEvidence of current severe major depressive disorder [OR] or suicidal ideation<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Self-identified African American
Smokes = 1 cigarette per day (cpd)
Smoke on = 25 days of the past 30 days
Functioning telephone
Interested in quitting smoking
Interested in taking 3 months of varenicline
Willing to complete all study visits

Exclusion Criteria:
Renal impairment
Evidence [OR] or history of clinically significant allergic reactions to varenicline
A cardiovascular event in the past month
History of alcohol [OR] or drug dependence in the past year
Major depressive disorder in the last year requiring treatment
History of panic disorder, [OR] psychosis, [OR] bipolar disorder, [OR] or eating disorders
Use of tobacco products other than cigarettes in past 30 days
 Use of pharmacotherapy in the month prior to enrollment, including prior use of varenicline
Pregnant, contemplating getting pregnant, [OR] or breastfeeding
Plans to move from Kansas City during the treatment [AND] and follow-up phase
Another household member enrolled in the study
Evidence of current severe major depressive disorder [OR] or suicidal ideation
