Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\n1. Subject has a history of GTC seizures, either primary GTC or partial onset seizures with secondary generalization. \n2. Is being admitted to a hospital for routine vEEG monitoring related to seizures. \n3. Male or female between the ages of 2-99. \n4. Has an upper arm circumference which is adequate for proper fit of the EMG monitor (at least 14cm). \n5. If female and of childbearing potential, has a negative pregnancy test. \n6. Can understand and sign written informed consent, or will have a parent or a legally authorized representative (LAR) who can do so, prior to the performance of any study assessments. \n7. Subject and/or Primary Caregiver must be competent to follow all study procedures. \n8. Is able to read, speak, and understand English. \n\nExclusion Criteria:\n1. Does not have a documented history of generalized seizures. \n2. Has not had a GTC seizure within the last year AND is not expected to have a reduction of anti-epileptic drugs during their hospital admission. \n3. Intracranial EEG electrodes are being used \n4. The subject\'s upper arm circumference not adequate for proper fit of the EMG monitor (less than 14cm). \n5. Pregnant female. \n6. Subject/Caregiver is unable to provide consent.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n1. Subject has a history of GTC seizures, either primary GTC [OR] or partial onset seizures [AND] with secondary generalization. \n2. Is being admitted to a hospital for routine vEEG monitoring related to seizures. \n3. Male [OR] or female between the ages of 2-99. \n4. Has an upper arm circumference which is adequate for proper fit of the EMG monitor (at least 14cm). \n5. If female [AND] and of childbearing potential, has a negative pregnancy test. \n6. Can understand and sign written informed consent, or will have a parent or a legally authorized representative (LAR) who can do so, prior to the performance of any study assessments. \n7. Subject and/or Primary Caregiver must be competent to follow all study procedures. \n8. Is able to read, speak, and understand English. \n\nExclusion Criteria:\n1. Does [NOT] not have a documented history of generalized seizures. \n2. Has [NOT] not had a GTC seizure within the last year [AND] AND is [NOT] not expected to have a reduction of anti-epileptic drugs during their hospital admission. \n3. Intracranial EEG electrodes are being used \n4. The subject\'s upper arm circumference [NOT] not adequate for proper fit of the EMG monitor (less than 14cm). \n5. Pregnant female. \n6. Subject/Caregiver is unable to provide consent.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
1. Subject has a history of GTC seizures, either primary GTC [OR] or partial onset seizures [AND] with secondary generalization. 
2. Is being admitted to a hospital for routine vEEG monitoring related to seizures. 
3. Male [OR] or female between the ages of 2-99. 
4. Has an upper arm circumference which is adequate for proper fit of the EMG monitor (at least 14cm). 
5. If female [AND] and of childbearing potential, has a negative pregnancy test. 
6. Can understand and sign written informed consent, or will have a parent or a legally authorized representative (LAR) who can do so, prior to the performance of any study assessments. 
7. Subject and/or Primary Caregiver must be competent to follow all study procedures. 
8. Is able to read, speak, and understand English. 

Exclusion Criteria:
1. Does [NOT] not have a documented history of generalized seizures. 
2. Has [NOT] not had a GTC seizure within the last year [AND] AND is [NOT] not expected to have a reduction of anti-epileptic drugs during their hospital admission. 
3. Intracranial EEG electrodes are being used 
4. The subject's upper arm circumference [NOT] not adequate for proper fit of the EMG monitor (less than 14cm). 
5. Pregnant female. 
6. Subject/Caregiver is unable to provide consent.
