erapy defined as fragments less than 3mm.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPatients with medical comorbidities [NOT] preventing them from definitive surgical therapy.\nPatients with persistent stone burden following definitive surgical therapy.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Male [OR] or Female.
No age restriction.
Diagnosed with an infection related stone.
Medically fit for definitive surgical management of stone.
Life expectancy greater than one year.
Stone [NOT] free after definitive surgical therapy defined as fragments less than 3mm.

Exclusion Criteria:
Patients with medical comorbidities [NOT] preventing them from definitive surgical therapy.
Patients with persistent stone burden following definitive surgical therapy.
