Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\n• All patients attending for a routine diagnostic endoscopic procedure at St Mary\'s Hospital NHS Trust for dyspepsia and abdominal pain \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPatients attending for a therapeutic endoscopic procedure e.g. variceal banding, stent insertion, balloon dilatation. \nPatients with a known diagnosis e.g. upper gastrointestinal cancer \nPatients previously treated with HP eradication therapy \nPatients who had taken PPI, H2 receptor antagonists and antibiotics within 4 weeks \nPatients with acute gastrointestinal bleeding \nPatients who\'d had previous gastric surgery \nPatients with chronic liver disease \nPatients with abnormal coagulation or any other contra-indication to use of standard biopsy in routine diagnostic endoscopic procedures \nPatients who are unable or unwilling to give informed consent \nPatients under the age of 18 years       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n• All patients attending for a routine diagnostic endoscopic procedure at St Mary\'s Hospital NHS Trust [AND] for dyspepsia [OR] and abdominal pain \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPatients attending for a therapeutic endoscopic procedure e.g. variceal banding, [OR] stent insertion, [OR] balloon dilatation. \nPatients with a known diagnosis e.g. upper gastrointestinal cancer \nPatients previously treated with HP eradication therapy \nPatients who had taken PPI, [OR] H2 receptor antagonists [OR] and antibiotics within 4 weeks \nPatients with acute gastrointestinal bleeding \nPatients who\'d had previous gastric surgery \nPatients with chronic liver disease \nPatients with abnormal coagulation [OR] or any other contra-indication to use of standard biopsy in routine diagnostic endoscopic procedures \nPatients who are unable or unwilling to give informed consent \nPatients under the age of 18 years<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
• All patients attending for a routine diagnostic endoscopic procedure at St Mary's Hospital NHS Trust [AND] for dyspepsia [OR] and abdominal pain 

Exclusion Criteria:
Patients attending for a therapeutic endoscopic procedure e.g. variceal banding, [OR] stent insertion, [OR] balloon dilatation. 
Patients with a known diagnosis e.g. upper gastrointestinal cancer 
Patients previously treated with HP eradication therapy 
Patients who had taken PPI, [OR] H2 receptor antagonists [OR] and antibiotics within 4 weeks 
Patients with acute gastrointestinal bleeding 
Patients who'd had previous gastric surgery 
Patients with chronic liver disease 
Patients with abnormal coagulation [OR] or any other contra-indication to use of standard biopsy in routine diagnostic endoscopic procedures 
Patients who are unable or unwilling to give informed consent 
Patients under the age of 18 years
