Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nSingleton pregnancy;\n8-22 weeks gestation\nPrevious pregnancy complicated by gestational diabetes\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nEstablished pre-existing diabetes (including unrecognised diabetes defined as a fasting plasma glucose = 7.0mmol/L and/ or HbA1c = 48mmol/mol); Contraindications to metformin therapy (creatinine = 130µmol/L/ alanine transaminase = 2.0 x upper limit normal/ previous intolerance to metformin)\nPlanned continued antenatal care/ delivery at centre not included in trial\nPlanned fast for cultural/ religious reasons e.g. Ramadan\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nSingleton pregnancy;\n8-22 weeks gestation\nPrevious pregnancy complicated by gestational diabetes\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nEstablished pre-existing diabetes (including unrecognised diabetes defined as a fasting plasma glucose = 7.0mmol/L [OR] and/ or HbA1c = 48mmol/mol); Contraindications to metformin therapy (creatinine = 130µmol/L/ alanine transaminase = 2.0 x upper limit normal/ previous intolerance to metformin)\nPlanned continued antenatal care/ [OR] delivery at centre [NOT] not included in trial\nPlanned fast for cultural/ [OR] religious reasons e.g. Ramadan<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Singleton pregnancy;
8-22 weeks gestation
Previous pregnancy complicated by gestational diabetes

Exclusion Criteria:
Established pre-existing diabetes (including unrecognised diabetes defined as a fasting plasma glucose = 7.0mmol/L [OR] and/ or HbA1c = 48mmol/mol); Contraindications to metformin therapy (creatinine = 130µmol/L/ alanine transaminase = 2.0 x upper limit normal/ previous intolerance to metformin)
Planned continued antenatal care/ [OR] delivery at centre [NOT] not included in trial
Planned fast for cultural/ [OR] religious reasons e.g. Ramadan
