Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nMen or women, 18 to 65 years old with a BMI of 35 kg/m2 or greater who will be undergoing bariatric surgery (VSG and RYGB)\nSigned written informed consent\nWomen of childbearing potential (WOCBP) must have a negative serum or urine pregnancy test (minimum sensitivity 25 IU/L or equivalent units of HCG) within 24 hours prior to the start of study drug\nWomen must not be breastfeeding\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nHistory of documented clotting/coagulation disorder\nHistory of cancer (within the last year)\nAny diagnosis requiring anti-coagulation\nHistory of hypersensitivity reaction to apixaban\nActive clinically significant bleeding\nCreatinine > 1.5 mg/dL\nParticipants currently receiving any type of anticoagulation or blood thinning medications, including heparin, low molecular weight heparins, Plavix, aspirin, NSAIDS\nCombined P-glycoprotein and strong cytochrome P450 (CYP) 3A4 inhibitor\nCombined P-glycoprotein and moderate CYP 3A4 inhibitor\nCombined P-glycoprotein inducer and strong CYP 3A4 inducer\nInducers of p-glycoprotein\nStrong inducers of CYP 3A4\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nMen [OR] or women, 18 to 65 years old [AND] with a BMI of 35 kg/m2 or greater [AND] who will be undergoing bariatric surgery (VSG [OR] and RYGB)\nSigned written informed consent\nWomen [AND] of childbearing potential (WOCBP) must have a negative serum [OR] or urine pregnancy test (minimum sensitivity 25 IU/L or equivalent units of HCG) within 24 hours prior to the start of study drug\nWomen must [NOT] not be breastfeeding\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nHistory of documented clotting/ [OR] coagulation disorder\nHistory of cancer (within the last year)\n Any diagnosis requiring anti-coagulation\nHistory of hypersensitivity reaction to apixaban\n Active clinically significant bleeding\nCreatinine > 1.5 mg/dL\nParticipants currently receiving any type of anticoagulation [OR] or blood thinning medications, including heparin, [OR] low molecular weight heparins, [OR] Plavix, [OR] aspirin, [OR] NSAIDS\n Combined P-glycoprotein [AND] and strong cytochrome P450 (CYP) 3A4 inhibitor\n Combined P-glycoprotein [AND] and moderate CYP 3A4 inhibitor\n Combined P-glycoprotein inducer [AND] and strong CYP 3A4 inducer\n Inducers of p-glycoprotein\n Strong inducers of CYP 3A4<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Men [OR] or women, 18 to 65 years old [AND] with a BMI of 35 kg/m2 or greater [AND] who will be undergoing bariatric surgery (VSG [OR] and RYGB)
Signed written informed consent
Women [AND] of childbearing potential (WOCBP) must have a negative serum [OR] or urine pregnancy test (minimum sensitivity 25 IU/L or equivalent units of HCG) within 24 hours prior to the start of study drug
Women must [NOT] not be breastfeeding

Exclusion Criteria:
History of documented clotting/ [OR] coagulation disorder
History of cancer (within the last year)
 Any diagnosis requiring anti-coagulation
History of hypersensitivity reaction to apixaban
 Active clinically significant bleeding
Creatinine > 1.5 mg/dL
Participants currently receiving any type of anticoagulation [OR] or blood thinning medications, including heparin, [OR] low molecular weight heparins, [OR] Plavix, [OR] aspirin, [OR] NSAIDS
 Combined P-glycoprotein [AND] and strong cytochrome P450 (CYP) 3A4 inhibitor
 Combined P-glycoprotein [AND] and moderate CYP 3A4 inhibitor
 Combined P-glycoprotein inducer [AND] and strong CYP 3A4 inducer
 Inducers of p-glycoprotein
 Strong inducers of CYP 3A4
