Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nLikely suffer moderate-to-severe OSA based on history and physical or have an established diagnosis of OSA (20=AHI=65) based on a prior in-lab Polysomnography\nDocumentation the subject not effectively treated with CPAP therapy. (Examples include non-compliance, discomfort, undesirable side effects, symptoms persist despite use). Subjects who have been prescribed, but refuse to try CPAP would be considered intolerant.\nAge 22 or above\nWilling and capable to have stimulation hardware permanently implanted, and to use the patient remote to activate the stimulation\nWilling and capable to return for all follow-up visits and conduct sleep studies at home, including the evaluation procedures and filling out questionnaires\nWilling and capable of providing informed consent\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nCentral + mixed apneas > 25% of the total apnea-hypopnea index (AHI)\nAny anatomical finding that would compromise the performance of upper airway stimulation, such as the presence of complete concentric collapse of the soft palate\nAny condition or procedure that has compromised neurological control of the upper airway\nPatients who are unable or do not have the necessary assistance to operate the patient remote\nPatients who are pregnant or plan to become pregnant\nPatients who will require magnetic resonance imaging (MRI)\nPatients with an implantable device that may be susceptible to unintended interaction with the Inspire system.\nBody Mass Index (BMI) of > 32\nAny chronic medical illness or condition that contraindicates a surgical procedure under general anesthesia, as judged by the clinical study Investigator\nHas a terminal illness with life expectancy < 12 months\nActive psychiatric disease (psychotic illness, major depression, or acute anxiety attacks) which prevents subject compliance with the requirements of the investigational study testing\nAny other reason the investigator deems subject is unfit for participation in the study\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nLikely suffer moderate- [OR] to-severe OSA based on history [OR] and physical [OR] or have an established diagnosis of OSA (20=AHI=65) based on a prior in-lab Polysomnography\nDocumentation the subject [NOT] not effectively treated with CPAP therapy. (Examples include [NOT] non-compliance, [OR] discomfort, [OR] undesirable side effects, [OR] symptoms persist [AND] despite use). Subjects who have been prescribed, [AND] but refuse to try CPAP would be considered intolerant.\nAge 22 or above\nWilling [AND] and capable to have stimulation hardware permanently implanted, [AND] and to use the patient remote to activate the stimulation\nWilling [AND] and capable to return for all follow-up visits [AND] and conduct sleep studies at home, including the evaluation procedures and filling out questionnaires\nWilling and capable of providing informed consent\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nCentral [OR] + mixed apneas > 25% of the total apnea-hypopnea index (AHI)\nAny anatomical finding that would compromise the performance of upper airway stimulation, such as the presence of complete concentric collapse of the soft palate\nAny condition [OR] or procedure that has compromised neurological control of the upper airway\nPatients who are [NOT] unable [OR] or do [NOT] not have the necessary assistance to operate the patient remote\nPatients who are pregnant [OR] or plan to become pregnant\nPatients who will require magnetic resonance imaging (MRI)\n Patients with an implantable device that may be susceptible to unintended interaction with the Inspire system.\nBody Mass Index (BMI) of > 32\nAny chronic medical illness [OR] or condition that contraindicates a surgical procedure under general anesthesia, as judged by the clinical study Investigator\nHas a terminal illness [AND] with life expectancy < 12 months\nActive psychiatric disease (psychotic illness, [OR] major depression, [OR] or acute anxiety attacks) which [NOT] prevents subject compliance with the requirements of the investigational study testing\nAny other reason the investigator deems subject is unfit for participation in the study<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Likely suffer moderate- [OR] to-severe OSA based on history [OR] and physical [OR] or have an established diagnosis of OSA (20=AHI=65) based on a prior in-lab Polysomnography
Documentation the subject [NOT] not effectively treated with CPAP therapy. (Examples include [NOT] non-compliance, [OR] discomfort, [OR] undesirable side effects, [OR] symptoms persist [AND] despite use). Subjects who have been prescribed, [AND] but refuse to try CPAP would be considered intolerant.
Age 22 or above
Willing [AND] and capable to have stimulation hardware permanently implanted, [AND] and to use the patient remote to activate the stimulation
Willing [AND] and capable to return for all follow-up visits [AND] and conduct sleep studies at home, including the evaluation procedures and filling out questionnaires
Willing and capable of providing informed consent

Exclusion Criteria:
Central [OR] + mixed apneas > 25% of the total apnea-hypopnea index (AHI)
Any anatomical finding that would compromise the performance of upper airway stimulation, such as the presence of complete concentric collapse of the soft palate
Any condition [OR] or procedure that has compromised neurological control of the upper airway
Patients who are [NOT] unable [OR] or do [NOT] not have the necessary assistance to operate the patient remote
Patients who are pregnant [OR] or plan to become pregnant
Patients who will require magnetic resonance imaging (MRI)
 Patients with an implantable device that may be susceptible to unintended interaction with the Inspire system.
Body Mass Index (BMI) of > 32
Any chronic medical illness [OR] or condition that contraindicates a surgical procedure under general anesthesia, as judged by the clinical study Investigator
Has a terminal illness [AND] with life expectancy < 12 months
Active psychiatric disease (psychotic illness, [OR] major depression, [OR] or acute anxiety attacks) which [NOT] prevents subject compliance with the requirements of the investigational study testing
Any other reason the investigator deems subject is unfit for participation in the study
