Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nCurrently smoke at least ten cigarettes a day\nHave been smoking for at least one year\nMeet criteria for schizophrenia, schizoaffective disorder, or another psychotic disorder based on structured clinical interview\nCan speak and write fluent conversational English\nAre between 18 and 70 years of age\nAre willing to make a smoking cessation attempt\nScore 26 or higher on the Montreal Cognitive Assessment\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nHave a history of myocardial infarction in the past 6 months\nHave a contraindication to NRT with no medical clearance from the primary care provider or study physician\nUse and unwillingness to stop use of other forms of nicotine such as cigars, pipes, or chewing tobacco\nAre pregnant\nMeet criteria for a current manic episode based on structured clinical interview\nAre currently enrolled in another smoking cessation trial\nAre currently imprisoned or in psychiatric hospitalization\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nCurrently smoke at least ten cigarettes a day\nHave been smoking for at least one year\n Meet criteria for schizophrenia, [OR] schizoaffective disorder, [OR] or another psychotic disorder based on structured clinical interview\n Can speak and write fluent conversational English\n Are between 18 and 70 years of age\n Are willing to make a smoking cessation attempt\nScore 26 or higher on the Montreal Cognitive Assessment\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nHave a history of myocardial infarction in the past 6 months\n Have a contraindication to NRT [AND] with [NOT] no medical clearance from the primary care provider or study physician\n Use [AND] and [NOT] unwillingness to [NOT] stop use of other forms of nicotine such as cigars, [OR] pipes, [OR] or chewing tobacco\n Are pregnant\n Meet criteria for a current manic episode based on structured clinical interview\n Are currently enrolled in another smoking cessation trial\n Are currently imprisoned [OR] or in psychiatric hospitalization<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Currently smoke at least ten cigarettes a day
Have been smoking for at least one year
 Meet criteria for schizophrenia, [OR] schizoaffective disorder, [OR] or another psychotic disorder based on structured clinical interview
 Can speak and write fluent conversational English
 Are between 18 and 70 years of age
 Are willing to make a smoking cessation attempt
Score 26 or higher on the Montreal Cognitive Assessment

Exclusion Criteria:
Have a history of myocardial infarction in the past 6 months
 Have a contraindication to NRT [AND] with [NOT] no medical clearance from the primary care provider or study physician
 Use [AND] and [NOT] unwillingness to [NOT] stop use of other forms of nicotine such as cigars, [OR] pipes, [OR] or chewing tobacco
 Are pregnant
 Meet criteria for a current manic episode based on structured clinical interview
 Are currently enrolled in another smoking cessation trial
 Are currently imprisoned [OR] or in psychiatric hospitalization
