File: NCT02426034 

Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_full/NCT02426034.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAge: 18 to75 years old;\nPathologically diagnosed with advanced gastric cancer (including adenocarcinoma of the gastroesophageal junction) with measurable metastases outside the stomach (measuring = 10mm on spiral CT scan, satisfying the criteria in RECIST 1.1);\nFailure of prior therapy (during or after treatment) in patients who have received at least two prior chemotherapy regimens;\nECOG PS of 0-2;\nHB = 90g / L\nANC = 1.5 × 109 / L\nPLT = 80 × 109 / L\nBilirubin <1.25 times the upper limit of normal (ULN)\nALT and AST <2.5 × ULN; liver metastases, if any, the ALT and AST<5 × ULN\nSerum Cr = 1 × ULN endogenous creatinine clearance>50ml/min (Cockcroft-Gault formula)\nAn expected survival of = 3 months;\nPatient received apatinib treatment regimen at investigators\' discretion;\nPatient has to voluntarily join the study and sign the Informed Consent Form for the study;\nPregnancy test (serum or urine) has to be performed for woman of childbearing age within 7 days before enrolment and the test result must be negative. They shall take appropriate methods for contraception during the study until the 8th week post the last administration of study drug. For men, (previous surgical sterilization accepted), shall agree to take appropriate methods of contraception during the study until the 8th week post the last administration of study drug.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nSubjects with poor-controlled arterial hypertension (systolic blood pressure> 140 mmHg and diastolic blood pressure > 90 mm Hg) despite standard medical management; Coronary heart disease greater than ClassII; II-level arrhythmia (including QT interval prolongation, for man = 450 ms, for woman = 470 ms) together with Class II cardiac dysfunction;\nFactors that could have an effect on oral medication (such as inability to swallow, chronic diarrhea and intestinal obstruction);\nSubjects with high gastrointestinal bleeding risk, including the following conditions: local active ulcer lesions with positive fecal occult blood test (++); history of black stool, or vomiting blood in the past 3 months;unresected primary lesion in stomach with positive fecal occult blood test (+), ulcerated gastric carcinoma with massive alimentary tract bleeding risk judged by PIs based on gastric endoscopy result;\nAbnormal Coagulation (INR>1.5<U+3001>APTT>1.5 UNL), with tendency of bleed;\nAssociated with CNS (central nervous system) metastases;\nPregnant or lactating women;\nOther conditions regimented at investigators\' discretion.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAge: 18 to75 years old;\nPathologically diagnosed with advanced gastric cancer (including adenocarcinoma of the gastroesophageal junction) [AND] with measurable metastases [NOT] outside the stomach (measuring = 10mm on spiral CT scan, satisfying the criteria in RECIST 1.1);\nFailure of prior therapy (during [OR] or after treatment) in patients [AND] who have received at least two prior chemotherapy regimens;\nECOG PS of 0-2;\nHB = 90g / L\nANC = 1.5 × 109 / L\n PLT = 80 × 109 / L\nBilirubin <1.25 times the upper limit of normal (ULN)\nALT [AND] and AST <2.5 × ULN; liver metastases, if any, the ALT [AND] and AST<5 × ULN\nSerum Cr = 1 × ULN endogenous creatinine clearance>50ml/min (Cockcroft-Gault formula)\nAn expected survival of = 3 months;\nPatient received apatinib treatment regimen at investigators\' discretion;\nPatient has to voluntarily join the study and sign the Informed Consent Form for the study;\nPregnancy test (serum [OR] or urine) has to be performed for woman of childbearing age within 7 days before enrolment and the test result must be negative. They shall take appropriate methods for contraception during the study until the 8th week post the last administration of study drug. For men, (previous surgical sterilization accepted), shall agree to take appropriate methods of contraception during the study until the 8th week post the last administration of study drug.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nSubjects with poor-controlled arterial hypertension (systolic blood pressure> 140 mmHg [AND] and diastolic blood pressure > 90 mm Hg) despite standard medical management; Coronary heart disease greater than ClassII; II-level arrhythmia (including QT interval prolongation, for man = 450 ms, for woman = 470 ms) together with Class II cardiac dysfunction;\nFactors that could have an effect on oral medication (such as [NOT] inability to swallow, chronic diarrhea [OR] and intestinal obstruction);\nSubjects with high gastrointestinal bleeding risk, including the following conditions: local active ulcer lesions [AND] with positive fecal occult blood test (++); history of black stool, [OR] or vomiting blood in the past 3 months;unresected primary lesion in stomach [AND] with positive fecal occult blood test (+), ulcerated gastric carcinoma [AND] with massive alimentary tract bleeding risk judged by PIs based on gastric endoscopy result;\nAbnormal Coagulation (INR>1.5<U+3001>APTT>1.5 UNL), [AND] with tendency of bleed;\nAssociated with CNS (central nervous system) metastases;\nPregnant [OR] or lactating women;\nOther conditions regimented at investigators\' discretion.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Age: 18 to75 years old;
Pathologically diagnosed with advanced gastric cancer (including adenocarcinoma of the gastroesophageal junction) [AND] with measurable metastases [NOT] outside the stomach (measuring = 10mm on spiral CT scan, satisfying the criteria in RECIST 1.1);
Failure of prior therapy (during [OR] or after treatment) in patients [AND] who have received at least two prior chemotherapy regimens;
ECOG PS of 0-2;
HB = 90g / L
ANC = 1.5 × 109 / L
 PLT = 80 × 109 / L
Bilirubin <1.25 times the upper limit of normal (ULN)
ALT [AND] and AST <2.5 × ULN; liver metastases, if any, the ALT [AND] and AST<5 × ULN
Serum Cr = 1 × ULN endogenous creatinine clearance>50ml/min (Cockcroft-Gault formula)
An expected survival of = 3 months;
Patient received apatinib treatment regimen at investigators' discretion;
Patient has to voluntarily join the study and sign the Informed Consent Form for the study;
Pregnancy test (serum [OR] or urine) has to be performed for woman of childbearing age within 7 days before enrolment and the test result must be negative. They shall take appropriate methods for contraception during the study until the 8th week post the last administration of study drug. For men, (previous surgical sterilization accepted), shall agree to take appropriate methods of contraception during the study until the 8th week post the last administration of study drug.

Exclusion Criteria:
Subjects with poor-controlled arterial hypertension (systolic blood pressure> 140 mmHg [AND] and diastolic blood pressure > 90 mm Hg) despite standard medical management; Coronary heart disease greater than ClassII; II-level arrhythmia (including QT interval prolongation, for man = 450 ms, for woman = 470 ms) together with Class II cardiac dysfunction;
Factors that could have an effect on oral medication (such as [NOT] inability to swallow, chronic diarrhea [OR] and intestinal obstruction);
Subjects with high gastrointestinal bleeding risk, including the following conditions: local active ulcer lesions [AND] with positive fecal occult blood test (++); history of black stool, [OR] or vomiting blood in the past 3 months;unresected primary lesion in stomach [AND] with positive fecal occult blood test (+), ulcerated gastric carcinoma [AND] with massive alimentary tract bleeding risk judged by PIs based on gastric endoscopy result;
Abnormal Coagulation (INR>1.5<U+3001>APTT>1.5 UNL), [AND] with tendency of bleed;
Associated with CNS (central nervous system) metastases;
Pregnant [OR] or lactating women;
Other conditions regimented at investigators' discretion.
