Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAge 18 or older.\nPatients diagnosed with acromegaly with GH-secreting pituitary adenoma on sellar MRI, meeting the biochemical criteria outlined above (refer to 1. Diagnosis of acromegaly) and with typical acromegalic features.\nNo prior use of somatostatin analogues.\nAdequate hepatic and renal function\nProvision of a signed written informed consent\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nSevere co-morbid illness such as untreatable other malignancy and/or active infections.\nPregnant or lactating women\nHypersensitivity to Sandostatin or any component of the formulation.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAge 18 or older.\nPatients diagnosed with acromegaly [AND] with GH-secreting pituitary adenoma on sellar MRI, meeting the biochemical criteria outlined above (refer to 1. Diagnosis of acromegaly) [AND] and with typical acromegalic features.\n [NOT] No prior use of somatostatin analogues.\nAdequate hepatic [AND] and renal function\nProvision of a signed written informed consent\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nSevere co-morbid illness such as untreatable other malignancy [OR] and/or active infections.\nPregnant [OR] or lactating women\nHypersensitivity to Sandostatin [OR] or any component of the formulation.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Age 18 or older.
Patients diagnosed with acromegaly [AND] with GH-secreting pituitary adenoma on sellar MRI, meeting the biochemical criteria outlined above (refer to 1. Diagnosis of acromegaly) [AND] and with typical acromegalic features.
 [NOT] No prior use of somatostatin analogues.
Adequate hepatic [AND] and renal function
Provision of a signed written informed consent

Exclusion Criteria:
Severe co-morbid illness such as untreatable other malignancy [OR] and/or active infections.
Pregnant [OR] or lactating women
Hypersensitivity to Sandostatin [OR] or any component of the formulation.
