Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAble to provide voluntary, written informed consent with comprehension of all aspects of the protocol, prior to any study procedures. \nHealthy obese male and female volunteers aged 18 to 55 years, inclusive. Heterozygous subjects may be 18 to 65 years inclusive. \nIn good general health, without significant medical history, physical examination findings, or clinical laboratory abnormalities. \nBody Mass Index of 30-40 kg/m2, inclusive. Heterozygous subjects may have a broader BMI range; to be eligible heterozygous subjects may have a BMI 27 -55 kg/ m2, inclusive. \nStable body weight during the previous 6 months, based on Investigator judgment. \nBlood pressure <140/90 mmHg at Screening and D-1. Measurement may be repeated within 24 hours, based on Investigator judgment. \nFemales must not be pregnant and must have a negative serum pregnancy test result at the Screening Visit and Day -1. \nFemales of childbearing potential must agree to be abstinent or else use any two of the following medically acceptable forms of contraception from the Screening Period through the Final Study Visit: hormonal, condom with spermicidal jelly, diaphragm or cervical cap with spermicidal jelly, or IUD. Hormonal contraception must have started at least 3 months prior to screening. A female whose male partner has had a vasectomy must agree to use one additional form of medically acceptable contraception. Subjects must agree to practice the above birth control methods for 30 days from the final visit as a safety precaution. \nFemales of non-childbearing potential, defined as surgically sterile (status post hysterectomy, bilateral oophorectomy, or bilateral tubal ligation) or post-menopausal for at least 12 months (and confirmed with a screening FSH level in the post-menopausal range), do not require contraception during the study. \nMales with female partners of childbearing potential must agree to use two medically acceptable forms of contraception as described above, with one of the two forms being condom with spermicide, from the Screening Period through the Final Study Visit. Males with female partners of childbearing potential who themselves are surgically sterile (status post vasectomy) must agree to use condoms with spermicide over the same period of time. Male subjects must agree to practice the above birth control methods for 30 days from the final visit as a safety precaution. \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nFasting blood glucose >126 mg/dL at screening. Heterozygous subjects will be excluded for a fasting blood glucose >140 mg/dL. \nResting heart rate <45 bpm or >90 bpm at screening. \nAbnormal thyroid stimulating hormone (TSH) or thyroxine (T4) levels on screening. \nElevated ALT or serum creatinine on screening or any clinically significant abnormalities on screening laboratory tests as determined by the Investigator. \nHistory of medically treated diabetes or of treated or medically diagnosed hypertension. Heterozygous subjects who have diagnosed hypertension and are well controlled on treatment (Refer to Exclusion Criteria 20 below), are eligible.. \nPresence of a skin lesion suspicious for malignancy, unless excised prior to Day 1. \nHistory of malignancy except for treated cervical carcinoma in situ in the past 5 years. \nActive or history of any clinically significant medical condition including renal, hepatic, pulmonary, gastrointestinal, cardiovascular, genitourinary, endocrine, immunologic, metabolic, neurologic, psychiatric or hematological disease, based on Investigator judgment. \nAcute illness or history of illness, which in the opinion of the Investigator, could pose a threat or harm to the subject or obscure interpretation of laboratory test results or interpretation of study data. \nPositive hepatitis B surface antigen, positive hepatitis C antibody or positive HIV test at screening or a history of positive testing (e.g. liver biopsy, serology) suggesting acute or chronic hepatitis. \nAbnormal 12-lead electrocardiogram (ECG) at screening or pre-dose (Day -1 or Day 1), except minor deviations deemed to be of no clinical significance by the Investigator. \nReceived any experimental drugs or devices within 30 days or 5 half lives, whichever is longer, prior to dosing. \nOngoing participation in a prior clinical study at the time of screening. \nBlood donation within 60 days prior to screening or intent to donate within 60 days after Final Study Visit. \nHospitalization for major surgery including but not limited to abdominal, thoracic, or cardiovascular surgery within the past 3 months prior to screening, or for a clinically significant non-surgical illness, based on Investigator judgment, within the past 3 months. \nPlanned elective surgery within 30 days of the Final Study Visit. \nPoor venous access or inability to tolerate venipuncture. \nHistory of significant drug hypersensitivity or anaphylaxis. \nHistory of hypersensitivity to proteins (e.g., allergy shots). \nUse of prescription medications on a regular basis. The last use of any prescription medication must have been greater than 5 half-lives for the specific medication or at least 14 days prior to admission (Day -1), whichever is longer. Hormonal contraception is allowed for female subjects. \nHeterozygous cohorts: Use of prescription medications on a regular basis is not allowed with the following exceptions: \nAntihypertensives (<3 medications on a stable dose for ≥ 30 days); \nStatins (dose must be ≤ half the maximum dose; must be on a stable dose ≥3 months); \nFibrates (must be on stable dose for ≥3 months); \nNiacin (must be on stable dose for ≥3 months); \nThyroxin (stable dose for ≥ 30 days); The last use of any other prescription medication will need follow the criteria for all other cohorts, as outlined above. \nUse of prescription medications not listed above may be allowed at the discretion of the Investigator upon consultation with Rhythm. \nUse of a non-prescription drug and herbal substances during the study (through the Final Study Visit). The last dose of any non-prescription drug must have been taken greater than 5 half-lives for that drug before receiving study drug. \nInability to attend all study visits or to comply with protocol requirements including fasting and restrictions on alcohol, caffeine, nicotine and concomitant medication intake. \nA significant history of drug/solvent abuse within 5 years of screening or a positive test for drugs of abuse test at screening or on Day -1. \nPositive alcohol (breath test) or nicotine screen at Screening Visit or Day 1 (positive nicotine screen does not apply to heterozygous cohort). \nHistory of alcohol abuse (defined as average intake of three or more units of alcohol per day) within 5 years of the Screening Visit. \nHistory of tobacco or tobacco product use unless abstinent for at least one year prior to the Screening Visit. This criterion does not apply to heterozygous subjects. \nPreviously randomized and dosed in this study. This criterion does not apply to heterozygous subjects. \nAny other reason, which in the opinion of the Investigator would confound proper evaluation of the study.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAble to provide voluntary, written informed consent with comprehension of all aspects of the protocol, prior to any study procedures. \nHealthy obese male [OR] and female volunteers aged 18 to 55 years, inclusive. Heterozygous subjects may be 18 to 65 years inclusive. \nIn good general health, [NOT] without significant medical history, [OR] physical examination findings, [OR] or clinical laboratory abnormalities. \nBody Mass Index of 30-40 kg/m2, inclusive. Heterozygous subjects may have a broader BMI range; to be eligible heterozygous subjects may have a BMI 27 -55 kg/ m2, inclusive. \nStable body weight during the previous 6 months, based on Investigator judgment. \nBlood pressure <140/90 mmHg at Screening [AND] and D-1. Measurement may be repeated within 24 hours, based on Investigator judgment. \nFemales [NOT] must [NOT] not be pregnant [AND] and must have a negative serum pregnancy test result at the Screening Visit [AND] and Day -1. \nFemales of childbearing potential must agree to be abstinent [OR] or else use any two of the following medically acceptable forms of contraception from the Screening Period through the Final Study Visit: hormonal, [OR] condom [AND] with spermicidal jelly, [OR] diaphragm [OR] or cervical cap [AND] with spermicidal jelly, [OR] or IUD. Hormonal contraception must have started at least 3 months prior to screening. A female [AND] whose male partner has had a vasectomy must agree to use one additional form of medically acceptable contraception. Subjects must agree to practice the above birth control methods for 30 days from the final visit as a safety precaution. \nFemales of [NOT] non-childbearing potential, defined as surgically sterile (status post hysterectomy, [OR] bilateral oophorectomy, [OR] or bilateral tubal ligation) [OR] or post-menopausal for at least 12 months (and confirmed with a screening FSH level in the post-menopausal range), do [NOT] not require contraception during the study. \nMales [AND] with female partners of childbearing potential must agree to use two medically acceptable forms of contraception as described above, with one of the two forms being condom [AND] with spermicide, from the Screening Period through the Final Study Visit. Males [AND] with female partners of childbearing potential [AND] who themselves are surgically sterile (status post vasectomy) must agree to use condoms [AND] with spermicide over the same period of time. Male subjects must agree to practice the above birth control methods for 30 days from the final visit as a safety precaution. \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nFasting blood glucose >126 mg/dL at screening. Heterozygous subjects will be [NOT] excluded for a fasting blood glucose >140 mg/dL. \nResting heart rate <45 bpm [OR] or >90 bpm at screening. \nAbnormal thyroid stimulating hormone (TSH) [OR] or thyroxine (T4) levels on screening. \nElevated ALT [OR] or serum creatinine on screening [OR] or any clinically significant abnormalities on screening laboratory tests as determined by the Investigator. \nHistory of medically treated diabetes [OR] or of treated [OR] or medically diagnosed hypertension. Heterozygous subjects [AND] who have diagnosed hypertension [AND] and are well controlled on treatment (Refer to Exclusion criteria 20 below), are eligible.. \nPresence of a skin lesion suspicious for malignancy, unless excised prior to Day 1. \nHistory of malignancy except for treated cervical carcinoma in situ in the past 5 years. \nActive [OR] or history of any clinically significant medical condition including renal, [OR] hepatic, [OR] pulmonary, [OR] gastrointestinal, [OR] cardiovascular, [OR] genitourinary, [OR] endocrine, [OR] immunologic, [OR] metabolic, [OR] neurologic, [OR] psychiatric [OR] or hematological disease, based on Investigator judgment. \nAcute illness [OR] or history of illness, which in the opinion of the Investigator, could pose a threat [OR] or harm to the subject [OR] or obscure interpretation of laboratory test results [OR] or interpretation of study data. \nPositive hepatitis B surface antigen, positive hepatitis C antibody [OR] or positive HIV test at screening [OR] or a history of positive testing (e.g. liver biopsy, [OR] serology) suggesting acute [OR] or chronic hepatitis. \nAbnormal 12-lead electrocardiogram (ECG) at screening [OR] or pre-dose (Day -1 [OR] or Day 1), except minor deviations deemed to be of no clinical significance by the Investigator. \nReceived any experimental drugs [OR] or devices within 30 days [OR] or 5 half lives, whichever is longer, prior to dosing. \nOngoing participation in a prior clinical study at the time of screening. \nBlood donation within 60 days prior to screening [OR] or intent to donate within 60 days after Final Study Visit. \nHospitalization for major surgery including but not limited to abdominal, [OR] thoracic, [OR] or cardiovascular surgery within the past 3 months prior to screening, [OR] or for a clinically significant [NOT] non-surgical illness, based on Investigator judgment, within the past 3 months. \nPlanned elective surgery within 30 days of the Final Study Visit. \nPoor venous access [OR] or [NOT] inability to tolerate venipuncture. \nHistory of significant drug hypersensitivity [OR] or anaphylaxis. \nHistory of hypersensitivity to proteins (e.g., allergy shots). \nUse of prescription medications on a regular basis. The last use of any prescription medication must have been greater than 5 half-lives for the specific medication [OR] or at least 14 days prior to admission (Day -1), whichever is longer. Hormonal contraception is allowed for female subjects. \nHeterozygous cohorts: Use of prescription medications on a regular basis is [NOT] not allowed with the following exceptions: \nAntihypertensives (<3 medications on a stable dose for ≥ 30 days); \nStatins (dose must be ≤ half the maximum dose; must be on a stable dose ≥3 months); \n Fibrates (must be on stable dose for ≥3 months); \n Niacin (must be on stable dose for ≥3 months); \n Thyroxin (stable dose for ≥ 30 days); The last use of any other prescription medication will need follow the criteria for all other cohorts, as outlined above. \nUse of prescription medications [NOT] not listed above may be allowed at the discretion of the Investigator upon consultation with Rhythm. \nUse of a [NOT] non-prescription drug [OR] and herbal substances during the study (through the Final Study Visit). The last dose of any [NOT] non-prescription drug must have been taken greater than 5 half-lives for that drug before receiving study drug. \n[NOT] Inability to attend all study visits [OR] or to comply with protocol requirements including fasting [OR] and [NOT] restrictions on alcohol, [OR] caffeine, [OR] nicotine [OR] and concomitant medication intake. \nA significant history of drug/ [OR] solvent abuse within 5 years of screening [OR] or a positive test for drugs of abuse test at screening [OR] or on Day -1. \nPositive alcohol (breath test) [OR] or nicotine screen at Screening Visit [OR] or Day 1 (positive nicotine screen does [NOT] not apply to heterozygous cohort). \nHistory of alcohol abuse (defined as average intake of three or more units of alcohol per day) within 5 years of the Screening Visit. \nHistory of tobacco [OR] or tobacco product use unless abstinent for at least one year prior to the Screening Visit. This criterion does [NOT] not apply to heterozygous subjects. \nPreviously randomized [OR] and dosed in this study. This criterion does [NOT] not apply to heterozygous subjects. \nAny other reason, which in the opinion of the Investigator would confound proper evaluation of the study.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Able to provide voluntary, written informed consent with comprehension of all aspects of the protocol, prior to any study procedures. 
Healthy obese male [OR] and female volunteers aged 18 to 55 years, inclusive. Heterozygous subjects may be 18 to 65 years inclusive. 
In good general health, [NOT] without significant medical history, [OR] physical examination findings, [OR] or clinical laboratory abnormalities. 
Body Mass Index of 30-40 kg/m2, inclusive. Heterozygous subjects may have a broader BMI range; to be eligible heterozygous subjects may have a BMI 27 -55 kg/ m2, inclusive. 
Stable body weight during the previous 6 months, based on Investigator judgment. 
Blood pressure <140/90 mmHg at Screening [AND] and D-1. Measurement may be repeated within 24 hours, based on Investigator judgment. 
Females [NOT] must [NOT] not be pregnant [AND] and must have a negative serum pregnancy test result at the Screening Visit [AND] and Day -1. 
Females of childbearing potential must agree to be abstinent [OR] or else use any two of the following medically acceptable forms of contraception from the Screening Period through the Final Study Visit: hormonal, [OR] condom [AND] with spermicidal jelly, [OR] diaphragm [OR] or cervical cap [AND] with spermicidal jelly, [OR] or IUD. Hormonal contraception must have started at least 3 months prior to screening. A female [AND] whose male partner has had a vasectomy must agree to use one additional form of medically acceptable contraception. Subjects must agree to practice the above birth control methods for 30 days from the final visit as a safety precaution. 
Females of [NOT] non-childbearing potential, defined as surgically sterile (status post hysterectomy, [OR] bilateral oophorectomy, [OR] or bilateral tubal ligation) [OR] or post-menopausal for at least 12 months (and confirmed with a screening FSH level in the post-menopausal range), do [NOT] not require contraception during the study. 
Males [AND] with female partners of childbearing potential must agree to use two medically acceptable forms of contraception as described above, with one of the two forms being condom [AND] with spermicide, from the Screening Period through the Final Study Visit. Males [AND] with female partners of childbearing potential [AND] who themselves are surgically sterile (status post vasectomy) must agree to use condoms [AND] with spermicide over the same period of time. Male subjects must agree to practice the above birth control methods for 30 days from the final visit as a safety precaution. 

Exclusion Criteria:
Fasting blood glucose >126 mg/dL at screening. Heterozygous subjects will be [NOT] excluded for a fasting blood glucose >140 mg/dL. 
Resting heart rate <45 bpm [OR] or >90 bpm at screening. 
Abnormal thyroid stimulating hormone (TSH) [OR] or thyroxine (T4) levels on screening. 
Elevated ALT [OR] or serum creatinine on screening [OR] or any clinically significant abnormalities on screening laboratory tests as determined by the Investigator. 
History of medically treated diabetes [OR] or of treated [OR] or medically diagnosed hypertension. Heterozygous subjects [AND] who have diagnosed hypertension [AND] and are well controlled on treatment (Refer to Exclusion criteria 20 below), are eligible.. 
Presence of a skin lesion suspicious for malignancy, unless excised prior to Day 1. 
History of malignancy except for treated cervical carcinoma in situ in the past 5 years. 
Active [OR] or history of any clinically significant medical condition including renal, [OR] hepatic, [OR] pulmonary, [OR] gastrointestinal, [OR] cardiovascular, [OR] genitourinary, [OR] endocrine, [OR] immunologic, [OR] metabolic, [OR] neurologic, [OR] psychiatric [OR] or hematological disease, based on Investigator judgment. 
Acute illness [OR] or history of illness, which in the opinion of the Investigator, could pose a threat [OR] or harm to the subject [OR] or obscure interpretation of laboratory test results [OR] or interpretation of study data. 
Positive hepatitis B surface antigen, positive hepatitis C antibody [OR] or positive HIV test at screening [OR] or a history of positive testing (e.g. liver biopsy, [OR] serology) suggesting acute [OR] or chronic hepatitis. 
Abnormal 12-lead electrocardiogram (ECG) at screening [OR] or pre-dose (Day -1 [OR] or Day 1), except minor deviations deemed to be of no clinical significance by the Investigator. 
Received any experimental drugs [OR] or devices within 30 days [OR] or 5 half lives, whichever is longer, prior to dosing. 
Ongoing participation in a prior clinical study at the time of screening. 
Blood donation within 60 days prior to screening [OR] or intent to donate within 60 days after Final Study Visit. 
Hospitalization for major surgery including but not limited to abdominal, [OR] thoracic, [OR] or cardiovascular surgery within the past 3 months prior to screening, [OR] or for a clinically significant [NOT] non-surgical illness, based on Investigator judgment, within the past 3 months. 
Planned elective surgery within 30 days of the Final Study Visit. 
Poor venous access [OR] or [NOT] inability to tolerate venipuncture. 
History of significant drug hypersensitivity [OR] or anaphylaxis. 
History of hypersensitivity to proteins (e.g., allergy shots). 
Use of prescription medications on a regular basis. The last use of any prescription medication must have been greater than 5 half-lives for the specific medication [OR] or at least 14 days prior to admission (Day -1), whichever is longer. Hormonal contraception is allowed for female subjects. 
Heterozygous cohorts: Use of prescription medications on a regular basis is [NOT] not allowed with the following exceptions: 
Antihypertensives (<3 medications on a stable dose for ≥ 30 days); 
Statins (dose must be ≤ half the maximum dose; must be on a stable dose ≥3 months); 
 Fibrates (must be on stable dose for ≥3 months); 
 Niacin (must be on stable dose for ≥3 months); 
 Thyroxin (stable dose for ≥ 30 days); The last use of any other prescription medication will need follow the criteria for all other cohorts, as outlined above. 
Use of prescription medications [NOT] not listed above may be allowed at the discretion of the Investigator upon consultation with Rhythm. 
Use of a [NOT] non-prescription drug [OR] and herbal substances during the study (through the Final Study Visit). The last dose of any [NOT] non-prescription drug must have been taken greater than 5 half-lives for that drug before receiving study drug. 
[NOT] Inability to attend all study visits [OR] or to comply with protocol requirements including fasting [OR] and [NOT] restrictions on alcohol, [OR] caffeine, [OR] nicotine [OR] and concomitant medication intake. 
A significant history of drug/ [OR] solvent abuse within 5 years of screening [OR] or a positive test for drugs of abuse test at screening [OR] or on Day -1. 
Positive alcohol (breath test) [OR] or nicotine screen at Screening Visit [OR] or Day 1 (positive nicotine screen does [NOT] not apply to heterozygous cohort). 
History of alcohol abuse (defined as average intake of three or more units of alcohol per day) within 5 years of the Screening Visit. 
History of tobacco [OR] or tobacco product use unless abstinent for at least one year prior to the Screening Visit. This criterion does [NOT] not apply to heterozygous subjects. 
Previously randomized [OR] and dosed in this study. This criterion does [NOT] not apply to heterozygous subjects. 
Any other reason, which in the opinion of the Investigator would confound proper evaluation of the study.
