Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nSigned written informed consent.\nAge 18 to 65.\nNormal and healthy (immune competent) as determined by medical history, physical exam, vital signs and clinical laboratory tests during the screening period.\nIf all lab results for quantitative IgA immunoglobulin level are lower than 15% below normal range, the subject may not proceed further in the screening process.\nSubject must meet all required subject suitability criteria that pertain to normal source plasma donors.\nNegative HIV serology during screening period.\nSubject must have been previously immunized for smallpox, at =3 years prior to commencement of screening assessments, and vaccination history must be confirmed by oral or written history and the presence of a visible pathognomonic smallpox vaccination scar.\nFemale subjects of childbearing potential must agree to use highly effective birth control methods.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nHistory of severe related adverse event(s) from previous participation in VA-001 or VA-006 trials or to any smallpox vaccination.\nEczema, history of eczema, exfoliative skin conditions, wounds, burns, or other skin conditions at the investigator\'s discretion.\nA history of immunodeficiency.\nCurrently or has recently received radiotherapy or chemotherapy, adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH), corticosteroids, or immunosuppressive drugs.\nEye disease treated with topical steroids.\nKnown or suspected disorders of immunoglobulin synthesis.\nLeukemia, lymphomas of any type, melanoma, or other malignant neoplasms affecting the bone marrow or lymphatic systems.\nHas been diagnosed with cancer and who will be undergoing chemotherapy or radiation therapy during the vaccination healing time.\nIs a transplant recipient (except for corneal transplant).\nIs pregnant, planning pregnancy or breast feeding (female subjects of childbearing potential must have negative pregnancy test prior to vaccination).\nHousehold or other close/intimate contact(s) under the age of 12 months.\nHistory of allergies to phenol, any of the antibiotics listed in the vaccine content, or any other component of ACAM2000 or its diluents.\nSubjects with kidney disease (except kidney stones).\nSubjects with abnormal EKG at screening (if applicable). To mitigate the risk of enrolling at risk subjects and potentially jeopardizing subject safety an EKG will be performed prior to vaccination with ACAM2000 smallpox vaccine in all potential subjects =50 years old and for all potential subjects <50 with two cardiac risk factors as listed immediately below including; severely or morbidly obese or higher obesity classification (BMI =36); high blood pressure; high blood cholesterol; diabetes or high blood sugar; a first degree relative who had a heart condition before the age of 50; and current tobacco smokers.\nSeverely or morbidly obese or higher obesity classification (BMI =36)\nHigh blood pressure diagnosed by a doctor\nHigh blood cholesterol diagnosed by a doctor\nDiabetes or high blood sugar diagnosed by a doctor\nA first degree relative (for example, mother, father, brother, sister) who had a heart condition before the age of 50\nCurrently smokes tobacco (cigarettes)\nArrhythmia\nSyncope related to cardiac disease\nPrevious myocardial infarction\nAngina\nCoronary artery disease\nCongestive heart failure\nCardiomyopathy\nStroke or transient ischemic attack\nMyocarditis\nPericarditis\nChest pain or shortness of breath with activity (such as climbing stairs), peripheral edema, heart palpitations, dry cough, irregular heartbeat, excessive fatigue, unexplained syncope\nOther heart conditions being treated by a physician\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nSigned written informed consent.\nAge 18 to 65.\nNormal [AND] and healthy (immune competent) as determined by medical history, [OR] physical exam, [OR] vital signs [AND] and clinical laboratory tests during the screening period.\nIf all lab results for quantitative IgA immunoglobulin level are lower than 15% below normal range, the subject may [NOT] not proceed further in the screening process.\nSubject must meet all required subject suitability criteria that pertain to normal source plasma donors.\nNegative HIV serology during screening period.\nSubject must have been previously immunized for smallpox, at =3 years prior to commencement of screening assessments, [AND] and vaccination history must be confirmed by oral [OR] or written history [AND] and the presence of a visible pathognomonic smallpox vaccination scar.\nFemale subjects [AND] of childbearing potential must agree to use highly effective birth control methods.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nHistory of severe related adverse event(s) from previous participation in VA-001 [OR] or VA-006 trials [OR] or to any smallpox vaccination.\nEczema, history of eczema, [OR] exfoliative skin conditions, [OR] wounds, [OR] burns, [OR] or other skin conditions at the investigator\'s discretion.\nA history of immunodeficiency.\nCurrently [OR] or has recently received radiotherapy [OR] or chemotherapy, [OR] adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH), [OR] corticosteroids, [OR] or immunosuppressive drugs.\nEye disease treated with topical steroids.\nKnown [OR] or suspected disorders of immunoglobulin synthesis.\nLeukemia, [OR] lymphomas of any type, [OR] melanoma, [OR] or other malignant neoplasms affecting the bone marrow [OR] or lymphatic systems.\nHas been diagnosed with cancer [AND] and who will be undergoing chemotherapy [OR] or radiation therapy during the vaccination healing time.\nIs a transplant recipient (except for corneal transplant).\n Is pregnant, [OR] planning pregnancy [OR] or breast feeding (female subjects [AND] of childbearing potential must have negative pregnancy test prior to vaccination).\nHousehold [OR] or other close/ [OR] intimate contact(s) under the age of 12 months.\nHistory of allergies to phenol, any of the antibiotics listed in the vaccine content, [OR] or any other component of ACAM2000 [OR] or its diluents.\nSubjects with kidney disease (except kidney stones).\n Subjects with abnormal EKG at screening (if applicable). To mitigate the risk of enrolling at risk subjects and potentially jeopardizing subject safety an EKG will be performed prior to vaccination with ACAM2000 smallpox vaccine in all potential subjects =50 years old [AND] and for all potential subjects <50 [AND] with two cardiac risk factors as listed immediately below including; severely [OR] or morbidly obese [OR] or higher obesity classification (BMI =36); high blood pressure; high blood cholesterol; diabetes [OR] or high blood sugar; a first degree relative [AND] who had a heart condition before the age of 50; and current tobacco smokers.\nSeverely [OR] or morbidly obese [OR] or higher obesity classification (BMI =36)\nHigh blood pressure diagnosed by a doctor\n High blood cholesterol diagnosed by a doctor\n Diabetes [OR] or high blood sugar diagnosed by a doctor\n A first degree relative (for example, mother, [OR] father, [OR] brother, [OR] sister) [AND] who had a heart condition before the age of 50\n Currently smokes tobacco (cigarettes)\n Arrhythmia\n Syncope related to cardiac disease\n Previous myocardial infarction\n Angina\n Coronary artery disease\n Congestive heart failure\n Cardiomyopathy\n Stroke [OR] or transient ischemic attack\n Myocarditis\n Pericarditis\n Chest pain [OR] or shortness of breath [AND] with activity (such as climbing stairs), peripheral edema, [OR] heart palpitations, [OR] dry cough, [OR] irregular heartbeat, [OR] excessive fatigue, [OR] unexplained syncope\nOther heart conditions being treated by a physician<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Signed written informed consent.
Age 18 to 65.
Normal [AND] and healthy (immune competent) as determined by medical history, [OR] physical exam, [OR] vital signs [AND] and clinical laboratory tests during the screening period.
If all lab results for quantitative IgA immunoglobulin level are lower than 15% below normal range, the subject may [NOT] not proceed further in the screening process.
Subject must meet all required subject suitability criteria that pertain to normal source plasma donors.
Negative HIV serology during screening period.
Subject must have been previously immunized for smallpox, at =3 years prior to commencement of screening assessments, [AND] and vaccination history must be confirmed by oral [OR] or written history [AND] and the presence of a visible pathognomonic smallpox vaccination scar.
Female subjects [AND] of childbearing potential must agree to use highly effective birth control methods.

Exclusion Criteria:
History of severe related adverse event(s) from previous participation in VA-001 [OR] or VA-006 trials [OR] or to any smallpox vaccination.
