examination, laboratory examination)       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nBody mass index (BMI): 18 ≤ BMI ≤ 32 kg/m² \nPostmenopausal state revealed by: \nMedical history, if applicable (natural menopause at least 12 months prior to first study drug administration; [OR] or surgical menopause by bilateral ovariectomy at least 3 months prior to first study drug administration), in addition: in women < 65 years old, follicle stimulating hormone (FSH) > 40 IU/L \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nIncompletely cured pre-existing diseases for which it can be assumed that the absorption, [OR] distribution, [OR] metabolism, [OR] elimination [OR] or effects of the study drugs will [NOT] not be normal \nKnown [OR] or suspected liver diseases \nClinically relevant findings(e.g. blood pressure, [OR] electrocardiogram(ECG); physical [OR] and gynecological examination, [OR] laboratory examination)       \n<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Body mass index (BMI): 18 ≤ BMI ≤ 32 kg/m² 
Postmenopausal state revealed by: 
Medical history, if applicable (natural menopause at least 12 months prior to first study drug administration; [OR] or surgical menopause by bilateral ovariectomy at least 3 months prior to first study drug administration), in addition: in women < 65 years old, follicle stimulating hormone (FSH) > 40 IU/L 

Exclusion Criteria:
Incompletely cured pre-existing diseases for which it can be assumed that the absorption, [OR] distribution, [OR] metabolism, [OR] elimination [OR] or effects of the study drugs will [NOT] not be normal 
Known [OR] or suspected liver diseases 
