hat significantly could affect test performance.\nConcurrent prescription of medicines for ADHD or medicines that significantly could affect test performance.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n18 years old or older.\nADHD is diagnosed according to Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders, fifth edition (DSM-5 criteria).\nSubstance Use Disorder is diagnosed according to DSM-5 criteria.\nQb-score 1.3 or higher on at least one of the weighted summary parameters QbActivity, [OR] QbInattention [OR] or QbImpulsivity on the QbTest.\nParticipants are given their written informed consent to participate in the study.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nAffected by alcohol [OR] or drugs during the last month.\nUntreated severe comorbid psychiatric [OR] or somatic illness.\nBloodpressure 150/95 or higher.\nIrregular pulse, [OR] or pulse 100 or higher.\n [NOT] No counter indications according to the Medikinet pill.\nConcurrent clinical diagnosis that significantly could affect test performance.\nConcurrent prescription of medicines for ADHD [OR] or medicines that significantly could affect test performance.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
18 years old or older.
ADHD is diagnosed according to Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders, fifth edition (DSM-5 criteria).
Substance Use Disorder is diagnosed according to DSM-5 criteria.
Qb-score 1.3 or higher on at least one of the weighted summary parameters QbActivity, [OR] QbInattention [OR] or QbImpulsivity on the QbTest.
Participants are given their written informed consent to participate in the study.

Exclusion Criteria:
Affected by alcohol [OR] or drugs during the last month.
Untreated severe comorbid psychiatric [OR] or somatic illness.
Bloodpressure 150/95 or higher.
Irregular pulse, [OR] or pulse 100 or higher.
 [NOT] No counter indications according to the Medikinet pill.
Concurrent clinical diagnosis that significantly could affect test performance.
Concurrent prescription of medicines for ADHD [OR] or medicines that significantly could affect test performance.
