File: NCT02510404 

Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_full/NCT02510404.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\n1. Diagnosis of primary immunodeficiency with established plan to undergo myeloablative or non-myeloablative allogeneic hematopoietic stem cell transplant for treatment thereof or diagnosis of a form of primary immunodeficiency for which hematopoietic stem cell transplantation is not indicated. \n2. Active infection with EBV, CMV, and/or Adenovirus, unable to be successfully controlled with standard therapy. \n3. Steroids less than 0.5 mg/kg/day prednisone \n4. Karnofsky/Lansky score of ≥ 50 \n5. ANC greater than 500/µL. \n6. Bilirubin <2x, AST <3x, Serum creatinine <2x upper limit of normal, Hgb >8.0 \n7. Pulse oximetry of > 90% on room air \n8. Negative pregnancy test (if female of childbearing potential) \n9. Patient or parent/guardian capable of providing informed consent. \n\nExclusion Criteria:\n1. Patients with other uncontrolled infections (see 2.3.2 for definitions) \n2. Patients who received ATG, Campath, or other T cell immunosuppressive monoclonal antibodies in the last 28 days \n3. Received donor lymphocyte infusion in last 28 days \n4. Diagnosis of Omenn\'s syndrome or MHC class I deficiency \n5. Active and uncontrolled malignancy \n6. Pregnant or lactating \n7. Unable to wean steroids to ≤0.5 mg/kg/day prednisone. \n8. Patients with Grade 3 hyperbilirubinemia       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n 1. Diagnosis of primary immunodeficiency [AND] with established plan to undergo myeloablative [OR] or [NOT] non-myeloablative allogeneic hematopoietic stem cell transplant for treatment thereof [OR] or diagnosis of a form of primary immunodeficiency [AND] for which hematopoietic stem cell transplantation is [NOT] not indicated. \n 2. Active infection with EBV, [OR] CMV, [OR] and/or Adenovirus, [NOT] unable to be successfully controlled with standard therapy. \n 3. Steroids less than 0.5 mg/kg/day prednisone \n 4. Karnofsky/ [OR] Lansky score of ≥ 50 \n 5. ANC greater than 500/µL. \n 6. Bilirubin <2x, AST <3x, Serum creatinine <2x upper limit of normal, [AND] Hgb >8.0 \n 7. Pulse oximetry of > 90% on room air \n 8. Negative pregnancy test (if female [AND] of childbearing potential) \n 9. Patient or parent/guardian capable of providing informed consent. \n\nExclusion Criteria:\n 1. Patients with other uncontrolled infections (see 2.3.2 for definitions) \n 2. Patients [AND] who received ATG, [OR] Campath, [OR] or other T cell immunosuppressive monoclonal antibodies in the last 28 days \n 3. Received donor lymphocyte infusion in last 28 days \n 4. Diagnosis of Omenn\'s syndrome [OR] or MHC class I deficiency \n 5. Active [AND] and uncontrolled malignancy \n 6. Pregnant [OR] or lactating \n 7. [NOT] Unable to wean steroids to ≤0.5 mg/kg/day prednisone. \n 8. Patients with Grade 3 hyperbilirubinemia<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
 1. Diagnosis of primary immunodeficiency [AND] with established plan to undergo myeloablative [OR] or [NOT] non-myeloablative allogeneic hematopoietic stem cell transplant for treatment thereof [OR] or diagnosis of a form of primary immunodeficiency [AND] for which hematopoietic stem cell transplantation is [NOT] not indicated. 
 2. Active infection with EBV, [OR] CMV, [OR] and/or Adenovirus, [NOT] unable to be successfully controlled with standard therapy. 
 3. Steroids less than 0.5 mg/kg/day prednisone 
 4. Karnofsky/ [OR] Lansky score of ≥ 50 
 5. ANC greater than 500/µL. 
 6. Bilirubin <2x, AST <3x, Serum creatinine <2x upper limit of normal, [AND] Hgb >8.0 
 7. Pulse oximetry of > 90% on room air 
 8. Negative pregnancy test (if female [AND] of childbearing potential) 
 9. Patient or parent/guardian capable of providing informed consent. 

Exclusion Criteria:
 1. Patients with other uncontrolled infections (see 2.3.2 for definitions) 
 2. Patients [AND] who received ATG, [OR] Campath, [OR] or other T cell immunosuppressive monoclonal antibodies in the last 28 days 
 3. Received donor lymphocyte infusion in last 28 days 
 4. Diagnosis of Omenn's syndrome [OR] or MHC class I deficiency 
 5. Active [AND] and uncontrolled malignancy 
 6. Pregnant [OR] or lactating 
 7. [NOT] Unable to wean steroids to ≤0.5 mg/kg/day prednisone. 
 8. Patients with Grade 3 hyperbilirubinemia
