/m2)\nSubjects deemed to be healthy as judged by the Medically Accountable Investigator (MAI) and determined by medical history, physical examination and medication history\nSubjects have no history of the following: ongoing acute or intermittent pain, postoperative pain, respiratory compromise, acute or severe asthma, or constipation (less than 1 bowel movement every 2 days)\nNegative urine drug screening test at the time of screening\nHave normal screening laboratories for white blood cells (WBC), hemoglobin (Hgb), platelets, sodium, potassium, chloride, bicarbonate, blood urea nitrogen (BUN), creatinine, ALT (liver function), AST (liver function) and bilirubin\nHave normal screening laboratories for urine protein and urine glucose\nFemale subjects must be of non-childbearing potential (as defined as surgically sterile [i.e. history of hysterectomy or tubal ligation] or postmenopausal for more than 1 year [no bleeding for 12 consecutive months], or if of childbearing potential must be non-pregnant at the time of enrollment and on the morning of the first day of each study session, and must agree to use hormonal or barrier birth control such as implants, injectables, combined oral contraceptives, some intrauterine devices (IUDs), sexual abstinence or a vasectomized parter\nAgrees not to participate in another clinical study/trial during the study period or to participate in an investigational drug study for at least one month after last study session\nAgrees not to donate blood to a blood bank throughout participation in the study and for at least 3 months after last study day\nHave a normal ECG; must not have the following to be acceptable: pathologic Q wave abnormalities, significant ST-T wave changes, left ventricular hypertrophy, right bundle branch block, left bundle branch block. (sinus rhythm is between 55-100 beats per minute)\nTemperature 35-37.9°C (95-100.3°F)\nSystolic blood pressure 90-140 mmHg\nDiastolic blood pressure 60-90 mmHg\nHeart rate 55-100 beats per minute\nRespiration rate 12-18 breaths per minute\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nWomen who are pregnant, lactating or breast feeding or have a positive serum pregnancy test at enrollment or positive urine pregnancy test on the morning of the first day of any study session\nSmokers (current use or use over the previous 2 months of nicotine-containing substances, including tobacco products (e.g. cigarettes, cigars, chewing tobacco, gum, patch or electronic cigarettes)\nParticipation in any ongoing investigational drug trial/study or clinical drug trial/study\nHistory of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease or cor pulmonale, or substantially decreased respiratory reserve, hypoxia, hypercapnia or pre-existing respiratory depression\nActive positive Hepatitis B, C and HIV serologies\nPositive urine drug screening test\nUse of any prescription medication during the session 0 to 30 days or over-the counter medication e.g. antihistamines or topical corticosteroids (vitamin, herbal supplements and birth control medications not included) during the session 0 to 3 days before entry to the study\nUse of medications or treatments that would significantly influence or exaggerate responses to the test product or that would alter inflammatory or immune response to the product or agents deemed to be immunosuppressive as determined by physician investigator with 72 hours prior to dosing (e.g. antihistamines, systemic or topical corticosteroids (within 3 weeks prior to dosing), cyclosporine, tacrolimus, cytotoxic drugs, immune globulin, Bacillus Calmette-Guerin (BCG), monoclonal antibodies, radiation therapy)\nUse of monoamine oxidase inhibitors 21 days prior to study\nCurrent use of mixed agonist/antagonist (such as pentazocine, nalbuphine or butorphanol) and partial agonist (buprenorphine) analgesics\nCurrent use of anticholinergics or other medications with anticholinergic activity\nConsumption of beverages containing alcohol, grapefruit juice, Seville oranges, or quinine (e.g. tonic water) or foods containing poppy seeds in the last 72 hours.\nDonation or loss of greater than one pint of blood within 60 days of entry to the study\nAny prior serious adverse reaction or hypersensitivity to fentanyl, morphine, codeine, hydrocodone, hydromorphone, oxycodone, oxymorphone, naltrexone or naloxone or any of the inactive ingredients in the TDDS (polyester/ethyl vinyl acetate, polyacrylate adhesive, silicone adhesive, dimethicone NF, or polyolefin)\nHave a diagnosis of schizophrenia or other major psychiatric diagnosis or mental illness (e.g. major depression)\nMedical history of personal drug or alcohol addiction or abuse\nAny condition that would, in the opinion of the MAI, place the subject at an unacceptable risk of injury or render the subject unable to meet the requirements of the protocol\nInability to communicate or cooperate with the investigators\nSubject has an obvious difference in skin color between arms or the presence of a skin condition, excessive hair at the application site (upper arm), sunburn, raised moles and scars, open sore, scar tissue, tattoo, or coloration that would interfere with placement of test articles, skin assessment, or reactions to drug\nFailure to pass opioid dependence challenge test on the first day study day of any study session (i.e., before taking the first dose of naltrexone hydrochloride). Each subject will be injected subcutaneously with naloxone hydrochloride (0.8 mg injection) and will be observed for 45 minutes for signs and symptoms of opioid withdrawal.\nWithin 4 weeks prior to dosing, use of medications or treatments that would significantly influence or exaggerate responses to the test product or that would alter inflammatory or immune response to the product or agents deemed to be immunosuppressive as determined by physician investigator\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nMen [OR] or [NOT] non-pregnant women [AND] of any ethnic background between the age of 18 and 45 years old\nSubjects must be [NOT] non-smokers (must have refrained from the use of nicotine-containing substances, including tobacco products (e.g. cigarettes, [OR] cigars, [OR] chewing tobacco, [OR] gum, [OR] patch [OR] or electronic cigarettes) over the previous 2 months [AND] and are [NOT] not currently using tobacco products\nProvide written informed consent before initiation of any study procedures\nAvailable for follow-up for the planned duration of the study\nAble to communicate well with the investigators\nAble to adhere to the study protocol schedule, study restrictions [AND] and examination schedule\nSubjects who are within their ideal body weight (BMI between >17 [AND] and =28 kg/m2)\nSubjects deemed to be healthy as judged by the Medically Accountable Investigator (MAI) and determined by medical history, [OR] physical examination [OR] and medication history\nSubjects have [NOT] no history of the following: ongoing acute [OR] or intermittent pain, [OR] postoperative pain, [OR] respiratory compromise, acute [OR] or severe asthma, [OR] or constipation (less than 1 bowel movement every 2 days)\nNegative urine drug screening test at the time of screening\nHave normal screening laboratories for white blood cells (WBC), hemoglobin (Hgb), platelets, sodium, [OR] potassium, [OR] chloride, [OR] bicarbonate, blood urea nitrogen (BUN), creatinine, ALT (liver function), AST (liver function) [OR] and bilirubin\nHave normal screening laboratories for urine protein [OR] and urine glucose\nFemale subjects must be of [NOT] non-childbearing potential (as defined as surgically sterile [i.e. history of hysterectomy [OR] or tubal ligation] [OR] or postmenopausal [AND] for more than 1 year ([NOT] no bleeding for 12 consecutive months), [OR] or if of childbearing potential must be [NOT] non-pregnant at the time of enrollment [AND] and on the morning of the first day of each study session, [AND] and must agree to use hormonal [OR] or barrier birth control such as implants, [OR] injectables, [OR] combined oral contraceptives, some intrauterine devices (IUDs), sexual abstinence [OR] or a vasectomized parter\nAgrees not to participate in another clinical study/ [OR] trial during the study period [OR] or to participate in an investigational drug study for at least one month after last study session\nAgrees not to donate blood to a blood bank throughout participation in the study [AND] and for at least 3 months after last study day\nHave a normal ECG; must [NOT] not have the following to be acceptable: pathologic Q wave abnormalities, significant ST-T wave changes, left ventricular hypertrophy, [OR] right bundle branch block, [OR] left bundle branch block. (sinus rhythm is between 55-100 beats per minute)\nTemperature 35-37.9°C (95-100.3°F)\nSystolic blood pressure 90-140 mmHg\n Diastolic blood pressure 60-90 mmHg\nHeart rate 55-100 beats per minute\nRespiration rate 12-18 breaths per minute\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nWomen [AND] who are pregnant, [OR] lactating [OR] or breast feeding [OR] or have a positive serum pregnancy test at enrollment [OR] or positive urine pregnancy test on the morning of the first day of any study session\nSmokers (current use [OR] or use over the previous 2 months of nicotine-containing substances, including tobacco products (e.g. cigarettes, [OR] cigars, [OR] chewing tobacco, [OR] gum, [OR] patch [OR] or electronic cigarettes)\n Participation in any ongoing investigational drug trial/ [OR] study or clinical drug trial/ [OR] study\nHistory of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease [OR] or cor pulmonale, [OR] or substantially decreased respiratory reserve, [OR] hypoxia, [OR] hypercapnia [OR] or pre-existing respiratory depression\n Active positive Hepatitis B, [OR] C [OR] and HIV serologies\n Positive urine drug screening test\nUse of any prescription medication during the session 0 to 30 days [OR] or over-the counter medication e.g. antihistamines [OR] or topical corticosteroids (vitamin, [OR] herbal supplements [OR] and birth control medications [NOT] not included) during the session 0 to 3 days before entry to the study\nUse of medications [OR] or treatments that would significantly influence [OR] or exaggerate responses to the test product [OR] or that would alter inflammatory [OR] or immune response to the product [OR] or agents deemed to be immunosuppressive as determined by physician investigator with 72 hours prior to dosing (e.g. antihistamines, [OR] systemic [OR] or topical corticosteroids (within 3 weeks prior to dosing), cyclosporine, [OR] tacrolimus, [OR] cytotoxic drugs, [OR] immune globulin, [OR] Bacillus Calmette-Guerin (BCG), [OR] monoclonal antibodies, [OR] radiation therapy)\nUse of monoamine oxidase inhibitors 21 days prior to study\nCurrent use of mixed agonist/ [OR] antagonist (such as pentazocine, [OR] nalbuphine [OR] or butorphanol) [OR] and partial agonist (buprenorphine) analgesics\n Current use of anticholinergics [OR] or other medications with anticholinergic activity\nConsumption of beverages containing alcohol, [OR] grapefruit juice, [OR] Seville oranges, [OR] or quinine (e.g. tonic water) [OR] or foods containing poppy seeds in the last 72 hours.\nDonation [OR] or loss of greater than one pint of blood within 60 days of entry to the study\nAny prior serious adverse reaction [OR] or hypersensitivity to fentanyl, [OR] morphine, [OR] codeine, [OR] hydrocodone, [OR] hydromorphone, [OR] oxycodone, [OR] oxymorphone, [OR] naltrexone [OR] or naloxone [OR] or any of the inactive ingredients in the TDDS (polyester/ [OR] ethyl vinyl acetate, [OR] polyacrylate adhesive, [OR] silicone adhesive, [OR] dimethicone NF, [OR] or polyolefin)\nHave a diagnosis of schizophrenia [OR] or other major psychiatric diagnosis [OR] or mental illness (e.g. major depression)\nMedical history of personal drug [OR] or alcohol addiction [OR] or abuse\nAny condition that would, in the opinion of the MAI, place the subject at an unacceptable risk of injury [OR] or render the subject [NOT] unable to meet the requirements of the protocol\n [NOT] Inability to communicate [OR] or cooperate with the investigators\nSubject has an obvious difference in skin color between arms [OR] or the presence of a skin condition, excessive hair at the application site (upper arm), sunburn, raised moles [OR] and scars, [OR] open sore, [OR] scar tissue, [OR] tattoo, [OR] or coloration that would interfere with placement of test articles, skin assessment, [OR] or reactions to drug\nFailure to pass opioid dependence challenge test on the first day study day of any study session (i.e., before taking the first dose of naltrexone hydrochloride). Each subject will be injected subcutaneously with naloxone hydrochloride (0.8 mg injection) and will be observed for 45 minutes for signs and symptoms of opioid withdrawal.\nWithin 4 weeks prior to dosing, use of medications [OR] or treatments that would significantly influence [OR] or exaggerate responses to the test product [OR] or that would alter inflammatory [OR] or immune response to the product [OR] or agents deemed to be immunosuppressive as determined by physician investigator<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Men [OR] or [NOT] non-pregnant women [AND] of any ethnic background between the age of 18 and 45 years old
Subjects must be [NOT] non-smokers (must have refrained from the use of nicotine-containing substances, including tobacco products (e.g. cigarettes, [OR] cigars, [OR] chewing tobacco, [OR] gum, [OR] patch [OR] or electronic cigarettes) over the previous 2 months [AND] and are [NOT] not currently using tobacco products
Provide written informed consent before initiation of any study procedures
Available for follow-up for the planned duration of the study
Able to communicate well with the investigators
Able to adhere to the study protocol schedule, study restrictions [AND] and examination schedule
Subjects who are within their ideal body weight (BMI between >17 [AND] and =28 kg/m2)
Subjects deemed to be healthy as judged by the Medically Accountable Investigator (MAI) and determined by medical history, [OR] physical examination [OR] and medication history
Subjects have [NOT] no history of the following: ongoing acute [OR] or intermittent pain, [OR] postoperative pain, [OR] respiratory compromise, acute [OR] or severe asthma, [OR] or constipation (less than 1 bowel movement every 2 days)
Negative urine drug screening test at the time of screening
Have normal screening laboratories for white blood cells (WBC), hemoglobin (Hgb), platelets, sodium, [OR] potassium, [OR] chloride, [OR] bicarbonate, blood urea nitrogen (BUN), creatinine, ALT (liver function), AST (liver function) [OR] and bilirubin
Have normal screening laboratories for urine protein [OR] and urine glucose
Female subjects must be of [NOT] non-childbearing potential (as defined as surgically sterile [i.e. history of hysterectomy [OR] or tubal ligation] [OR] or postmenopausal [AND] for more than 1 year ([NOT] no bleeding for 12 consecutive months), [OR] or if of childbearing potential must be [NOT] non-pregnant at the time of enrollment [AND] and on the morning of the first day of each study session, [AND] and must agree to use hormonal [OR] or barrier birth control such as implants, [OR] injectables, [OR] combined oral contraceptives, some intrauterine devices (IUDs), sexual abstinence [OR] or a vasectomized parter
Agrees not to participate in another clinical study/ [OR] trial during the study period [OR] or to participate in an investigational drug study for at least one month after last study session
Agrees not to donate blood to a blood bank throughout participation in the study [AND] and for at least 3 months after last study day
Have a normal ECG; must [NOT] not have the following to be acceptable: pathologic Q wave abnormalities, significant ST-T wave changes, left ventricular hypertrophy, [OR] right bundle branch block, [OR] left bundle branch block. (sinus rhythm is between 55-100 beats per minute)
Temperature 35-37.9°C (95-100.3°F)
Systolic blood pressure 90-140 mmHg
 Diastolic blood pressure 60-90 mmHg
Heart rate 55-100 beats per minute
Respiration rate 12-18 breaths per minute

Exclusion Criteria:
Women [AND] who are pregnant, [OR] lactating [OR] or breast feeding [OR] or have a positive serum pregnancy test at enrollment [OR] or positive urine pregnancy test on the morning of the first day of any study session
Smokers (current use [OR] or use over the previous 2 months of nicotine-containing substances, including tobacco products (e.g. cigarettes, [OR] cigars, [OR] chewing tobacco, [OR] gum, [OR] patch [OR] or electronic cigarettes)
 Participation in any ongoing investigational drug trial/ [OR] study or clinical drug trial/ [OR] study
History of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease [OR] or cor pulmonale, [OR] or substantially decreased respiratory reserve, [OR] hypoxia, [OR] hypercapnia [OR] or pre-existing respiratory depression
 Active positive Hepatitis B, [OR] C [OR] and HIV serologies
 Positive urine drug screening test
Use of any prescription medication during the session 0 to 30 days [OR] or over-the counter medication e.g. antihistamines [OR] or topical corticosteroids (vitamin, [OR] herbal supplements [OR] and birth control medications [NOT] not included) during the session 0 to 3 days before entry to the study
Use of medications [OR] or treatments that would significantly influence [OR] or exaggerate responses to the test product [OR] or that would alter inflammatory [OR] or immune response to the product [OR] or agents deemed to be immunosuppressive as determined by physician investigator with 72 hours prior to dosing (e.g. antihistamines, [OR] systemic [OR] or topical corticosteroids (within 3 weeks prior to dosing), cyclosporine, [OR] tacrolimus, [OR] cytotoxic drugs, [OR] immune globulin, [OR] Bacillus Calmette-Guerin (BCG), [OR] monoclonal antibodies, [OR] radiation therapy)
Use of monoamine oxidase inhibitors 21 days prior to study
Current use of mixed agonist/ [OR] antagonist (such as pentazocine, [OR] nalbuphine [OR] or butorphanol) [OR] and partial agonist (buprenorphine) analgesics
 Current use of anticholinergics [OR] or other medications with anticholinergic activity
Consumption of beverages containing alcohol, [OR] grapefruit juice, [OR] Seville oranges, [OR] or quinine (e.g. tonic water) [OR] or foods containing poppy seeds in the last 72 hours.
Donation [OR] or loss of greater than one pint of blood within 60 days of entry to the study
Any prior serious adverse reaction [OR] or hypersensitivity to fentanyl, [OR] morphine, [OR] codeine, [OR] hydrocodone, [OR] hydromorphone, [OR] oxycodone, [OR] oxymorphone, [OR] naltrexone [OR] or naloxone [OR] or any of the inactive ingredients in the TDDS (polyester/ [OR] ethyl vinyl acetate, [OR] polyacrylate adhesive, [OR] silicone adhesive, [OR] dimethicone NF, [OR] or polyolefin)
Have a diagnosis of schizophrenia [OR] or other major psychiatric diagnosis [OR] or mental illness (e.g. major depression)
Medical history of personal drug [OR] or alcohol addiction [OR] or abuse
Any condition that would, in the opinion of the MAI, place the subject at an unacceptable risk of injury [OR] or render the subject [NOT] unable to meet the requirements of the protocol
 [NOT] Inability to communicate [OR] or cooperate with the investigators
Subject has an obvious difference in skin color between arms [OR] or the presence of a skin condition, excessive hair at the application site (upper arm), sunburn, raised moles [OR] and scars, [OR] open sore, [OR] scar tissue, [OR] tattoo, [OR] or coloration that would interfere with placement of test articles, skin assessment, [OR] or reactions to drug
Failure to pass opioid dependence challenge test on the first day study day of any study session (i.e., before taking the first dose of naltrexone hydrochloride). Each subject will be injected subcutaneously with naloxone hydrochloride (0.8 mg injection) and will be observed for 45 minutes for signs and symptoms of opioid withdrawal.
Within 4 weeks prior to dosing, use of medications [OR] or treatments that would significantly influence [OR] or exaggerate responses to the test product [OR] or that would alter inflammatory [OR] or immune response to the product [OR] or agents deemed to be immunosuppressive as determined by physician investigator
