Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nDiagnosed with cutaneous vasculitis, urticaria, psoriasis, acne, bullous skin diseases, sterile pustulosis, leprosy, pneumocystis pneumonia and any other patients who need dapsone administration.\nSubjects are dapsone-naive.\nAll subjects must have a clinical need for treatment with dapsone that precedes the decision to participate in the study.\nAll subjects are willing to complete the 6-weeks period clinical trial.\nAll subjects are written informed consent.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nHas previously received Dapsone therapy.\nThe subject or any of their healthcare providers is aware of the subjects HLA type.\nHas been diagnosed with Glucose-6-phosphate dehydrogenase deficiency or methemoglobin reductase deficiency\nSatisfies any contraindications or restrictions to Dapsone therapy as listed in the product labels.\nCurrent severe illness, including heart, liver and renal failure, major organ allograft, malignancy requiring parenteral chemotherapy that can not be discontinued for the duration of the trial, or any other conditions which, in the opinion of the Investigator, would make the patient unsuitable for the study.\nAny laboratory abnormality at Screening which, in the opinion of the Investigator, should preclude the subject\'s participation in the study [alanine aminotransferase (ALT), glutamic oxaloacetic transaminase(ALT), et al).\nPregnant women or women who are breastfeeding.\nSubject is, in the opinion of the Investigator, unable to complete the 6 week Observation period and the EPT assessments as required.\nA positive result for HLA-B*1301 in those subjects randomised to the genetic screening arm.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nDiagnosed with cutaneous vasculitis, [OR] urticaria, [OR] psoriasis, [OR] acne, [OR] bullous skin diseases, [OR] sterile pustulosis, [OR] leprosy, [OR] pneumocystis pneumonia [OR] and any other patients [AND] who need dapsone administration.\nSubjects are dapsone- [NOT] naive.\nAll subjects must have a clinical need for treatment [AND] with dapsone that precedes the decision to participate in the study.\nAll subjects are willing to complete the 6-weeks period clinical trial.\nAll subjects are written informed consent.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nHas previously received Dapsone therapy.\nThe subject or any of their healthcare providers is aware of the subjects HLA type.\n Has been diagnosed with Glucose-6-phosphate dehydrogenase deficiency [OR] or methemoglobin reductase deficiency\nSatisfies any contraindications [OR] or restrictions to Dapsone therapy as listed in the product labels.\nCurrent severe illness, including heart, [OR] liver [OR] and renal failure, major organ allograft, [OR] malignancy requiring parenteral chemotherapy that can [NOT] not be [NOT] discontinued for the duration of the trial, [OR] or any other conditions which, in the opinion of the Investigator, would make the patient unsuitable for the study.\nAny laboratory abnormality at Screening which, in the opinion of the Investigator, should [NOT] preclude the subject\'s participation in the study [alanine aminotransferase (ALT), glutamic oxaloacetic transaminase(ALT), et al].\nPregnant women [OR] or women [AND] who are breastfeeding.\nSubject is, in the opinion of the Investigator, [NOT] unable to complete the 6 week Observation period [AND] and the EPT assessments as required.\nA positive result for HLA-B*1301 in those subjects randomised to the genetic screening arm.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Diagnosed with cutaneous vasculitis, [OR] urticaria, [OR] psoriasis, [OR] acne, [OR] bullous skin diseases, [OR] sterile pustulosis, [OR] leprosy, [OR] pneumocystis pneumonia [OR] and any other patients [AND] who need dapsone administration.
Subjects are dapsone- [NOT] naive.
All subjects must have a clinical need for treatment [AND] with dapsone that precedes the decision to participate in the study.
All subjects are willing to complete the 6-weeks period clinical trial.
All subjects are written informed consent.

Exclusion Criteria:
Has previously received Dapsone therapy.
The subject or any of their healthcare providers is aware of the subjects HLA type.
 Has been diagnosed with Glucose-6-phosphate dehydrogenase deficiency [OR] or methemoglobin reductase deficiency
Satisfies any contraindications [OR] or restrictions to Dapsone therapy as listed in the product labels.
Current severe illness, including heart, [OR] liver [OR] and renal failure, major organ allograft, [OR] malignancy requiring parenteral chemotherapy that can [NOT] not be [NOT] discontinued for the duration of the trial, [OR] or any other conditions which, in the opinion of the Investigator, would make the patient unsuitable for the study.
Any laboratory abnormality at Screening which, in the opinion of the Investigator, should [NOT] preclude the subject's participation in the study [alanine aminotransferase (ALT), glutamic oxaloacetic transaminase(ALT), et al].
Pregnant women [OR] or women [AND] who are breastfeeding.
Subject is, in the opinion of the Investigator, [NOT] unable to complete the 6 week Observation period [AND] and the EPT assessments as required.
A positive result for HLA-B*1301 in those subjects randomised to the genetic screening arm.
