Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nProvide signed and dated informed consent form.\nWilling to comply with all study procedures and be available for the duration of the study.\nMale or female, aged = 18 to = 60 years on day of inclusion.\nIn good general health based on medical history and physical exam\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nSubject is pregnant, or lactating, or of childbearing potential (to be considered of non-childbearing potential, a female must be post-menopausal for at least 1 year, surgically sterile, or using an effective method of contraception or abstinence from at least 4 weeks prior to the first vaccination and until at least 4 weeks after the last vaccination.\nParticipation in the 4 weeks preceding the first trial vaccination, or planned participation during the present trial period, in another clinical trial investigating a vaccine, drug, medical device, or medical procedure.\nPrevious history of receiving the rabies vaccine.\nPrevious history of receiving rabies immune globulin.\nAny major psychiatric disorder, such as severe depression, severe anxiety disorder, psychosis, schizophrenia, other major psychiatric disorders, or seizures. History of mild depression or anxiety disorder that are well controlled are not exclusion criteria.\nUse of any immunosuppressive drug at the time of the study or 30 days previously. Topical steroids will not be considered an immunosuppressive drug and their use will not be considered an exclusion criteria.\nAny immunosuppressive disorder, such as HIV infection, common variable immunodeficiency, active cancers or chemotherapy.\nHistory of renal insufficiency or requiring dialysis.\nHave any condition that would, in the opinion of the site investigator, place the subject at an unacceptable risk of injury or render the subject unable to meet the requirements of the protocol.\nIdentified as an employee of the Investigator or study center, with direct involvement in the proposed study or other studies under the direction of that Investigator or study center, as well as family members (i.e., immediate, husband, wife and their children, adopted or natural) of the employee or the Investigator.\nPrevious adverse reaction to any of the antimalarial drugs used in this study.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nProvide signed and dated informed consent form.\nWilling to comply with all study procedures and be available for the duration of the study.\nMale [OR] or female, aged = 18 to = 60 years on day of inclusion.\nIn good general health based on medical history [AND] and physical exam\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nSubject is pregnant, [OR] or lactating, [OR] or of childbearing potential (to be considered of [NOT] non-childbearing potential, a female must be post-menopausal [OR] for at least 1 year, surgically sterile, [OR] or using an effective method of contraception [OR] or abstinence from at least 4 weeks prior to the first vaccination and until at least 4 weeks after the last vaccination.\nParticipation in the 4 weeks preceding the first trial vaccination, [OR] or planned participation during the present trial period, in another clinical trial investigating a vaccine, [OR] drug, [OR] medical device, [OR] or medical procedure.\nPrevious history of receiving the rabies vaccine.\nPrevious history of receiving rabies immune globulin.\n Any major psychiatric disorder, such as severe depression, severe anxiety disorder, [OR] psychosis, [OR] schizophrenia, other major psychiatric disorders, [OR] or seizures. History of mild depression [OR] or anxiety disorder that are well controlled are [NOT] not exclusion criteria.\nUse of any immunosuppressive drug at the time of the study [OR] or 30 days previously. Topical steroids will [NOT] not be considered an immunosuppressive drug and their use will [NOT] not be considered an exclusion criteria.\nAny immunosuppressive disorder, such as HIV infection, common variable immunodeficiency, active cancers [OR] or chemotherapy.\n History of renal insufficiency [OR] or requiring dialysis.\nHave any condition that would, in the opinion of the site investigator, place the subject at an unacceptable risk of injury [OR] or render the subject [NOT] unable to meet the requirements of the protocol.\nIdentified as an employee of the Investigator or study center, with direct involvement in the proposed study [OR] or other studies under the direction of that Investigator or study center, as well as family members (i.e., immediate, husband, wife [OR] and their children, adopted [OR] or natural) of the employee [OR] or the Investigator.\nPrevious adverse reaction to any of the antimalarial drugs used in this study.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Provide signed and dated informed consent form.
Willing to comply with all study procedures and be available for the duration of the study.
Male [OR] or female, aged = 18 to = 60 years on day of inclusion.
In good general health based on medical history [AND] and physical exam

Exclusion Criteria:
Subject is pregnant, [OR] or lactating, [OR] or of childbearing potential (to be considered of [NOT] non-childbearing potential, a female must be post-menopausal [OR] for at least 1 year, surgically sterile, [OR] or using an effective method of contraception [OR] or abstinence from at least 4 weeks prior to the first vaccination and until at least 4 weeks after the last vaccination.
Participation in the 4 weeks preceding the first trial vaccination, [OR] or planned participation during the present trial period, in another clinical trial investigating a vaccine, [OR] drug, [OR] medical device, [OR] or medical procedure.
Previous history of receiving the rabies vaccine.
Previous history of receiving rabies immune globulin.
 Any major psychiatric disorder, such as severe depression, severe anxiety disorder, [OR] psychosis, [OR] schizophrenia, other major psychiatric disorders, [OR] or seizures. History of mild depression [OR] or anxiety disorder that are well controlled are [NOT] not exclusion criteria.
Use of any immunosuppressive drug at the time of the study [OR] or 30 days previously. Topical steroids will [NOT] not be considered an immunosuppressive drug and their use will [NOT] not be considered an exclusion criteria.
Any immunosuppressive disorder, such as HIV infection, common variable immunodeficiency, active cancers [OR] or chemotherapy.
 History of renal insufficiency [OR] or requiring dialysis.
Have any condition that would, in the opinion of the site investigator, place the subject at an unacceptable risk of injury [OR] or render the subject [NOT] unable to meet the requirements of the protocol.
Identified as an employee of the Investigator or study center, with direct involvement in the proposed study [OR] or other studies under the direction of that Investigator or study center, as well as family members (i.e., immediate, husband, wife [OR] and their children, adopted [OR] or natural) of the employee [OR] or the Investigator.
Previous adverse reaction to any of the antimalarial drugs used in this study.
