Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nhealthy parturients with uncomplicated, single gestation pregnancies, full term (38-42 weeks of gestation) pregnancy, agreed to participate\n\nExclusion Criteria:\na disease that might affect hepatic or renal function, contraindications to opioid analgesics, fetal growth retardation, signs of fetal asphyxia by cardiotocography, meconium stained amniotic fluid or placental insufficiency. The subjects should not have received fentanyl during the previous 14 days.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nhealthy parturients [AND] with uncomplicated, single gestation pregnancies, full term (38-42 weeks of gestation) pregnancy, agreed to participate\n\nExclusion Criteria:\na disease that might affect hepatic [OR] or renal function, contraindications to opioid analgesics, fetal growth retardation, signs of fetal asphyxia by cardiotocography, [OR] meconium stained amniotic fluid [OR] or placental insufficiency. The subjects should [NOT] not have received fentanyl during the previous 14 days.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
healthy parturients [AND] with uncomplicated, single gestation pregnancies, full term (38-42 weeks of gestation) pregnancy, agreed to participate

Exclusion Criteria:
a disease that might affect hepatic [OR] or renal function, contraindications to opioid analgesics, fetal growth retardation, signs of fetal asphyxia by cardiotocography, [OR] meconium stained amniotic fluid [OR] or placental insufficiency. The subjects should [NOT] not have received fentanyl during the previous 14 days.
