Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\n18 years of age or older;\nSuffer from schizophrenia/schizoaffective disorder meeting Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders, Fourth Edition, Text Revision (DSM-IV-TR) criteria;\nHave a total baseline score on the Brief Psychiatric Rating Scale (BPRS) = 45;\nBe capable and willing to provide written informed consent to participate in this study;\nAgree to abide by the study protocol and its restrictions and be able to complete all aspects of the study, including all visits and tests\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPatients posing a serious suicidal risk and/or violence as judged by the investigator;\nDelirium\nDementia\nAmnestic and other cognitive disorder;\nPatients with a history of hypothyroidism unless taking a stable dose of thyroid medication and asymptomatic or euthyroid for 6 months;\nPatients who meet DSM-IV-TR criteria for any significant current substance abuse;\nhepatic insufficiency (three times the upper limit of normal (ULN) for aspartate aminotransferase (AST) and/or alanine aminotransferase (ALT)); liver transplant recipient; cirrhosis of the liver;\nmalignancy (except basal cell carcinoma) and/or chemotherapy within 1 year prior to screening; malignancy more than 1 year prior to screening must have been local and without metastasis and/or recurrence, and if treated with chemotherapy, without nervous system complications;\nsignificant unstable medical condition or life threatening disease with anticipated survival of less than 6 months;\nneed for therapies that may obscure the results of treatment and/or of the study\nParticipation in another clinical trial within 30 days of the screening visit;\nAnticipated inability to attend scheduled study visits;\nPatients who in the judgment of the Investigator may be unreliable or uncooperative with the evaluation procedure outlined in this protocol;\nPatients with a history of prior pharmacogenomic testing;\nAny change in psychotropic medication (including change in dosage) between screening and baseline;\nPatients who are known to be pregnant or lactating;\nPatients with a history of gastric bypass surgery.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n18 years of age or older;\nSuffer from schizophrenia/ [OR] schizoaffective disorder meeting Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders, Fourth Edition, Text Revision (DSM-IV-TR) criteria;\nHave a total baseline score on the Brief Psychiatric Rating Scale (BPRS) = 45;\n Be capable and willing to provide written informed consent to participate in this study;\nAgree to abide by the study protocol and its restrictions and be able to complete all aspects of the study, including all visits and tests\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPatients posing a serious suicidal risk [OR] and/or violence as judged by the investigator;\nDelirium\n Dementia\n Amnestic and other cognitive disorder;\nPatients with a history of hypothyroidism [OR] unless taking a stable dose of thyroid medication [AND] and asymptomatic [OR] or euthyroid for 6 months;\nPatients who meet DSM-IV-TR criteria for any significant current substance abuse;\nhepatic insufficiency (three times the upper limit of normal (ULN) for aspartate aminotransferase (AST) [OR] and/or alanine aminotransferase (ALT)); liver transplant recipient; cirrhosis of the liver;\nmalignancy (except basal cell carcinoma) [OR] and/or chemotherapy within 1 year prior to screening; malignancy more than 1 year prior to screening must have been local [AND] and [NOT] without metastasis [OR] and/or recurrence, [AND] and if treated with chemotherapy, [NOT] without nervous system complications;\nsignificant unstable medical condition [OR] or life threatening disease [AND] with anticipated survival of less than 6 months;\nneed for therapies that may obscure the results of treatment [OR] and/or of the study\nParticipation in another clinical trial within 30 days of the screening visit;\nAnticipated [NOT] inability to attend scheduled study visits;\nPatients who in the judgment of the Investigator may be unreliable [OR] or uncooperative with the evaluation procedure outlined in this protocol;\nPatients with a history of prior pharmacogenomic testing;\n Any change in psychotropic medication (including change in dosage) between screening [AND] and baseline;\nPatients who are known to be pregnant [OR] or lactating;\nPatients with a history of gastric bypass surgery.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
18 years of age or older;
Suffer from schizophrenia/ [OR] schizoaffective disorder meeting Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders, Fourth Edition, Text Revision (DSM-IV-TR) criteria;
Have a total baseline score on the Brief Psychiatric Rating Scale (BPRS) = 45;
 Be capable and willing to provide written informed consent to participate in this study;
Agree to abide by the study protocol and its restrictions and be able to complete all aspects of the study, including all visits and tests

Exclusion Criteria:
Patients posing a serious suicidal risk [OR] and/or violence as judged by the investigator;
Delirium
 Dementia
 Amnestic and other cognitive disorder;
Patients with a history of hypothyroidism [OR] unless taking a stable dose of thyroid medication [AND] and asymptomatic [OR] or euthyroid for 6 months;
Patients who meet DSM-IV-TR criteria for any significant current substance abuse;
hepatic insufficiency (three times the upper limit of normal (ULN) for aspartate aminotransferase (AST) [OR] and/or alanine aminotransferase (ALT)); liver transplant recipient; cirrhosis of the liver;
malignancy (except basal cell carcinoma) [OR] and/or chemotherapy within 1 year prior to screening; malignancy more than 1 year prior to screening must have been local [AND] and [NOT] without metastasis [OR] and/or recurrence, [AND] and if treated with chemotherapy, [NOT] without nervous system complications;
significant unstable medical condition [OR] or life threatening disease [AND] with anticipated survival of less than 6 months;
need for therapies that may obscure the results of treatment [OR] and/or of the study
Participation in another clinical trial within 30 days of the screening visit;
Anticipated [NOT] inability to attend scheduled study visits;
Patients who in the judgment of the Investigator may be unreliable [OR] or uncooperative with the evaluation procedure outlined in this protocol;
Patients with a history of prior pharmacogenomic testing;
 Any change in psychotropic medication (including change in dosage) between screening [AND] and baseline;
Patients who are known to be pregnant [OR] or lactating;
Patients with a history of gastric bypass surgery.
