Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPrevious diagnoses of COPD and HF under optimized clinical treatment as judged by the accompanying physician\nReduced left ventricular ejection fraction (<50%)\nNon-reversible airway obstruction (post-bronchodilator FEV1/FVC < 0.7 and FEV1 < 80 %)\nRespiratory muscle weakness (Pi,max < 70cmH2O)\nPersistent dyspnea on daily life (Baseline Dyspnea Index focal score <or= 8).\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nInability to perform exercise tests\nDiagnosed psychiatric or cognitive disorders\nProgressive neurological or neuromuscular disorders having a major impact on exercise capacity\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPrevious diagnoses of COPD [OR] and HF under optimized clinical treatment as judged by the accompanying physician\nReduced left ventricular ejection fraction (<50%)\n [NOT] Non-reversible airway obstruction (post-bronchodilator FEV1/ [OR] FVC < 0.7 [AND] and FEV1 < 80 %)\nRespiratory muscle weakness (Pi,max < 70cmH2O)\nPersistent dyspnea on daily life (Baseline Dyspnea Index focal score <or= 8).\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nInability to perform exercise tests\nDiagnosed psychiatric [OR] or cognitive disorders\nProgressive neurological [OR] or neuromuscular disorders having a major impact on exercise capacity<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Previous diagnoses of COPD [OR] and HF under optimized clinical treatment as judged by the accompanying physician
Reduced left ventricular ejection fraction (<50%)
 [NOT] Non-reversible airway obstruction (post-bronchodilator FEV1/ [OR] FVC < 0.7 [AND] and FEV1 < 80 %)
Respiratory muscle weakness (Pi,max < 70cmH2O)
Persistent dyspnea on daily life (Baseline Dyspnea Index focal score <or= 8).

Exclusion Criteria:
Inability to perform exercise tests
Diagnosed psychiatric [OR] or cognitive disorders
Progressive neurological [OR] or neuromuscular disorders having a major impact on exercise capacity
