Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nMidsubstance pain in the achilles tendon\nSymptoms for at least 3 months\nUltrasound scanning at the first visit shows thickness of the achilles tendon above 7 mm or 20% thicker than the contralateral.\nPatient can read and understand danish\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nEarlier operations in the foot and leg, that is judged to complicate training\nknown arthritis.\nknown diabetes\nLeg ulcerations or infections in the foot.\nJudged unable to comply with the training protocol.\nDaily use of pain killers\nGlucocorticosteroid injection to the diseased achilles tendon within the last 6 months.\nEarlier allergic reactions to glucocorticosteroid or local anesthetic.\nPregnancy or planning to become pregnant\nBMI above 30.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nMidsubstance pain in the achilles tendon\nSymptoms for at least 3 months\nUltrasound scanning at the first visit shows thickness of the achilles tendon above 7 mm [OR] or 20% thicker than the contralateral.\nPatient can read and understand danish\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nEarlier operations in the foot [OR] and leg, that is judged to complicate training\nknown arthritis.\n known diabetes\nLeg ulcerations [OR] or infections in the foot.\n Judged unable to comply with the training protocol.\nDaily use of pain killers\nGlucocorticosteroid injection to the diseased achilles tendon within the last 6 months.\nEarlier allergic reactions to glucocorticosteroid [OR] or local anesthetic.\nPregnancy [OR] or planning to become pregnant\nBMI above 30.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Midsubstance pain in the achilles tendon
Symptoms for at least 3 months
Ultrasound scanning at the first visit shows thickness of the achilles tendon above 7 mm [OR] or 20% thicker than the contralateral.
Patient can read and understand danish

Exclusion Criteria:
Earlier operations in the foot [OR] and leg, that is judged to complicate training
known arthritis.
 known diabetes
Leg ulcerations [OR] or infections in the foot.
 Judged unable to comply with the training protocol.
Daily use of pain killers
Glucocorticosteroid injection to the diseased achilles tendon within the last 6 months.
Earlier allergic reactions to glucocorticosteroid [OR] or local anesthetic.
Pregnancy [OR] or planning to become pregnant
BMI above 30.
