Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nestimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) > 60 ml/min\npreserved left ventricular ejection fraction (>= 50%) on echocardiography\nHEALTHY: normal cardiac structure and function on echocardiography, BP < 140/90\nHYPERTENSIVE: history of BP >140/90, 1 or more antihypertensive medications, LV ejection fraction (LVEF) at least 50%, current BP < 160/90\nHFpEF: physician-confirmed diagnosis of HF, symptomatic HF, LVEF at least 50%, elevated LV filling pressure by catheterization, echocardiographic criteria or B-type-natriuretic peptide > 100, current BP < 160/90\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nExclusion Criteria: coronary artery disease, diabetes mellitus, contraindications to cardiac magnetic resonance imaging (CMR), weight >350 lbs, inability to lie flat for imaging, anemia, contraindications to regadenoson or aminophylline\nHEALTHY: known cardiovascular disease, cardiac risk factors or use of cardiac medications\nHYPERTENSIVE: known cardiovascular disease or risk factors aside from hypertension or use of cardiac medications\nHFpEF: prior history of LVEF below 50%, acute decompensated HF, moderate or greater valvular disease, significant cardiac arrhythmias, pericardial disease, congenital heart disease, primary pulmonary hypertension\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nestimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) > 60 ml/min\npreserved left ventricular ejection fraction (>= 50%) on echocardiography\nHEALTHY: normal cardiac structure [AND] and function on echocardiography, BP < 140/90\nHYPERTENSIVE: history of BP >140/90, 1 or more antihypertensive medications, LV ejection fraction (LVEF) at least 50%, current BP < 160/90\nHFpEF: physician-confirmed diagnosis of HF, symptomatic HF, LVEF at least 50%, elevated LV filling pressure by catheterization, [OR] echocardiographic criteria [OR] or B-type-natriuretic peptide > 100, current BP < 160/90\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nExclusion Criteria: coronary artery disease, [OR] diabetes mellitus, contraindications to cardiac magnetic resonance imaging (CMR), weight >350 lbs, [NOT] inability to lie flat for imaging, [OR] anemia, contraindications to regadenoson [OR] or aminophylline\nHEALTHY: known cardiovascular disease, [OR] cardiac risk factors [OR] or use of cardiac medications\nHYPERTENSIVE: known cardiovascular disease [OR] or risk factors aside from hypertension [OR] or use of cardiac medications\nHFpEF: prior history of LVEF below 50%, acute decompensated HF, [OR] moderate [OR] or greater valvular disease, significant cardiac arrhythmias, [OR] pericardial disease, [OR] congenital heart disease, [OR] primary pulmonary hypertension<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) > 60 ml/min
preserved left ventricular ejection fraction (>= 50%) on echocardiography
HEALTHY: normal cardiac structure [AND] and function on echocardiography, BP < 140/90
HYPERTENSIVE: history of BP >140/90, 1 or more antihypertensive medications, LV ejection fraction (LVEF) at least 50%, current BP < 160/90
HFpEF: physician-confirmed diagnosis of HF, symptomatic HF, LVEF at least 50%, elevated LV filling pressure by catheterization, [OR] echocardiographic criteria [OR] or B-type-natriuretic peptide > 100, current BP < 160/90

Exclusion Criteria:
Exclusion Criteria: coronary artery disease, [OR] diabetes mellitus, contraindications to cardiac magnetic resonance imaging (CMR), weight >350 lbs, [NOT] inability to lie flat for imaging, [OR] anemia, contraindications to regadenoson [OR] or aminophylline
HEALTHY: known cardiovascular disease, [OR] cardiac risk factors [OR] or use of cardiac medications
HYPERTENSIVE: known cardiovascular disease [OR] or risk factors aside from hypertension [OR] or use of cardiac medications
HFpEF: prior history of LVEF below 50%, acute decompensated HF, [OR] moderate [OR] or greater valvular disease, significant cardiac arrhythmias, [OR] pericardial disease, [OR] congenital heart disease, [OR] primary pulmonary hypertension
