l infarction confirmed by ECG, as well as troponin I [AND] and CK-MB levels.\nPresence of hemodynamically relevant stenosis of one artery (i.e., the infarct-related artery) confirmed by coronary angiography (CAG), [AND] with the occlusion of other arteries [NOT] not exceeding 30%.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nNA<|eot_id|>']
