Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nage =18 at screening\nnot intending to move away from the clinic\'s catchment area for the next 2 years\nHIV-1 antibody negative\nreports commercial sex work\ncontact information is provided\nwritten informed consent\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nHIV infection at screening\nparticipation in previous or concurrent HIV vaccine trials\nlactating, pregnant or planning pregnancy\nrenal function impairment (serum creatinine >1.5 mg/dl), Fanconi syndrome\nabnormal liver function tests (AST/ALT > 43 U/L), liver disease, viral hepatitis, hepatitis B virus (HBV) infection\nserum phosphorus <2.2mg/dl, osteoporosis\nknown sensitivity to components of the Truvada® formulation\nany immunosuppressive treatment, such as systemic corticosteroids\nassumption of medication that interacts with Truvada®\nhigh likelihood of poor adherence to PREP and clinic attendance\nany condition that in the opinion of the attending physician could endanger the health of the participant or render her unsuitable to participate in the trial\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nage =18 at screening\n [NOT] not intending to move away from the clinic\'s catchment area for the next 2 years\nHIV-1 antibody [NOT] negative\nreports commercial sex work\ncontact information is provided\nwritten informed consent\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nHIV infection at screening\nparticipation in previous [OR] or concurrent HIV vaccine trials\nlactating, [OR] pregnant [OR] or planning pregnancy\nrenal function impairment (serum creatinine >1.5 mg/dl), Fanconi syndrome\nabnormal liver function tests (AST/ [OR] ALT > 43 U/L), liver disease, [OR] viral hepatitis, [OR] hepatitis B virus (HBV) infection\nserum phosphorus <2.2mg/dl, [OR] osteoporosis\nknown sensitivity to components of the Truvada® formulation\nany immunosuppressive treatment, such as systemic corticosteroids\nassumption of medication that interacts with Truvada®\nhigh likelihood of poor adherence to PREP [AND] and clinic attendance\nany condition that in the opinion of the attending physician could endanger the health of the participant [OR] or render her unsuitable to participate in the trial<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
age =18 at screening
 [NOT] not intending to move away from the clinic's catchment area for the next 2 years
HIV-1 antibody [NOT] negative
reports commercial sex work
contact information is provided
written informed consent

Exclusion Criteria:
HIV infection at screening
participation in previous [OR] or concurrent HIV vaccine trials
lactating, [OR] pregnant [OR] or planning pregnancy
renal function impairment (serum creatinine >1.5 mg/dl), Fanconi syndrome
abnormal liver function tests (AST/ [OR] ALT > 43 U/L), liver disease, [OR] viral hepatitis, [OR] hepatitis B virus (HBV) infection
serum phosphorus <2.2mg/dl, [OR] osteoporosis
known sensitivity to components of the Truvada® formulation
any immunosuppressive treatment, such as systemic corticosteroids
assumption of medication that interacts with Truvada®
high likelihood of poor adherence to PREP [AND] and clinic attendance
any condition that in the opinion of the attending physician could endanger the health of the participant [OR] or render her unsuitable to participate in the trial
