Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients with de novo stenotic lesions who are suitable for coronary stenting with drug-eluting stent\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n1. High risk profiles for ischemic adverse events such as A. ST-segment elevation myocardial infarction (STEMI) B. Patients with cardiogenic shock or concomitant severe decompensated heart failure C. Myocardial infarction or stent thrombosis in spite of the maintenance of antiplatelet therapy D. Restenosis in stented segments or previous sites of balloon angioplasty 2. Patients who cannot follow allocated DAPT schedule due to the planned surgery or elective procedure within 3 months after the stenting 3. Recent history of major surgery or evident events of gastrointestinal bleeding within 1 month from the procedure 4. Patients on anticoagulation therapy with warfarin or other anticoagulants 5. Life expectancy less than 1 year (such as malignancies or other chronic systemic diseases) 6. Pregnant women 7. Past history of allergy or other contraindications for the following medications/materials: aspirin, clopidogrel, heparin, cobalt chromium, sirolimus\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients with de novo stenotic lesions [AND] who are suitable for coronary stenting [AND] with drug-eluting stent\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n1. High risk profiles for ischemic adverse events such as A. ST-segment elevation myocardial infarction (STEMI) B. Patients with cardiogenic shock [OR] or concomitant severe decompensated heart failure C. Myocardial infarction [OR] or stent thrombosis in spite of the maintenance of antiplatelet therapy D. Restenosis in stented segments [OR] or previous sites of balloon angioplasty 2. Patients who [NOT] cannot follow allocated DAPT schedule due to the planned surgery [OR] or elective procedure within 3 months after the stenting 3. Recent history of major surgery [OR] or evident events of gastrointestinal bleeding within 1 month from the procedure 4. Patients on anticoagulation therapy [AND] with warfarin [OR] or other anticoagulants 5. Life expectancy less than 1 year (such as malignancies [OR] or other chronic systemic diseases) 6. Pregnant women 7. Past history of allergy [OR] or other contraindications for the following medications/ [OR] materials: aspirin, [OR] clopidogrel, [OR] heparin, [OR] cobalt chromium, [OR] sirolimus<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Patients with de novo stenotic lesions [AND] who are suitable for coronary stenting [AND] with drug-eluting stent

Exclusion Criteria:
1. High risk profiles for ischemic adverse events such as A. ST-segment elevation myocardial infarction (STEMI) B. Patients with cardiogenic shock [OR] or concomitant severe decompensated heart failure C. Myocardial infarction [OR] or stent thrombosis in spite of the maintenance of antiplatelet therapy D. Restenosis in stented segments [OR] or previous sites of balloon angioplasty 2. Patients who [NOT] cannot follow allocated DAPT schedule due to the planned surgery [OR] or elective procedure within 3 months after the stenting 3. Recent history of major surgery [OR] or evident events of gastrointestinal bleeding within 1 month from the procedure 4. Patients on anticoagulation therapy [AND] with warfarin [OR] or other anticoagulants 5. Life expectancy less than 1 year (such as malignancies [OR] or other chronic systemic diseases) 6. Pregnant women 7. Past history of allergy [OR] or other contraindications for the following medications/ [OR] materials: aspirin, [OR] clopidogrel, [OR] heparin, [OR] cobalt chromium, [OR] sirolimus
