Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients aged 19 or older\nPatients who have submitted a written consent to participate in the clinical trial\nDe novo lesion\nPatients scheduled for elective intervention to treat ischemic cardiovascular disease\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPatients with any contraindications or hypersensitivity related to antiplatelet therapy\nPatients with Acute Myocardial Infarction (ST elevation myocardial infarction, Non ST elevation myocardial infarction)\nPatients who are anticipated to receive treatment or surgery that may require desisting the administration of antiplatelet therapy for 2 weeks or longer during the period of the clinical trial\nChronic total occlusion (CTO) lesions, in-stent restenosis (ISR)\nPatients experiencing cardiogenic shock\nWomen who are breastfeeding, pregnant, or desiring pregnancy\nPatients with findings of hemorrhage\nPatients with a life expectancy of less than 1 year\nPatients who have received a drug-eluting stent (DES) procedure within the past 6 months\nAny other patients judged by the investigator to be unsuitable for the trial\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients aged 19 or older\nPatients who have submitted a written consent to participate in the clinical trial\nDe novo lesion\nPatients scheduled for elective intervention to treat ischemic cardiovascular disease\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPatients with any contraindications [OR] or hypersensitivity related to antiplatelet therapy\nPatients with Acute Myocardial Infarction (ST elevation myocardial infarction, [OR] Non ST elevation myocardial infarction)\nPatients who are anticipated to receive treatment [OR] or surgery that may require desisting the administration of antiplatelet therapy for 2 weeks or longer during the period of the clinical trial\nChronic total occlusion (CTO) lesions, [OR] in-stent restenosis (ISR)\nPatients experiencing cardiogenic shock\nWomen [AND] who are breastfeeding, [OR] pregnant, [OR] or desiring pregnancy\nPatients with findings of hemorrhage\nPatients with a life expectancy of less than 1 year\nPatients who have received a drug-eluting stent (DES) procedure within the past 6 months\nAny other patients judged by the investigator to be unsuitable for the trial<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Patients aged 19 or older
Patients who have submitted a written consent to participate in the clinical trial
De novo lesion
Patients scheduled for elective intervention to treat ischemic cardiovascular disease

Exclusion Criteria:
Patients with any contraindications [OR] or hypersensitivity related to antiplatelet therapy
Patients with Acute Myocardial Infarction (ST elevation myocardial infarction, [OR] Non ST elevation myocardial infarction)
Patients who are anticipated to receive treatment [OR] or surgery that may require desisting the administration of antiplatelet therapy for 2 weeks or longer during the period of the clinical trial
Chronic total occlusion (CTO) lesions, [OR] in-stent restenosis (ISR)
Patients experiencing cardiogenic shock
Women [AND] who are breastfeeding, [OR] pregnant, [OR] or desiring pregnancy
Patients with findings of hemorrhage
Patients with a life expectancy of less than 1 year
Patients who have received a drug-eluting stent (DES) procedure within the past 6 months
Any other patients judged by the investigator to be unsuitable for the trial
