of the formulation).\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nFemale subjects aged =/> 18 years [AND] and of reproductive age.\nCapacity to give consent for study participation, after being adequately informed of the aims, benefits, risks, time and motion of the study.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nParticipation in another clinical trial.\nKnown [OR] or suspected (or history of) malignancy [OR] or chronic illness.\n Serious organic [OR] or mental disease diagnosed by a psychiatrist (e.g., major depression currently treated with antidepressant medication) suspected on the basis of the medical history [OR] and/or clinical examination.\nConditions that may affect the compliance to the study.\n Contraindications to therapy with the study drug [OR] or hypersensitivity to the study drug (active ingredient [OR] or excipients of the formulation).<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Female subjects aged =/> 18 years [AND] and of reproductive age.
Capacity to give consent for study participation, after being adequately informed of the aims, benefits, risks, time and motion of the study.

Exclusion Criteria:
Participation in another clinical trial.
Known [OR] or suspected (or history of) malignancy [OR] or chronic illness.
 Serious organic [OR] or mental disease diagnosed by a psychiatrist (e.g., major depression currently treated with antidepressant medication) suspected on the basis of the medical history [OR] and/or clinical examination.
Conditions that may affect the compliance to the study.
 Contraindications to therapy with the study drug [OR] or hypersensitivity to the study drug (active ingredient [OR] or excipients of the formulation).
