File: NCT02630628 

Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_full/NCT02630628.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nBiopsy-proven LN Class III/IV±V (ISN/RPS 2003), with biopsy performed within 12 weeks of randomization.\nPositive anti-dsDNA.\nActive LN with proteinuria (urine protein/creatinine ratio >1.0 or 24-hr urine protein >1.0 g at baseline), with or without hematuria.\nBoth \'incident\' (i.e. new) patients and \'flare\' patients can be included.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nRenal disease unrelated to SLE (e.g. diabetes mellitus, other glomerular or tubulointerstitial disease, renovascular disease), or transplanted kidney.\nEstimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR by MDRD) =20 mL/min per 1.73 m2 or serum creatinine >300 micromol/L (3.39 mg/dL) at screening.\nRenal biopsy showing cellular or fibrocellular crescent in more than 25% of glomeruli.\nCNS or other severe organ manifestation of lupus that necessitate aggressive immunosuppressive therapy on its own.\nCo-morbidities that require corticosteroid therapy (e.g. asthma, inflammatory bowel disease).\nTreatment with prednisolone (or prednisone, or equivalent) at >20 mg/D for over 4 weeks within the past 3 months.\nTreatment with MMF at >1.5 g/D for over 4 weeks within the past 3 months.\nKnown hypersensitivity or intolerability to prednisolone (or prednisone, or equivalent), TAC, or MMF at a dose of 1.25 g or below per day.\nSubjects who are already on treatment with TAC, cyclosporine or any other calcineurin inhibitor for over 4 weeks within the past 12 months.\nTreatment with cyclophosphamide, leflunomide, or methotrexate for over 2 weeks, or use of biological agent(s) regardless of duration, within the past 6 months (Note: prior use of azathioprine, mizoribine, intravenous immunoglobulins and anti-malarials is allowed).\nUncontrolled hypertension with systolic BP >160 mmHg or diastolic BP >95 mmHg.\nWomen who are pregnant or breastfeeding.\nWomen with childbearing potential or their male partners, who refuse to use an effective birth control method\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nBiopsy-proven LN Class III/IV±V (ISN/RPS 2003), [AND] with biopsy performed within 12 weeks of randomization.\nPositive anti-dsDNA.\nActive LN [AND] with proteinuria (urine protein/creatinine ratio >1.0 [OR] or 24-hr urine protein >1.0 g at baseline), [AND] with or without hematuria.\nBoth \'incident\' (i.e. new) patients [OR] and \'flare\' patients can be included.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nRenal disease unrelated to SLE (e.g. diabetes mellitus, other glomerular [OR] or tubulointerstitial disease, [OR] renovascular disease), [OR] or transplanted kidney.\nEstimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR by MDRD) =20 mL/min per 1.73 m2 [OR] or serum creatinine >300 micromol/L (3.39 mg/dL) at screening.\nRenal biopsy showing cellular [OR] or fibrocellular crescent in more than 25% of glomeruli.\nCNS [OR] or other severe organ manifestation of lupus that necessitate aggressive immunosuppressive therapy on its own.\nCo-morbidities that require corticosteroid therapy (e.g. asthma, [OR] inflammatory bowel disease).\nTreatment with prednisolone [OR] (or prednisone, [OR] or equivalent) at >20 mg/D for over 4 weeks within the past 3 months.\nTreatment with MMF at >1.5 g/D for over 4 weeks within the past 3 months.\n Known hypersensitivity [OR] or intolerability to prednisolone [OR] (or prednisone, [OR] or equivalent), TAC, [OR] or MMF at a dose of 1.25 g or below per day.\nSubjects who are already on treatment with TAC, [OR] cyclosporine [OR] or any other calcineurin inhibitor for over 4 weeks within the past 12 months.\n Treatment with cyclophosphamide, [OR] leflunomide, [OR] or methotrexate for over 2 weeks, [OR] or use of biological agent(s) regardless of duration, within the past 6 months (Note: prior use of azathioprine, [OR] mizoribine, [OR] intravenous immunoglobulins [OR] and anti-malarials is allowed).\nUncontrolled hypertension [AND] with systolic BP >160 mmHg [OR] or diastolic BP >95 mmHg.\nWomen [AND] who are pregnant [OR] or breastfeeding.\nWomen [AND] with childbearing potential [OR] or their male partners, [AND] who refuse to use an effective birth control method<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Biopsy-proven LN Class III/IV±V (ISN/RPS 2003), [AND] with biopsy performed within 12 weeks of randomization.
Positive anti-dsDNA.
Active LN [AND] with proteinuria (urine protein/creatinine ratio >1.0 [OR] or 24-hr urine protein >1.0 g at baseline), [AND] with or without hematuria.
Both 'incident' (i.e. new) patients [OR] and 'flare' patients can be included.

Exclusion Criteria:
Renal disease unrelated to SLE (e.g. diabetes mellitus, other glomerular [OR] or tubulointerstitial disease, [OR] renovascular disease), [OR] or transplanted kidney.
Estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR by MDRD) =20 mL/min per 1.73 m2 [OR] or serum creatinine >300 micromol/L (3.39 mg/dL) at screening.
Renal biopsy showing cellular [OR] or fibrocellular crescent in more than 25% of glomeruli.
CNS [OR] or other severe organ manifestation of lupus that necessitate aggressive immunosuppressive therapy on its own.
Co-morbidities that require corticosteroid therapy (e.g. asthma, [OR] inflammatory bowel disease).
Treatment with prednisolone [OR] (or prednisone, [OR] or equivalent) at >20 mg/D for over 4 weeks within the past 3 months.
Treatment with MMF at >1.5 g/D for over 4 weeks within the past 3 months.
 Known hypersensitivity [OR] or intolerability to prednisolone [OR] (or prednisone, [OR] or equivalent), TAC, [OR] or MMF at a dose of 1.25 g or below per day.
Subjects who are already on treatment with TAC, [OR] cyclosporine [OR] or any other calcineurin inhibitor for over 4 weeks within the past 12 months.
 Treatment with cyclophosphamide, [OR] leflunomide, [OR] or methotrexate for over 2 weeks, [OR] or use of biological agent(s) regardless of duration, within the past 6 months (Note: prior use of azathioprine, [OR] mizoribine, [OR] intravenous immunoglobulins [OR] and anti-malarials is allowed).
Uncontrolled hypertension [AND] with systolic BP >160 mmHg [OR] or diastolic BP >95 mmHg.
Women [AND] who are pregnant [OR] or breastfeeding.
Women [AND] with childbearing potential [OR] or their male partners, [AND] who refuse to use an effective birth control method
