Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients with anaemia (males Hb <130 g/L, females <120 g/L) undergoing elective cardiac surgery, and available to receive trial drug 1- 10 weeks prior to surgery\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPregnancy\nKnown hypersensitivity to study drug (ferric carboxymaltose or equivalent) or its excipients\nKnown or suspected haemoglobinopathy/thalassaemia\nBone marrow disease\nHaemochromatosis\nRenal dialysis\nErythropoietin or IV iron in the previous 4 weeks\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients with anaemia (males Hb <130 g/L, females <120 g/L) undergoing elective cardiac surgery, [AND] and available to receive trial drug 1- 10 weeks prior to surgery\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPregnancy\nKnown hypersensitivity to study drug (ferric carboxymaltose [OR] or equivalent) or its excipients\n Known [OR] or suspected haemoglobinopathy/ [OR] thalassaemia\nBone marrow disease\nHaemochromatosis\n Renal dialysis\n Erythropoietin [OR] or IV iron in the previous 4 weeks<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Patients with anaemia (males Hb <130 g/L, females <120 g/L) undergoing elective cardiac surgery, [AND] and available to receive trial drug 1- 10 weeks prior to surgery

Exclusion Criteria:
Pregnancy
Known hypersensitivity to study drug (ferric carboxymaltose [OR] or equivalent) or its excipients
 Known [OR] or suspected haemoglobinopathy/ [OR] thalassaemia
Bone marrow disease
Haemochromatosis
 Renal dialysis
 Erythropoietin [OR] or IV iron in the previous 4 weeks
