tem, which lower the seizure threshold such as antipsychotic drugs (chlorpromazine, [OR] clozapine) [OR] or tricyclic antidepressants.\nPregnant females, [OR] and\nOngoing cord compression [OR] or a syrinx in the spinal cord [OR] or who suffer from a spinal cord disease such as spinal stenosis, [OR] spina bifida [OR] or herniated cervical disk.\nUncontrolled medical problems including pulmonary, [OR] cardiovascular [OR] or orthopedic disease,\nAny debilitating disease that causes exercise intolerance\nPremorbid, ongoing major depression [OR] or psychosis, [OR] altered cognitive status\nHistory of head injury [OR] or stroke,\n Metal plate in skull\nHistory of seizures\nReceiving drugs acting primarily on the central nervous system, which lower the seizure threshold such as antipsychotic drugs (chlorpromazine, [OR] clozapine) [OR] or tricyclic antidepressants.\nPregnant females, [OR] and\nOngoing cord compression [OR] or a syrinx in the spinal cord [OR] or who suffer from a spinal cord disease such as spinal stenosis, [OR] spina bifida [OR] or herniated cervical disk.<|eot_id|>']
