erfere with MRI\nsuccinic semialdehyde dehydrogenase deficiency\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\ncurrent diagnosis of narcolepsy [AND] with cataplexy [OR] OR healthy control\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nuse of any sedative hypnotics, [OR] tranquilizers, [OR] anticonvulsants, [OR] antihistamines (except [NOT] non-sedating), [OR] benzodiazepines, [OR] clonidine [OR] or any medication known to affect dopamine at start of baseline period\nsignificant unstable [OR] or uncontrolled medical/ [OR] psychiatric disease\nsignificant history of head trauma/ [OR] surgery [OR] or seizure disorder\nradiation exposure exceeding 20mSv in last 12 months\npregnancy\nsubstance abuse/ [OR] dependence (including alcohol)\nhave sleep apnea, [OR] or are shift workers\non a sodium-restricted diet\nhas ever taken Xyrem [OR] / sodium oxybate [OR] / GHB at any time\nclaustrophobia\nmetal implants [OR] / objects in the body that may interfere with MRI\nsuccinic semialdehyde dehydrogenase deficiency<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
current diagnosis of narcolepsy [AND] with cataplexy [OR] OR healthy control

Exclusion Criteria:
use of any sedative hypnotics, [OR] tranquilizers, [OR] anticonvulsants, [OR] antihistamines (except [NOT] non-sedating), [OR] benzodiazepines, [OR] clonidine [OR] or any medication known to affect dopamine at start of baseline period
significant unstable [OR] or uncontrolled medical/ [OR] psychiatric disease
significant history of head trauma/ [OR] surgery [OR] or seizure disorder
radiation exposure exceeding 20mSv in last 12 months
pregnancy
substance abuse/ [OR] dependence (including alcohol)
have sleep apnea, [OR] or are shift workers
on a sodium-restricted diet
has ever taken Xyrem [OR] / sodium oxybate [OR] / GHB at any time
claustrophobia
metal implants [OR] / objects in the body that may interfere with MRI
succinic semialdehyde dehydrogenase deficiency
