Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nFemale \nAge ≥18 years \nPatients with a lesion > 0.5 cm in largest diameter size, initially scored BI-RADS® 3, 4a, 4b or 4c in B-mode ultrasound \nInformed consent about histological examination (core cut biopsy (CCB), vacuum-assisted biopsy (VAB), fine needle aspiration (FNA) or surgery) has already been given in the course of clinical routine \nSigned informed consent of study participation \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPregnant or lactating women \nWomen with breast implants on the same side as the lesion \nWomen that underwent local radiation or chemotherapy within the last 12 months \nWomen with history of breast cancer or breast surgery in the same quadrant \nLesions in or close to scar tissue (< 1cm) \nSkin lesions or lesions that have been biopsied previously \nLesion larger than 4 cm in the longest dimension \nNo lesion should be included when more than 50% of the lesion is further down than 4 cm beneath the skin level.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nFemale \nAge ≥18 years \nPatients with a lesion > 0.5 cm in largest diameter size, initially scored BI-RADS® 3, 4a, 4b [OR] or 4c in B-mode ultrasound \nInformed consent about histological examination (core cut biopsy (CCB), vacuum-assisted biopsy (VAB), fine needle aspiration (FNA) [OR] or surgery) has already been given in the course of clinical routine \nSigned informed consent of study participation \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPregnant [OR] or lactating women \nWomen [AND] with breast implants on the same side as the lesion \nWomen [AND] that underwent local radiation [OR] or chemotherapy within the last 12 months \nWomen [AND] with history of breast cancer [OR] or breast surgery in the same quadrant \nLesions in [OR] or close to scar tissue (< 1cm) \nSkin lesions [OR] or lesions that have been biopsied previously \nLesion larger than 4 cm in the longest dimension \n [NOT] No lesion should be included when more than 50% of the lesion is further down than 4 cm beneath the skin level.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Female 
Age ≥18 years 
Patients with a lesion > 0.5 cm in largest diameter size, initially scored BI-RADS® 3, 4a, 4b [OR] or 4c in B-mode ultrasound 
Informed consent about histological examination (core cut biopsy (CCB), vacuum-assisted biopsy (VAB), fine needle aspiration (FNA) [OR] or surgery) has already been given in the course of clinical routine 
Signed informed consent of study participation 

Exclusion Criteria:
Pregnant [OR] or lactating women 
Women [AND] with breast implants on the same side as the lesion 
Women [AND] that underwent local radiation [OR] or chemotherapy within the last 12 months 
Women [AND] with history of breast cancer [OR] or breast surgery in the same quadrant 
Lesions in [OR] or close to scar tissue (< 1cm) 
Skin lesions [OR] or lesions that have been biopsied previously 
Lesion larger than 4 cm in the longest dimension 
 [NOT] No lesion should be included when more than 50% of the lesion is further down than 4 cm beneath the skin level.
