File: NCT02644629 

Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_full/NCT02644629.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAge 18-65\nDiagnosis of MDD (Major Depressive Disorder), made or affirmed by a senior psychiatrist in Shalvata\nMADRS score > 20\nTreated with conventional anti-depressant, administered within a formal psychiatric clinic or by a certified psychiatrist.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nActive or past psychotic disorder, including a history of psychotic affective state\nMental Retardation or Autistic Spectrum Disorder\nProminent personality disorder\nCardiac or neurologic active medical condition, including past CVA/TIA (Cardiovascular Accident/Transient Ischemic Attack) or any other unstable medical condition.\nChronic nasal congestion\nActive or recent drug or alcohol abuse\nSubstantial suicidality in a patient requiring admission but refuses to do so, and signs an "against medical advice" release form as part of clinical evaluation, and does not answer the terms for involuntary admission.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAge 18-65\nDiagnosis of MDD (Major Depressive Disorder), made or affirmed by a senior psychiatrist in Shalvata\nMADRS score > 20\nTreated with conventional anti-depressant, administered within a formal psychiatric clinic [OR] or by a certified psychiatrist.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nActive [OR] or past psychotic disorder, including a history of psychotic affective state\nMental Retardation [OR] or Autistic Spectrum Disorder\nProminent personality disorder\nCardiac [OR] or neurologic active medical condition, including past CVA/ [OR] TIA (Cardiovascular Accident/ [OR] Transient Ischemic Attack) or any other unstable medical condition.\nChronic nasal congestion\nActive [OR] or recent drug [OR] or alcohol abuse\nSubstantial suicidality in a patient requiring admission [AND] but refuses to do so, and signs an "against medical advice" release form as part of clinical evaluation, [AND] and does [NOT] not answer the terms for involuntary admission.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Age 18-65
Diagnosis of MDD (Major Depressive Disorder), made or affirmed by a senior psychiatrist in Shalvata
MADRS score > 20
Treated with conventional anti-depressant, administered within a formal psychiatric clinic [OR] or by a certified psychiatrist.

Exclusion Criteria:
Active [OR] or past psychotic disorder, including a history of psychotic affective state
Mental Retardation [OR] or Autistic Spectrum Disorder
Prominent personality disorder
Cardiac [OR] or neurologic active medical condition, including past CVA/ [OR] TIA (Cardiovascular Accident/ [OR] Transient Ischemic Attack) or any other unstable medical condition.
Chronic nasal congestion
Active [OR] or recent drug [OR] or alcohol abuse
Substantial suicidality in a patient requiring admission [AND] but refuses to do so, and signs an "against medical advice" release form as part of clinical evaluation, [AND] and does [NOT] not answer the terms for involuntary admission.
