Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients undergoing ambulatory hand surgery for carpal tunnel and trigger finger, under local anesthesia with or without sedation.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nASA> 3;\nCoagulopathy;\nRenal disease,\nLiver disease,\nHistory of recent gastro-intestinal bleeding\nPregnancy.\nDiagnosis of chronic pain currently taking opioid pain medication or with a history of drug abuse.\nPatients with a self-described allergy to ASA, acetaminophen, NSAIDS and codeine.\nAll patients receiving a brachial plexus block for anesthesia and/or analgesia\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients undergoing ambulatory hand surgery for carpal tunnel [OR] and trigger finger, under local anesthesia [AND] with or without sedation.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nASA> 3;\nCoagulopathy;\n Renal disease,\n Liver disease,\n History of recent gastro-intestinal bleeding\nPregnancy.\nDiagnosis of chronic pain currently taking opioid pain medication [OR] or with a history of drug abuse.\nPatients with a self-described allergy to ASA, [OR] acetaminophen, [OR] NSAIDS [OR] and codeine.\nAll patients receiving a brachial plexus block for anesthesia [OR] and/or analgesia<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Patients undergoing ambulatory hand surgery for carpal tunnel [OR] and trigger finger, under local anesthesia [AND] with or without sedation.

Exclusion Criteria:
ASA> 3;
Coagulopathy;
 Renal disease,
 Liver disease,
 History of recent gastro-intestinal bleeding
Pregnancy.
Diagnosis of chronic pain currently taking opioid pain medication [OR] or with a history of drug abuse.
Patients with a self-described allergy to ASA, [OR] acetaminophen, [OR] NSAIDS [OR] and codeine.
All patients receiving a brachial plexus block for anesthesia [OR] and/or analgesia
