File: NCT02652572 

Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_full/NCT02652572.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\n1. Age 18 years or older \n2. Diagnosis of venous leg ulcer(s), as clinically determined by the investigator by a positive venous reflux test (venous refilling <20 seconds) using Doppler ultrasound for at least 4 weeks prior to screening day, which have not adequately responded to conventional ulcer therapy. \n3. Designated venous leg ulcer meets the following criteria at both the screening and baseline visits. If the patient has multiple ulcers, at least one ulcer must meet the following criteria at both the screening and baseline visits: \n1. Present for at least 4 weeks \n2. CEAP Classification Stage 6 \n3. Surface ulcer with an area > 15cm2 post debridement \n4. Viable, granulating wound (investigator discretion) \n4. Ulcers that extend through the epidermis but not through the muscle, tendon, or bone (Stage II or III ulcers as defined by the IAET). \n5. Female patients of childbearing potential must have a negative pregnancy test at screening and must agree to use hormonal contraceptive, intrauterine device, diaphragm with spermicide, condom with spermicide, or abstinence throughout until 2 weeks after the last administration of study drug \n6. Signed informed consent \n\nExclusion Criteria:\n1. Decrease in size of the designated target ulcer(s) by ≥ 30% during the 7-day screening period \n2. Cannot tolerate or comply with compression therapy. \n3. An ulcer which shows signs of severe clinical infection, defined as pus oozing from the ulcer site \n4. An ulcer positive for β-hemolytic streptococci upon culture \n5. The ulcer has > 50% slough, significant necrotic tissue, bone, tendon, or capsule exposure or avascular ulcer beds \n6. Is highly exuding (i.e. requires daily change of dressing) \n7. Ankle brachial pressure index <0.65 \n8. Patients with active systemic infections \n9. Patients with clinically significant medical conditions as determined by the investigator including renal, hepatic, hematologic, neurologic or immune disease. Examples include but are not limited to: \n1. Renal insufficiency as an estimated GFR which is < 30 mL/min/1.7m2 \n2. Abnormal blood biochemistry defined as 3 times that of the upper limit of the normal range. \n3. Hepatic insufficiency defined as total bilirubin > 2 mg/dL or serum albumin < 25 g/L \n4. HbA1c > 9% \n5. Hemoglobin < 10 g/dL \n6. Hematocrit < 0.30 \n7. Platelet count < 100,000 \n10. Presence of an active systemic or local cancer or tumor of any kind (with the exception of non-melanoma skin cancer) \n11. Patients with severe rheumatoid arthritis (with more than 20 persistently inflamed joints, or below lower normal limit blood albumin level, or evidence of bone and cartilage damage on x-ray, or inflammation in tissues other than joints) and other collagen vascular diseases. \n12. Patients with active connective tissue disease \n13. Treatment with systemic corticosteroids (>15 mg/day), or current immunosuppressive agents \n14. Previous or current radiation therapy or likelihood to receive this therapy during study participation \n15. Pregnant or nursing patients \n16. Known prior inability or unavailability to complete required study visits during study participation \n17. Significant peripheral edema as per investigator\'s discretion \n18. A psychiatric condition (e.g., suicidal ideation) or chronic alcohol or drug abuse problem, determined from the patient\'s medical history, which, in the opinion of the investigator, may pose a threat to patient compliance \n19. Use of a platelet-derived growth factor within 28 days before screening \n20. Use of any investigational drug or therapy within 28 days before screening \n21. Has any other factor which may, in the opinion of the investigator, compromise participation and/or follow-up in the study       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n1. Age 18 years or older \n2. Diagnosis of venous leg ulcer(s), as clinically determined by the investigator by a positive venous reflux test (venous refilling <20 seconds) using Doppler ultrasound for at least 4 weeks prior to screening day, which have [NOT] not adequately responded to conventional ulcer therapy. \n3. Designated venous leg ulcer meets the following criteria at both the screening [AND] and baseline visits. If the patient has multiple ulcers, at least one ulcer must meet the following criteria at both the screening [AND] and baseline visits: \n1. Present for at least 4 weeks \n2. CEAP Classification Stage 6 \n3. Surface ulcer [AND] with an area > 15cm2 post debridement \n4. Viable, granulating wound (investigator discretion) \n4. Ulcers that extend through the epidermis [AND] but [NOT] not through the muscle, [OR] tendon, [OR] or bone (Stage II [OR] or III ulcers as defined by the IAET). \n5. Female patients [AND] of childbearing potential must have a negative pregnancy test at screening [AND] and must agree to use hormonal contraceptive, [OR] intrauterine device, [OR] diaphragm [AND] with spermicide, condom [AND] with spermicide, [OR] or abstinence throughout until 2 weeks after the last administration of study drug \n6. Signed informed consent \n\nExclusion Criteria:\n1. Decrease in size of the designated target ulcer(s) by ≥ 30% during the 7-day screening period \n2. Cannot tolerate [OR] or comply with compression therapy. \n3. An ulcer which shows signs of severe clinical infection, defined as pus oozing from the ulcer site \n4. An ulcer positive for β-hemolytic streptococci upon culture \n5. The ulcer has > 50% slough, significant necrotic tissue, bone, [OR] tendon, [OR] or capsule exposure [OR] or avascular ulcer beds \n6. Is highly exuding (i.e. requires daily change of dressing) \n7. Ankle brachial pressure index <0.65 \n8. Patients with active systemic infections \n9. Patients with clinically significant medical conditions as determined by the investigator including renal, [OR] hepatic, [OR] hematologic, [OR] neurologic [OR] or immune disease. Examples include but are not limited to: \n1. Renal insufficiency as an estimated GFR which is < 30 mL/min/1.7 m2 \n2. Abnormal blood biochemistry defined as 3 times that of the upper limit of the normal range. \n3. Hepatic insufficiency defined as total bilirubin > 2 mg/dL [OR] or serum albumin < 25 g/L \n4. HbA1c > 9% \n5. Hemoglobin < 10 g/dL \n6. Hematocrit < 0.30 \n7. Platelet count < 100,000 \n10. Presence of an active systemic [OR] or local cancer [OR] or tumor of any kind (with the exception of [NOT] non-melanoma skin cancer) \n11. Patients with severe rheumatoid arthritis (with more than 20 persistently inflamed joints, [OR] or below lower normal limit blood albumin level, [OR] or evidence of bone [OR] and cartilage damage on x-ray, [OR] or inflammation in tissues other than joints) [AND] and other collagen vascular diseases. \n12. Patients with active connective tissue disease \n13. Treatment with systemic corticosteroids (>15 mg/day), [OR] or current immunosuppressive agents \n14. Previous [OR] or current radiation therapy [OR] or likelihood to receive this therapy during study participation \n15. Pregnant [OR] or nursing patients \n16. Known prior [NOT] inability [OR] or [NOT] unavailability to complete required study visits during study participation \n17. Significant peripheral edema as per investigator\'s discretion \n18. A psychiatric condition (e.g., suicidal ideation) [OR] or chronic alcohol [OR] or drug abuse problem, determined from the patient\'s medical history, which, in the opinion of the investigator, may pose a threat to patient compliance \n19. Use of a platelet-derived growth factor within 28 days before screening \n20. Use of any investigational drug [OR] or therapy within 28 days before screening \n21. Has any other factor which may, in the opinion of the investigator, compromise participation [OR] and/or follow-up in the study<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
1. Age 18 years or older 
2. Diagnosis of venous leg ulcer(s), as clinically determined by the investigator by a positive venous reflux test (venous refilling <20 seconds) using Doppler ultrasound for at least 4 weeks prior to screening day, which have [NOT] not adequately responded to conventional ulcer therapy. 
3. Designated venous leg ulcer meets the following criteria at both the screening [AND] and baseline visits. If the patient has multiple ulcers, at least one ulcer must meet the following criteria at both the screening [AND] and baseline visits: 
1. Present for at least 4 weeks 
2. CEAP Classification Stage 6 
3. Surface ulcer [AND] with an area > 15cm2 post debridement 
4. Viable, granulating wound (investigator discretion) 
4. Ulcers that extend through the epidermis [AND] but [NOT] not through the muscle, [OR] tendon, [OR] or bone (Stage II [OR] or III ulcers as defined by the IAET). 
5. Female patients [AND] of childbearing potential must have a negative pregnancy test at screening [AND] and must agree to use hormonal contraceptive, [OR] intrauterine device, [OR] diaphragm [AND] with spermicide, condom [AND] with spermicide, [OR] or abstinence throughout until 2 weeks after the last administration of study drug 
6. Signed informed consent 

Exclusion Criteria:
1. Decrease in size of the designated target ulcer(s) by ≥ 30% during the 7-day screening period 
2. Cannot tolerate [OR] or comply with compression therapy. 
3. An ulcer which shows signs of severe clinical infection, defined as pus oozing from the ulcer site 
4. An ulcer positive for β-hemolytic streptococci upon culture 
5. The ulcer has > 50% slough, significant necrotic tissue, bone, [OR] tendon, [OR] or capsule exposure [OR] or avascular ulcer beds 
6. Is highly exuding (i.e. requires daily change of dressing) 
7. Ankle brachial pressure index <0.65 
8. Patients with active systemic infections 
9. Patients with clinically significant medical conditions as determined by the investigator including renal, [OR] hepatic, [OR] hematologic, [OR] neurologic [OR] or immune disease. Examples include but are not limited to: 
1. Renal insufficiency as an estimated GFR which is < 30 mL/min/1.7 m2 
2. Abnormal blood biochemistry defined as 3 times that of the upper limit of the normal range. 
3. Hepatic insufficiency defined as total bilirubin > 2 mg/dL [OR] or serum albumin < 25 g/L 
4. HbA1c > 9% 
5. Hemoglobin < 10 g/dL 
6. Hematocrit < 0.30 
7. Platelet count < 100,000 
10. Presence of an active systemic [OR] or local cancer [OR] or tumor of any kind (with the exception of [NOT] non-melanoma skin cancer) 
11. Patients with severe rheumatoid arthritis (with more than 20 persistently inflamed joints, [OR] or below lower normal limit blood albumin level, [OR] or evidence of bone [OR] and cartilage damage on x-ray, [OR] or inflammation in tissues other than joints) [AND] and other collagen vascular diseases. 
12. Patients with active connective tissue disease 
13. Treatment with systemic corticosteroids (>15 mg/day), [OR] or current immunosuppressive agents 
14. Previous [OR] or current radiation therapy [OR] or likelihood to receive this therapy during study participation 
15. Pregnant [OR] or nursing patients 
16. Known prior [NOT] inability [OR] or [NOT] unavailability to complete required study visits during study participation 
17. Significant peripheral edema as per investigator's discretion 
18. A psychiatric condition (e.g., suicidal ideation) [OR] or chronic alcohol [OR] or drug abuse problem, determined from the patient's medical history, which, in the opinion of the investigator, may pose a threat to patient compliance 
19. Use of a platelet-derived growth factor within 28 days before screening 
20. Use of any investigational drug [OR] or therapy within 28 days before screening 
21. Has any other factor which may, in the opinion of the investigator, compromise participation [OR] and/or follow-up in the study
