File: NCT02668016 

Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_full/NCT02668016.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAged 18 years or older\nPreviously taken one or more statins\nWithdrawn from statins because of perceived side effects\nDeveloped side effects within 2 weeks of initiation\nClinical indication for statins for primary or secondary prevention of cardiovascular disease or dyslipidaemia, on either no medication or non-statin lipid lowering therapy (e.g, ezetimibe)\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nHistory of neuropathy\nRegularly taking prescribed analgesia\nHistory of a chronic pain condition\nHistory of severe mental illness (as their experience of symptoms may already be altered)\nCurrent use of fibrates (because of the risk of interaction with statins but will not exclude participants taking ezetimibe).\nSevere previous reaction or reaction considered immunological, such as anaphylaxis, facial swelling, severe rash, muscle ache with rise in serum creatine kinase, inflammatory myopathy, rhabdomyolysis or liver function abnormalities (aspartate transaminase (AST) or alanine transaminase (ALT) greater than 3 times upper limit or normal).\nSide-effects taking longer than 2 weeks to develop (because in such participants much longer blocks of treatment would be required, if the present study is positive such studies will be planned for the future)*.\nHistory of statin intolerance with drug interaction to antiretroviral drugs.\nHistory of statin intolerance to any other drug.\nPregnant or breast feeding.\nSide effects taking longer than 2 weeks to present.\nIn clinical judgement of study doctor, participant should not participate.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAged 18 years or older\nPreviously taken one or more statins\n Withdrawn from statins because of perceived side effects\nDeveloped side effects within 2 weeks of initiation\nClinical indication for statins for primary [OR] or secondary prevention of cardiovascular disease [OR] or dyslipidaemia, on either [NOT] no medication [OR] or [NOT] non-statin lipid lowering therapy (e.g, ezetimibe)\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nHistory of neuropathy\nRegularly taking prescribed analgesia\n History of a chronic pain condition\n History of severe mental illness (as their experience of symptoms may already be altered)\nCurrent use of fibrates (because of the risk of interaction with statins [NOT] but will [NOT] not exclude participants taking ezetimibe).\nSevere previous reaction [OR] or reaction considered immunological, such as anaphylaxis, [OR] facial swelling, severe rash, [OR] muscle ache [AND] with rise in serum creatine kinase, inflammatory myopathy, [OR] rhabdomyolysis [OR] or liver function abnormalities (aspartate transaminase (AST) [OR] or alanine transaminase (ALT) greater than 3 times upper limit or normal).\nSide-effects taking longer than 2 weeks to develop (because in such participants much longer blocks of treatment would be required, if the present study is positive such studies will be planned for the future)*.\nHistory of statin intolerance [AND] with drug interaction to antiretroviral drugs.\n History of statin intolerance [AND] to any other drug.\nPregnant [OR] or breast feeding.\nSide effects taking longer than 2 weeks to present.\nIn clinical judgement of study doctor, participant should [NOT] not participate.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Aged 18 years or older
Previously taken one or more statins
 Withdrawn from statins because of perceived side effects
Developed side effects within 2 weeks of initiation
Clinical indication for statins for primary [OR] or secondary prevention of cardiovascular disease [OR] or dyslipidaemia, on either [NOT] no medication [OR] or [NOT] non-statin lipid lowering therapy (e.g, ezetimibe)

Exclusion Criteria:
History of neuropathy
Regularly taking prescribed analgesia
 History of a chronic pain condition
 History of severe mental illness (as their experience of symptoms may already be altered)
Current use of fibrates (because of the risk of interaction with statins [NOT] but will [NOT] not exclude participants taking ezetimibe).
Severe previous reaction [OR] or reaction considered immunological, such as anaphylaxis, [OR] facial swelling, severe rash, [OR] muscle ache [AND] with rise in serum creatine kinase, inflammatory myopathy, [OR] rhabdomyolysis [OR] or liver function abnormalities (aspartate transaminase (AST) [OR] or alanine transaminase (ALT) greater than 3 times upper limit or normal).
Side-effects taking longer than 2 weeks to develop (because in such participants much longer blocks of treatment would be required, if the present study is positive such studies will be planned for the future)*.
History of statin intolerance [AND] with drug interaction to antiretroviral drugs.
 History of statin intolerance [AND] to any other drug.
Pregnant [OR] or breast feeding.
Side effects taking longer than 2 weeks to present.
In clinical judgement of study doctor, participant should [NOT] not participate.
