File: NCT02678962 

Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_full/NCT02678962.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAge from 40 to 80 years old, either gender;\nPatients with bilateral age related cataracts, require bilateral cataract phacoemulsification combined Intraocular Lens implantation;\nWilling to undergo second eye surgery within 7 days after first eye surgery;\nThe potential postoperative visual acuity of 20/40 or better in both eyes;\nPreoperative measurement of corneal astigmatism indicate the subjects are suitable for multifocal intraocular lenses implantation;\nCapability to understand the informed consent and willing and able to attend study\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPreexisting ocular diseases or conditions other than age related cataracts, have contraindications for cataract surgery;\nPreexisting systemic diseases or conditions that may confound the results of the study;\nPrevious ocular surgery history or ocular trauma that may confound the results of the study;\nRequire combined surgery that may confound the results of the study;\nPrevious participation in other clinical trial within 30 days of this study start;\nSystemic or ocular medications that may confound the outcome of the intervention\nPregnant, lactating, or planning to become pregnant during the course of the trial;\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAge from 40 to 80 years old, either gender;\nPatients with bilateral age related cataracts, require bilateral cataract phacoemulsification combined Intraocular Lens implantation;\nWilling to undergo second eye surgery within 7 days after first eye surgery;\nThe potential postoperative visual acuity of 20/40 or better in both eyes;\nPreoperative measurement of corneal astigmatism indicate the subjects are suitable for multifocal intraocular lenses implantation;\nCapability to understand the informed consent and willing and able to attend study\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPreexisting ocular diseases [OR] or conditions other than age related cataracts, have contraindications for cataract surgery;\nPreexisting systemic diseases [OR] or conditions that may confound the results of the study;\n Previous ocular surgery history [OR] or ocular trauma that may confound the results of the study;\n Require combined surgery that may confound the results of the study;\n Previous participation in other clinical trial within 30 days of this study start;\n Systemic [OR] or ocular medications that may confound the outcome of the intervention\nPregnant, [OR] lactating, [OR] or planning to become pregnant during the course of the trial;<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Age from 40 to 80 years old, either gender;
Patients with bilateral age related cataracts, require bilateral cataract phacoemulsification combined Intraocular Lens implantation;
Willing to undergo second eye surgery within 7 days after first eye surgery;
The potential postoperative visual acuity of 20/40 or better in both eyes;
Preoperative measurement of corneal astigmatism indicate the subjects are suitable for multifocal intraocular lenses implantation;
Capability to understand the informed consent and willing and able to attend study

Exclusion Criteria:
Preexisting ocular diseases [OR] or conditions other than age related cataracts, have contraindications for cataract surgery;
Preexisting systemic diseases [OR] or conditions that may confound the results of the study;
 Previous ocular surgery history [OR] or ocular trauma that may confound the results of the study;
 Require combined surgery that may confound the results of the study;
 Previous participation in other clinical trial within 30 days of this study start;
 Systemic [OR] or ocular medications that may confound the outcome of the intervention
Pregnant, [OR] lactating, [OR] or planning to become pregnant during the course of the trial;
