Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nMales or non-pregnant, non-nursing females between the ages of 2-65 years\nLTBI diagnosis as per Canadian TB Standards using either the Tuberculin Skin Test (TST) or the Interferon Gamma Release Assay (IGRA)\nChildren 2-5 years with negative TSTs who have been in close contact with a case of active TB disease recently\nAble and willing to provide fully informed consent or parent/guardian able to provide consent\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nSuspected or confirmed active TB disease\nKnown allergies to any of the study medications by participant self-report\nhave a positive pregnancy test at screening, or\nare not willing to use a reliable method of barrier contraception during the study, or\nare breastfeeding\nhormonal contraception\nHIV infected participants who are on anti-retroviral drugs\nother drugs that interact with 3HP (see Table 1)\nKnown contact with an INH or rifampin resistant case\nWeight < 10 kg\nEvidence of possible liver damage defined by an aspartate transaminase (AST) level that is more than 3x the upper limit of normal in an asymptomatic patient\nPorphyria reported by patient\nInability to adhere to protocol.\nPatients may be excluded from the study for other reasons, at the investigator\'s discretion with detailed documentation.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nMales [OR] or [NOT] non-pregnant, [NOT] non-nursing females between the ages of 2-65 years\nLTBI diagnosis as per Canadian TB Standards using either the Tuberculin Skin Test (TST) [OR] or the Interferon Gamma Release Assay (IGRA)\nChildren 2-5 years [AND] with negative TSTs [AND] who have been in close contact with a case of active TB disease recently\nAble and willing to provide fully informed consent or parent/guardian able to provide consent\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nSuspected [OR] or confirmed active TB disease\nKnown allergies to any of the study medications by participant self-report\nhave a positive pregnancy test at screening, [OR] or\nare [NOT] not willing to use a reliable method of barrier contraception during the study, [OR] or\nare breastfeeding\nhormonal contraception\nHIV infected participants [AND] who are on anti-retroviral drugs\n other drugs that interact with 3HP (see Table 1)\nKnown contact with an INH [OR] or rifampin resistant case\nWeight < 10 kg\nEvidence of possible liver damage defined by an aspartate transaminase (AST) level that is more than 3x the upper limit of normal in an asymptomatic patient\nPorphyria reported by patient\nInability to adhere to protocol.\nPatients may be [NOT] excluded from the study for other reasons, at the investigator\'s discretion with detailed documentation.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Males [OR] or [NOT] non-pregnant, [NOT] non-nursing females between the ages of 2-65 years
LTBI diagnosis as per Canadian TB Standards using either the Tuberculin Skin Test (TST) [OR] or the Interferon Gamma Release Assay (IGRA)
Children 2-5 years [AND] with negative TSTs [AND] who have been in close contact with a case of active TB disease recently
Able and willing to provide fully informed consent or parent/guardian able to provide consent

Exclusion Criteria:
Suspected [OR] or confirmed active TB disease
Known allergies to any of the study medications by participant self-report
have a positive pregnancy test at screening, [OR] or
are [NOT] not willing to use a reliable method of barrier contraception during the study, [OR] or
are breastfeeding
hormonal contraception
HIV infected participants [AND] who are on anti-retroviral drugs
 other drugs that interact with 3HP (see Table 1)
Known contact with an INH [OR] or rifampin resistant case
Weight < 10 kg
Evidence of possible liver damage defined by an aspartate transaminase (AST) level that is more than 3x the upper limit of normal in an asymptomatic patient
Porphyria reported by patient
Inability to adhere to protocol.
Patients may be [NOT] excluded from the study for other reasons, at the investigator's discretion with detailed documentation.
