Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients 18 years of age or older with >3 unformed stools/24 hours with positive stool test for C. difficile.\nPatients receiving = 1 high or medium risk antibiotic for treatment of an infection other than CDI, for an anticipated duration of = 5 days from the time of enrollment.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPatients with severe-complicated disease that would compromise oral therapy (hypotenstion or shock, ileus or bowel obstruction, megacolon).\nPatients with an allergy to oral vancomycin or fidaxomicin.\nPatients anticipated to receive metronidazole after enrollment.\nPatients who already received oral vancomycin or metronidazole (either oral or intravenous) for > 24 hours within the preceding 72 hours at the time of enrollment.\nPatients anticipated to receive adjunctive C. difficile therapy (rifaxamin, nitazoxanide, tigecycline) after enrollment.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients 18 years of age or older [AND] with >3 unformed stools/24 hours [AND] with positive stool test for C. difficile.\nPatients receiving = 1 high [OR] or medium risk antibiotic for treatment of an infection other than CDI, for an anticipated duration of = 5 days from the time of enrollment.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPatients with severe-complicated disease that would compromise oral therapy (hypotenstion [OR] or shock, [OR] ileus [OR] or bowel obstruction, [OR] megacolon).\nPatients with an allergy to oral vancomycin [OR] or fidaxomicin.\n Patients anticipated to receive metronidazole after enrollment.\nPatients who already received oral vancomycin [OR] or metronidazole (either oral [OR] or intravenous) for > 24 hours within the preceding 72 hours at the time of enrollment.\nPatients anticipated to receive adjunctive C. difficile therapy (rifaxamin, [OR] nitazoxanide, [OR] tigecycline) after enrollment.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Patients 18 years of age or older [AND] with >3 unformed stools/24 hours [AND] with positive stool test for C. difficile.
Patients receiving = 1 high [OR] or medium risk antibiotic for treatment of an infection other than CDI, for an anticipated duration of = 5 days from the time of enrollment.

Exclusion Criteria:
Patients with severe-complicated disease that would compromise oral therapy (hypotenstion [OR] or shock, [OR] ileus [OR] or bowel obstruction, [OR] megacolon).
Patients with an allergy to oral vancomycin [OR] or fidaxomicin.
 Patients anticipated to receive metronidazole after enrollment.
Patients who already received oral vancomycin [OR] or metronidazole (either oral [OR] or intravenous) for > 24 hours within the preceding 72 hours at the time of enrollment.
Patients anticipated to receive adjunctive C. difficile therapy (rifaxamin, [OR] nitazoxanide, [OR] tigecycline) after enrollment.
