ical problems including pulmonary, cardiovascular or orthopedic disease\nAny debilitating disease prior to the SCI that caused exercise intolerance\nPremorbid, ongoing major depression or psychosis, altered cognitive status\nHistory of head injury or stroke\nMetal plate in skull\nHistory of seizures\nReceiving drugs acting primarily on the central nervous system, which lower the seizure threshold (see appendix 2)\nPregnant females\nOngoing cord compression or a syrinx in the spinal cord or who suffer from a spinal cord disease such as spinal stenosis, spina bifida, MS, or herniated disk\nIndividuals with scalp shrapnel, cochlear implants, or aneurysm clips.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nMale [OR] and females between ages 18-85 years\nRight handed\nAble to complete precision grips with both hands\nAble to complete full wrist flexion- [OR] extension bilaterally\nAble to walk unassisted\nAble to complete full ankle flexion- [OR] extension bilaterally\nMale [OR] and females between ages 18-85 years\nSCI ( 2 months of injury)\nSpinal Cord injury at or above L5\nThe ability to produce a visible precision grip force with one hand\nAble to perform some small wrist flexion [OR] and extension\nThe ability to perform a small visible contraction with dorsiflexion [OR] and hip flexor muscles\nNo subjects will be excluded based on their race, religion, ethnicity, gender [OR] or HIV status.\nASIA A,B,C, [OR] or D\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nUncontrolled medical problems including pulmonary, [OR] cardiovascular [OR] or orthopedic disease\nAny debilitating disease prior to the SCI that caused exercise intolerance\nPremorbid, ongoing major depression [OR] or psychosis, [OR] altered cognitive status\nHistory of head injury [OR] or stroke\nMetal plate in skull\nHistory of seizures\nReceiving drugs acting primarily on the central nervous system, which lower the seizure threshold (see appendix 2)\nPregnant females\nOngoing cord compression [OR] or a syrinx in the spinal cord [OR] or who suffer from a spinal cord disease such as spinal stenosis, [OR] spina bifida, [OR] MS, [OR] or herniated disk\nIndividuals with scalp shrapnel, [OR] cochlear implants, [OR] or aneurysm clips.<|eot_id|>']
