Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPhysically healthy adults age 18-55 who meet DSM-5 criteria for insomnia and Criterion A (exposure to a traumatic event) for PTSD. The index trauma must have occurred within the past 5 years and at least 3 months before enrolling, and insomnia symptoms must have started or worsened after the exposure to the index trauma\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPsychiatric disorders other than insomnia, PTSD and specific phobias; including bipolar and psychotic disorders and meeting criteria for DSM-5 moderate alcohol or drug use disorders within the past year.\nDiagnosis of a sleep disorder other than insomnia including PSG findings of apnea/hypopnea or periodic limb movement indices > 10/hour;\nMedical conditions that require consistent use of medication or compromise sleep;\nHistory of moderate to severe traumatic brain injury or mild traumatic brain injury with ongoing post-concussive symptoms;\nSuicidal ideation with intent to act or with specific plan and intent in the past 6 months (Type 4 - 5 ideation on the Columbia Suicide Severity Rating Scale) or a concerning history of prior suicidal behavior.\nCaffeine use exceeding 5 cups of coffee per day or its equivalent;\nHabitual bedtimes after 3 AM, habitual rise times after 10 AM, or habitual napping > 1hour/day;\nPregnancy or breastfeeding, or expecting to conceive while in study;\nPositive urine toxicology.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPhysically healthy adults age 18-55 [AND] who meet DSM-5 criteria for insomnia [AND] and Criterion A (exposure to a traumatic event) for PTSD. The index trauma must have occurred within the past 5 years [AND] and at least 3 months before enrolling, [AND] and insomnia symptoms must have started [OR] or worsened after the exposure to the index trauma\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPsychiatric disorders other than insomnia, [OR] PTSD [OR] and specific phobias; including bipolar [OR] and psychotic disorders [AND] and meeting criteria for DSM-5 moderate alcohol [OR] or drug use disorders within the past year.\nDiagnosis of a sleep disorder other than insomnia including PSG findings of apnea/ [OR] hypopnea [OR] or periodic limb movement indices > 10/hour;\nMedical conditions that require consistent use of medication [OR] or compromise sleep;\nHistory of moderate [OR] to severe traumatic brain injury [OR] or mild traumatic brain injury [AND] with ongoing post-concussive symptoms;\nSuicidal ideation [AND] with intent to act [OR] or with specific plan [AND] and intent in the past 6 months (Type 4 - 5 ideation on the Columbia Suicide Severity Rating Scale) [OR] or a concerning history of prior suicidal behavior.\nCaffeine use exceeding 5 cups of coffee per day [OR] or its equivalent;\nHabitual bedtimes after 3 AM, habitual rise times after 10 AM, [OR] or habitual napping > 1hour/day;\nPregnancy [OR] or breastfeeding, [OR] or expecting to conceive while in study;\nPositive urine toxicology.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Physically healthy adults age 18-55 [AND] who meet DSM-5 criteria for insomnia [AND] and Criterion A (exposure to a traumatic event) for PTSD. The index trauma must have occurred within the past 5 years [AND] and at least 3 months before enrolling, [AND] and insomnia symptoms must have started [OR] or worsened after the exposure to the index trauma

Exclusion Criteria:
Psychiatric disorders other than insomnia, [OR] PTSD [OR] and specific phobias; including bipolar [OR] and psychotic disorders [AND] and meeting criteria for DSM-5 moderate alcohol [OR] or drug use disorders within the past year.
Diagnosis of a sleep disorder other than insomnia including PSG findings of apnea/ [OR] hypopnea [OR] or periodic limb movement indices > 10/hour;
Medical conditions that require consistent use of medication [OR] or compromise sleep;
History of moderate [OR] to severe traumatic brain injury [OR] or mild traumatic brain injury [AND] with ongoing post-concussive symptoms;
Suicidal ideation [AND] with intent to act [OR] or with specific plan [AND] and intent in the past 6 months (Type 4 - 5 ideation on the Columbia Suicide Severity Rating Scale) [OR] or a concerning history of prior suicidal behavior.
Caffeine use exceeding 5 cups of coffee per day [OR] or its equivalent;
Habitual bedtimes after 3 AM, habitual rise times after 10 AM, [OR] or habitual napping > 1hour/day;
Pregnancy [OR] or breastfeeding, [OR] or expecting to conceive while in study;
Positive urine toxicology.
