tment for at least 3 months.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nAge < 45 [OR] or > 55 years.\nBlood disorders [OR] or coagulopathy.\nDiagnosed [OR] or suspected local gynecologic lesion (polyp, [OR] adenomyosis, [OR] myoma, [OR] malignancy [OR] or cervical pathology).\nUse intrauterine contraceptive device.\nPregnancy related conditions.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Perimenopausal women complaining of abnormal uterine bleeding (menorrhagia, [OR] metrorrhagia, [OR] polymenorrhoea [OR] or polymenorrhagia) [NOT] without local gynecological cause.
Failure of medical treatment for at least 3 months.

Exclusion Criteria:
