Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nHas given written informed consent before any study-related activity is performed\nAdvanced hormone-dependent prostate cancer for which androgen deprivation therapy is indicated, and independently from this trial, Firmagon® is intended to be used for treatment\nAge greater than or equal to 18 years and less than 80 years\nAdvanced hormone-dependent prostate cancer without any other clinically significant disorder\nEasten Cooperative Oncology Group score = 2\nPSA = 2 ng/mL at screening\nLife expectancy of at least 12 months as per the investigator\'s judgement\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPrevious or concurrent hormonal management of prostate cancer\nContraindication for prescription of Firmagon®\nConcurrent treatment with a 5-a-reductase inhibitor\nConsidered as a candidate for curative therapy\nHistory of severe untreated asthma, anaphylactic reactions or severe urticaria and/or angioedema\nQTc interval over 450 msec or risk factors for torsades de pointes or on Class IA and Class III anti arrhythmic medications\nCancer within the last 5 years except prostate cancer and surgically removed basal or squamous cell carcinoma of the skin\nKnown or suspected hepatic, symptomatic biliary disease (this includes moderate to severe chronic hepatic impairment)\nPatients with clinically significant laboratory abnormalities / disorders other than prostate cancer\nPatient with Hepatitis B Virus (HBV), Hepatitis C Virus (HCV) and Human Immunodeficiency Virus (HIV) infections\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nHas given written informed consent before any study-related activity is performed\nAdvanced hormone-dependent prostate cancer for which androgen deprivation therapy is indicated, [AND] and independently from this trial, Firmagon® is intended to be used for treatment\nAge greater than or equal to 18 years [AND] and less than 80 years\nAdvanced hormone-dependent prostate cancer [NOT] without any other clinically significant disorder\nEasten Cooperative Oncology Group score = 2\nPSA = 2 ng/mL at screening\nLife expectancy of at least 12 months as per the investigator\'s judgement\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPrevious [OR] or concurrent hormonal management of prostate cancer\nContraindication for prescription of Firmagon®\nConcurrent treatment with a 5-a-reductase inhibitor\nConsidered as a candidate for curative therapy\nHistory of severe [NOT] untreated asthma, [OR] anaphylactic reactions [OR] or severe urticaria [OR] and/or angioedema\nQTc interval over 450 msec [OR] or risk factors for torsades de pointes [OR] or on Class IA [OR] and Class III anti arrhythmic medications\nCancer within the last 5 years except prostate cancer [OR] and surgically removed basal [OR] or squamous cell carcinoma of the skin\nKnown [OR] or suspected hepatic, symptomatic biliary disease (this includes moderate [OR] to severe chronic hepatic impairment)\nPatients with clinically significant laboratory abnormalities [OR] / disorders other than prostate cancer\nPatient with Hepatitis B Virus (HBV), [OR] Hepatitis C Virus (HCV) [OR] and Human Immunodeficiency Virus (HIV) infections<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Has given written informed consent before any study-related activity is performed
Advanced hormone-dependent prostate cancer for which androgen deprivation therapy is indicated, [AND] and independently from this trial, Firmagon® is intended to be used for treatment
Age greater than or equal to 18 years [AND] and less than 80 years
Advanced hormone-dependent prostate cancer [NOT] without any other clinically significant disorder
Easten Cooperative Oncology Group score = 2
PSA = 2 ng/mL at screening
Life expectancy of at least 12 months as per the investigator's judgement

Exclusion Criteria:
Previous [OR] or concurrent hormonal management of prostate cancer
Contraindication for prescription of Firmagon®
Concurrent treatment with a 5-a-reductase inhibitor
Considered as a candidate for curative therapy
History of severe [NOT] untreated asthma, [OR] anaphylactic reactions [OR] or severe urticaria [OR] and/or angioedema
QTc interval over 450 msec [OR] or risk factors for torsades de pointes [OR] or on Class IA [OR] and Class III anti arrhythmic medications
Cancer within the last 5 years except prostate cancer [OR] and surgically removed basal [OR] or squamous cell carcinoma of the skin
Known [OR] or suspected hepatic, symptomatic biliary disease (this includes moderate [OR] to severe chronic hepatic impairment)
Patients with clinically significant laboratory abnormalities [OR] / disorders other than prostate cancer
Patient with Hepatitis B Virus (HBV), [OR] Hepatitis C Virus (HCV) [OR] and Human Immunodeficiency Virus (HIV) infections
