Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nBetween the ages of 21-60\nRight-handed\nCapable of giving informed consent and complying with study procedures\nReports drinking a minimum of 5 standard drinks for men or 4 standard drinks for women on at least 4 days per week on average over the past 28 days\nMeets DSM-V criteria for current Alcohol Use Disorder\nSeeking treatment for Alcohol Use Disorder\nAgree to not seek additional treatment, apart from Alcoholics Anonymous\nWilling to attempt to abstain from alcohol completely for the duration of the study\nWilling to be hospitalized on a research unit for 24 hours, longer if detoxification is needed.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nRisk of severe alcohol withdrawal (e.g. history of seizures or delirium tremens)\nCurrent Moderate or Severe Substance Use Disorder, other than Alcohol, Nicotine or Caffeine Use Disorders\nLifetime history of Bipolar Disorder, Schizophrenia or Schizoaffective Disorder\nAny current psychiatric disorder, other than Alcohol Use Disorder, that, in the judgment of the investigator, will require treatment that will interfere with study participation.\nCurrent severe depression (HAM-D >24) or anxiety (HAM-A >24)\nSignificant suicide or violence risk\nCurrently taking any psychotropic medications\nLegally mandated to participate in treatment\nHistory of prior treatment with disulfiram\nSufficiently socially unstable as to preclude participation (e.g. homeless)\nContraindications to disulfiram treatment (liver disease, kidney disease, cardiac disease, seizure disorder, hypothyroidism, diabetes mellitus, pregnancy or lactation, allergy to disulfiram or thiuran derivatives)\nNeurological or medical conditions that would interfere with MRI scanning (e.g. history of stroke, seizure, brain tumor, brain infection, traumatic brain injury, multiple sclerosis, dementia, metal device in body, pregnancy, claustrophobia, color blindness, severe hearing impairment, weight>300 lbs., wheelchair-bound)\nCurrently taking medications containing alcohol, metronidazole, isoniazid, paraldehyde, phenytoin, warfarin, or theophylline.\nSignificant alcohol withdrawal (CIWA>8) at screening, after confirming a blood alcohol level of zero.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nBetween the ages of 21-60\nRight-handed\nCapable of giving informed consent and complying with study procedures\nReports drinking a minimum of 5 standard drinks for men [OR] or 4 standard drinks for women on at least 4 days per week on average over the past 28 days\nMeets DSM-V criteria for current Alcohol Use Disorder\nSeeking treatment for Alcohol Use Disorder\nAgree to [NOT] not seek additional treatment, apart from Alcoholics Anonymous\nWilling to attempt to [NOT] abstain from alcohol completely for the duration of the study\nWilling to be hospitalized on a research unit for 24 hours, longer if detoxification is needed.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nRisk of severe alcohol withdrawal (e.g. history of seizures [OR] or delirium tremens)\nCurrent Moderate [OR] or Severe Substance Use Disorder, other than Alcohol, [OR] Nicotine [OR] or Caffeine Use Disorders\nLifetime history of Bipolar Disorder, [OR] Schizophrenia [OR] or Schizoaffective Disorder\n Any current psychiatric disorder, other than Alcohol Use Disorder, that, in the judgment of the investigator, will require treatment that will interfere with study participation.\nCurrent severe depression (HAM-D >24) [OR] or anxiety (HAM-A >24)\nSignificant suicide [OR] or violence risk\n Currently taking any psychotropic medications\n Legally mandated to participate in treatment\n History of prior treatment with disulfiram\n Sufficiently socially unstable as to [NOT] preclude participation (e.g. homeless)\nContraindications to disulfiram treatment (liver disease, [OR] kidney disease, [OR] cardiac disease, [OR] seizure disorder, [OR] hypothyroidism, [OR] diabetes mellitus, [OR] pregnancy [OR] or lactation, allergy to disulfiram [OR] or thiuran derivatives)\nNeurological [OR] or medical conditions that would interfere with MRI scanning (e.g. history of stroke, [OR] seizure, [OR] brain tumor, [OR] brain infection, [OR] traumatic brain injury, [OR] multiple sclerosis, [OR] dementia, [OR] metal device in body, [OR] pregnancy, [OR] claustrophobia, [OR] color blindness, severe hearing impairment, [OR] weight>300 lbs., [OR] wheelchair-bound)\nCurrently taking medications containing alcohol, [OR] metronidazole, [OR] isoniazid, [OR] paraldehyde, [OR] phenytoin, [OR] warfarin, [OR] or theophylline.\n Significant alcohol withdrawal (CIWA>8) at screening, after confirming a blood alcohol level of zero.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Between the ages of 21-60
Right-handed
Capable of giving informed consent and complying with study procedures
Reports drinking a minimum of 5 standard drinks for men [OR] or 4 standard drinks for women on at least 4 days per week on average over the past 28 days
Meets DSM-V criteria for current Alcohol Use Disorder
Seeking treatment for Alcohol Use Disorder
Agree to [NOT] not seek additional treatment, apart from Alcoholics Anonymous
Willing to attempt to [NOT] abstain from alcohol completely for the duration of the study
Willing to be hospitalized on a research unit for 24 hours, longer if detoxification is needed.

Exclusion Criteria:
Risk of severe alcohol withdrawal (e.g. history of seizures [OR] or delirium tremens)
Current Moderate [OR] or Severe Substance Use Disorder, other than Alcohol, [OR] Nicotine [OR] or Caffeine Use Disorders
Lifetime history of Bipolar Disorder, [OR] Schizophrenia [OR] or Schizoaffective Disorder
 Any current psychiatric disorder, other than Alcohol Use Disorder, that, in the judgment of the investigator, will require treatment that will interfere with study participation.
Current severe depression (HAM-D >24) [OR] or anxiety (HAM-A >24)
Significant suicide [OR] or violence risk
 Currently taking any psychotropic medications
 Legally mandated to participate in treatment
 History of prior treatment with disulfiram
 Sufficiently socially unstable as to [NOT] preclude participation (e.g. homeless)
Contraindications to disulfiram treatment (liver disease, [OR] kidney disease, [OR] cardiac disease, [OR] seizure disorder, [OR] hypothyroidism, [OR] diabetes mellitus, [OR] pregnancy [OR] or lactation, allergy to disulfiram [OR] or thiuran derivatives)
Neurological [OR] or medical conditions that would interfere with MRI scanning (e.g. history of stroke, [OR] seizure, [OR] brain tumor, [OR] brain infection, [OR] traumatic brain injury, [OR] multiple sclerosis, [OR] dementia, [OR] metal device in body, [OR] pregnancy, [OR] claustrophobia, [OR] color blindness, severe hearing impairment, [OR] weight>300 lbs., [OR] wheelchair-bound)
Currently taking medications containing alcohol, [OR] metronidazole, [OR] isoniazid, [OR] paraldehyde, [OR] phenytoin, [OR] warfarin, [OR] or theophylline.
 Significant alcohol withdrawal (CIWA>8) at screening, after confirming a blood alcohol level of zero.
