Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nCHB patients who had received NAs for more than 12 months.\nHepatitis B e antigen (HBeAg)-negative and anti-HBeAg positive.\nHepatitis B surface antigen (HBsAg) positive and <1500 IU/mL.\nHepatitis B virus DNA not detectable(Roche Cobas).\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPatients with liver cirrhosis, Hepatocellular Carcinoma or other malignancies.\nPatients with other factors causing liver diseases.\nPregnant and lactating women.\nPatients with concomitant HIV infection or congenital immune deficiency diseases.\nPatients with diabetes, autoimmune diseases.\nPatients with important organ dysfunctions.\nPatients with serious complications (e.g., infection, hepatic encephalopathy, hepatorenal syndrome, gastrointestinal bleeding.)\nPatients who receive antineoplastic or immunomodulatory therapy in the past 12 months.\nPatients who can\'t come back to clinic for follow-up on schedule.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nCHB patients [AND] who had received NAs for more than 12 months.\nHepatitis B e antigen (HBeAg)-negative [AND] and anti-HBeAg positive.\nHepatitis B surface antigen (HBsAg) positive [AND] and <1500 IU/mL.\nHepatitis B virus DNA [NOT] not detectable(Roche Cobas).\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPatients with liver cirrhosis, [OR] Hepatocellular Carcinoma [OR] or other malignancies.\nPatients with other factors causing liver diseases.\nPregnant [OR] and lactating women.\nPatients with concomitant HIV infection [OR] or congenital immune deficiency diseases.\nPatients with diabetes, [OR] autoimmune diseases.\nPatients with important organ dysfunctions.\nPatients with serious complications (e.g., infection, [OR] hepatic encephalopathy, [OR] hepatorenal syndrome, [OR] gastrointestinal bleeding.)\nPatients who receive antineoplastic [OR] or immunomodulatory therapy in the past 12 months.\nPatients who can\'t come back to clinic for follow-up on schedule.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
CHB patients [AND] who had received NAs for more than 12 months.
Hepatitis B e antigen (HBeAg)-negative [AND] and anti-HBeAg positive.
Hepatitis B surface antigen (HBsAg) positive [AND] and <1500 IU/mL.
Hepatitis B virus DNA [NOT] not detectable(Roche Cobas).

Exclusion Criteria:
Patients with liver cirrhosis, [OR] Hepatocellular Carcinoma [OR] or other malignancies.
Patients with other factors causing liver diseases.
Pregnant [OR] and lactating women.
Patients with concomitant HIV infection [OR] or congenital immune deficiency diseases.
Patients with diabetes, [OR] autoimmune diseases.
Patients with important organ dysfunctions.
Patients with serious complications (e.g., infection, [OR] hepatic encephalopathy, [OR] hepatorenal syndrome, [OR] gastrointestinal bleeding.)
Patients who receive antineoplastic [OR] or immunomodulatory therapy in the past 12 months.
Patients who can't come back to clinic for follow-up on schedule.
