Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients with diagnosis of multiple myeloma according to criteria of the International Myeloma Working Group \nPatients in whom a LEN-DEX-based treatment regimen is indicated \nAdult patients ≥ 19 years of age who are able to freely provide informed consent \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nConcomitant antiplatelet or anticoagulant use \nCalculated creatinine clearance < 30 mL/min by Cockcroft-Gault formula \nAlanine aminotransferase (ALT) or aspartate aminotransferase (AST) > 3 times upper limit of normal (ULN) \nTotal bilirubin > 2 x ULN \nThrombocytopenia < 50 x 10 gigalitres (Gl) \nHigh bleeding risk or spontaneously prolonged prothrombin time or activated partial thromboplastin time > 1.5 x ULN \nBody weight <50 or >120 kg \nConcomitant use of CYP3A4 or p-glycoprotein inducers or inhibitors \nUse of Ginkgo biloba or St. John\'s Wort within 14 days before first dose of study drug \nDexamethasone use within last 3 months \nWomen of Childbearing potential without proper contraceptive measures, pregnancy or breast feeding \nLife expectancy less than 3 months \nInability to swallow or issues with malabsorption \nAny other medical, social, logistical, geographical or psychological factors, which in the opinion of the investigator, would prohibit follow-up, compliance and study completion       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients with diagnosis of multiple myeloma according to criteria of the International Myeloma Working Group \nPatients in whom a LEN-DEX-based treatment regimen is indicated \nAdult patients ≥ 19 years of age [AND] who are able to freely provide informed consent \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nConcomitant antiplatelet [OR] or anticoagulant use \nCalculated creatinine clearance < 30 mL/min by Cockcroft-Gault formula \nAlanine aminotransferase (ALT) [OR] or aspartate aminotransferase (AST) > 3 times upper limit of normal (ULN) \nTotal bilirubin > 2 x ULN \nThrombocytopenia < 50 x 10 gigalitres (Gl) \nHigh bleeding risk [OR] or spontaneously prolonged prothrombin time [OR] or activated partial thromboplastin time > 1.5 x ULN \nBody weight <50 [OR] or >120 kg \nConcomitant use of CYP3A4 [OR] or p-glycoprotein inducers [OR] or inhibitors \nUse of Ginkgo biloba [OR] or St. John\'s Wort within 14 days before first dose of study drug \nDexamethasone use within last 3 months \nWomen [AND] of Childbearing potential [NOT] without proper contraceptive measures, [OR] pregnancy [OR] or breast feeding \nLife expectancy less than 3 months \nInability to swallow [OR] or issues with malabsorption \nAny other medical, [OR] social, [OR] logistical, [OR] geographical [OR] or psychological factors, which in the opinion of the investigator, would [NOT] prohibit follow-up, compliance [AND] and study completion<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Patients with diagnosis of multiple myeloma according to criteria of the International Myeloma Working Group 
Patients in whom a LEN-DEX-based treatment regimen is indicated 
Adult patients ≥ 19 years of age [AND] who are able to freely provide informed consent 

Exclusion Criteria:
Concomitant antiplatelet [OR] or anticoagulant use 
Calculated creatinine clearance < 30 mL/min by Cockcroft-Gault formula 
Alanine aminotransferase (ALT) [OR] or aspartate aminotransferase (AST) > 3 times upper limit of normal (ULN) 
Total bilirubin > 2 x ULN 
Thrombocytopenia < 50 x 10 gigalitres (Gl) 
High bleeding risk [OR] or spontaneously prolonged prothrombin time [OR] or activated partial thromboplastin time > 1.5 x ULN 
Body weight <50 [OR] or >120 kg 
Concomitant use of CYP3A4 [OR] or p-glycoprotein inducers [OR] or inhibitors 
Use of Ginkgo biloba [OR] or St. John's Wort within 14 days before first dose of study drug 
Dexamethasone use within last 3 months 
Women [AND] of Childbearing potential [NOT] without proper contraceptive measures, [OR] pregnancy [OR] or breast feeding 
Life expectancy less than 3 months 
Inability to swallow [OR] or issues with malabsorption 
Any other medical, [OR] social, [OR] logistical, [OR] geographical [OR] or psychological factors, which in the opinion of the investigator, would [NOT] prohibit follow-up, compliance [AND] and study completion
