Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAge = 19 and = 70 years;\nPresence of liver cirrhosis\nSerum albumin level = 3.5g/dl, ultrasound or CT scan confirmed ascites (=Grade 1)\nNo administration of diuretics and BCAA within the past 1 week\nVoluntary consent to take part in this trial\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nChild-Pugh score > 12\nHaving been diagnosed as HCC within the past 5 years\nSerum creatinine > 1.5mg/dl\nSerum bilirubin > 5.0mg/dl\nPresence of such complications as SBP, or hepatic encephalopathy(West Haven grade = 3)\nPatients who experienced organ failure by acute exacerbation of liver cirrhosis within the past 1 month\nPresence of serious cardiac or respiratory disease\nContraindicated to either diuretics or BCAA\nHaving commenced anti-viral treatment against hepatitis C, B within the past 1 month\nPregnant or lactating women\nChronic alcohol taker\nWoman patients who do not agree to the contraception from baseline to 12 month\nUnsuitable patients judged by investigator\nPatients participating in another clinical trial within 1 month\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAge = 19 [AND] and = 70 years;\nPresence of liver cirrhosis\nSerum albumin level = 3.5g/dl, ultrasound [OR] or CT scan confirmed ascites (=Grade 1)\n [NOT] No administration of diuretics [OR] and BCAA within the past 1 week\nVoluntary consent to take part in this trial\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nChild-Pugh score > 12\n Having been diagnosed as HCC within the past 5 years\nSerum creatinine > 1.5mg/dl\nSerum bilirubin > 5.0mg/dl\nPresence of such complications as SBP, [OR] or hepatic encephalopathy(West Haven grade = 3)\nPatients who experienced organ failure by acute exacerbation of liver cirrhosis within the past 1 month\nPresence of serious cardiac [OR] or respiratory disease\nContraindicated to either diuretics [OR] or BCAA\n Having commenced anti-viral treatment against hepatitis C, [OR] B within the past 1 month\nPregnant [OR] or lactating women\nChronic alcohol taker\nWoman patients [AND] who do [NOT] not agree to the contraception from baseline to 12 month\nUnsuitable patients judged by investigator\nPatients participating in another clinical trial within 1 month<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Age = 19 [AND] and = 70 years;
Presence of liver cirrhosis
Serum albumin level = 3.5g/dl, ultrasound [OR] or CT scan confirmed ascites (=Grade 1)
 [NOT] No administration of diuretics [OR] and BCAA within the past 1 week
Voluntary consent to take part in this trial

Exclusion Criteria:
Child-Pugh score > 12
 Having been diagnosed as HCC within the past 5 years
Serum creatinine > 1.5mg/dl
Serum bilirubin > 5.0mg/dl
Presence of such complications as SBP, [OR] or hepatic encephalopathy(West Haven grade = 3)
Patients who experienced organ failure by acute exacerbation of liver cirrhosis within the past 1 month
Presence of serious cardiac [OR] or respiratory disease
Contraindicated to either diuretics [OR] or BCAA
 Having commenced anti-viral treatment against hepatitis C, [OR] B within the past 1 month
Pregnant [OR] or lactating women
Chronic alcohol taker
Woman patients [AND] who do [NOT] not agree to the contraception from baseline to 12 month
Unsuitable patients judged by investigator
Patients participating in another clinical trial within 1 month
