Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nWomen aged 25-75 years old.\nWomen with recently diagnosed breast cancer and who will receive NAC to reduce tumor burden before surgery. (including locally advanced breast cancer (LABC) according to clinical assessment; or tumor size > 2cm, that is, at least T2 in TNM staging).\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nEstimated GFR (eGFR) < 60 mL/min/1.73 m2 and blood glucose > 135 mg/dl; Past or present history of acute renal failure, renal dialysis, diabetes mellitus.\nWomen who received metallic fixation, coronary artery stent in recent 3 months; or women who received mechanical valve replacement that is not compatible with MR magnet; or women with aneurysmal clips, pacemakers.\nPast history of claustrophobia.\nWomen who are pregnant or who are planning to be pregnant, or who are lactating (though the possibility in our target population should be very low)\nPast history of breast cancer within recent 5 years before the currently diagnosed breast cancer.\nWomen who received chemotherapy for other disease entity in recent 1 year.\nWomen who cannot cooperate with the examinations.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nWomen aged 25-75 years old.\nWomen [AND] with recently diagnosed breast cancer [AND] and who will receive NAC to reduce tumor burden before surgery. (including locally advanced breast cancer (LABC) according to clinical assessment; [OR] or tumor size > 2cm, that is, at least T2 in TNM staging).\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nEstimated GFR (eGFR) < 60 mL/min/1.73 m2 [AND] and blood glucose > 135 mg/dl; Past [OR] or present history of acute renal failure, [OR] renal dialysis, [OR] diabetes mellitus.\nWomen [AND] who received metallic fixation, [OR] coronary artery stent in recent 3 months; [OR] or women [AND] who received mechanical valve replacement that is [NOT] not compatible with MR magnet; [OR] or women [AND] with aneurysmal clips, [OR] pacemakers.\nPast history of claustrophobia.\nWomen [AND] who are pregnant [OR] or who are planning to be pregnant, [OR] or who are lactating (though the possibility in our target population should be very low)\nPast history of breast cancer within recent 5 years before the currently diagnosed breast cancer.\nWomen [AND] who received chemotherapy for other disease entity in recent 1 year.\nWomen [AND] who [NOT] cannot cooperate with the examinations.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Women aged 25-75 years old.
Women [AND] with recently diagnosed breast cancer [AND] and who will receive NAC to reduce tumor burden before surgery. (including locally advanced breast cancer (LABC) according to clinical assessment; [OR] or tumor size > 2cm, that is, at least T2 in TNM staging).

Exclusion Criteria:
Estimated GFR (eGFR) < 60 mL/min/1.73 m2 [AND] and blood glucose > 135 mg/dl; Past [OR] or present history of acute renal failure, [OR] renal dialysis, [OR] diabetes mellitus.
Women [AND] who received metallic fixation, [OR] coronary artery stent in recent 3 months; [OR] or women [AND] who received mechanical valve replacement that is [NOT] not compatible with MR magnet; [OR] or women [AND] with aneurysmal clips, [OR] pacemakers.
Past history of claustrophobia.
Women [AND] who are pregnant [OR] or who are planning to be pregnant, [OR] or who are lactating (though the possibility in our target population should be very low)
Past history of breast cancer within recent 5 years before the currently diagnosed breast cancer.
Women [AND] who received chemotherapy for other disease entity in recent 1 year.
Women [AND] who [NOT] cannot cooperate with the examinations.
