Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\n= 20years of age;\ndiagnosis of stroke (>6months);\nsedentary or insufficiently active;\nhave a writing medical permission to participate in the training program.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\ncognitive impairment (Mini-Mental Status Examination score: illiterate 13 points; elementary and middle school 18 points; and high-school 26 points; or inability to respond to verbal command);\ninability to walk independently for at least 10 minutes, with or without walking devices;\npain or other disorders precluding their participation.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n= 20years of age;\ndiagnosis of stroke (>6months);\nsedentary [OR] or insufficiently active;\nhave a writing medical permission to participate in the training program.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\ncognitive impairment (Mini-Mental Status Examination score: illiterate 13 points; elementary and middle school 18 points; and high-school 26 points; [OR] or [NOT] inability to respond to verbal command);\n [NOT] inability to walk independently for at least 10 minutes, [AND] with or [NOT] without walking devices;\npain [OR] or other disorders precluding their participation.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
= 20years of age;
diagnosis of stroke (>6months);
sedentary [OR] or insufficiently active;
have a writing medical permission to participate in the training program.

Exclusion Criteria:
cognitive impairment (Mini-Mental Status Examination score: illiterate 13 points; elementary and middle school 18 points; and high-school 26 points; [OR] or [NOT] inability to respond to verbal command);
 [NOT] inability to walk independently for at least 10 minutes, [AND] with or [NOT] without walking devices;
pain [OR] or other disorders precluding their participation.
