 less than one year\nPregnancy or women with potential childbearing\nType I DM\nTreatment with insulin\nHistory of pancreatitis\nWho cannot read the informed consent form (e.g. illiteracy, foreigner)\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nNon-ST segement elevation acute coronary syndrome\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nLeft main disease\nKnown hypersensitivity [OR] or contraindication to any of the following medications: Heparin, [OR] aspirin, [OR] clopidogrel, [OR] sirolimus, [OR] siptagliptin [OR] and statin\nCongestive heart failure (patients with LVEF <30% [OR] or cardiogenic shock)\nUncontrolled myocardial ischemia (repeated chest pain [OR] or dyspnea after revascularization)\nUncontrolled ventricular arrhythmia\nHistory of malignancy [AND] with chemotherapy\nSerious hematologic disease (e.g. CML, [OR] MDS)\nCurrent infectious disease needs antibiotics therapy\nCreatinine level >1.5 mg/dL [OR] or dependence on dialysis\nOther severe concurrent illness (e.g. active infection, [OR] malignancy).\nLife expectancy of less than one year\nPregnancy [OR] or women [AND] with potential childbearing\nType I DM\nTreatment with insulin\nHistory of pancreatitis\nWho cannot read the informed consent form (e.g. illiteracy, [OR] foreigner)<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Non-ST segement elevation acute coronary syndrome

Exclusion Criteria:
Left main disease
Known hypersensitivity [OR] or contraindication to any of the following medications: Heparin, [OR] aspirin, [OR] clopidogrel, [OR] sirolimus, [OR] siptagliptin [OR] and statin
Congestive heart failure (patients with LVEF <30% [OR] or cardiogenic shock)
Uncontrolled myocardial ischemia (repeated chest pain [OR] or dyspnea after revascularization)
Uncontrolled ventricular arrhythmia
History of malignancy [AND] with chemotherapy
Serious hematologic disease (e.g. CML, [OR] MDS)
Current infectious disease needs antibiotics therapy
Creatinine level >1.5 mg/dL [OR] or dependence on dialysis
Other severe concurrent illness (e.g. active infection, [OR] malignancy).
Life expectancy of less than one year
Pregnancy [OR] or women [AND] with potential childbearing
Type I DM
Treatment with insulin
History of pancreatitis
Who cannot read the informed consent form (e.g. illiteracy, [OR] foreigner)
