Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\n1) histologically confirmed (patients not receiving a single sputum cytology diagnosis) non-small cell lung cancer patients,with wild-type EGFR and ALK-negative; 2) According to IASLC2009 new TNM staging of lung cancer stage <U+2162>B or <U+2163>, previously untreated or relapsed after 1 year of lung cancer resection; 3) have at least one evaluable lesions,according to version 1.1 of the standard in accordance with a judgment RECIST(longest diameter on a spiral CT at least 10mm,on a regular CT longest diameter at least 20mm); 4) Male or female, aged 18 to 75 years; 5) ECOG PS 0 or 1; 6) expected survival at least 3 months; 7) adequate hematological function: absolute neutrophil count (ANC) at least 2×10^9/L and platelet count at least 100×10^9/L and hemoglobin at least 9 g/dL; 8) adequate liver function: total bilirubin less than upper limit of normal (ULN); AST and ALT less than 2.5 times upper limit of normal (ULN); alkaline phosphatase less than 5 times the upper limit of normal (ULN); 9) adequate renal function: serum creatinine less than upper limit of normal (ULN) or calculated creatinine clearance at least 60 mL/min; 10) ECG is normal, there is no non-healing wounds on the body; 11) had not received previous treatment anticancer drugs, or had only received for previous non-metastatic tumors adjuvant or neoadjuvant chemotherapy, but when you start to study treatment has ended more than 6 months; 12) have conducted previous surgery patients required to study treatment was started more than four weeks, and the patient had recovered; 13) have an intact uterus in women prior to enrollment in the study must have a negative pregnancy test result (unless it is already 24 months of amenorrhea) within 28 days. If the pregnancy test from the first administration more than seven days, urine pregnancy test is required for authentication (less than 7 days before the first dose); 14) previous to biological agents, particularly E.coli genetically engineered products without serious allergic reactions; 15) signed informed consent.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n1) pregnancy, breast-feeding women, or female patients of childbearing potential but did not take contraceptive measures;2) existing severe acute infection and is not controlled; or purulent and chronic infection, delayed healing wounds; 3) the original severe heart disease, including congestive heart failure, uncontrolled high-risk arrhythmias, unstable angina, myocardial infarction, severe heart valve disease and resistant hypertension; 4) suffering from neurological and psychiatric diseases or mental disorders is not easy to control, poor compliance, and can not be described with treatment responders; primary brain or central nervous metastasis disease has not been controlled, with significant cranial hypertension or neuropsychiatric symptoms; 5) have bleeding tendencies; 6) other researchers believe that patients should not participate in the present trial.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n1) histologically confirmed (patients [NOT] not receiving a single sputum cytology diagnosis) non-small cell lung cancer patients,with wild-type EGFR [AND] and ALK-negative; 2) According to IASLC2009 new TNM staging of lung cancer stage <U+2162>B [OR] or <U+2163>, previously [NOT] untreated [OR] or relapsed after 1 year of lung cancer resection; 3) have at least one evaluable lesions,according to version 1.1 of the standard in accordance with a judgment RECIST(longest diameter on a spiral CT at least 10mm,on a regular CT longest diameter at least 20mm); 4) Male [OR] or female, aged 18 to 75 years; 5) ECOG PS 0 or 1; 6) expected survival at least 3 months; 7) adequate hematological function: absolute neutrophil count (ANC) at least 2×10^9/L [AND] and platelet count at least 100×10^9/L [AND] and hemoglobin at least 9 g/dL; 8) adequate liver function: total bilirubin less than upper limit of normal (ULN); AST [AND] and ALT less than 2.5 times upper limit of normal (ULN); alkaline phosphatase less than 5 times the upper limit of normal (ULN); 9) adequate renal function: serum creatinine less than upper limit of normal (ULN) [OR] or calculated creatinine clearance at least 60 mL/min; 10) ECG is normal, there is [NOT] no [NOT] non-healing wounds on the body; 11) had [NOT] not received previous treatment anticancer drugs, [OR] or had only received for previous [NOT] non-metastatic tumors adjuvant [OR] or neoadjuvant chemotherapy, [AND] but when you start to study treatment has ended more than 6 months; 12) have conducted previous surgery patients required to study treatment was started more than four weeks, [AND] and the patient had recovered; 13) have an intact uterus in women prior to enrollment in the study must have a negative pregnancy test result (unless it is already 24 months of amenorrhea) within 28 days. If the pregnancy test from the first administration more than seven days, urine pregnancy test is required for authentication (less than 7 days before the first dose); 14) previous to biological agents, particularly E.coli genetically engineered products [NOT] without serious allergic reactions; 15) signed informed consent.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n1) pregnancy, [OR] breast-feeding women, [OR] or female patients of childbearing potential [AND] but did [NOT] not take contraceptive measures;2) existing severe acute infection [AND] and is [NOT] not controlled; [OR] or purulent [OR] and chronic infection, delayed healing wounds; 3) the original severe heart disease, including congestive heart failure, uncontrolled high-risk arrhythmias, unstable angina, [OR] myocardial infarction, severe heart valve disease [OR] and resistant hypertension; 4) suffering from neurological [OR] and psychiatric diseases [OR] or mental disorders is [NOT] not easy to control, poor compliance, [AND] and can [NOT] not be described with treatment responders; primary brain [OR] or central nervous metastasis disease has [NOT] not been controlled, [AND] with significant cranial hypertension [OR] or neuropsychiatric symptoms; 5) have bleeding tendencies; 6) other researchers believe that patients should [NOT] not participate in the present trial.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
1) histologically confirmed (patients [NOT] not receiving a single sputum cytology diagnosis) non-small cell lung cancer patients,with wild-type EGFR [AND] and ALK-negative; 2) According to IASLC2009 new TNM staging of lung cancer stage <U+2162>B [OR] or <U+2163>, previously [NOT] untreated [OR] or relapsed after 1 year of lung cancer resection; 3) have at least one evaluable lesions,according to version 1.1 of the standard in accordance with a judgment RECIST(longest diameter on a spiral CT at least 10mm,on a regular CT longest diameter at least 20mm); 4) Male [OR] or female, aged 18 to 75 years; 5) ECOG PS 0 or 1; 6) expected survival at least 3 months; 7) adequate hematological function: absolute neutrophil count (ANC) at least 2×10^9/L [AND] and platelet count at least 100×10^9/L [AND] and hemoglobin at least 9 g/dL; 8) adequate liver function: total bilirubin less than upper limit of normal (ULN); AST [AND] and ALT less than 2.5 times upper limit of normal (ULN); alkaline phosphatase less than 5 times the upper limit of normal (ULN); 9) adequate renal function: serum creatinine less than upper limit of normal (ULN) [OR] or calculated creatinine clearance at least 60 mL/min; 10) ECG is normal, there is [NOT] no [NOT] non-healing wounds on the body; 11) had [NOT] not received previous treatment anticancer drugs, [OR] or had only received for previous [NOT] non-metastatic tumors adjuvant [OR] or neoadjuvant chemotherapy, [AND] but when you start to study treatment has ended more than 6 months; 12) have conducted previous surgery patients required to study treatment was started more than four weeks, [AND] and the patient had recovered; 13) have an intact uterus in women prior to enrollment in the study must have a negative pregnancy test result (unless it is already 24 months of amenorrhea) within 28 days. If the pregnancy test from the first administration more than seven days, urine pregnancy test is required for authentication (less than 7 days before the first dose); 14) previous to biological agents, particularly E.coli genetically engineered products [NOT] without serious allergic reactions; 15) signed informed consent.

Exclusion Criteria:
1) pregnancy, [OR] breast-feeding women, [OR] or female patients of childbearing potential [AND] but did [NOT] not take contraceptive measures;2) existing severe acute infection [AND] and is [NOT] not controlled; [OR] or purulent [OR] and chronic infection, delayed healing wounds; 3) the original severe heart disease, including congestive heart failure, uncontrolled high-risk arrhythmias, unstable angina, [OR] myocardial infarction, severe heart valve disease [OR] and resistant hypertension; 4) suffering from neurological [OR] and psychiatric diseases [OR] or mental disorders is [NOT] not easy to control, poor compliance, [AND] and can [NOT] not be described with treatment responders; primary brain [OR] or central nervous metastasis disease has [NOT] not been controlled, [AND] with significant cranial hypertension [OR] or neuropsychiatric symptoms; 5) have bleeding tendencies; 6) other researchers believe that patients should [NOT] not participate in the present trial.
