Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nWilling and able to provide written informed consent and accept study procedures and time schedule.\nAge = 18 years.\nPatients suffering from chronic heart failure (the heart failure diagnosis must have been made or confirmed by a cardiologist and/or hospital physician at any time in the patient\'s medical history).\nPatients with reduced ejection fraction (= 40%) as confirmed at any time point in the patient\'s medical history.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nUse of investigational drugs either within 5 half-lives of enrollment, or within 30 days, or until the expected pharmacodynamic effect has returned to baseline, whichever is longer.\nMajor surgery in the last 3 months prior to baseline or planned major surgery or cardiac intervention during the study.\nCancer or other significant co-morbidities implying that the patient\'s condition is unstable.\nComorbidities that can be associated with elevated natriuretic peptide (NP) levels: renal insufficiency, (eGFR < 25 ml/min/1.73 m² calculated according to MDRD formula), recent (less than 3 months) cerebral trauma or recent (less than 3 months) cerebrovascular incident, novel diagnosis or acute exacerbation of COPD within the last 3 months.\nPatients who are primarily managed and regularly followed-up by a cardiologist for their HF\nHighly frail patients whose estimated lifespan due to comorbidities by the judgement of the investigator is less than 6 months.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nWilling and able to provide written informed consent and accept study procedures and time schedule.\nAge = 18 years.\nPatients suffering from chronic heart failure (the heart failure diagnosis must have been made or confirmed by a cardiologist and/or hospital physician at any time in the patient\'s medical history).\nPatients with reduced ejection fraction (= 40%) as confirmed at any time point in the patient\'s medical history.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nUse of investigational drugs either within 5 half-lives of enrollment, [OR] or within 30 days, [OR] or until the expected pharmacodynamic effect has returned to baseline, whichever is longer.\nMajor surgery in the last 3 months prior to baseline [OR] or planned major surgery [OR] or cardiac intervention during the study.\nCancer [OR] or other significant co-morbidities implying that the patient\'s condition is unstable.\nComorbidities that can be associated with elevated natriuretic peptide (NP) levels: renal insufficiency, (eGFR < 25 ml/min/1.73 m² calculated according to MDRD formula), recent (less than 3 months) cerebral trauma [OR] or recent (less than 3 months) cerebrovascular incident, novel diagnosis [OR] or acute exacerbation of COPD within the last 3 months.\nPatients who are primarily managed and regularly followed-up by a cardiologist for their HF\nHighly frail patients whose estimated lifespan due to comorbidities by the judgement of the investigator is less than 6 months.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Willing and able to provide written informed consent and accept study procedures and time schedule.
Age = 18 years.
Patients suffering from chronic heart failure (the heart failure diagnosis must have been made or confirmed by a cardiologist and/or hospital physician at any time in the patient's medical history).
Patients with reduced ejection fraction (= 40%) as confirmed at any time point in the patient's medical history.

Exclusion Criteria:
Use of investigational drugs either within 5 half-lives of enrollment, [OR] or within 30 days, [OR] or until the expected pharmacodynamic effect has returned to baseline, whichever is longer.
Major surgery in the last 3 months prior to baseline [OR] or planned major surgery [OR] or cardiac intervention during the study.
Cancer [OR] or other significant co-morbidities implying that the patient's condition is unstable.
Comorbidities that can be associated with elevated natriuretic peptide (NP) levels: renal insufficiency, (eGFR < 25 ml/min/1.73 m² calculated according to MDRD formula), recent (less than 3 months) cerebral trauma [OR] or recent (less than 3 months) cerebrovascular incident, novel diagnosis [OR] or acute exacerbation of COPD within the last 3 months.
Patients who are primarily managed and regularly followed-up by a cardiologist for their HF
Highly frail patients whose estimated lifespan due to comorbidities by the judgement of the investigator is less than 6 months.
