Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_full/NCT02816762.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nSubjects aged 18 to 80 years old\nOverweight or obesity (BMI =25 kg/m2)\nPrevious diagnosis of type 2 diabetes, fulfilling at least one of the following criteria: 1) current treatment with oral antidiabetic drugs and/or insulin; 2) a fasting glucose value above 126 mg/dl on at least 2 occasions; 3) blood glucose level at 2 hours after an oral glucose tolerance test is equal to or more than 200 mg/dl; or 4) a glycated hemoglobin (HbA1c) level > 6.5 %\nClinical diagnosis of diabetic nephropathy, with a urinary albumin/creatinine ratio >30 mg/g and an estimated glomerular filtration rate more than 20 ml/min per 1.73 m2.\nTreatment with stable doses of angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitors, angiotensin II receptor blockers or anti-aldosterone agents in the last four weeks.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nNon diabetic nephropathy (confirmed by biopsy).\nDialysis for acute renal failure within the 6 previous months.\nEvidence in the clinic history of relevant bilateral stenosis of renal artery (> 75%)\nUrinary albumin/creatinine ratio higher than 3000 mg/g, at the baseline visit.\nSystolic blood pressure = 180 mmHg or diastolic blood pressure = 110 mm Hg at the baseline visit.\nStroke, transient ischemic attack, acute coronary syndrome, or hospitalization for heart failure worsening, within the previous 30 days.\nProfessional drivers, risk profession or respiratory failure.\nSevere daytime sleepiness (Epworth sleepiness scale >18)\nConcomitant treatment with high doses of acetylsalicylic acid (> 500 mg/day) or continuous treatment with non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs\nPrevious treatment with CPAP\nParticipation in another clinical trial within the 30 days prior to randomization.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nSubjects aged 18 to 80 years old\nOverweight [OR] or obesity (BMI =25 kg/m2)\n Previous diagnosis of type 2 diabetes, fulfilling at least one of the following criteria: 1) current treatment with oral antidiabetic drugs [OR] and/or insulin; 2) a fasting glucose value above 126 mg/dl on at least 2 occasions; 3) blood glucose level at 2 hours after an oral glucose tolerance test is equal to or more than 200 mg/dl; [OR] or 4) a glycated hemoglobin (HbA1c) level > 6.5 %\nClinical diagnosis of diabetic nephropathy, [AND] with a urinary albumin/ [OR] creatinine ratio >30 mg/g [AND] and an estimated glomerular filtration rate more than 20 ml/min per 1.73 m2.\nTreatment with stable doses of angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitors, [OR] angiotensin II receptor blockers [OR] or anti-aldosterone agents in the last four weeks.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n [NOT] Non diabetic nephropathy (confirmed by biopsy).\nDialysis for acute renal failure within the 6 previous months.\nEvidence in the clinic history of relevant bilateral stenosis of renal artery (> 75%)\nUrinary albumin/ [OR] creatinine ratio higher than 3000 mg/g, at the baseline visit.\nSystolic blood pressure = 180 mmHg [OR] or diastolic blood pressure = 110 mm Hg at the baseline visit.\nStroke, [OR] transient ischemic attack, [OR] acute coronary syndrome, [OR] or hospitalization for heart failure worsening, within the previous 30 days.\nProfessional drivers, risk profession [OR] or respiratory failure.\nSevere daytime sleepiness (Epworth sleepiness scale >18)\nConcomitant treatment with high doses of acetylsalicylic acid (> 500 mg/day) [OR] or continuous treatment with non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs\nPrevious treatment with CPAP\nParticipation in another clinical trial within the 30 days prior to randomization.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Subjects aged 18 to 80 years old
Overweight [OR] or obesity (BMI =25 kg/m2)
 Previous diagnosis of type 2 diabetes, fulfilling at least one of the following criteria: 1) current treatment with oral antidiabetic drugs [OR] and/or insulin; 2) a fasting glucose value above 126 mg/dl on at least 2 occasions; 3) blood glucose level at 2 hours after an oral glucose tolerance test is equal to or more than 200 mg/dl; [OR] or 4) a glycated hemoglobin (HbA1c) level > 6.5 %
Clinical diagnosis of diabetic nephropathy, [AND] with a urinary albumin/ [OR] creatinine ratio >30 mg/g [AND] and an estimated glomerular filtration rate more than 20 ml/min per 1.73 m2.
Treatment with stable doses of angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitors, [OR] angiotensin II receptor blockers [OR] or anti-aldosterone agents in the last four weeks.

Exclusion Criteria:
 [NOT] Non diabetic nephropathy (confirmed by biopsy).
Dialysis for acute renal failure within the 6 previous months.
Evidence in the clinic history of relevant bilateral stenosis of renal artery (> 75%)
Urinary albumin/ [OR] creatinine ratio higher than 3000 mg/g, at the baseline visit.
Systolic blood pressure = 180 mmHg [OR] or diastolic blood pressure = 110 mm Hg at the baseline visit.
Stroke, [OR] transient ischemic attack, [OR] acute coronary syndrome, [OR] or hospitalization for heart failure worsening, within the previous 30 days.
Professional drivers, risk profession [OR] or respiratory failure.
Severe daytime sleepiness (Epworth sleepiness scale >18)
Concomitant treatment with high doses of acetylsalicylic acid (> 500 mg/day) [OR] or continuous treatment with non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs
Previous treatment with CPAP
Participation in another clinical trial within the 30 days prior to randomization.
