Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPrior Myocardial Infarction and\nSustained monomorphic VT documented on 12-lead ECG or rhythm strip terminated by pharmacologic means or DC cardioversion\n=3 episodes of VT treated with antitachycardia pacing (ATP), at least one of which was symptomatic\n= 5 episodes of VT treated with antitachycardia pacing (ATP) regardless of symptoms\n=1 appropriate ICD shocks,\n=3 VT episodes within 24 hours\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nUnable or unwilling to provide informed consent.\nActive ischemia (acute thrombus diagnosed by coronary angiography, or dynamic ST segment changes demonstrated on ECG) or another reversible cause of VT (e.g. drug-induced arrhythmia), had recent acute coronary syndrome within 30 days, coronary revascularization (<90 days bypass surgery, <30 days percutaneous coronary intervention), or have CCS functional class IV angina. Note that biomarker level elevation alone after ventricular arrhythmias does not denote acute coronary syndrome or active ischemia.\nAre ineligible to take the antiarrhythmic drug to which they would be assigned due to allergy, intolerance or contraindication\nAre known to have protruding left ventricular thrombus or mechanical aortic and mitral valves\nHave had a prior catheter ablation procedure for VT\nAre in renal failure (Creatinine clearance <15 mL/min), have NYHA Functional class IV heart failure, or a systemic illness likely to limit survival to <1 year\nHave had recent ST elevation myocardial infarction or non-ST elevation MI (< 30 days); note that biomarker elevation alone after ventricular arrhythmias does not denote MI.\nAre pregnant.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPrior Myocardial Infarction [AND] and\nSustained monomorphic VT documented on 12-lead ECG [OR] or rhythm strip terminated by pharmacologic means [OR] or DC cardioversion\n =3 episodes of VT treated with antitachycardia pacing (ATP), at least one of which was symptomatic\n = 5 episodes of VT treated with antitachycardia pacing (ATP) regardless of symptoms\n =1 appropriate ICD shocks,\n =3 VT episodes within 24 hours\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nUnable or unwilling to provide informed consent.\nActive ischemia (acute thrombus diagnosed by coronary angiography, [OR] or dynamic ST segment changes demonstrated on ECG) [OR] or another reversible cause of VT (e.g. drug-induced arrhythmia), had recent acute coronary syndrome within 30 days, coronary revascularization (<90 days bypass surgery, <30 days percutaneous coronary intervention), [OR] or have CCS functional class IV angina. Note that biomarker level elevation alone after ventricular arrhythmias does [NOT] not denote acute coronary syndrome [OR] or active ischemia.\nAre ineligible to take the antiarrhythmic drug to which they would be assigned due to allergy, [OR] intolerance [OR] or contraindication\nAre known to have protruding left ventricular thrombus [OR] or mechanical aortic [OR] and mitral valves\n Have had a prior catheter ablation procedure for VT\n Are in renal failure (Creatinine clearance <15 mL/min), have NYHA Functional class IV heart failure, [OR] or a systemic illness likely to [NOT] limit survival to <1 year\n Have had recent ST elevation myocardial infarction [OR] or [NOT] non-ST elevation MI (< 30 days); note that biomarker elevation alone after ventricular arrhythmias does [NOT] not denote MI.\n Are pregnant.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Prior Myocardial Infarction [AND] and
Sustained monomorphic VT documented on 12-lead ECG [OR] or rhythm strip terminated by pharmacologic means [OR] or DC cardioversion
 =3 episodes of VT treated with antitachycardia pacing (ATP), at least one of which was symptomatic
 = 5 episodes of VT treated with antitachycardia pacing (ATP) regardless of symptoms
 =1 appropriate ICD shocks,
 =3 VT episodes within 24 hours

Exclusion Criteria:
Unable or unwilling to provide informed consent.
Active ischemia (acute thrombus diagnosed by coronary angiography, [OR] or dynamic ST segment changes demonstrated on ECG) [OR] or another reversible cause of VT (e.g. drug-induced arrhythmia), had recent acute coronary syndrome within 30 days, coronary revascularization (<90 days bypass surgery, <30 days percutaneous coronary intervention), [OR] or have CCS functional class IV angina. Note that biomarker level elevation alone after ventricular arrhythmias does [NOT] not denote acute coronary syndrome [OR] or active ischemia.
Are ineligible to take the antiarrhythmic drug to which they would be assigned due to allergy, [OR] intolerance [OR] or contraindication
Are known to have protruding left ventricular thrombus [OR] or mechanical aortic [OR] and mitral valves
 Have had a prior catheter ablation procedure for VT
 Are in renal failure (Creatinine clearance <15 mL/min), have NYHA Functional class IV heart failure, [OR] or a systemic illness likely to [NOT] limit survival to <1 year
 Have had recent ST elevation myocardial infarction [OR] or [NOT] non-ST elevation MI (< 30 days); note that biomarker elevation alone after ventricular arrhythmias does [NOT] not denote MI.
 Are pregnant.
