Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nST-segment elevation acute myocardial infarction patients during the first 12 hours of sympton onset;\nIntention to perform primary percutaneous coronary intervention;\nSigned informed consent;\nPatient eligible for transradial and transfemoral primary percutaneous coronary intervention, being pre-requisites: (a) familiarity of the operator with the radial and femoral techniques using vascular closure devices, (b) agreement of the operator to use the access route determined by the randomization process.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nLess than 18 years of age;\nPregnancy;\nChronic use of vitamin K antagonists or direct thrombin inhibitors, or oral Xa-factor antagonists;\nHypersensitivity to antiplatelet and/or anticoagulant drugs;\nActive bleeding or high bleeding risk (severe liver failure, active peptic ulcer, creatinine clearance < 30 mL/min, platelets count < 100.000 mm3);\nUncontrolled systemic hypertension;\nCardiogenic shock;\nPrevious myocardial revascularization surgery with = 1 internal mammary or radial artery graft;\nDocumented chronic peripheral arterial disease preventing the use of the femoral technique;\nSevere concomitant disease with life expectancy below 12 months;\nParticipation in drug or devices investigative clinical trials in the last 30 days;\nMedical, geographic or social conditions impairing the participation in the study or inability to understand and sign the informed consent term.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nST-segment elevation acute myocardial infarction patients during the first 12 hours of sympton onset;\nIntention to perform primary percutaneous coronary intervention;\nSigned informed consent;\nPatient eligible for transradial [OR] and transfemoral primary percutaneous coronary intervention, being pre-requisites: (a) familiarity of the operator with the radial [OR] and femoral techniques using vascular closure devices, (b) agreement of the operator to use the access route determined by the randomization process.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nLess than 18 years of age;\nPregnancy;\nChronic use of vitamin K antagonists [OR] or direct thrombin inhibitors, [OR] or oral Xa-factor antagonists;\nHypersensitivity to antiplatelet [OR] and/or anticoagulant drugs;\nActive bleeding [OR] or high bleeding risk (severe liver failure, active peptic ulcer, [OR] creatinine clearance < 30 mL/min, [OR] platelets count < 100.000 mm3);\nUncontrolled systemic hypertension;\nCardiogenic shock;\nPrevious myocardial revascularization surgery [AND] with = 1 internal mammary [OR] or radial artery graft;\nDocumented chronic peripheral arterial disease [NOT] preventing the use of the femoral technique;\nSevere concomitant disease [AND] with life expectancy below 12 months;\nParticipation in drug [OR] or devices investigative clinical trials in the last 30 days;\nMedical, [OR] geographic [OR] or social conditions impairing the participation in the study or inability to understand and sign the informed consent term.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
ST-segment elevation acute myocardial infarction patients during the first 12 hours of sympton onset;
Intention to perform primary percutaneous coronary intervention;
Signed informed consent;
Patient eligible for transradial [OR] and transfemoral primary percutaneous coronary intervention, being pre-requisites: (a) familiarity of the operator with the radial [OR] and femoral techniques using vascular closure devices, (b) agreement of the operator to use the access route determined by the randomization process.

Exclusion Criteria:
Less than 18 years of age;
Pregnancy;
Chronic use of vitamin K antagonists [OR] or direct thrombin inhibitors, [OR] or oral Xa-factor antagonists;
Hypersensitivity to antiplatelet [OR] and/or anticoagulant drugs;
Active bleeding [OR] or high bleeding risk (severe liver failure, active peptic ulcer, [OR] creatinine clearance < 30 mL/min, [OR] platelets count < 100.000 mm3);
Uncontrolled systemic hypertension;
Cardiogenic shock;
Previous myocardial revascularization surgery [AND] with = 1 internal mammary [OR] or radial artery graft;
Documented chronic peripheral arterial disease [NOT] preventing the use of the femoral technique;
Severe concomitant disease [AND] with life expectancy below 12 months;
Participation in drug [OR] or devices investigative clinical trials in the last 30 days;
Medical, [OR] geographic [OR] or social conditions impairing the participation in the study or inability to understand and sign the informed consent term.
