Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\noutpatients aged 18-70 years\nconfirmed diagnosis of H. pylori infection by at least one of the following methods: 13C-urea breath test, histology, rapid urease test or bacterial culture\nan intention of H. pylori eradication treatment and have written inform consent\nability to read short messages on the mobile phone\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nadvanced chronic disease that would not allow the patient to complete the treatment or follow-up or attend visits\nallergy to any of the drugs used in this study\nprevious Helicobacter Pylori eradication treatment\npregnancy or breastfeeding (female participants with childbearing potential were required to use medically accepted contraception for the duration of the study)\ntaking antibiotics or PPIs or bismuth salts within four weeks\nprevious gastrointestinal surgery\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\noutpatients aged 18-70 years\nconfirmed diagnosis of H. pylori infection by at least one of the following methods: 13C-urea breath test, [OR] histology, [OR] rapid urease test [OR] or bacterial culture\nan intention of H. pylori eradication treatment and have written inform consent\nability to read short messages on the mobile phone\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nadvanced chronic disease that would [NOT] not allow the patient to complete the treatment [OR] or follow-up [OR] or attend visits\nallergy to any of the drugs used in this study\nprevious Helicobacter Pylori eradication treatment\npregnancy [OR] or breastfeeding (female participants with childbearing potential were required to use medically accepted contraception for the duration of the study)\ntaking antibiotics [OR] or PPIs [OR] or bismuth salts within four weeks\nprevious gastrointestinal surgery<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
outpatients aged 18-70 years
confirmed diagnosis of H. pylori infection by at least one of the following methods: 13C-urea breath test, [OR] histology, [OR] rapid urease test [OR] or bacterial culture
an intention of H. pylori eradication treatment and have written inform consent
ability to read short messages on the mobile phone

Exclusion Criteria:
advanced chronic disease that would [NOT] not allow the patient to complete the treatment [OR] or follow-up [OR] or attend visits
allergy to any of the drugs used in this study
previous Helicobacter Pylori eradication treatment
pregnancy [OR] or breastfeeding (female participants with childbearing potential were required to use medically accepted contraception for the duration of the study)
taking antibiotics [OR] or PPIs [OR] or bismuth salts within four weeks
previous gastrointestinal surgery
