eceive antineoplastic or immunomodulatory therapy in the past 12 months.\nPatients with a previous use of IFN anti hepatitis B virus treatment or have NAs drug resistance.\nPatients who can\'t come back to clinic for follow-up on schedule.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nCHB patients [AND] who had received single NAs for more than 12 months.\nHepatitis B e antigen (HBeAg)-negative.\nHepatitis B surface antigen (HBsAg) positive [AND] and <1000 IU/mL.\nHepatitis B virus DNA <100 IU/mL.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPatients with liver cirrhosis, [OR] Hepatocellular Carcinoma [OR] or AFP >2 ULN [OR] or other malignancies.\nPatients with other factors causing liver diseases.\nPregnant [OR] and lactating women.\nPatients with concomitant HIV infection [OR] or congenital immune deficiency diseases.\nPatients with diabetes, [OR] autoimmune diseases.\nPatients with important organ dysfunctions.\nPatients with serious complications (e.g., infection, [OR] hepatic encephalopathy, [OR] hepatorenal syndrome, [OR] gastrointestinal bleeding.)\nPatients who receive antineoplastic [OR] or immunomodulatory therapy in the past 12 months.\nPatients with a previous use of IFN anti hepatitis B virus treatment [OR] or have NAs drug resistance.\nPatients who can\'t come back to clinic for follow-up on schedule.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
CHB patients [AND] who had received single NAs for more than 12 months.
Hepatitis B e antigen (HBeAg)-negative.
Hepatitis B surface antigen (HBsAg) positive [AND] and <1000 IU/mL.
Hepatitis B virus DNA <100 IU/mL.

Exclusion Criteria:
Patients with liver cirrhosis, [OR] Hepatocellular Carcinoma [OR] or AFP >2 ULN [OR] or other malignancies.
Patients with other factors causing liver diseases.
Pregnant [OR] and lactating women.
Patients with concomitant HIV infection [OR] or congenital immune deficiency diseases.
Patients with diabetes, [OR] autoimmune diseases.
Patients with important organ dysfunctions.
Patients with serious complications (e.g., infection, [OR] hepatic encephalopathy, [OR] hepatorenal syndrome, [OR] gastrointestinal bleeding.)
Patients who receive antineoplastic [OR] or immunomodulatory therapy in the past 12 months.
Patients with a previous use of IFN anti hepatitis B virus treatment [OR] or have NAs drug resistance.
Patients who can't come back to clinic for follow-up on schedule.
