Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nA positive history of chronic claudication,\nExercise-limiting claudication established by history and direct observation during a screening walking test administered by the evaluating vascular surgeon,\nArterial occlusive disease per ankle Brachial index measurements and/or other imaging modalities,\nStable blood pressure regimen, stable lipid regimen, stable diabetes regimen and risk factor control for 6 weeks.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nRest pain or tissue loss due to PAD (Fontaine stage III and IV),\nacute lower extremity ischemic event secondary to thromboembolic disease or acute trauma,\nWalking capacity significantly limited by conditions other than claudication including leg (joint/musculoskeletal, neurologic) and systemic (heart, lung disease) pathology,\nCurrent use of either ACE inhibitors or angiotensin II receptor blockers,\nChronic kidney disease with estimated Glomerular Filtration Rate < 30 ml/min/1.73 m2,\nHistory of bilateral severe renal artery stenosis and 7) History of angioedema related to previous ACE-inhibitor treatment or known hypersensitivity to ramipril or other ACE inhibitors.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nA positive history of chronic claudication,\nExercise-limiting claudication established by history [AND] and direct observation during a screening walking test administered by the evaluating vascular surgeon,\nArterial occlusive disease per ankle Brachial index measurements [OR] and/or other imaging modalities,\nStable blood pressure regimen, stable lipid regimen, stable diabetes regimen [AND] and risk factor control for 6 weeks.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nRest pain [OR] or tissue loss due to PAD (Fontaine stage III and IV),\nacute lower extremity ischemic event secondary to thromboembolic disease [OR] or acute trauma,\nWalking capacity significantly limited by conditions other than claudication including leg (joint/ [OR] musculoskeletal, [OR] neurologic) [OR] and systemic (heart, [OR] lung disease) pathology,\nCurrent use of either ACE inhibitors [OR] or angiotensin II receptor blockers,\nChronic kidney disease [AND] with estimated Glomerular Filtration Rate < 30 ml/min/1.73 m2,\nHistory of bilateral severe renal artery stenosis [AND] and 7) History of angioedema related to previous ACE-inhibitor treatment [OR] or known hypersensitivity to ramipril [OR] or other ACE inhibitors.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
A positive history of chronic claudication,
Exercise-limiting claudication established by history [AND] and direct observation during a screening walking test administered by the evaluating vascular surgeon,
Arterial occlusive disease per ankle Brachial index measurements [OR] and/or other imaging modalities,
Stable blood pressure regimen, stable lipid regimen, stable diabetes regimen [AND] and risk factor control for 6 weeks.

Exclusion Criteria:
Rest pain [OR] or tissue loss due to PAD (Fontaine stage III and IV),
acute lower extremity ischemic event secondary to thromboembolic disease [OR] or acute trauma,
Walking capacity significantly limited by conditions other than claudication including leg (joint/ [OR] musculoskeletal, [OR] neurologic) [OR] and systemic (heart, [OR] lung disease) pathology,
Current use of either ACE inhibitors [OR] or angiotensin II receptor blockers,
Chronic kidney disease [AND] with estimated Glomerular Filtration Rate < 30 ml/min/1.73 m2,
History of bilateral severe renal artery stenosis [AND] and 7) History of angioedema related to previous ACE-inhibitor treatment [OR] or known hypersensitivity to ramipril [OR] or other ACE inhibitors.
