hs after RYGB\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nFasting plasma glucose > 7,0 mM, HbA1c > 48 mmol/mol 3 months after RYGB.\nDysregulated thyroid diseases, use of antithyroid treatment.\nLate diabetic complications as retinopathy, [OR] renal insufficiency, [OR] neuropathy [OR] or previous pancreatitis.\nComplications to RYGB. Documented reactive hypoglycaemia, severe dumping (vomiting, [OR] diarrhea, [OR] severe abdominal pain after food intake).\nCholecystectomy<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Uncomplicated RYGB performed minimum 3 months prior to the study.
Fasting plasma glucose < 7,0 mM, HbA1c < 48 mmol/mol 3 months after RYGB

Exclusion Criteria:
Fasting plasma glucose > 7,0 mM, HbA1c > 48 mmol/mol 3 months after RYGB.
Dysregulated thyroid diseases, use of antithyroid treatment.
Late diabetic complications as retinopathy, [OR] renal insufficiency, [OR] neuropathy [OR] or previous pancreatitis.
Complications to RYGB. Documented reactive hypoglycaemia, severe dumping (vomiting, [OR] diarrhea, [OR] severe abdominal pain after food intake).
Cholecystectomy
