Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nOf either gender, aged ≥19 and ≤70 years \nAtopic dermatitis subjects who are coincident with Hanifin and Rajka diagnosis criteria \nSubacute and chronic atopic subjects who have atopic dermatitis symptoms continually at least 6 months \nSubjects with over moderate atopic dermatitis (SCORAD score > 20) \nSubjects who understand and voluntarily sign an informed consent form \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nSubjects who have systemic infection \nSubjects who have human Immunodeficiency virus (HIV), hepatitis B virus (HBV), and hepatitis C virus (HCV) \nSubjects who need to take the medicine which is prohibited during this study \nSubjects who have asthma \nSubjects who can not stop treatment with topical steroids (group 1~5), oral antibiotics, whole body photochemotherapy, immunosuppressive drug within 4 weeks before the treatment visit \nPregnant, breast-feeding women or women who plan to become pregnant during this study (Females of childbearing potential must have a negative urine pregnancy test) \nSubjects who currently participate in other clinical trial or participated in other clinical trial within 30 days \nSubjects who had a serious adverse events during stem cell therapy \nSubjects who had a hypersensitivity to antibiotics or antimycotics \nSubjects who creatinine value is more than two times of the upper limit of the normal range at screening test \nSubjects who aspartate transaminase/alkaline transaminase (AST/ALT) value is more than three times of the upper limit of the normal range at screening test \nSubjects who have any other condition which the investigator judges would make patients unsuitable for study participation       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nOf either gender, aged ≥19 [AND] and ≤70 years \nAtopic dermatitis subjects who are coincident with Hanifin and Rajka diagnosis criteria \nSubacute [OR] and chronic atopic subjects [AND] who have atopic dermatitis symptoms continually at least 6 months \nSubjects with over moderate atopic dermatitis (SCORAD score > 20) \nSubjects who understand and voluntarily sign an informed consent form \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nSubjects who have systemic infection \nSubjects who have human Immunodeficiency virus (HIV), [OR] hepatitis B virus (HBV), [OR] and hepatitis C virus (HCV) \nSubjects who need to take the medicine which is [NOT] prohibited during this study \n Subjects who have asthma \nSubjects who [NOT] can [NOT] not [NOT] stop treatment with topical steroids (group 1~5), [OR] oral antibiotics, [OR] whole body photochemotherapy, [OR] immunosuppressive drug within 4 weeks before the treatment visit \nPregnant, [OR] breast-feeding women [OR] or women [AND] who plan to become pregnant during this study (Females of childbearing potential must have a negative urine pregnancy test) \nSubjects who currently participate in other clinical trial [OR] or participated in other clinical trial within 30 days \nSubjects who had a serious adverse events during stem cell therapy \n Subjects who had a hypersensitivity to antibiotics [OR] or antimycotics \n Subjects who creatinine value is more than two times of the upper limit of the normal range at screening test \n Subjects who aspartate transaminase/ [OR] alkaline transaminase (AST/ [OR] ALT) value is more than three times of the upper limit of the normal range at screening test \nSubjects who have any other condition which the investigator judges would make patients [NOT] unsuitable for study participation<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Of either gender, aged ≥19 [AND] and ≤70 years 
Atopic dermatitis subjects who are coincident with Hanifin and Rajka diagnosis criteria 
Subacute [OR] and chronic atopic subjects [AND] who have atopic dermatitis symptoms continually at least 6 months 
Subjects with over moderate atopic dermatitis (SCORAD score > 20) 
Subjects who understand and voluntarily sign an informed consent form 

Exclusion Criteria:
Subjects who have systemic infection 
Subjects who have human Immunodeficiency virus (HIV), [OR] hepatitis B virus (HBV), [OR] and hepatitis C virus (HCV) 
Subjects who need to take the medicine which is [NOT] prohibited during this study 
 Subjects who have asthma 
Subjects who [NOT] can [NOT] not [NOT] stop treatment with topical steroids (group 1~5), [OR] oral antibiotics, [OR] whole body photochemotherapy, [OR] immunosuppressive drug within 4 weeks before the treatment visit 
Pregnant, [OR] breast-feeding women [OR] or women [AND] who plan to become pregnant during this study (Females of childbearing potential must have a negative urine pregnancy test) 
Subjects who currently participate in other clinical trial [OR] or participated in other clinical trial within 30 days 
Subjects who had a serious adverse events during stem cell therapy 
 Subjects who had a hypersensitivity to antibiotics [OR] or antimycotics 
 Subjects who creatinine value is more than two times of the upper limit of the normal range at screening test 
 Subjects who aspartate transaminase/ [OR] alkaline transaminase (AST/ [OR] ALT) value is more than three times of the upper limit of the normal range at screening test 
Subjects who have any other condition which the investigator judges would make patients [NOT] unsuitable for study participation
