Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAge between 18 and 78 year-old. \nPrevious liver transplantation(more than 6 month). \nGenotype 1 and 4 infection. \nHepatitis C recurrence defined by the presence of abnormal liver function test, positive HCV-RNA, histological signs of hepatitis C recurrence. \nViral load ≥10000UI/mL. \nImmunosuppression with tacrolimus and/or mycophenolate (Prednisone use is allowed at low dose, ≤10 mg/d). \nTreatment naïve or treatment experienced (Peg-RBV or triple therapy). \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nGenotype 2, 3, 5 or 6 infection. \nDecompensated cirrhosis defined by the presence of actual or previous history of clinical decompensation including ascites, hepatic encephalopathy, variceal bleeding or spontaneous bacterial peritonitis, or a Child-Pugh B or C. \nHepatocellular carcinoma after liver transplantation. \nTotal bilirubin > 3 mg/dL. \nImmunosuppression with cyclosporine or an mTOR inhibitor (everolimus or sirolimus). \nSevere extrahepatic diseases: cardiovascular, respiratory, cerebrovascular and poorly controlled diabetes. \nPlatelets < 75 x 109 cells/L. \nNeutrophil count < 0.5 x 109 cells/L. \nHemoglobin < 9 g/dL. \nAlbumin < 3g/dL. \nHIV infection. \nHepatitis B infection. \nActive intake of toxic amounts of alcohol or recreational drugs. \nFemales who are pregnant, become to be pregnant or breastfeeding or males whose partners are pregnant, become to be pregnant or breastfeeding. \nIntake of disallowed medications including(but not limited to): \n1. Antibiotics: clarithromycin, erythromycin, telithromycin, nafcillin, rifampin \n2. Antifungals: itraconazole, ketoconazole, voriconazole \n3. Antihypertensives: nifedipine \n4. Anticonvulsants: carbamazepine, phenytoin, phenobarbital \n5. Bosentan \n6. Modafinil \n7. St.Jonh\'s Wort \n8. Immunosuppressants: cyclosporin, everolimus, sirolimus \n9. Diabetes agents: glibenclamide, glyburide \n10. Lipid lowering agents: gemfibrozil \n11. Eltrombopag \n12. Lapatinib \n13. HIV medications: efavirenz, etravirine, all ritonavir boosted and unboosted HIV protease inhibitors \n14. Statins: simvastatin, fluvastatin, rosuvastatin at doses greater than 10 mg/d, atorvastatin at doses greater than 10 mg/d.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAge between 18 and 78 year-old. \nPrevious liver transplantation(more than 6 month). \nGenotype 1 [OR] and 4 infection. \nHepatitis C recurrence defined by the presence of abnormal liver function test, positive HCV-RNA, histological signs of hepatitis C recurrence. \nViral load ≥10000UI/mL. \nImmunosuppression with tacrolimus [OR] and/or mycophenolate (Prednisone use is allowed at low dose, ≤10 mg/d). \nTreatment [NOT] naïve [OR] or treatment experienced (Peg-RBV [OR] or triple therapy). \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nGenotype 2, [OR] 3, [OR] 5 [OR] or 6 infection. \nDecompensated cirrhosis defined by the presence of actual [OR] or previous history of clinical decompensation including ascites, [OR] hepatic encephalopathy, [OR] variceal bleeding [OR] or spontaneous bacterial peritonitis, [OR] or a Child-Pugh B [OR] or C. \nHepatocellular carcinoma after liver transplantation. \nTotal bilirubin > 3 mg/dL. \nImmunosuppression with cyclosporine [OR] or an mTOR inhibitor (everolimus [OR] or sirolimus). \nSevere extrahepatic diseases: cardiovascular, [OR] respiratory, [OR] cerebrovascular [OR] and poorly controlled diabetes. \nPlatelets < 75 x 109 cells/L. \nNeutrophil count < 0.5 x 109 cells/L. \nHemoglobin < 9 g/dL. \nAlbumin < 3g/dL. \nHIV infection. \nHepatitis B infection. \nActive intake of toxic amounts of alcohol [OR] or recreational drugs. \nFemales [AND] who are pregnant, [OR] become to be pregnant [OR] or breastfeeding [OR] or males [AND] whose partners are pregnant, [OR] become to be pregnant [OR] or breastfeeding. \nIntake of disallowed medications including(but not limited to): \n1. Antibiotics: clarithromycin, [OR] erythromycin, [OR] telithromycin, [OR] nafcillin, [OR] rifampin \n2. Antifungals: itraconazole, [OR] ketoconazole, [OR] voriconazole \n3. Antihypertensives: nifedipine \n4. Anticonvulsants: carbamazepine, [OR] phenytoin, [OR] phenobarbital \n5. Bosentan \n6. Modafinil \n7. St.Jonh\'s Wort \n8. Immunosuppressants: cyclosporin, [OR] everolimus, [OR] sirolimus \n9. Diabetes agents: glibenclamide, [OR] glyburide \n10. Lipid lowering agents: gemfibrozil \n11. Eltrombopag \n12. Lapatinib \n13. HIV medications: efavirenz, [OR] etravirine, all ritonavir boosted [OR] and unboosted HIV protease inhibitors \n14. Statins: simvastatin, [OR] fluvastatin, [OR] rosuvastatin at doses greater than 10 mg/d, atorvastatin at doses greater than 10 mg/d.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Age between 18 and 78 year-old. 
Previous liver transplantation(more than 6 month). 
Genotype 1 [OR] and 4 infection. 
Hepatitis C recurrence defined by the presence of abnormal liver function test, positive HCV-RNA, histological signs of hepatitis C recurrence. 
Viral load ≥10000UI/mL. 
Immunosuppression with tacrolimus [OR] and/or mycophenolate (Prednisone use is allowed at low dose, ≤10 mg/d). 
Treatment [NOT] naïve [OR] or treatment experienced (Peg-RBV [OR] or triple therapy). 

Exclusion Criteria:
Genotype 2, [OR] 3, [OR] 5 [OR] or 6 infection. 
Decompensated cirrhosis defined by the presence of actual [OR] or previous history of clinical decompensation including ascites, [OR] hepatic encephalopathy, [OR] variceal bleeding [OR] or spontaneous bacterial peritonitis, [OR] or a Child-Pugh B [OR] or C. 
Hepatocellular carcinoma after liver transplantation. 
Total bilirubin > 3 mg/dL. 
Immunosuppression with cyclosporine [OR] or an mTOR inhibitor (everolimus [OR] or sirolimus). 
Severe extrahepatic diseases: cardiovascular, [OR] respiratory, [OR] cerebrovascular [OR] and poorly controlled diabetes. 
Platelets < 75 x 109 cells/L. 
Neutrophil count < 0.5 x 109 cells/L. 
Hemoglobin < 9 g/dL. 
Albumin < 3g/dL. 
HIV infection. 
Hepatitis B infection. 
Active intake of toxic amounts of alcohol [OR] or recreational drugs. 
Females [AND] who are pregnant, [OR] become to be pregnant [OR] or breastfeeding [OR] or males [AND] whose partners are pregnant, [OR] become to be pregnant [OR] or breastfeeding. 
Intake of disallowed medications including(but not limited to): 
1. Antibiotics: clarithromycin, [OR] erythromycin, [OR] telithromycin, [OR] nafcillin, [OR] rifampin 
2. Antifungals: itraconazole, [OR] ketoconazole, [OR] voriconazole 
3. Antihypertensives: nifedipine 
4. Anticonvulsants: carbamazepine, [OR] phenytoin, [OR] phenobarbital 
5. Bosentan 
6. Modafinil 
7. St.Jonh's Wort 
8. Immunosuppressants: cyclosporin, [OR] everolimus, [OR] sirolimus 
9. Diabetes agents: glibenclamide, [OR] glyburide 
10. Lipid lowering agents: gemfibrozil 
11. Eltrombopag 
12. Lapatinib 
13. HIV medications: efavirenz, [OR] etravirine, all ritonavir boosted [OR] and unboosted HIV protease inhibitors 
14. Statins: simvastatin, [OR] fluvastatin, [OR] rosuvastatin at doses greater than 10 mg/d, atorvastatin at doses greater than 10 mg/d.
