Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nProbable or definite diagnosis of autoimmune hepatitis according to the International Autoimmune Hepatitis Study Group criteria\nFirst presentation of AIH requiring treatment according to the current EASL guidelines\nAge = 18 years\nMust provide informed consent and agree to comply with the trial protocol\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nOverlap syndrome with Primary Sclerosing Cholangitis (PSC) or Primary Biliary Cholangitis (PBC) (Paris criteria, strong positive Anti-Mitochondrial Antibodies (AMA), past liver biopsy or cholangiographic findings compatible with PBC or PSC).\nPresentation with acute liver failure, defined as presence of hepatic encephalopathy and coagulopathy (INR > 1.5)\nCurrent treatment with prednisone/prednisolone and/or immunosuppressive medication for an indication other than autoimmune hepatitis\nCurrent systemic infection\nOther clinically significant medical conditions that could interfere with the trial\nIf female of childbearing potential: known pregnancy, or unwilling to practice anticontraceptive measures.\nHistory of noncompliance with medical regimens, or patients who are considered to be potentially unreliable or unable to participate\nMental instability or incompetence, such that the validity of informed consent or compliance with the trial is uncertain\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nProbable [OR] or definite diagnosis of autoimmune hepatitis according to the International Autoimmune Hepatitis Study Group criteria\nFirst presentation of AIH requiring treatment according to the current EASL guidelines\nAge = 18 years\nMust provide informed consent and agree to comply with the trial protocol\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nOverlap syndrome [AND] with Primary Sclerosing Cholangitis (PSC) [OR] or Primary Biliary Cholangitis (PBC) (Paris criteria, strong positive Anti-Mitochondrial Antibodies (AMA), past liver biopsy [OR] or cholangiographic findings compatible with PBC [OR] or PSC).\nPresentation with acute liver failure, defined as presence of hepatic encephalopathy [OR] and coagulopathy (INR > 1.5)\nCurrent treatment with prednisone/ [OR] prednisolone [OR] and/or immunosuppressive medication for an indication other than autoimmune hepatitis\nCurrent systemic infection\nOther clinically significant medical conditions that could interfere with the trial\nIf female [AND] of childbearing potential: known pregnancy, [OR] or unwilling to practice anticontraceptive measures.\nHistory of [NOT] noncompliance with medical regimens, [OR] or patients who are considered to be potentially unreliable [OR] or unable to participate\nMental instability [OR] or incompetence, such that the validity of informed consent or compliance with the trial is uncertain<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Probable [OR] or definite diagnosis of autoimmune hepatitis according to the International Autoimmune Hepatitis Study Group criteria
First presentation of AIH requiring treatment according to the current EASL guidelines
Age = 18 years
Must provide informed consent and agree to comply with the trial protocol

Exclusion Criteria:
Overlap syndrome [AND] with Primary Sclerosing Cholangitis (PSC) [OR] or Primary Biliary Cholangitis (PBC) (Paris criteria, strong positive Anti-Mitochondrial Antibodies (AMA), past liver biopsy [OR] or cholangiographic findings compatible with PBC [OR] or PSC).
Presentation with acute liver failure, defined as presence of hepatic encephalopathy [OR] and coagulopathy (INR > 1.5)
Current treatment with prednisone/ [OR] prednisolone [OR] and/or immunosuppressive medication for an indication other than autoimmune hepatitis
Current systemic infection
Other clinically significant medical conditions that could interfere with the trial
If female [AND] of childbearing potential: known pregnancy, [OR] or unwilling to practice anticontraceptive measures.
History of [NOT] noncompliance with medical regimens, [OR] or patients who are considered to be potentially unreliable [OR] or unable to participate
Mental instability [OR] or incompetence, such that the validity of informed consent or compliance with the trial is uncertain
