Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAll patients admitted to the Duke CICU, who require intubation and sedation for mechanical ventilation that is expected to be >24 hours in duration will be included, unless they meet the specified exclusion criteria.\nPatients intubated within one hour prior to care transition to the CICU will also be screened for inclusion.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nExclusion criteria include patients following resuscitation from cardiac arrest who are treated on the cooling protocol\npatients who have suffered a neurologic event (seizure, stroke) or who have baseline dementia, both of which could limit delirium assessment\npatients with child class B and C liver disease\npatients with known allergy to study medications.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAll patients admitted to the Duke CICU, [AND] who require intubation [AND] and sedation for mechanical ventilation that is expected to be >24 hours in duration will be included, unless they meet the specified exclusion criteria.\nPatients intubated within one hour prior to care transition to the CICU will also be screened for inclusion.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nExclusion criteria include patients following resuscitation from cardiac arrest [AND] who are treated on the cooling protocol\npatients who have suffered a neurologic event (seizure, [OR] stroke) [OR] or who have baseline dementia, both of which could limit delirium assessment\npatients with child class B [OR] and C liver disease\npatients with known allergy to study medications.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
All patients admitted to the Duke CICU, [AND] who require intubation [AND] and sedation for mechanical ventilation that is expected to be >24 hours in duration will be included, unless they meet the specified exclusion criteria.
Patients intubated within one hour prior to care transition to the CICU will also be screened for inclusion.

Exclusion Criteria:
Exclusion criteria include patients following resuscitation from cardiac arrest [AND] who are treated on the cooling protocol
patients who have suffered a neurologic event (seizure, [OR] stroke) [OR] or who have baseline dementia, both of which could limit delirium assessment
patients with child class B [OR] and C liver disease
patients with known allergy to study medications.
