Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nClinical and radiologic diagnosis of primary knee osteoarthritis (Kellgren & Lawrence I, II or III); \nCapability to understand the Informed Consent Form; \nChronic pain for at least 3 months prior to inclusion, measured by VAS. (VAS 4 or above); \nAbsence of skin injures, infections or tumor in the target knee; \nAvailability to comply with the visits. \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nHistory of spinal cord stenosis or clinical symptoms of lumbar radiculopathy; \nHistory or onset neurological diseases; \nGeneralized pain or fibromyalgia; \nInability to walk; \nHistory of knee surgery in the target knee; \nSecondary causes of osteoarthritis; \nUse of statins and quinolones in the previous year; \nUncontrolled and ongoing psychiatric diseases; \nInvasive knee treatments with hyaluronic acid infusion, corticosteroids and anaesthetics, in the target knee, up to 6 months previous to study inclusion.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nClinical [OR] and radiologic diagnosis of primary knee osteoarthritis (Kellgren & Lawrence I, II or III); \nCapability to understand the Informed Consent Form; \nChronic pain  for at least 3 months prior to inclusion, measured by VAS. (VAS 4 or above); \n[NOT] Absence of skin injures, [OR] infections [OR] or tumor in the target knee; \nAvailability to comply with the visits. \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nHistory of spinal cord stenosis [OR] or clinical symptoms of lumbar radiculopathy; \nHistory [OR] or onset neurological diseases; \nGeneralized pain [OR] or fibromyalgia; \n [NOT] Inability to walk; \nHistory of knee surgery in the target knee; \nSecondary causes of osteoarthritis; \nUse of statins [OR] and quinolones in the previous year; \nUncontrolled [OR] and ongoing psychiatric diseases; \nInvasive knee treatments [AND] with hyaluronic acid infusion, [OR] corticosteroids [OR] and anaesthetics, in the target knee, up to 6 months previous to study inclusion.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Clinical [OR] and radiologic diagnosis of primary knee osteoarthritis (Kellgren & Lawrence I, II or III); 
Capability to understand the Informed Consent Form; 
Chronic pain  for at least 3 months prior to inclusion, measured by VAS. (VAS 4 or above); 
[NOT] Absence of skin injures, [OR] infections [OR] or tumor in the target knee; 
Availability to comply with the visits. 

Exclusion Criteria:
History of spinal cord stenosis [OR] or clinical symptoms of lumbar radiculopathy; 
History [OR] or onset neurological diseases; 
Generalized pain [OR] or fibromyalgia; 
 [NOT] Inability to walk; 
History of knee surgery in the target knee; 
Secondary causes of osteoarthritis; 
Use of statins [OR] and quinolones in the previous year; 
Uncontrolled [OR] and ongoing psychiatric diseases; 
Invasive knee treatments [AND] with hyaluronic acid infusion, [OR] corticosteroids [OR] and anaesthetics, in the target knee, up to 6 months previous to study inclusion.
