Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nMale or female = 18 years of age at Visit 1.\nSweat chloride equal or greater than 60 mEq/L by quantitative pilocarpine iontophoresis test.\nTwo well-characterized mutations in the cystic fibrosis transmembrane conductance regulator (CFTR) gene\nAbnormal nasal potential difference (NPD) as measured by a change in NPD in response to a low chloride solution and isoproterenol of less than -5 mV.\nDocumentation of the presence of an acute pulmonary exacerbation, based on CF Foundation guidelines, as diagnosed by a faculty member of the Denver Adult CF Program.\nRespiratory culture(s) demonstrating evidence of Pseudomonas aeruginosa or Achromobacter species airway infection.\nSubject is able to produce sputum, undergo phlebotomy, and provide written consent.\nThe subject\'s treating physician has determined that they should receive either tobramycin or colistin intravenously as one of the designated agents for their APE treatment. Subjects who are able to receive either tobramycin or colistin as part of their antibiotic regimen will be randomized into one of three arms. If a treating physician deems that a subject cannot receive tobramycin due to vestibular toxicity, ototoxicity or bacterial resistance, the subject will be randomized to either standard or PK-adjusted colistin.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nNA\n\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nMale [OR] or female = 18 years of age at Visit 1.\nSweat chloride equal or greater than 60 mEq/L by quantitative pilocarpine iontophoresis test.\nTwo well-characterized mutations in the cystic fibrosis transmembrane conductance regulator (CFTR) gene\nAbnormal nasal potential difference (NPD) as measured by a change in NPD in response to a low chloride solution [OR] and isoproterenol of less than -5 mV.\nDocumentation of the presence of an acute pulmonary exacerbation, based on CF Foundation guidelines, as diagnosed by a faculty member of the Denver Adult CF Program.\nRespiratory culture(s) demonstrating evidence of Pseudomonas aeruginosa [OR] or Achromobacter species airway infection.\nSubject is able to produce sputum, undergo phlebotomy, and provide written consent.\nThe subject\'s treating physician has determined that they should receive either tobramycin [OR] or colistin intravenously as one of the designated agents for their APE treatment. Subjects who are able to receive either tobramycin [OR] or colistin as part of their antibiotic regimen will be randomized into one of three arms. If a treating physician deems that a subject cannot receive tobramycin due to vestibular toxicity, [OR] ototoxicity [OR] or bacterial resistance, the subject will be randomized to either standard [OR] or PK-adjusted colistin.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nNA<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Male [OR] or female = 18 years of age at Visit 1.
Sweat chloride equal or greater than 60 mEq/L by quantitative pilocarpine iontophoresis test.
Two well-characterized mutations in the cystic fibrosis transmembrane conductance regulator (CFTR) gene
Abnormal nasal potential difference (NPD) as measured by a change in NPD in response to a low chloride solution [OR] and isoproterenol of less than -5 mV.
Documentation of the presence of an acute pulmonary exacerbation, based on CF Foundation guidelines, as diagnosed by a faculty member of the Denver Adult CF Program.
Respiratory culture(s) demonstrating evidence of Pseudomonas aeruginosa [OR] or Achromobacter species airway infection.
Subject is able to produce sputum, undergo phlebotomy, and provide written consent.
The subject's treating physician has determined that they should receive either tobramycin [OR] or colistin intravenously as one of the designated agents for their APE treatment. Subjects who are able to receive either tobramycin [OR] or colistin as part of their antibiotic regimen will be randomized into one of three arms. If a treating physician deems that a subject cannot receive tobramycin due to vestibular toxicity, [OR] ototoxicity [OR] or bacterial resistance, the subject will be randomized to either standard [OR] or PK-adjusted colistin.

Exclusion Criteria:
NA
