Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nHabitual exerciser defined as = 30 minutes of at least moderate or high intensity exercise = 3 times per week. After consent, and at the subsequent screening visit, a VO2 max test will be performed, and subjects with a low value (< 35 mL/kg/min) will be excluded (screen failure). Based on our previous experience, we anticipate that <10% of the subjects will fall into this category\nMen: (0.006012 x H3) + (14.6 x W) + 604 = TBV\nWomen: (0.005835 x H3) + (15 x W) + 183 = TBV [H=height in inches; W=weight in pounds]\nHas access to transportation to visit the blood collection facility and to return to Stony Brook for all study visits.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nAny significant acute or chronic medical illness or problem, including, but not limited to, diabetes, hypertension, cardiac disease, asthma, chronic obstructive lung disease\nCurrent or recent (last 60 days) tobacco or nicotine use\nHistory of sickle cell trait or disease or any other acquired or hereditary hematological abnormality\nHistory of fainting or other significant adverse reaction during phlebotomy or donation of blood\nKnown prolonged QTc (or evidence of such at screening) on electrocardiogram defined as >470 ms\nKnown or suspected illicit drug or alcohol abuse\nKnown or suspected HIV, Hepatitis B, or Hepatitis C infection\nHistory of thrombophilia or anticoagulant therapy\nPregnancy\nObesity defined as BMI>30\nRecent history of blood donation: a) Single whole blood unit donation within the past 8 weeks; b) Double RBC donation by apheresis within the past 16 weeks; or c) Plasma donation by apheresis within the past 4 weeks\nInadequate RBC mass based on TBV <4500 ml (above) or screening Hb <14 g/dL\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nHabitual exerciser defined as = 30 minutes of at least moderate [OR] or high intensity exercise = 3 times per week. After consent, and at the subsequent screening visit, a VO2 max test will be performed, and subjects with a low value (< 35 mL/kg/min) will be [NOT] excluded (screen failure). Based on our previous experience, we anticipate that <10% of the subjects will fall into this category\nMen: (0.006012 x H3) + (14.6 x W) + 604 = TBV\nWomen: (0.005835 x H3) + (15 x W) + 183 = TBV [H=height in inches; W=weight in pounds]\nHas access to transportation to visit the blood collection facility and to return to Stony Brook for all study visits.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nAny significant acute [OR] or chronic medical illness [OR] or problem, including, but not limited to, diabetes, [OR] hypertension, [OR] cardiac disease, [OR] asthma, [OR] chronic obstructive lung disease\nCurrent [OR] or recent (last 60 days) tobacco [OR] or nicotine use\nHistory of sickle cell trait [OR] or disease [OR] or any other acquired [OR] or hereditary hematological abnormality\nHistory of fainting [OR] or other significant adverse reaction during phlebotomy [OR] or donation of blood\n Known prolonged QTc [OR] (or evidence of such at screening) on electrocardiogram defined as >470 ms\n Known [OR] or suspected illicit drug [OR] or alcohol abuse\n Known [OR] or suspected HIV, [OR] Hepatitis B, [OR] or Hepatitis C infection\n History of thrombophilia [OR] or anticoagulant therapy\n Pregnancy\n Obesity defined as BMI>30\n Recent history of blood donation: a) Single whole blood unit donation within the past 8 weeks; b) Double RBC donation by apheresis within the past 16 weeks; [OR] or c) Plasma donation by apheresis within the past 4 weeks\n Inadequate RBC mass based on TBV <4500 ml (above) [OR] or screening Hb <14 g/dL<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Habitual exerciser defined as = 30 minutes of at least moderate [OR] or high intensity exercise = 3 times per week. After consent, and at the subsequent screening visit, a VO2 max test will be performed, and subjects with a low value (< 35 mL/kg/min) will be [NOT] excluded (screen failure). Based on our previous experience, we anticipate that <10% of the subjects will fall into this category
Men: (0.006012 x H3) + (14.6 x W) + 604 = TBV
Women: (0.005835 x H3) + (15 x W) + 183 = TBV [H=height in inches; W=weight in pounds]
Has access to transportation to visit the blood collection facility and to return to Stony Brook for all study visits.

Exclusion Criteria:
Any significant acute [OR] or chronic medical illness [OR] or problem, including, but not limited to, diabetes, [OR] hypertension, [OR] cardiac disease, [OR] asthma, [OR] chronic obstructive lung disease
Current [OR] or recent (last 60 days) tobacco [OR] or nicotine use
History of sickle cell trait [OR] or disease [OR] or any other acquired [OR] or hereditary hematological abnormality
History of fainting [OR] or other significant adverse reaction during phlebotomy [OR] or donation of blood
 Known prolonged QTc [OR] (or evidence of such at screening) on electrocardiogram defined as >470 ms
 Known [OR] or suspected illicit drug [OR] or alcohol abuse
 Known [OR] or suspected HIV, [OR] Hepatitis B, [OR] or Hepatitis C infection
 History of thrombophilia [OR] or anticoagulant therapy
 Pregnancy
 Obesity defined as BMI>30
 Recent history of blood donation: a) Single whole blood unit donation within the past 8 weeks; b) Double RBC donation by apheresis within the past 16 weeks; [OR] or c) Plasma donation by apheresis within the past 4 weeks
 Inadequate RBC mass based on TBV <4500 ml (above) [OR] or screening Hb <14 g/dL
