 of the knee or chondrocalcinosis, hemochromatosis, inflammatory arthritis, arthropathy of the knee associated with juxta-articular Paget\'s disease of the femur or tibia, hemophilic arthropathy, infectious arthritis, Charcot\'s knee joint, villonodular synovitis, and synovial chondromatosis\nPatients taking immunosuppressant medication\nPatients with abnormal hematology or serum chemistry lab results\nPatients receiving injection to treatment knee within 2 months of study enrollment\nBMI greater than 35 or less than 20\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients with symptomatic FAI\nClinical [OR] and radiographic evidence of FAI\nPatients able to provide consent to study participation\nCompletion of 6 weeks of physical therapy program\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nEstablished Osteoarthritis (Kellgren-Lawrence > 3)\nMinimum joint space > 2 mm as measured on AP radiograph\nHip dysplasia (center edge angle < 20° on AP radiograph)\nPatients with clinically significant cardiovascular, [OR] renal, [OR] hepatic, [OR] endocrine disease, [OR] cancer [OR] or diabetes\nPatients with ongoing infection including HIV [OR] and Hepatitis\nPatient with history of osteomyelitis/ [OR] septic arthritis\nAnticoagulation therapy\nPatients who are pregnant [OR] or breast feeding\nPatients with systemic, [OR] rheumatic [OR] or inflammatory disease of the knee [OR] or chondrocalcinosis, [OR] hemochromatosis, [OR] inflammatory arthritis, [OR] arthropathy of the knee associated with juxta-articular Paget\'s disease [OR] of the femur [OR] or tibia, [OR] hemophilic arthropathy, [OR] infectious arthritis, [OR] Charcot\'s knee joint, [OR] villonodular synovitis, [OR] and synovial chondromatosis\nPatients taking immunosuppressant medication\nPatients with abnormal hematology [OR] or serum chemistry lab results\nPatients receiving injection to treatment knee within 2 months of study enrollment\nBMI greater than 35 [OR] or less than 20<|eot_id|>']
