Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\npatients affected by mono-lateral symptomatic knee articular degenerative pathology with history of chronic (for at least 4 months) pain or swelling;\nimaging findings of degenerative changes of the joint (osteoarthritis or chondropathy with Kellgren Lawrence Score from 0 to 3 at X-ray evaluation).\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nage > 80 years;\nKellgren-Lawrence score at X-ray evaluation > 3;\nmajor axial deviation (varus >5°, valgus > 5°),\nsystemic disorders such as diabetes, rheumatoid arthritis, haematological diseases (coagulopathy), severe cardiovascular diseases, infections, immunodepression;\npatients in therapy with anticoagulants or antiaggregants;\nuse of NSAIDs in the 5 days before blood donation;\npatients with Hb values < 11 g/dl and platelet values < 150,000/mmc.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\npatients affected by mono-lateral symptomatic knee articular degenerative pathology [AND] with history of chronic (for at least 4 months) pain [OR] or swelling;\nimaging findings of degenerative changes of the joint (osteoarthritis [OR] or chondropathy [AND] with Kellgren Lawrence Score from 0 to 3 at X-ray evaluation).\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nage > 80 years;\nKellgren-Lawrence score at X-ray evaluation > 3;\nmajor axial deviation (varus >5°, valgus > 5°),\nsystemic disorders such as diabetes, [OR] rheumatoid arthritis, [OR] haematological diseases (coagulopathy), severe cardiovascular diseases, [OR] infections, [OR] immunodepression;\npatients in therapy with anticoagulants [OR] or antiaggregants;\nuse of NSAIDs in the 5 days before blood donation;\npatients with Hb values < 11 g/dl [AND] and platelet values < 150,000/mmc.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
patients affected by mono-lateral symptomatic knee articular degenerative pathology [AND] with history of chronic (for at least 4 months) pain [OR] or swelling;
imaging findings of degenerative changes of the joint (osteoarthritis [OR] or chondropathy [AND] with Kellgren Lawrence Score from 0 to 3 at X-ray evaluation).

Exclusion Criteria:
age > 80 years;
Kellgren-Lawrence score at X-ray evaluation > 3;
major axial deviation (varus >5°, valgus > 5°),
systemic disorders such as diabetes, [OR] rheumatoid arthritis, [OR] haematological diseases (coagulopathy), severe cardiovascular diseases, [OR] infections, [OR] immunodepression;
patients in therapy with anticoagulants [OR] or antiaggregants;
use of NSAIDs in the 5 days before blood donation;
patients with Hb values < 11 g/dl [AND] and platelet values < 150,000/mmc.
