ients aged 18 to 85 years\nDiagnosed with Major Depressive Disorder, unipolar [OR] or bipolar depression\nUndergoing ECT for treatment of their symptoms\nCurrently residing in Manitoba\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nRelative contraindications to ECT therapy (recent MI [OR] or CVA, increased intracranial pressure, [OR] intracranial mass lesion, [OR] intracranial aneurysm, [OR] epilepsy, known cardiac arrhythmia, [OR] pheochromocytoma, [OR] pregnancy)\nContraindications to etomidate (sepsis, primary [OR] or secondary adrenal insufficiency, [OR] porphyria)\nDSM-V diagnosis of a lifetime history of psychotic spectrum disorder\nDrug [OR] or alcohol dependence, [OR] or abuse within the past 3 months, soy-bean oil allergy<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Adults patients aged 18 to 85 years
Diagnosed with Major Depressive Disorder, unipolar [OR] or bipolar depression
Undergoing ECT for treatment of their symptoms
Currently residing in Manitoba

Exclusion Criteria:
Relative contraindications to ECT therapy (recent MI [OR] or CVA, increased intracranial pressure, [OR] intracranial mass lesion, [OR] intracranial aneurysm, [OR] epilepsy, known cardiac arrhythmia, [OR] pheochromocytoma, [OR] pregnancy)
Contraindications to etomidate (sepsis, primary [OR] or secondary adrenal insufficiency, [OR] porphyria)
DSM-V diagnosis of a lifetime history of psychotic spectrum disorder
Drug [OR] or alcohol dependence, [OR] or abuse within the past 3 months, soy-bean oil allergy
