ychiatric disorder that, in the opinion of the investigator, may interfere with study assessments or compliance\nCurrent or historical evidence of any clinically significant disease or condition that, in the opinion of the investigator, may increase the risk of surgery or complicate the subject\'s postoperative course.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nEnglish speaking\nbetween 18 and 75 years old\nAmerican Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA) 1-3 patients undergoing primary total hip arthroplasty\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nASA 4 [OR] or 5\nrevision hip arthroplasty\ndiagnosis of chronic pain\ndaily chronic opioid use (over 3 months of continuous opioid use)\n [NOT] inability to communicate pain scores [OR] or need for analgesia\nacute hip fracture\nInfection at the site of block placement\nAge under 18 years old [OR] or greater than 75 years old\nPregnant women\nIntolerance/ [OR] allergy to local anesthetics\nWeight <50 kg\nSuspected, [OR] or known addiction to [OR] or abuse of illicit drug(s), [OR] prescription medicine(s), [OR] or alcohol within the past 2 years.\nUncontrolled anxiety, [OR] schizophrenia, [OR] or other psychiatric disorder that, in the opinion of the investigator, may interfere with study assessments [OR] or compliance\nCurrent [OR] or historical evidence of any clinically significant disease [OR] or condition that, in the opinion of the investigator, may increase the risk of surgery [OR] or complicate the subject\'s postoperative course.<|eot_id|>']
