File: NCT02934269 

Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_full/NCT02934269.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nHealthy male and/or female subjects between the ages of 18 and 55 years, and a body mass index (BMI) of ≥ 18 and ≤ 33 kg/m2 with body weight ≥ 50 and ≤ 90 kg at screening. \nFemales must have been surgically sterilized (hysterectomy, bilateral oophorectomy, or bilateral salpingo-oophorectomy; proper documentation required) at least 6 months before screening, or be postmenopausal (defined as 24 consecutive months without menses before screening, with a follicle-stimulating hormone [FSH] level of > 40 IU/L at screening). \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nExposure/treatment to an investigational (new chemical entity) or marketed drug or biologic within 30 days preceding the first dose administration, or five half-lives of that investigational drug or biologic, if known (whichever is longer). \nDonation blood or serum within 8 weeks before the first dose administration to a blood bank or blood donation center. \nHistory of alcohol or drug abuse (as defined by the current version of the DSM) within 2 years before the first dose administration, or positive alcohol or drug screen. \nVaccination within 30 days prior to the first dose administration or has plans to receive a vaccination during the course of the study (including the follow phone call on Day 105).       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nHealthy male [OR] and/or female subjects between the ages of 18 and 55 years, [AND] and a body mass index (BMI) of ≥ 18 [AND] and ≤ 33 kg/m2 [AND] with body weight ≥ 50 [AND] and ≤ 90 kg at screening. \nFemales must have been surgically sterilized (hysterectomy, [OR] bilateral oophorectomy, [OR] or bilateral salpingo-oophorectomy; proper documentation required) at least 6 months before screening, [OR] or be postmenopausal (defined as 24 consecutive months [NOT] without menses before screening, [AND] with a follicle-stimulating hormone [FSH] level of > 40 IU/L at screening). \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nExposure/ [OR] treatment to an investigational (new chemical entity) [OR] or marketed drug [OR] or biologic within 30 days preceding the first dose administration, [OR] or five half-lives of that investigational drug [OR] or biologic, if known (whichever is longer). \nDonation blood [OR] or serum within 8 weeks before the first dose administration to a blood bank [OR] or blood donation center. \nHistory of alcohol [OR] or drug abuse (as defined by the current version of the DSM) within 2 years before the first dose administration, [OR] or positive alcohol [OR] or drug screen. \nVaccination within 30 days prior to the first dose administration [OR] or has plans to receive a vaccination during the course of the study (including the follow phone call on Day 105).<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Healthy male [OR] and/or female subjects between the ages of 18 and 55 years, [AND] and a body mass index (BMI) of ≥ 18 [AND] and ≤ 33 kg/m2 [AND] with body weight ≥ 50 [AND] and ≤ 90 kg at screening. 
Females must have been surgically sterilized (hysterectomy, [OR] bilateral oophorectomy, [OR] or bilateral salpingo-oophorectomy; proper documentation required) at least 6 months before screening, [OR] or be postmenopausal (defined as 24 consecutive months [NOT] without menses before screening, [AND] with a follicle-stimulating hormone [FSH] level of > 40 IU/L at screening). 

Exclusion Criteria:
Exposure/ [OR] treatment to an investigational (new chemical entity) [OR] or marketed drug [OR] or biologic within 30 days preceding the first dose administration, [OR] or five half-lives of that investigational drug [OR] or biologic, if known (whichever is longer). 
Donation blood [OR] or serum within 8 weeks before the first dose administration to a blood bank [OR] or blood donation center. 
History of alcohol [OR] or drug abuse (as defined by the current version of the DSM) within 2 years before the first dose administration, [OR] or positive alcohol [OR] or drug screen. 
Vaccination within 30 days prior to the first dose administration [OR] or has plans to receive a vaccination during the course of the study (including the follow phone call on Day 105).
