Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nInformed consent of parent(s) or legal guardian; informed consent or assent of subject as applicable.\nMale or female children between the ages of 10 and 35 years with congenital heart disease that has been palliated with a Fontan circulation.\nAbility of perform a maximal exercise test as defined by a respiratory exchange ratio (RER) greater than 1.0 at the time of maximal exercise\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nThe use of beta blockers within 2 months of randomization\nPatients actively listed for transplantation at time of entry into the study or anticipated to undergo heart transplantation, interventional catheterization, or corrective cardiac surgery during the 7 months following entry into the study\nSustained or symptomatic ventricular dysrhythmias uncontrolled by drug therapy or the use of an implantable defibrillator, and/or significant cardiac conduction defects, e.g., 2nd degree or 3rd degree AV block, or sick sinus syndrome, unless a functioning pacemaker is in place\nUncorrected obstructive or severe regurgitant valve disease, nondilated cardiomyopathy, or significant systemic ventricular outflow obstruction\nKnown renovascular hypertension or evidence of pulmonary hypertension (pulmonary vascular resistance > 6 Wood units) unresponsive to vasodilator agents such as oxygen, nitroprusside, or nitric oxide\nHistory or current clinical evidence of moderate-to-severe fixed obstructive pulmonary disease or severe reactive airway diseases (e.g., asthma) requiring hospitalization within the past 2 years or patient currently using long-term inhaled bronchodilators\nRenal, hepatic, gastrointestinal, or biliary disorder that could impair absorption, metabolism or excretion of orally administered medication\nConcurrent terminal illness or other severe disease (e.g., active neoplasm) or other significant laboratory value(s) which, in the opinion of the investigator, could preclude participation or survival\nEndocrine disorders such as primary aldosteronism, pheochromocytoma, hyper- or hypothyroidism, insulin-dependent diabetes mellitus\nUnwillingness or inability to cooperate, or for the parents or guardians to give consent, or for the child to give assent, or any condition of sufficient severity to impair cooperation in the study\nPregnancy or possible pregnancy at time of randomization, or female of child bearing potential who are lactating, or sexually active and not taking adequate contraceptive precautions (e.g., intrauterine device or oral contraceptives for 3 months prior to entry into the study)\nUse of an investigational drug within 30 days of randomization, or within 5 half-lives of the investigational drug (the longer period will apply)\nHistory of drug sensitivity or allergic reaction to alpha-blockers or beta-blockers\nUse of any of the following medications within two weeks of randomization: MAO inhibitors, Calcium channel blockers, alpha blockers, beta blockers, disopyramide, flecainide, encainide, moricizine, propafenone, sotalol, or beta adrenergic agonists\nHospital admission for protein losing enteropathy or plastic bronchitis within 3 months of randomization\nActive and/or chronic protein losing enteropathy or plastic bronchitis (on inhaled medication to control the plastic bronchitis).\nHypoalbuminemia defined as serum albumin <2.0g/dL\nRenal dysfunction defined as serum creatinine >2.0mg/dL\nHepatic dysfunction defined as serum AST and/or ALT> 3 times upper limit of normal (approximately 120 IU/L however, will vary depending on age),\nSignificant anemia or polycythemia defined as hemoglobin >18gm/dL or hemoglobin <7gm/dL\nSeverely elevated serum BNP defined as BNP>300pg/ml\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nInformed consent of parent(s) or legal guardian; informed consent or assent of subject as applicable.\nMale [OR] or female children between the ages of 10 and 35 years [AND] with congenital heart disease [AND] that has been palliated with a Fontan circulation.\nAbility of perform a maximal exercise test as defined by a respiratory exchange ratio (RER) greater than 1.0 at the time of maximal exercise\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nThe use of beta blockers within 2 months of randomization\nPatients actively listed for transplantation at time of entry into the study [OR] or anticipated to undergo heart transplantation, [OR] interventional catheterization, [OR] or corrective cardiac surgery during the 7 months following entry into the study\nSustained [OR] or symptomatic ventricular dysrhythmias uncontrolled by drug therapy [OR] or the use of an implantable defibrillator, [OR] and/or significant cardiac conduction defects, e.g., 2nd degree [OR] or 3rd degree AV block, [OR] or sick sinus syndrome, unless a functioning pacemaker is in place\nUncorrected obstructive [OR] or severe regurgitant valve disease, [OR] nondilated cardiomyopathy, [OR] or significant systemic ventricular outflow obstruction\nKnown renovascular hypertension [OR] or evidence of pulmonary hypertension (pulmonary vascular resistance > 6 Wood units) unresponsive to vasodilator agents such as oxygen, [OR] nitroprusside, [OR] or nitric oxide\nHistory [OR] or current clinical evidence of moderate- [OR] to-severe fixed obstructive pulmonary disease [OR] or severe reactive airway diseases (e.g., asthma) requiring hospitalization within the past 2 years [OR] or patient currently using long-term inhaled bronchodilators\nRenal, [OR] hepatic, [OR] gastrointestinal, [OR] or biliary disorder that could impair absorption, [OR] metabolism [OR] or excretion of orally administered medication\nConcurrent terminal illness [OR] or other severe disease (e.g., active neoplasm) [OR] or other significant laboratory value(s) which, in the opinion of the investigator, could [NOT] preclude participation or survival\nEndocrine disorders such as primary aldosteronism, [OR] pheochromocytoma, [OR] hyper- [OR] or hypothyroidism, [OR] insulin-dependent diabetes mellitus\nUnwillingness [OR] or [NOT] inability to cooperate, or for the parents or guardians to give consent, or for the child to give assent, or any condition of sufficient severity to [NOT] impair cooperation in the study\nPregnancy [OR] or possible pregnancy at time of randomization, [OR] or female [AND] of child bearing potential [AND] who are lactating, [OR] or sexually active [AND] and [NOT] not taking adequate contraceptive precautions (e.g., intrauterine device [OR] or oral contraceptives for 3 months prior to entry into the study)\nUse of an investigational drug within 30 days of randomization, [OR] or within 5 half-lives of the investigational drug (the longer period will apply)\nHistory of drug sensitivity [OR] or allergic reaction to alpha-blockers [OR] or beta-blockers\nUse of any of the following medications within two weeks of randomization: MAO inhibitors, [OR] Calcium channel blockers, [OR] alpha blockers, [OR] beta blockers, [OR] disopyramide, [OR] flecainide, [OR] encainide, [OR] moricizine, [OR] propafenone, [OR] sotalol, [OR] or beta adrenergic agonists\nHospital admission for protein losing enteropathy [OR] or plastic bronchitis within 3 months of randomization\nActive [OR] and/or chronic protein losing enteropathy [OR] or plastic bronchitis (on inhaled medication to control the plastic bronchitis).\nHypoalbuminemia defined as serum albumin <2.0g/dL\nRenal dysfunction defined as serum creatinine >2.0mg/dL\n Hepatic dysfunction defined as serum AST [OR] and/or ALT> 3 times upper limit of normal (approximately 120 IU/L however, will vary depending on age),\n Significant anemia [OR] or polycythemia defined as hemoglobin >18gm/dL [OR] or hemoglobin <7gm/dL\n Severely elevated serum BNP defined as BNP>300pg/ml<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Informed consent of parent(s) or legal guardian; informed consent or assent of subject as applicable.
Male [OR] or female children between the ages of 10 and 35 years [AND] with congenital heart disease [AND] that has been palliated with a Fontan circulation.
Ability of perform a maximal exercise test as defined by a respiratory exchange ratio (RER) greater than 1.0 at the time of maximal exercise

Exclusion Criteria:
The use of beta blockers within 2 months of randomization
Patients actively listed for transplantation at time of entry into the study [OR] or anticipated to undergo heart transplantation, [OR] interventional catheterization, [OR] or corrective cardiac surgery during the 7 months following entry into the study
Sustained [OR] or symptomatic ventricular dysrhythmias uncontrolled by drug therapy [OR] or the use of an implantable defibrillator, [OR] and/or significant cardiac conduction defects, e.g., 2nd degree [OR] or 3rd degree AV block, [OR] or sick sinus syndrome, unless a functioning pacemaker is in place
Uncorrected obstructive [OR] or severe regurgitant valve disease, [OR] nondilated cardiomyopathy, [OR] or significant systemic ventricular outflow obstruction
Known renovascular hypertension [OR] or evidence of pulmonary hypertension (pulmonary vascular resistance > 6 Wood units) unresponsive to vasodilator agents such as oxygen, [OR] nitroprusside, [OR] or nitric oxide
History [OR] or current clinical evidence of moderate- [OR] to-severe fixed obstructive pulmonary disease [OR] or severe reactive airway diseases (e.g., asthma) requiring hospitalization within the past 2 years [OR] or patient currently using long-term inhaled bronchodilators
Renal, [OR] hepatic, [OR] gastrointestinal, [OR] or biliary disorder that could impair absorption, [OR] metabolism [OR] or excretion of orally administered medication
Concurrent terminal illness [OR] or other severe disease (e.g., active neoplasm) [OR] or other significant laboratory value(s) which, in the opinion of the investigator, could [NOT] preclude participation or survival
Endocrine disorders such as primary aldosteronism, [OR] pheochromocytoma, [OR] hyper- [OR] or hypothyroidism, [OR] insulin-dependent diabetes mellitus
Unwillingness [OR] or [NOT] inability to cooperate, or for the parents or guardians to give consent, or for the child to give assent, or any condition of sufficient severity to [NOT] impair cooperation in the study
Pregnancy [OR] or possible pregnancy at time of randomization, [OR] or female [AND] of child bearing potential [AND] who are lactating, [OR] or sexually active [AND] and [NOT] not taking adequate contraceptive precautions (e.g., intrauterine device [OR] or oral contraceptives for 3 months prior to entry into the study)
Use of an investigational drug within 30 days of randomization, [OR] or within 5 half-lives of the investigational drug (the longer period will apply)
History of drug sensitivity [OR] or allergic reaction to alpha-blockers [OR] or beta-blockers
Use of any of the following medications within two weeks of randomization: MAO inhibitors, [OR] Calcium channel blockers, [OR] alpha blockers, [OR] beta blockers, [OR] disopyramide, [OR] flecainide, [OR] encainide, [OR] moricizine, [OR] propafenone, [OR] sotalol, [OR] or beta adrenergic agonists
Hospital admission for protein losing enteropathy [OR] or plastic bronchitis within 3 months of randomization
Active [OR] and/or chronic protein losing enteropathy [OR] or plastic bronchitis (on inhaled medication to control the plastic bronchitis).
Hypoalbuminemia defined as serum albumin <2.0g/dL
Renal dysfunction defined as serum creatinine >2.0mg/dL
 Hepatic dysfunction defined as serum AST [OR] and/or ALT> 3 times upper limit of normal (approximately 120 IU/L however, will vary depending on age),
 Significant anemia [OR] or polycythemia defined as hemoglobin >18gm/dL [OR] or hemoglobin <7gm/dL
 Severely elevated serum BNP defined as BNP>300pg/ml
