Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAn average defecation frequency (DF) of <3 per week based on a 3-week defecation diary (patient-reported)\nMeet at least one other criterion of the Rome-IV criteria for idiopathic constipation based on the 3-week defecation diary (1)\nRefractory to conservative treatment\nAge: 14-80 years\nStraining during =25% of defecations\nLumpy or hard stools in =25% of defecations\nSensation of incomplete evacuation for =25% of defecations\nSensation of anorectal obstruction/blockage for =25% of defecations\nManual manoeuvres to facilitate =25% of defecations\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nObstructed outlet syndrome (objectified by defeacography)\nIrritable bowel syndrome (Rome-IV criteria for irritable bowel syndrome)\nCongenital or organic bowel pathology\nRectal prolapse\nAnatomical limitations preventing placement of an electrode\nSkin and perineal disease with risk of infection\nPrevious large bowel/rectal surgery\nStoma\nCoexisting neurological disease\nSignificant psychological co-morbidity as assessed subjectively by the investigator\nBeing or attempting to become pregnant during study follow-up\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAn average defecation frequency (DF) of <3 per week based on a 3-week defecation diary (patient-reported)\nMeet at least one other criterion of the Rome-IV criteria for idiopathic constipation based on the 3-week defecation diary (1)\nRefractory to conservative treatment\nAge: 14-80 years\nStraining during =25% of defecations\nLumpy [OR] or hard stools in =25% of defecations\n Sensation of [NOT] incomplete evacuation for =25% of defecations\nSensation of anorectal obstruction/ [OR] blockage for =25% of defecations\nManual manoeuvres to facilitate =25% of defecations\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nObstructed outlet syndrome (objectified by defeacography)\nIBS (Rome-IV criteria for irritable bowel syndrome)\nCongenital [OR] or organic bowel pathology\nRectal prolapse\nAnatomical limitations [NOT] preventing placement of an electrode\nSkin [OR] and perineal disease with risk of infection\nPrevious large bowel/ [OR] rectal surgery\nStoma\nCoexisting neurological disease\nSignificant psychological co-morbidity as assessed subjectively by the investigator\nBeing [OR] or attempting to become pregnant during study follow-up<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
An average defecation frequency (DF) of <3 per week based on a 3-week defecation diary (patient-reported)
Meet at least one other criterion of the Rome-IV criteria for idiopathic constipation based on the 3-week defecation diary (1)
Refractory to conservative treatment
Age: 14-80 years
Straining during =25% of defecations
Lumpy [OR] or hard stools in =25% of defecations
 Sensation of [NOT] incomplete evacuation for =25% of defecations
Sensation of anorectal obstruction/ [OR] blockage for =25% of defecations
Manual manoeuvres to facilitate =25% of defecations

Exclusion Criteria:
Obstructed outlet syndrome (objectified by defeacography)
IBS (Rome-IV criteria for irritable bowel syndrome)
Congenital [OR] or organic bowel pathology
Rectal prolapse
Anatomical limitations [NOT] preventing placement of an electrode
Skin [OR] and perineal disease with risk of infection
Previous large bowel/ [OR] rectal surgery
Stoma
Coexisting neurological disease
Significant psychological co-morbidity as assessed subjectively by the investigator
Being [OR] or attempting to become pregnant during study follow-up
