nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients with craniotomy [AND] for supratentorial tumors under general anesthesia\nAmerican Society of Anaesthesiologists (ASA) 2 [AND] and stable ASA 3 patients\nElective surgery\nPatients with Glasgow Coma Scale (GCS) 15/15\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPatients with a history of allergy [OR] or hypersensitivity to tramadol.\nHistory of epilepsy [OR] or convulsions due to any reason.\nChronic usage of analgesic drugs.\n Patients using monoamine oxidase inhibitors.\n Patients with clinical signs of raised ICP.\nObesity (women [AND] with a body mass index >35 kg/m2 [OR] or men [AND] with a body mass index >42 kg/m2)\nLanguage barrier.\nPatients taking B-blockers [OR] or Ca channel blockers.\n Patients above 65 years of age ( Physiology difference)<|eot_id|>']
