Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nFulfills NIH criteria for bariatric surgery\nPlanned operation of laparoscopic Roux-en Y gastric bypass (LRYGB) or laparoscopic sleeve gastrectomy (LSG) as primary bariatric procedure\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nBMI <35 and > 60 kg/m2\nInability to walk (bed-bound or wheelchair dependence)\nopen abdominal surgeries except simple appendectomy and common OB/GYN procedures in the pelvis (hysterectomy, C-section, and oophorectomy, tubal ligation)\nlaparoscopic bowel or solid organ resection except laparoscopic cholecystectomy\nventral hernia repair with mesh\nPreoperative chronic opiate use for chronic pain defined as opiate usage at least 60 mg/day of morphine equivalent for = 3 months (as defined by International Association for the Study of Pain22) in the one year period prior to the bariatric surgery\nThe American Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA) score > 3\nHistory of hypersensitivity or adverse reaction to bupivacaine or narcotics\nInability to speak English\nventral hernia repair\nCholecystectomy\nhiatal hernia repair with posterior cruroplasty\nextensive lysis of adhesions\nother procedures that mandate addition of "trocar(s)" or "feeding tube"\nAddition of trocar(s) or conversion of surgery to hand-assisted or open\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nFulfills NIH criteria for bariatric surgery\nPlanned operation of laparoscopic Roux-en Y gastric bypass (LRYGB) [OR] or laparoscopic sleeve gastrectomy (LSG) as primary bariatric procedure\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nBMI <35 [OR] and > 60 kg/m2\nInability to walk (bed-bound [OR] or wheelchair dependence)\nopen abdominal surgeries except simple appendectomy [OR] and common OB/GYN procedures in the pelvis (hysterectomy, [OR] C-section, [OR] and oophorectomy, [OR] tubal ligation)\nlaparoscopic bowel [OR] or solid organ resection except laparoscopic cholecystectomy\nventral hernia repair with mesh\nPreoperative chronic opiate use for chronic pain defined as opiate usage at least 60 mg/day of morphine equivalent for = 3 months (as defined by International Association for the Study of Pain22) in the one year period prior to the bariatric surgery\nThe American Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA) score > 3\nHistory of hypersensitivity [OR] or adverse reaction to bupivacaine [OR] or narcotics\n [NOT] Inability to speak English\nventral hernia repair\nCholecystectomy\nhiatal hernia repair [AND] with posterior cruroplasty\nextensive lysis of adhesions\nother procedures that mandate addition of "trocar(s)" [OR] or "feeding tube"\n Addition of trocar(s) [OR] or conversion of surgery to hand-assisted [OR] or open<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Fulfills NIH criteria for bariatric surgery
Planned operation of laparoscopic Roux-en Y gastric bypass (LRYGB) [OR] or laparoscopic sleeve gastrectomy (LSG) as primary bariatric procedure

Exclusion Criteria:
BMI <35 [OR] and > 60 kg/m2
Inability to walk (bed-bound [OR] or wheelchair dependence)
open abdominal surgeries except simple appendectomy [OR] and common OB/GYN procedures in the pelvis (hysterectomy, [OR] C-section, [OR] and oophorectomy, [OR] tubal ligation)
laparoscopic bowel [OR] or solid organ resection except laparoscopic cholecystectomy
ventral hernia repair with mesh
Preoperative chronic opiate use for chronic pain defined as opiate usage at least 60 mg/day of morphine equivalent for = 3 months (as defined by International Association for the Study of Pain22) in the one year period prior to the bariatric surgery
The American Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA) score > 3
History of hypersensitivity [OR] or adverse reaction to bupivacaine [OR] or narcotics
 [NOT] Inability to speak English
ventral hernia repair
Cholecystectomy
hiatal hernia repair [AND] with posterior cruroplasty
extensive lysis of adhesions
other procedures that mandate addition of "trocar(s)" [OR] or "feeding tube"
 Addition of trocar(s) [OR] or conversion of surgery to hand-assisted [OR] or open
