-aminotransferase (ALAT), aspartate-aminotransferase (ASAT), gamma-glutamyl transferase (gammaGT), alkalic phosphatase (AP), bilirubin, amylase, lipase, cystatin C, creatinine, white blood cell count, haemoglobin, platelet count, prothrombin time, aPTT, fibrinogen, thrombin time, factors II,V,VII and X\nUse of therapeutic or recreational drugs influencing plasmatic coagulation\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nMotor complete tetraplegia for at least 3 months\nAge from 18 to 74 years\nBody mass index (BMI) from 18 to 35kg/m2\nInformed consent as documented by signature\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nAny anti-coagulation therapy (apart from rivaroxaban for second objective)\nHypersensitivity [OR] or allergy to factor Xa inhibitors\nAcute bacterial endocarditis\nBleeding disorder\nClinically relevant active bleeding\nGastrointestinal ulcer [OR] or tumor\nHepatic dysfunction [AND] with increased bleeding risk\nRenal failure [OR] / patients undergoing dialysis\nPregnancy [OR] and breast feeding\nGastrectomy, [OR] biliopancreatic diversion, [OR] resection [OR] or re-routing of small intestines\nFeeding tube\nRecent blood donation\nAbnormalities of laboratory values: alanine-aminotransferase (ALAT), aspartate-aminotransferase (ASAT), gamma-glutamyl transferase (gammaGT), alkalic phosphatase (AP), bilirubin, amylase, [OR] lipase, [OR] cystatin C, creatinine, white blood cell count, haemoglobin, platelet count, prothrombin time, [OR] aPTT, [OR] fibrinogen, [OR] thrombin time, factors II,V,VII and X\nUse of therapeutic [OR] or recreational drugs influencing plasmatic coagulation<|eot_id|>']
