Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nControlled hypertension: systolic BP < 150 and diastolic BP < 90 mmHg in persons aged 60 years or older, systolic BP < 140 and diastolic BP < 90 mmHg in persons 40 through 59 years according to the JNC 8th guideline\nEvidence of diastolic dysfunction showing E/E\' > 10\nThe patient agrees to the study protocol and the schedule of clinical and echocardiographic follow-up, and provides informed, written consent, as approved by the appropriate Institutional Review Board/Ethical Committee of the respective clinical site\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nUnwillingness or inability to comply with the procedures described in this protocol\nPlanned cardiac surgery or planned major non-cardiac surgery within the study period.\nStroke or coronary revascularization in the past 6 months.\nClinically significant pulmonary disease.\nUntreated hyperthyroidism, or hypothyroidism.\nA diagnosis of cancer (other than superficial squamous or basal cell skin cancer) in the past 3 years or current treatment for the active cancer.\nFemale of child-bearing potential who do not use adequate contraception and women who are pregnant or breast-feeding\nAny clinically significant abnormality identified at the screening visit, physical examination, laboratory tests, or electrocardiogram which, in the judgment of the Investigator, would preclude safe completion of the study.\nLV ejection fraction < 50%.\nSignificant renal disease manifested by serum creatinine > 2.5 mg/dL\nHepatic disease or biliary tract obstruction, or significant hepatic enzyme elevation (ALT or AST > 3 times upper limit of normal).\nHistory of intolerance to ARB or amlodipine.\nHypertrophic or restrictive cardiomyopathy.\nModerate or severe valvular disease.\nConstrictive pericarditis\nAtrial fibrillation with a heart rate > 120/min.\nSitting systolic BP < 100 mmHg\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nControlled hypertension: systolic BP < 150 [AND] and diastolic BP < 90 mmHg in persons aged 60 years or older, systolic BP < 140 [AND] and diastolic BP < 90 mmHg in persons 40 through 59 years according to the JNC 8th guideline\nEvidence of diastolic dysfunction showing E/E\' > 10\nThe patient agrees to the study protocol and the schedule of clinical and echocardiographic follow-up, and provides informed, written consent, as approved by the appropriate Institutional Review Board/Ethical Committee of the respective clinical site\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nUnwillingness [OR] or [NOT] inability to comply with the procedures described in this protocol\nPlanned cardiac surgery [OR] or planned major [NOT] non-cardiac surgery within the study period.\nStroke [OR] or coronary revascularization in the past 6 months.\nClinically significant pulmonary disease.\nUntreated hyperthyroidism, [OR] or hypothyroidism.\nA diagnosis of cancer (other than superficial squamous [OR] or basal cell skin cancer) in the past 3 years [OR] or current treatment for the active cancer.\nFemale [AND] of child-bearing potential [AND] who do [NOT] not use adequate contraception [AND] and women [AND] who are pregnant [OR] or breast-feeding\nAny clinically significant abnormality identified at the screening visit, [OR] physical examination, [OR] laboratory tests, [OR] or electrocardiogram which, in the judgment of the Investigator, would [NOT] preclude safe completion of the study.\nLV ejection fraction < 50%.\nSignificant renal disease manifested by serum creatinine > 2.5 mg/dL\nHepatic disease [OR] or biliary tract obstruction, [OR] or significant hepatic enzyme elevation (ALT [OR] or AST > 3 times upper limit of normal).\nHistory of intolerance to ARB [OR] or amlodipine.\nHypertrophic [OR] or restrictive cardiomyopathy.\nModerate [OR] or severe valvular disease.\nConstrictive pericarditis\nAtrial fibrillation [AND] with a heart rate > 120/min.\nSitting systolic BP < 100 mmHg<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Controlled hypertension: systolic BP < 150 [AND] and diastolic BP < 90 mmHg in persons aged 60 years or older, systolic BP < 140 [AND] and diastolic BP < 90 mmHg in persons 40 through 59 years according to the JNC 8th guideline
Evidence of diastolic dysfunction showing E/E' > 10
The patient agrees to the study protocol and the schedule of clinical and echocardiographic follow-up, and provides informed, written consent, as approved by the appropriate Institutional Review Board/Ethical Committee of the respective clinical site

Exclusion Criteria:
Unwillingness [OR] or [NOT] inability to comply with the procedures described in this protocol
Planned cardiac surgery [OR] or planned major [NOT] non-cardiac surgery within the study period.
Stroke [OR] or coronary revascularization in the past 6 months.
Clinically significant pulmonary disease.
Untreated hyperthyroidism, [OR] or hypothyroidism.
A diagnosis of cancer (other than superficial squamous [OR] or basal cell skin cancer) in the past 3 years [OR] or current treatment for the active cancer.
Female [AND] of child-bearing potential [AND] who do [NOT] not use adequate contraception [AND] and women [AND] who are pregnant [OR] or breast-feeding
Any clinically significant abnormality identified at the screening visit, [OR] physical examination, [OR] laboratory tests, [OR] or electrocardiogram which, in the judgment of the Investigator, would [NOT] preclude safe completion of the study.
LV ejection fraction < 50%.
Significant renal disease manifested by serum creatinine > 2.5 mg/dL
Hepatic disease [OR] or biliary tract obstruction, [OR] or significant hepatic enzyme elevation (ALT [OR] or AST > 3 times upper limit of normal).
History of intolerance to ARB [OR] or amlodipine.
Hypertrophic [OR] or restrictive cardiomyopathy.
Moderate [OR] or severe valvular disease.
Constrictive pericarditis
Atrial fibrillation [AND] with a heart rate > 120/min.
Sitting systolic BP < 100 mmHg
