Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nKidney transplant recipients at Washington University/Barnes-Jewish Hospital\nExperiencing GI toxicity from MPA as determined by the treating physician within 12 months post-renal transplant\nOn standard immunosuppression with tacrolimus and prednisone\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nDual organ or kidney after another solid organ transplant\nPresence of a preexisting significant GI condition that does not have a presumed causal relationship with MPA\nEvidence of any GI disorder induced by an infection, underlying medical condition, or concomitant medication other than MPA\neGFR<40 ml/min at time of possible conversion\nProteinuria >1 gram/day at time of possible conversion\nHemoglobin <10 g/dL\nWBC <3 K/cumm\nPlatelets <100 K/cumm\nWound healing issues at time of possible conversion (eg, wound dehiscence, wound infection, incisional hernia, lymphocele, seroma)\nElevated total cholesterol (>350 mg/dL) and/or triglycerides (>500 ng/dL) at time of possible conversion\nHypersensitivity to everolimus, sirolimus, or other rapamycin deriviatives\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nKidney transplant recipients at Washington University/ [OR] Barnes-Jewish Hospital\nExperiencing GI toxicity from MPA as determined by the treating physician within 12 months post-renal transplant\nOn standard immunosuppression [AND] with tacrolimus [AND] and prednisone\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nDual organ [OR] or kidney after another solid organ transplant\nPresence of a preexisting significant GI condition that does [NOT] not have a presumed causal relationship with MPA\nEvidence of any GI disorder induced by an infection, underlying medical condition, [OR] or concomitant medication other than MPA\neGFR<40 ml/min at time of possible conversion\nProteinuria >1 gram/day at time of possible conversion\nHemoglobin <10 g/dL\nWBC <3 K/cumm\n Platelets <100 K/cumm\nWound healing issues at time of possible conversion (eg, wound dehiscence, [OR] wound infection, [OR] incisional hernia, [OR] lymphocele, [OR] seroma)\nElevated total cholesterol  (>350 mg/dL) [OR] and/or triglycerides (>500 ng/dL) at time of possible conversion\nHypersensitivity to everolimus, [OR] sirolimus, [OR] or other rapamycin deriviatives<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Kidney transplant recipients at Washington University/ [OR] Barnes-Jewish Hospital
Experiencing GI toxicity from MPA as determined by the treating physician within 12 months post-renal transplant
On standard immunosuppression [AND] with tacrolimus [AND] and prednisone

Exclusion Criteria:
Dual organ [OR] or kidney after another solid organ transplant
Presence of a preexisting significant GI condition that does [NOT] not have a presumed causal relationship with MPA
Evidence of any GI disorder induced by an infection, underlying medical condition, [OR] or concomitant medication other than MPA
eGFR<40 ml/min at time of possible conversion
Proteinuria >1 gram/day at time of possible conversion
Hemoglobin <10 g/dL
WBC <3 K/cumm
 Platelets <100 K/cumm
Wound healing issues at time of possible conversion (eg, wound dehiscence, [OR] wound infection, [OR] incisional hernia, [OR] lymphocele, [OR] seroma)
Elevated total cholesterol  (>350 mg/dL) [OR] and/or triglycerides (>500 ng/dL) at time of possible conversion
Hypersensitivity to everolimus, [OR] sirolimus, [OR] or other rapamycin deriviatives
