Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nwomen and men between 18 - 80 years of age\ntype 2 diabetes mellitus\nearly to moderate stage diabetic retinopathy (ETDRS: 20 (microaneurysms only) to 35 (microaneurysms/ hemorrhages and/or hard exsudates)) in one or both eyes\nstable HbA1c (± 0.5%) for at least 12 weeks\nantidiabetic treatment with either diet, metformin, DPP4, GLP1, pioglitazone, acarbose, or respective combinations\nHbA1c = 6.5 and = 10.0 %\nbody mass index < 46 kg/m2\noffice blood pressure = 150/95 mmHg (confirmed on a second day; 24h ambulatory blood pressure measurement (ABPM) is allowed to check accuracy of office values; inclusion with 24h mean blood pressure = 145/90 mm Hg is possible); patients with hypertension should be treated according to current treatment guidelines\nat least 6 weeks after surgical sterilization by bilateral tubal ligation or bilateral oophorectomy\nhysterectomy\n= 50 years and in postmenopausal state > 1 year\n< 50 years and in postmenopausal state > 1 year with serum follicle stimulating hormone (FSH) > 40 IU/l and serum estrogen < 30 ng/l or a negative estrogen test, both at screening or women of childbearing potential with a negative serum beta human chorionic gonadotropin (ß-hCG) pregnancy test at screening who agree to meet one of the following criteria from the time of screening, during the study and for a period of 4 days following the last administration of study medication:\ncorrect use of one of the following accepted contraception methods: hormonal contraceptives (combined oral contraceptives, implants, transdermal patches, hormonal vaginal devices or injections with prolonged release), intrauterine device (IUD/IUS) or a double barrier method, e.g. condom and occlusive cap (diaphragm or cervical/vault caps) with spermicide (foam, gel, film, cream or suppository)\ntrue abstinence (periodic abstinence and withdrawal are not acceptable methods of contraception)\nsexual relationship only with female partners\nsterile male partners\nsigned written informed consent and willingness to comply with treatment and follow-up procedures\ncapability of understanding the investigational nature, potential risks and benefits of the clinical trial\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nType 1 diabetes\nuncontrolled diabetes mellitus type 2 with fasting glucose > 13.3 mmol/l confirmed on a second day\nknown or suspected hypersensitivity to empagliflozin, glimepiride, or any excipients; and / or known or suspected hypersensitivity to sulfonylureas, sulfonamides or SGLT2 inhibitors in general\nhistory of multiple severe hypoglycemic episodes within the last two years\nuse of Insulin, SGLT2-inhibitor, sulfonylurea derivate or a glinide within past 3 months\nclinical significant macular edema in both eyes and indication for intravitreal anti-VEGF treatment for both eyes at screening or baseline visit. Eyes with a small amount of intraretinal or subretinal fluid (seen in OCT) but no need for intravitreal treatment as judged by the investigator (according to current practice patterns) may be included. Eyes with a history of intravitreal treatment of macular edema which do not need ongoing intravitreal treatment at the time of screening may be included.\neye diseases or pathologies that prevent clear ophthalmoscopy and evaluation of study parameters, thus not allowing study participation according to the investigator´s judgment, such as (but not only) vitreous hemorrhage, mature cataract, macular pathologies other than diabetic maculopathy\nhistory of ketoacidosis or metabolic acidosis\nuse of loop diuretics\nhistory of > 1 urogenital infection/year\nany history of stroke, transient ischemic attack (TIA), instable angina pectoris or myocardial infarction within last 3 months prior to baseline visit\ncongestive heart failure New York Heart Association (NYHA) III and IV\nsevere valvular or left ventricular outflow obstruction disease needing intervention;\natrial fibrillation/flutter with a mean ventricular response rate at rest >100 beats per minute\nchronic lower urinary tract infections (but not simple asymptomatic bacteriuria)\neGFR < 60 ml/min/1,73 m2 (MDRD-formula, confirmed on a second day)\nchronic diarrhea, any clinical signs of volume depletion or a hematocrit > 48 % (women) and > 53 % (men)\nelevated risk for volume depletion, e.g. history of severe volume depletion that required medical therapy\nchronic liver disease (including known active hepatitis) and/or screening alanine transaminase (ALT) or aspartate transaminase (AST) > 3 x upper limit of normal (ULN) (confirmed on a second day)\nSubjects with known seropositivity to human immunodeficiency virus.\nacute illness at screening or randomization according to judgement by the investigator or patient\ndrug or alcohol abuse\npsychosomatic or psychiatric diseases requiring hospitalization during the last 12 months\nclinical evidence of current malignancy with exception of basal cell or squamous cell carcinoma of the skin, and cervical intraepithelial neoplasia (5 years prior to randomization)\nany medical or surgical intervention planned for the next 13 months after randomization not allowing study participation according to the investigator´s judgment\ncurrent participation in any other clinical trial or participation in another clinical trial within 30 days before screening\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nwomen [OR] and men between 18 - 80 years of age\ntype 2 diabetes mellitus\nearly to moderate stage diabetic retinopathy (ETDRS: 20 (microaneurysms only) to 35 (microaneurysms/ [OR] hemorrhages [OR] and/or hard exsudates)) in one [OR] or both eyes\nstable HbA1c (± 0.5%) for at least 12 weeks\nantidiabetic treatment with either diet, [OR] metformin, [OR] DPP4, [OR] GLP1, [OR] pioglitazone, [OR] acarbose, [OR] or respective combinations\nHbA1c = 6.5 [AND] and = 10.0 %\nbody mass index < 46 kg/m2\noffice blood pressure = 150/95 mmHg (confirmed on a second day; 24h ambulatory blood pressure measurement (ABPM) is allowed to check accuracy of office values; inclusion with 24h mean blood pressure = 145/90 mm Hg is possible); patients with hypertension should be treated according to current treatment guidelines\nat least 6 weeks after surgical sterilization by bilateral tubal ligation [OR] or bilateral oophorectomy\nhysterectomy\n= 50 years [AND] and in postmenopausal state > 1 year\n< 50 years [AND] and in postmenopausal state > 1 year [AND] with serum follicle stimulating hormone (FSH) > 40 IU/l [AND] and serum estrogen < 30 ng/l [OR] or a negative estrogen test, both at screening [OR] or women [AND] of childbearing potential [AND] with a negative serum beta human chorionic gonadotropin (ß-hCG) pregnancy test at screening [AND] who agree to meet one of the following criteria from the time of screening, during the study [AND] and for a period of 4 days following the last administration of study medication:\ncorrect use of one of the following accepted contraception methods: hormonal contraceptives (combined oral contraceptives, [OR] implants, [OR] transdermal patches, [OR] hormonal vaginal devices [OR] or injections with prolonged release), intrauterine device (IUD/ [OR] IUS) [OR] or a double barrier method, e.g. condom [OR] and occlusive cap (diaphragm [OR] or cervical/ [OR] vault caps) [AND] with spermicide (foam, [OR] gel, [OR] film, [OR] cream [OR] or suppository)\ntrue abstinence (periodic abstinence [OR] and withdrawal are [NOT] not acceptable methods of contraception)\nsexual relationship only with female partners\nsterile male partners\nsigned written informed consent and willingness to comply with treatment and follow-up procedures\ncapability of understanding the investigational nature, potential risks [AND] and benefits of the clinical trial\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nType 1 diabetes\nuncontrolled diabetes mellitus type 2 [AND] with fasting glucose > 13.3 mmol/l confirmed on a second day\nknown [OR] or suspected hypersensitivity to empagliflozin, [OR] glimepiride, [OR] or any excipients; [OR] and / or known [OR] or suspected hypersensitivity to sulfonylureas, [OR] sulfonamides [OR] or SGLT2 inhibitors in general\nhistory of multiple severe hypoglycemic episodes within the last two years\nuse of Insulin, [OR] SGLT2-inhibitor, [OR] sulfonylurea derivate [OR] or a glinide within past 3 months\nclinical significant macular edema in both eyes [AND] and indication for intravitreal anti-VEGF treatment for both eyes at screening [OR] or baseline visit. Eyes [AND] with a small amount of intraretinal [OR] or subretinal fluid (seen in OCT) [AND] but [NOT] no need for intravitreal treatment as judged by the investigator (according to current practice patterns) may be included. Eyes [AND] with a history of intravitreal treatment of macular edema which do [NOT] not need ongoing intravitreal treatment at the time of screening may be included.\neye diseases [OR] or pathologies that [NOT] prevent clear ophthalmoscopy [AND] and evaluation of study parameters, thus [NOT] not allowing study participation according to the investigator´s judgment, such as (but not only) vitreous hemorrhage, mature cataract, [OR] macular pathologies other than diabetic maculopathy\nhistory of ketoacidosis [OR] or metabolic acidosis\nuse of loop diuretics\nhistory of > 1 urogenital infection/year\nany history of stroke, [OR] transient ischemic attack (TIA), instable angina pectoris [OR] or myocardial infarction within last 3 months prior to baseline visit\ncongestive heart failure New York Heart Association (NYHA) III and IV\nsevere valvular [OR] or left ventricular outflow obstruction disease needing intervention;\natrial fibrillation/ [OR] flutter [AND] with a mean ventricular response rate at rest >100 beats per minute\nchronic lower urinary tract infections (but [NOT] not simple asymptomatic bacteriuria)\neGFR < 60 ml/min/1,73 m2 (MDRD-formula, confirmed on a second day)\nchronic diarrhea, any clinical signs of volume depletion [OR] or a hematocrit > 48 % (women) [OR] and > 53 % (men)\nelevated risk for volume depletion, e.g. history of severe volume depletion that required medical therapy\nchronic liver disease (including known active hepatitis) [OR] and/or screening alanine transaminase (ALT) [OR] or aspartate transaminase (AST) > 3 x upper limit of normal (ULN) (confirmed on a second day)\nSubjects with known seropositivity to human immunodeficiency virus.\nacute illness at screening [OR] or randomization according to judgement by the investigator [OR] or patient\ndrug [OR] or alcohol abuse\npsychosomatic [OR] or psychiatric diseases requiring hospitalization during the last 12 months\nclinical evidence of current malignancy [AND] with exception of basal cell [OR] or squamous cell carcinoma of the skin, [OR] and cervical intraepithelial neoplasia (5 years prior to randomization)\nany medical [OR] or surgical intervention planned for the next 13 months after randomization [NOT] not allowing study participation according to the investigator´s judgment\ncurrent participation in any other clinical trial [OR] or participation in another clinical trial within 30 days before screening<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
women [OR] and men between 18 - 80 years of age
type 2 diabetes mellitus
early to moderate stage diabetic retinopathy (ETDRS: 20 (microaneurysms only) to 35 (microaneurysms/ [OR] hemorrhages [OR] and/or hard exsudates)) in one [OR] or both eyes
stable HbA1c (± 0.5%) for at least 12 weeks
antidiabetic treatment with either diet, [OR] metformin, [OR] DPP4, [OR] GLP1, [OR] pioglitazone, [OR] acarbose, [OR] or respective combinations
HbA1c = 6.5 [AND] and = 10.0 %
body mass index < 46 kg/m2
office blood pressure = 150/95 mmHg (confirmed on a second day; 24h ambulatory blood pressure measurement (ABPM) is allowed to check accuracy of office values; inclusion with 24h mean blood pressure = 145/90 mm Hg is possible); patients with hypertension should be treated according to current treatment guidelines
at least 6 weeks after surgical sterilization by bilateral tubal ligation [OR] or bilateral oophorectomy
hysterectomy
= 50 years [AND] and in postmenopausal state > 1 year
< 50 years [AND] and in postmenopausal state > 1 year [AND] with serum follicle stimulating hormone (FSH) > 40 IU/l [AND] and serum estrogen < 30 ng/l [OR] or a negative estrogen test, both at screening [OR] or women [AND] of childbearing potential [AND] with a negative serum beta human chorionic gonadotropin (ß-hCG) pregnancy test at screening [AND] who agree to meet one of the following criteria from the time of screening, during the study [AND] and for a period of 4 days following the last administration of study medication:
correct use of one of the following accepted contraception methods: hormonal contraceptives (combined oral contraceptives, [OR] implants, [OR] transdermal patches, [OR] hormonal vaginal devices [OR] or injections with prolonged release), intrauterine device (IUD/ [OR] IUS) [OR] or a double barrier method, e.g. condom [OR] and occlusive cap (diaphragm [OR] or cervical/ [OR] vault caps) [AND] with spermicide (foam, [OR] gel, [OR] film, [OR] cream [OR] or suppository)
true abstinence (periodic abstinence [OR] and withdrawal are [NOT] not acceptable methods of contraception)
sexual relationship only with female partners
sterile male partners
signed written informed consent and willingness to comply with treatment and follow-up procedures
capability of understanding the investigational nature, potential risks [AND] and benefits of the clinical trial

Exclusion Criteria:
Type 1 diabetes
uncontrolled diabetes mellitus type 2 [AND] with fasting glucose > 13.3 mmol/l confirmed on a second day
known [OR] or suspected hypersensitivity to empagliflozin, [OR] glimepiride, [OR] or any excipients; [OR] and / or known [OR] or suspected hypersensitivity to sulfonylureas, [OR] sulfonamides [OR] or SGLT2 inhibitors in general
history of multiple severe hypoglycemic episodes within the last two years
use of Insulin, [OR] SGLT2-inhibitor, [OR] sulfonylurea derivate [OR] or a glinide within past 3 months
clinical significant macular edema in both eyes [AND] and indication for intravitreal anti-VEGF treatment for both eyes at screening [OR] or baseline visit. Eyes [AND] with a small amount of intraretinal [OR] or subretinal fluid (seen in OCT) [AND] but [NOT] no need for intravitreal treatment as judged by the investigator (according to current practice patterns) may be included. Eyes [AND] with a history of intravitreal treatment of macular edema which do [NOT] not need ongoing intravitreal treatment at the time of screening may be included.
eye diseases [OR] or pathologies that [NOT] prevent clear ophthalmoscopy [AND] and evaluation of study parameters, thus [NOT] not allowing study participation according to the investigator´s judgment, such as (but not only) vitreous hemorrhage, mature cataract, [OR] macular pathologies other than diabetic maculopathy
history of ketoacidosis [OR] or metabolic acidosis
use of loop diuretics
history of > 1 urogenital infection/year
any history of stroke, [OR] transient ischemic attack (TIA), instable angina pectoris [OR] or myocardial infarction within last 3 months prior to baseline visit
congestive heart failure New York Heart Association (NYHA) III and IV
severe valvular [OR] or left ventricular outflow obstruction disease needing intervention;
atrial fibrillation/ [OR] flutter [AND] with a mean ventricular response rate at rest >100 beats per minute
chronic lower urinary tract infections (but [NOT] not simple asymptomatic bacteriuria)
eGFR < 60 ml/min/1,73 m2 (MDRD-formula, confirmed on a second day)
chronic diarrhea, any clinical signs of volume depletion [OR] or a hematocrit > 48 % (women) [OR] and > 53 % (men)
elevated risk for volume depletion, e.g. history of severe volume depletion that required medical therapy
chronic liver disease (including known active hepatitis) [OR] and/or screening alanine transaminase (ALT) [OR] or aspartate transaminase (AST) > 3 x upper limit of normal (ULN) (confirmed on a second day)
Subjects with known seropositivity to human immunodeficiency virus.
acute illness at screening [OR] or randomization according to judgement by the investigator [OR] or patient
drug [OR] or alcohol abuse
psychosomatic [OR] or psychiatric diseases requiring hospitalization during the last 12 months
clinical evidence of current malignancy [AND] with exception of basal cell [OR] or squamous cell carcinoma of the skin, [OR] and cervical intraepithelial neoplasia (5 years prior to randomization)
any medical [OR] or surgical intervention planned for the next 13 months after randomization [NOT] not allowing study participation according to the investigator´s judgment
current participation in any other clinical trial [OR] or participation in another clinical trial within 30 days before screening
