Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAge 65 - 79\nHistory of coronary artery disease (MI/heart attack, stroke, heart failure, or peripheral artery disease)\nCancer, with no active treatment in the last year\nMCI (MoCA >18<26 -inclusive of 1 point if <12 years of education Group 2\nDecline physical function (walking speed < 1 m/s) Group 3 (Either or both)\nAbdominal obesity (>88cm women, >102cm men) AND hypertension (treated or resting blood pressure >140/90\nAbdominal obesity (>88cm women, >102cm men) AND hyperlipidemia (treated or fasting total cholesterol >240 English literacy Willing to provide informed consent\n\nExclusion Criteria:\neGFR <45\nType 2 diabetes (HbA1c>6.5) or type 1 diabetes\nAny tobacco or nicotine product use in the past year\nLow vitamin B12 Levels (< 300 pg/mL)\nSelf-reported severe difficulty or inability to walk 400m or climb 10 steps (from Q 2 and 19 on PAT-D)\nSelf-reported difficulty or inability to perform basic ADL functions (from Q 10, 13, 14, 16 on PAT-D)\nExcessive alcohol use (>14 drinks/week)\nCancer requiring treatment in past year (except skin)\nDementia - diagnosed and/or MoCA score <18\nParkinson\'s or other neurological disease\nChronic liver disease or cirrhosis\nEnd stage renal disease or on dialysis\nRheumatic conditions (Rheumatoid arthritis, lupus, and any other autoimmune disease the -PI deems them to be ineligible for)\nThyroid problems the PI deems them to be ineligible for\nGout\nInvolved in another interventional study\nHemoglobin <8 or diagnosed with anemia\nRecent unintentional weight change (+/- 10 lbs. in the last 12 months)\nBMI <18.5\nLikely to not follow the protocol\nPI deems unfit to participate\nAlready taking Metformin or any other drug intended to treat diabetes\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAge 65 - 79\nHistory of coronary artery disease (MI/ [OR] heart attack, [OR] stroke, [OR] heart failure, [OR] or peripheral artery disease)\nCancer, [AND] with [NOT] no active treatment in the last year\nMCI (MoCA >18<26 -inclusive of 1 point if <12 years of education Group 2\nDecline physical function (walking speed < 1 m/s) Group 3 (Either or both)\nAbdominal obesity (>88cm women, >102cm men) [AND] AND hypertension (treated [OR] or resting blood pressure >140/90\nAbdominal obesity (>88cm women, >102cm men) [AND] AND hyperlipidemia (treated [OR] or fasting total cholesterol >240 English literacy Willing to provide informed consent\n\nExclusion Criteria:\neGFR <45\nType 2 diabetes (HbA1c>6.5) [OR] or type 1 diabetes\nAny tobacco [OR] or nicotine product use in the past year\nLow vitamin B12 Levels (< 300 pg/mL)\nSelf-reported severe difficulty [OR] or [NOT] inability to walk 400m [OR] or climb 10 steps (from Q 2 and 19 on PAT-D)\n Self-reported [NOT] difficulty [OR] or [NOT] inability to perform basic ADL functions (from Q 10, 13, 14, 16 on PAT-D)\nExcessive alcohol use (>14 drinks/week)\nCancer requiring treatment in past year (except skin)\nDementia - diagnosed [OR] and/or MoCA score <18\nParkison\'s [OR] or other neurological disease\nChronic liver disease [OR] or cirrhosis\nEnd stage renal disease [OR] or on dialysis\nRheumatic conditions (Rheumatoid arthritis, [OR] lupus, [OR] and any other autoimmune disease the -PI deems them to be ineligible for)\nThyroid problems the PI deems them to be ineligible for\nGout\nInvolved in another interventional study\nHemoglobin <8 [OR] or diagnosed with anemia\nRecent unintentional weight change (+/- 10 lbs. in the last 12 months)\nBMI <18.5\nLikely to [NOT] not follow the protocol\nPI deems unfit to participate\nAlready taking Metformin [OR] or any other drug intended to treat diabetes<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Age 65 - 79
History of coronary artery disease (MI/ [OR] heart attack, [OR] stroke, [OR] heart failure, [OR] or peripheral artery disease)
Cancer, [AND] with [NOT] no active treatment in the last year
MCI (MoCA >18<26 -inclusive of 1 point if <12 years of education Group 2
Decline physical function (walking speed < 1 m/s) Group 3 (Either or both)
Abdominal obesity (>88cm women, >102cm men) [AND] AND hypertension (treated [OR] or resting blood pressure >140/90
Abdominal obesity (>88cm women, >102cm men) [AND] AND hyperlipidemia (treated [OR] or fasting total cholesterol >240 English literacy Willing to provide informed consent

Exclusion Criteria:
eGFR <45
Type 2 diabetes (HbA1c>6.5) [OR] or type 1 diabetes
Any tobacco [OR] or nicotine product use in the past year
Low vitamin B12 Levels (< 300 pg/mL)
Self-reported severe difficulty [OR] or [NOT] inability to walk 400m [OR] or climb 10 steps (from Q 2 and 19 on PAT-D)
 Self-reported [NOT] difficulty [OR] or [NOT] inability to perform basic ADL functions (from Q 10, 13, 14, 16 on PAT-D)
Excessive alcohol use (>14 drinks/week)
Cancer requiring treatment in past year (except skin)
Dementia - diagnosed [OR] and/or MoCA score <18
Parkison's [OR] or other neurological disease
Chronic liver disease [OR] or cirrhosis
End stage renal disease [OR] or on dialysis
Rheumatic conditions (Rheumatoid arthritis, [OR] lupus, [OR] and any other autoimmune disease the -PI deems them to be ineligible for)
Thyroid problems the PI deems them to be ineligible for
Gout
Involved in another interventional study
Hemoglobin <8 [OR] or diagnosed with anemia
Recent unintentional weight change (+/- 10 lbs. in the last 12 months)
BMI <18.5
Likely to [NOT] not follow the protocol
PI deems unfit to participate
Already taking Metformin [OR] or any other drug intended to treat diabetes
