Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAble to give informed consent\nRight-handed\nAge between 18-50 years old,\nPhysically and neurologically healthy [confirmed by a comprehensive medical history]\nCurrent PTSD diagnosis\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nclinically significant medical or neurologic condition or neurocognitive dysfunction that would affect function and/or task performance and/or interfere with the study protocol\nany current (or within past 2 months) medical condition requiring medication that would interact with dronabinol or interfere with the study protocol\nrisk of harm to self or others that requires immediate intervention\npresence of contraindications, current or past allergic or adverse reaction, or known sensitivity to cannabinoid-like substances (dronabinol/marijuana/cannabis/THC, cannabinoid oil, sesame oil, gelatin, glycerin, and titanium dioxide)\nlack of fluency in English\npositive drug screen or alcohol breathalyzer\nunwilling/unable to sign informed consent document\ncurrently pregnant (positive pregnancy test), planning pregnancy, or lactating (women)\nunder 18 or over 50 years of age\ntraumatic brain injury (as defined by The American Congress of Rehabilitation as a person who has had a traumatically induced physiological disruption of brain function (i.e., the head being struck, the head striking an object, and/or the brain undergoing an acceleration/deceleration movement (i.e., whiplash) without direct external trauma to the head), as manifested by at least one of the following: any loss of consciousness; any loss of memory for events immediately before or after the injury; any alteration in mental status at the time of the incident; or focal neurological deficits that may or may not be transient)\ninability to tolerate small, enclosed spaces without anxiety (e.g. claustrophobia), as determined by self-report and/or a preliminary session in a mock scanner\nleft-handed;\npresence of ferrous-containing metals within the body (e.g., aneurysm clips, shrapnel/retained particles)\nanticipation of a required drug test in the 4 weeks following the study.\ncurrent diagnosis of a mood, anxiety, or other disorder that is more clinically salient than PTSD\ncurrent moderate or severe alcohol/drug use disorder or in the past 8 weeks\ncurrent or past diagnosis of bipolar and other related disorders, schizophrenia spectrum, or other psychotic disorders\nconcomitant treatments with medication known to have drug interactions with dronabinol, such as, central nervous system depressants (barbiturates, benzodiazepines, buspirone, lithium, etc) and anticholinergic agents (atropine, scopolamine, antihistamines, etc).\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAble to give informed consent\nRight-handed\nAge between 18-50 years old,\nPhysically [AND] and neurologically healthy [confirmed by a comprehensive medical history]\nCurrent PTSD diagnosis\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nclinically significant medical [OR] or neurologic condition [OR] or neurocognitive dysfunction that would affect function [OR] and/or task performance [OR] and/or interfere with the study protocol\nany current (or within past 2 months) medical condition requiring medication that would interact with dronabinol [OR] or interfere with the study protocol\nrisk of harm to self [OR] or others that requires immediate intervention\npresence of contraindications, current [OR] or past allergic [OR] or adverse reaction, [OR] or known sensitivity to cannabinoid-like substances (dronabinol/ [OR] marijuana/ [OR] cannabis/ [OR] THC, cannabinoid oil, [OR] sesame oil, [OR] gelatin, [OR] glycerin, [OR] and titanium dioxide)\nlack of fluency in English\npositive drug screen [OR] or alcohol breathalyzer\nunwilling/unable to sign informed consent document\ncurrently pregnant (positive pregnancy test), planning pregnancy, [OR] or lactating (women)\nunder 18 [OR] or over 50 years of age\ntraumatic brain injury (as defined by The American Congress of Rehabilitation as a person who has had a traumatically induced physiological disruption of brain function (i.e., the head being struck, the head striking an object, [OR] and/or the brain undergoing an acceleration/ [OR] deceleration movement (i.e., whiplash) [NOT] without direct external trauma to the head), as manifested by at least one of the following: any loss of consciousness; any loss of memory for events immediately before [OR] or after the injury; any alteration in mental status at the time of the incident; [OR] or focal neurological deficits that may [OR] or may [NOT] not be transient)\ninability to tolerate small, enclosed spaces [NOT] without anxiety (e.g. claustrophobia), as determined by self-report and/or a preliminary session in a mock scanner\nleft-handed;\npresence of ferrous-containing metals within the body (e.g., aneurysm clips, [OR] shrapnel/ [OR] retained particles)\nanticipation of a required drug test in the 4 weeks following the study.\ncurrent diagnosis of a mood, [OR] anxiety, [OR] or other disorder that is more clinically salient than PTSD\ncurrent moderate [OR] or severe alcohol/ [OR] drug use disorder [OR] or in the past 8 weeks\ncurrent [OR] or past diagnosis of bipolar [OR] and other related disorders, [OR] schizophrenia spectrum, [OR] or other psychotic disorders\nconcomitant treatments with medication known to have drug interactions with dronabinol, such as, central nervous system depressants (barbiturates, [OR] benzodiazepines, [OR] buspirone, [OR] lithium, etc) [OR] and anticholinergic agents (atropine, [OR] scopolamine, [OR] antihistamines, etc).<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Able to give informed consent
Right-handed
Age between 18-50 years old,
Physically [AND] and neurologically healthy [confirmed by a comprehensive medical history]
Current PTSD diagnosis

Exclusion Criteria:
clinically significant medical [OR] or neurologic condition [OR] or neurocognitive dysfunction that would affect function [OR] and/or task performance [OR] and/or interfere with the study protocol
any current (or within past 2 months) medical condition requiring medication that would interact with dronabinol [OR] or interfere with the study protocol
risk of harm to self [OR] or others that requires immediate intervention
presence of contraindications, current [OR] or past allergic [OR] or adverse reaction, [OR] or known sensitivity to cannabinoid-like substances (dronabinol/ [OR] marijuana/ [OR] cannabis/ [OR] THC, cannabinoid oil, [OR] sesame oil, [OR] gelatin, [OR] glycerin, [OR] and titanium dioxide)
lack of fluency in English
positive drug screen [OR] or alcohol breathalyzer
unwilling/unable to sign informed consent document
currently pregnant (positive pregnancy test), planning pregnancy, [OR] or lactating (women)
under 18 [OR] or over 50 years of age
traumatic brain injury (as defined by The American Congress of Rehabilitation as a person who has had a traumatically induced physiological disruption of brain function (i.e., the head being struck, the head striking an object, [OR] and/or the brain undergoing an acceleration/ [OR] deceleration movement (i.e., whiplash) [NOT] without direct external trauma to the head), as manifested by at least one of the following: any loss of consciousness; any loss of memory for events immediately before [OR] or after the injury; any alteration in mental status at the time of the incident; [OR] or focal neurological deficits that may [OR] or may [NOT] not be transient)
inability to tolerate small, enclosed spaces [NOT] without anxiety (e.g. claustrophobia), as determined by self-report and/or a preliminary session in a mock scanner
left-handed;
presence of ferrous-containing metals within the body (e.g., aneurysm clips, [OR] shrapnel/ [OR] retained particles)
anticipation of a required drug test in the 4 weeks following the study.
current diagnosis of a mood, [OR] anxiety, [OR] or other disorder that is more clinically salient than PTSD
current moderate [OR] or severe alcohol/ [OR] drug use disorder [OR] or in the past 8 weeks
current [OR] or past diagnosis of bipolar [OR] and other related disorders, [OR] schizophrenia spectrum, [OR] or other psychotic disorders
concomitant treatments with medication known to have drug interactions with dronabinol, such as, central nervous system depressants (barbiturates, [OR] benzodiazepines, [OR] buspirone, [OR] lithium, etc) [OR] and anticholinergic agents (atropine, [OR] scopolamine, [OR] antihistamines, etc).
