al chemotherapy (HIPEC)\nGastrectomy (subtotal [OR] or total)\nCholecystectomy [OR] or bile duct resection\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nAge less than 18 years\nAmerican Society of Anesthesiologist Class 5\nProjected life expectancy less than 30 days\nKnown [OR] or suspected hypersensitivity to either propofol, e.g. egg [OR] or soy allergy, [OR] or volatile general anesthetic agents\nKnown [OR] or suspected history of malignant hyperthermia<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Lobectomy [OR] or pneumonectomy
Esophagectomy
Radical (total) cystectomy
 Pancreatectomy
Partial hepatectomy
Hyperthermic intraperitoneal chemotherapy (HIPEC)
Gastrectomy (subtotal [OR] or total)
Cholecystectomy [OR] or bile duct resection

Exclusion Criteria:
Age less than 18 years
American Society of Anesthesiologist Class 5
Projected life expectancy less than 30 days
Known [OR] or suspected hypersensitivity to either propofol, e.g. egg [OR] or soy allergy, [OR] or volatile general anesthetic agents
Known [OR] or suspected history of malignant hyperthermia
