ored Anesthesia Care (i.e., regional anesthesia alone [NOT] without plans for general anesthesia)\nSurgery involving the eye, [OR] eyebrow, [OR] forehead, [OR] or frontal scalp near the sensor placement\nPoor health literacy\nAllergy, [OR] or have experienced any drug reaction to ketamine\nPregnant [OR] or lactating\nCurrently in active alcohol withdrawal<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Current diagnosis of otolaryngeal cancer [AND] and undergoing surgery with general anesthesia
Competent to provide informed consent

Exclusion Criteria:
Emergency surgery
Monitored Anesthesia Care (i.e., regional anesthesia alone [NOT] without plans for general anesthesia)
Surgery involving the eye, [OR] eyebrow, [OR] forehead, [OR] or frontal scalp near the sensor placement
Poor health literacy
Allergy, [OR] or have experienced any drug reaction to ketamine
Pregnant [OR] or lactating
Currently in active alcohol withdrawal
