Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\na very high cardiovascular risk and LDL-cholesterol> 1.8 mmol / l\na high cardiovascular risk and LDL-cholesterol> 2.5 mmol / l\nPatient with a high or very high cardiovascular risk treated by lipidlowering therapy with statin\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nhypersensitivity to perindopril or to other ACE inhibitors, amlodipine, atorvastatin, dihydropyridines or to or statins\nangioneurotic edema in medical history (hereditary / idiopathic or associated with prior treatment with ACE inhibitors)\nsevere hypotension, shock, including cardiogenic shock\nhemodynamically unstable heart failure\nActive liver disease or unexplained persistent elevations of serum transaminases more than three times normal\nWomen of childbearing age without reliable contraception\npregnancy\nbreastfeeding\nPatients with contraindications listed in the currently valid SP\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\na very high cardiovascular risk [AND] and LDL-cholesterol> 1.8 mmol / l\n a high cardiovascular risk [AND] and LDL-cholesterol> 2.5 mmol / l\nPatient with a high [OR] or very high cardiovascular risk treated by lipidlowering therapy with statin\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nhypersensitivity to perindopril [OR] or to other ACE inhibitors, [OR] amlodipine, [OR] atorvastatin, [OR] dihydropyridines [OR] or to or statins\nangioneurotic edema in medical history (hereditary [OR] / idiopathic or associated with prior treatment with ACE inhibitors)\nsevere hypotension, [OR] shock, including cardiogenic shock\nhemodynamically unstable heart failure\nActive liver disease [OR] or unexplained persistent elevations of serum transaminases more than three times normal\nWomen [AND] of childbearing age [NOT] without reliable contraception\npregnancy\nbreastfeeding\nPatients with contraindications listed in the currently valid SP<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
a very high cardiovascular risk [AND] and LDL-cholesterol> 1.8 mmol / l
 a high cardiovascular risk [AND] and LDL-cholesterol> 2.5 mmol / l
Patient with a high [OR] or very high cardiovascular risk treated by lipidlowering therapy with statin

Exclusion Criteria:
hypersensitivity to perindopril [OR] or to other ACE inhibitors, [OR] amlodipine, [OR] atorvastatin, [OR] dihydropyridines [OR] or to or statins
angioneurotic edema in medical history (hereditary [OR] / idiopathic or associated with prior treatment with ACE inhibitors)
severe hypotension, [OR] shock, including cardiogenic shock
hemodynamically unstable heart failure
Active liver disease [OR] or unexplained persistent elevations of serum transaminases more than three times normal
Women [AND] of childbearing age [NOT] without reliable contraception
pregnancy
breastfeeding
Patients with contraindications listed in the currently valid SP
