File: NCT03056287 

Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_full/NCT03056287.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\n1) age 50-70 \n2) stroke within the past 6 to 60 months, \n3) major depressive disorder (PHQ-9 > 10) and diagnosed using the Structured Clinical Interview for Depression (SCID) according to the Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders, Fourth Edition (DSM-IV), \n4) residual paresis in the lower extremity (Fugl-Meyer LE motor score <34), \n5) ability to walk without assistance and without an AFO on the treadmill ≥ 30 seconds at speeds ranging from 0.2-0.8 m/s, \n6) no antidepressant medications or clinically able to discontinue medications, \n7) HRSD question #9 regarding suicide <2, \n8) provision of informed consent. In addition, all subjects who meet criteria for the training portion must complete an exercise tolerance test and be cleared for participation by the study cardiologist. \n\nExclusion Criteria:\n1. Unable to ambulate at least 150 feet prior to stroke, or experienced intermittent claudication while walking; \n2. history of congestive heart failure, unstable cardiac arrhythmias, hypertrophic cardiomyopathy, severe aortic stenosis, angina or dyspnea at rest or during ADL\'s; \n3. History of oxygen dependence; \n4. Preexisting neurological disorders, dementia or previous stroke; \n5. History of major head trauma; \n6. Legal blindness or severe visual impairment; \n7. history of psychosis or other Axis I disorder that is primary; \n8. Life expectancy <1 yr.; \n9. Severe arthritis or other problems that limit passive range of motion; \n10. History of DVT or pulmonary embolism within 6 months; \n11. Uncontrolled diabetes with recent weight loss, diabetic coma, or frequent insulin reactions; \n12. Severe hypertension with systolic >200 mmHg and diastolic >110 mmHg at rest; \n13. attempt of suicide in the last 2 years or at suicidal risk assessed by SCID interview; \n14. Previous or current enrollment in a clinical trial to enhance motor recovery; 15) currently exercising ≥ 2 times per week (≥20 minutes); \n16) Presence of non-MR compatible implants, pregnancy or severe claustrophobia.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n1) age 50-70 \n2) stroke within the past 6 to 60 months, \n3) major depressive disorder (PHQ-9 > 10) [AND] and diagnosed using the Structured Clinical Interview for Depression (SCID) according to the Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders, Fourth Edition (DSM-IV), \n4) residual paresis in the lower extremity (Fugl-Meyer LE motor score <34), \n5) ability to walk [NOT] without assistance [AND] and [NOT] without an AFO on the treadmill ≥ 30 seconds at speeds ranging from 0.2-0.8 m/s, \n6) [NOT] no antidepressant medications [OR] or clinically able to [NOT] discontinue medications, \n7) HRSD question #9 regarding suicide <2, \n8) provision of informed consent. In addition, all subjects who meet criteria for the training portion must complete an exercise tolerance test and be cleared for participation by the study cardiologist. \n\nExclusion Criteria:\n1. Unable to ambulate at least 150 feet prior to stroke, [OR] or experienced intermittent claudication while walking; \n2. history of congestive heart failure, unstable cardiac arrhythmias, [OR] hypertrophic cardiomyopathy, severe aortic stenosis, [OR] angina [OR] or dyspnea at rest [OR] or during ADL\'s; \n3. History of oxygen dependence; \n4. Preexisting neurological disorders, [OR] dementia [OR] or previous stroke; \n5. History of major head trauma; \n6. Legal blindness [OR] or severe visual impairment; \n7. history of psychosis [OR] or other Axis I disorder that is primary; \n8. Life expectancy <1 yr.; \n9. Severe arthritis [OR] or other problems that [NOT] limit passive range of motion; \n10. History of DVT [OR] or pulmonary embolism within 6 months; \n11. Uncontrolled diabetes [AND] with recent weight loss, [OR] diabetic coma, [OR] or frequent insulin reactions; \n12. Severe hypertension [AND] with systolic >200 mmHg [AND] and diastolic >110 mmHg at rest; \n13. attempt of suicide in the last 2 years [OR] or at suicidal risk assessed by SCID interview; \n14. Previous [OR] or current enrollment in a clinical trial to enhance motor recovery; 15) currently exercising ≥ 2 times per week (≥20 minutes); \n16) Presence of non-MR compatible implants, [OR] pregnancy [OR] or severe claustrophobia.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
1) age 50-70 
2) stroke within the past 6 to 60 months, 
3) major depressive disorder (PHQ-9 > 10) [AND] and diagnosed using the Structured Clinical Interview for Depression (SCID) according to the Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders, Fourth Edition (DSM-IV), 
4) residual paresis in the lower extremity (Fugl-Meyer LE motor score <34), 
5) ability to walk [NOT] without assistance [AND] and [NOT] without an AFO on the treadmill ≥ 30 seconds at speeds ranging from 0.2-0.8 m/s, 
6) [NOT] no antidepressant medications [OR] or clinically able to [NOT] discontinue medications, 
7) HRSD question #9 regarding suicide <2, 
8) provision of informed consent. In addition, all subjects who meet criteria for the training portion must complete an exercise tolerance test and be cleared for participation by the study cardiologist. 

Exclusion Criteria:
1. Unable to ambulate at least 150 feet prior to stroke, [OR] or experienced intermittent claudication while walking; 
2. history of congestive heart failure, unstable cardiac arrhythmias, [OR] hypertrophic cardiomyopathy, severe aortic stenosis, [OR] angina [OR] or dyspnea at rest [OR] or during ADL's; 
3. History of oxygen dependence; 
4. Preexisting neurological disorders, [OR] dementia [OR] or previous stroke; 
5. History of major head trauma; 
6. Legal blindness [OR] or severe visual impairment; 
7. history of psychosis [OR] or other Axis I disorder that is primary; 
8. Life expectancy <1 yr.; 
9. Severe arthritis [OR] or other problems that [NOT] limit passive range of motion; 
10. History of DVT [OR] or pulmonary embolism within 6 months; 
11. Uncontrolled diabetes [AND] with recent weight loss, [OR] diabetic coma, [OR] or frequent insulin reactions; 
12. Severe hypertension [AND] with systolic >200 mmHg [AND] and diastolic >110 mmHg at rest; 
13. attempt of suicide in the last 2 years [OR] or at suicidal risk assessed by SCID interview; 
14. Previous [OR] or current enrollment in a clinical trial to enhance motor recovery; 15) currently exercising ≥ 2 times per week (≥20 minutes); 
16) Presence of non-MR compatible implants, [OR] pregnancy [OR] or severe claustrophobia.
