0 mg/dl)\n Serum bicarbonate <15 mmol/L\nPICU admission\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nAge > 18 Years\nPhysician discretion\nSeptic [OR] or hypovolemic shock\nSigns of life-threatening cerebral edema [OR] or multi-organ failure upon presentation to the emergency room [OR] or pediatric intensive care unit\nEnrollment time more than 1 hr since arrival to emergency room [OR] or PICU\nPregnancy<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Age between 0 and 18 years
Venous pH less than 7.25
Ketonuria as confirmed on urine point-of-care testing [OR] or urinalysis
Hyperglycemia (Serum glucose > 200 mg/dl)
 Serum bicarbonate <15 mmol/L
PICU admission

Exclusion Criteria:
Age > 18 Years
Physician discretion
Septic [OR] or hypovolemic shock
Signs of life-threatening cerebral edema [OR] or multi-organ failure upon presentation to the emergency room [OR] or pediatric intensive care unit
Enrollment time more than 1 hr since arrival to emergency room [OR] or PICU
Pregnancy
