File: NCT03083197 

Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_full/NCT03083197.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAge = 15 years old\nHospitalization with acute undifferentiated fever (temperature > 37.5 C, tympanic) =14 days or patients admitted to hospital with a history of fever = 14 days who subsequently develop fever within 24 hours of admission\nClinically suspected scrub typhus: defined as acute undifferentiated fever with no clear focus of infection and negative malaria blood smear and/or negative malaria RDT. Patients may have one, none, or a combination of other clinical findings such as eschar, rash, lymphadenopathy, headache, myalgia, cough, nausea and abdominal discomfort.\nA positive scrub typhus RDT (Scrub Typhus IgM RDT, InBios International, Seattle, WA, USA) and/or positive PCR-based detection of O. tsutsugamushi DNA from the admission blood sample\nWritten informed consent and/or, written informed assent as required\nAble to take oral medication\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nKnown hypersensitivity to tetracycline, doxycycline or azithromycin\nAdministration of doxycycline, azithromycin, chloramphenicol, rifampicin, or tetracycline during the preceding 7 days\nPregnancy or breast-feeding\nPatients with myasthenia gravis or systemic lupus erythematosus\nPatients with an established infection (diagnostic test required) e.g. acute malaria, dengue, leptospirosis, typhoid, Japanese encephalitis etc.\nCurrent TB or TB treatment in = 6 months (contain active antibiotics against Orientia spp.)\nCurrent HAART use for HIV, long term use of immunosuppressants (e.g. steroids, chemotherapy, TNF-inhibitors and related agents)\nPatients with severe disease whom the clinical team feel their condition necessitates the need for additional scrub typhus treatment beyond the allocated antibiotic treatment assigned at randomization (e.g. IV chloramphenicol and/or PO/NG rifampicin)\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAge = 15 years old\nHospitalization with acute undifferentiated fever (temperature > 37.5 C, tympanic) =14 days [OR] or patients admitted to hospital [AND] with a history of fever = 14 days [AND] who subsequently develop fever within 24 hours of admission\nClinically suspected scrub typhus: defined as acute undifferentiated fever [AND] with [NOT] no clear focus of infection [AND] and negative malaria blood smear [OR] and/or negative malaria RDT. Patients may have one, none, or a combination of other clinical findings such as eschar, [OR] rash, [OR] lymphadenopathy, [OR] headache, [OR] myalgia, [OR] cough, [OR] nausea [OR] and abdominal discomfort.\nA positive scrub typhus RDT (Scrub Typhus IgM RDT, InBios International, Seattle, WA, USA) [OR] and/or positive PCR-based detection of O. tsutsugamushi DNA from the admission blood sample\nWritten informed consent and/or, written informed assent as required\nAble to take oral medication\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nKnown hypersensitivity to tetracycline, [OR] doxycycline [OR] or azithromycin\n Administration of doxycycline, [OR] azithromycin, [OR] chloramphenicol, [OR] rifampicin, [OR] or tetracycline during the preceding 7 days\nPregnancy [OR] or breast-feeding\nPatients with myasthenia gravis [OR] or systemic lupus erythematosus\nPatients with an established infection (diagnostic test required) e.g. acute malaria, [OR] dengue, [OR] leptospirosis, [OR] typhoid, [OR] Japanese encephalitis etc.\nCurrent TB [OR] or TB treatment in = 6 months (contain active antibiotics against Orientia spp.)\n Current HAART use for HIV, long term use of immunosuppressants (e.g. steroids, [OR] chemotherapy, [OR] TNF-inhibitors and related agents)\nPatients with severe disease whom the clinical team feel their condition necessitates the need for additional scrub typhus treatment beyond the allocated antibiotic treatment assigned at randomization (e.g. IV chloramphenicol [OR] and/or PO/ [OR] NG rifampicin)<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Age = 15 years old
Hospitalization with acute undifferentiated fever (temperature > 37.5 C, tympanic) =14 days [OR] or patients admitted to hospital [AND] with a history of fever = 14 days [AND] who subsequently develop fever within 24 hours of admission
Clinically suspected scrub typhus: defined as acute undifferentiated fever [AND] with [NOT] no clear focus of infection [AND] and negative malaria blood smear [OR] and/or negative malaria RDT. Patients may have one, none, or a combination of other clinical findings such as eschar, [OR] rash, [OR] lymphadenopathy, [OR] headache, [OR] myalgia, [OR] cough, [OR] nausea [OR] and abdominal discomfort.
A positive scrub typhus RDT (Scrub Typhus IgM RDT, InBios International, Seattle, WA, USA) [OR] and/or positive PCR-based detection of O. tsutsugamushi DNA from the admission blood sample
Written informed consent and/or, written informed assent as required
Able to take oral medication

Exclusion Criteria:
Known hypersensitivity to tetracycline, [OR] doxycycline [OR] or azithromycin
 Administration of doxycycline, [OR] azithromycin, [OR] chloramphenicol, [OR] rifampicin, [OR] or tetracycline during the preceding 7 days
Pregnancy [OR] or breast-feeding
Patients with myasthenia gravis [OR] or systemic lupus erythematosus
Patients with an established infection (diagnostic test required) e.g. acute malaria, [OR] dengue, [OR] leptospirosis, [OR] typhoid, [OR] Japanese encephalitis etc.
Current TB [OR] or TB treatment in = 6 months (contain active antibiotics against Orientia spp.)
 Current HAART use for HIV, long term use of immunosuppressants (e.g. steroids, [OR] chemotherapy, [OR] TNF-inhibitors and related agents)
Patients with severe disease whom the clinical team feel their condition necessitates the need for additional scrub typhus treatment beyond the allocated antibiotic treatment assigned at randomization (e.g. IV chloramphenicol [OR] and/or PO/ [OR] NG rifampicin)
