ve renal failure requiring dialysis\nPoorly controlled pulmonary disease (severe asthma [OR] or COPD) -Contraindication to regional anesthesia (recent anticoagulant use)\nSleep apnea [OR] or morbid obesity [AND] with possible sleep apnea\nAllergy to methadone\nSignificant preoperative pain requiring treatment with high doses of opioids (more than 6-8 Norco tablets [OR] or equivalence per day) [OR] or recent history of opioid abuse<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
All patients presenting for elective shoulder arthroscopic procedures will be eligible for enrollment.

Exclusion Criteria:
Preoperative renal failure requiring dialysis
Poorly controlled pulmonary disease (severe asthma [OR] or COPD) -Contraindication to regional anesthesia (recent anticoagulant use)
Sleep apnea [OR] or morbid obesity [AND] with possible sleep apnea
Allergy to methadone
Significant preoperative pain requiring treatment with high doses of opioids (more than 6-8 Norco tablets [OR] or equivalence per day) [OR] or recent history of opioid abuse
