File: NCT03096613 

Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_full/NCT03096613.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAged 18 years or older, male or female.\nSystolic heart failure with New York Heart Association (NYHA) class II-III.\nLeft ventricular ejection fraction (LVEF) less than 40% by echocardiography during screening and randomization.\nSCH (TSH: upper limits of normal (ULN) -10mIU/L, and FT4 level within reference range).\nHaving received standard HF therapy for at least 2 weeks, having reached target dose or max tolerable dose.\nProvided informed consent.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nAcute heart failure or acute exacerbation of chronic heart failure within the past 2 weeks.\nScheduled cardiac resynchronization therapy or heart transplantation.\nHistory of malignant tumor or life expectancy under 12 months.\nAlready on medications that may affect thyroid function (L-T4, carbimazole, propylthiouracil, amiodarone, lithium).\nPregnancy and lactation period.\nParticipation in another clinical trial within the past 30 days.\nContraindication or intolerance to evidence-based therapy for CHF, such as beta-blocker, angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitor or angiotensin receptor blocker.\nKnown hypersensitivity to the trial treatment(s) or diluents (when applicable), including placebo or other comparator drug(s).\nUntreated adrenal insufficiency.\nUntreated pituitary insufficiency.\nUntreated thyrotoxicosis.\nTreatment with levothyroxine must not be initiated in patients with acute myocardial infarction, acute myocarditis, or acute pancarditis.\nSevere renal dysfunction (eGFR=30 ml/min/1.73m2).\nSignificant hepatic impairment (Serum GPT > 120 U/L).\nAny disorder which, in the opinion of the investigator, might jeopardise subject\'s safety or compliance with the protocol.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAged 18 years or older, male [OR] or female.\nSystolic heart failure [AND] with New York Heart Association (NYHA) class II-III.\n Left ventricular ejection fraction (LVEF) less than 40% by echocardiography during screening [AND] and randomization.\nSCH (TSH: upper limits of normal (ULN) -10mIU/L, [AND] and FT4 level within reference range).\nHaving received standard HF therapy for at least 2 weeks, having reached target dose [OR] or max tolerable dose.\nProvided informed consent.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nAcute heart failure [OR] or acute exacerbation of chronic heart failure within the past 2 weeks.\n Scheduled cardiac resynchronization therapy [OR] or heart transplantation.\n History of malignant tumor [OR] or life expectancy under 12 months.\n Already on medications that may affect thyroid function (L-T4, [OR] carbimazole, [OR] propylthiouracil, [OR] amiodarone, [OR] lithium).\n Pregnancy [OR] and lactation period.\n Participation in another clinical trial within the past 30 days.\n Contraindication [OR] or intolerance to evidence-based therapy for CHF, such as beta-blocker, [OR] angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitor [OR] or angiotensin receptor blocker.\n Known hypersensitivity to the trial treatment(s) [OR] or diluents (when applicable), including placebo [OR] or other comparator drug(s).\n Untreated adrenal insufficiency.\n Untreated pituitary insufficiency.\n Untreated thyrotoxicosis.\n Treatment with levothyroxine must [NOT] not be initiated in patients with acute myocardial infarction, [OR] acute myocarditis, [OR] or acute pancarditis.\n Severe renal dysfunction (eGFR=30 ml/min/1.73 m2).\n Significant hepatic impairment (Serum GPT > 120 U/L).\n Any disorder which, in the opinion of the investigator, might jeopardise subject\'s safety [OR] or compliance with the protocol.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Aged 18 years or older, male [OR] or female.
Systolic heart failure [AND] with New York Heart Association (NYHA) class II-III.
 Left ventricular ejection fraction (LVEF) less than 40% by echocardiography during screening [AND] and randomization.
SCH (TSH: upper limits of normal (ULN) -10mIU/L, [AND] and FT4 level within reference range).
Having received standard HF therapy for at least 2 weeks, having reached target dose [OR] or max tolerable dose.
Provided informed consent.

Exclusion Criteria:
Acute heart failure [OR] or acute exacerbation of chronic heart failure within the past 2 weeks.
 Scheduled cardiac resynchronization therapy [OR] or heart transplantation.
 History of malignant tumor [OR] or life expectancy under 12 months.
 Already on medications that may affect thyroid function (L-T4, [OR] carbimazole, [OR] propylthiouracil, [OR] amiodarone, [OR] lithium).
 Pregnancy [OR] and lactation period.
 Participation in another clinical trial within the past 30 days.
 Contraindication [OR] or intolerance to evidence-based therapy for CHF, such as beta-blocker, [OR] angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitor [OR] or angiotensin receptor blocker.
 Known hypersensitivity to the trial treatment(s) [OR] or diluents (when applicable), including placebo [OR] or other comparator drug(s).
 Untreated adrenal insufficiency.
 Untreated pituitary insufficiency.
 Untreated thyrotoxicosis.
 Treatment with levothyroxine must [NOT] not be initiated in patients with acute myocardial infarction, [OR] acute myocarditis, [OR] or acute pancarditis.
 Severe renal dysfunction (eGFR=30 ml/min/1.73 m2).
 Significant hepatic impairment (Serum GPT > 120 U/L).
 Any disorder which, in the opinion of the investigator, might jeopardise subject's safety [OR] or compliance with the protocol.
