Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAdult subjects aged 18 years or older\nScheduled for elective posterior lumbar spinal fusion surgery between 1 and 3 levels\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nBaseline cognitive deficits sufficient to make objective pain self-assessments unreliable in the estimation of the Study Investigators.\nImmunocompromised subject\nCoagulopathy\nSevere liver and renal dysfunction\nPreoperative neurological deficits\nThe dura damage during surgery\nInability to follow directions or comprehend the English language.\nFemales who are pregnant as determined by positive pregnancy test on or before the day of surgery.\nPrisoners.\nPatient refusal to provide informed consent.\nAllergy to amide local anesthetics (lidocaine, bupivacaine, ropivacaine) or opioid (fentanyl).\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAdult subjects aged 18 years or older\nScheduled for elective posterior lumbar spinal fusion surgery between 1 and 3 levels\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nBaseline cognitive deficits sufficient to make objective pain self-assessments unreliable in the estimation of the Study Investigators.\nImmunocompromised subject\nCoagulopathy\nSevere liver [OR] and renal dysfunction\nPreoperative neurological deficits\nThe dura damage during surgery\n[NOT] Inability to follow directions or comprehend the English language.\nFemales [AND] who are pregnant as determined by positive pregnancy test on or before the day of surgery.\nPrisoners.\nPatient refusal to provide informed consent.\nAllergy to amide local anesthetics (lidocaine, [OR] bupivacaine, [OR] ropivacaine) [OR] or opioid (fentanyl).<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Adult subjects aged 18 years or older
Scheduled for elective posterior lumbar spinal fusion surgery between 1 and 3 levels

Exclusion Criteria:
Baseline cognitive deficits sufficient to make objective pain self-assessments unreliable in the estimation of the Study Investigators.
Immunocompromised subject
Coagulopathy
Severe liver [OR] and renal dysfunction
Preoperative neurological deficits
The dura damage during surgery
[NOT] Inability to follow directions or comprehend the English language.
Females [AND] who are pregnant as determined by positive pregnancy test on or before the day of surgery.
Prisoners.
Patient refusal to provide informed consent.
Allergy to amide local anesthetics (lidocaine, [OR] bupivacaine, [OR] ropivacaine) [OR] or opioid (fentanyl).
