Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nHealthy, women ages 18 to 39yo with BMI <30\nRegular menstrual cycles with duration between 24-35 days\nCompletion of screening visit where ovulation will be assessed with blood draw for progesterone level (must be 5ng/mL or greater)\nNot seeking pregnancy during the study period\nUse of a non-hormonal form of contraception, such as: sterilization (tubal ligation, Essure), copper IUD (intrauterine device), barrier methods or abstinence\nMust speak English or Spanish\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nCurrently pregnant or breastfeeding\nSevere pelvic organ prolapse or prolapse to any degree that may prevent retention of the vaginal ring after insertion\nUse of oral contraceptive pills, patches, implants or hormonal intrauterine contraception in the month prior to screening\nUse of depo medroxyprogesterone within 6 months of screening\nUse of medications that interact with contraceptive steroid hormones: anti-epileptic medications, rifampin, rifabutin, fosamprenavir, etc\nMedical condition with safety deemed to be category 3 or 4 when using a combined hormonal contraceptive, as determined by the Center for Disease Control Medical Eligibility Criteria: current or past history of breast cancer, severe decompensated cirrhosis, history of deep vein thrombosis or pulmonary embolus, diabetes with nephropathy/retinopathy/neuropathy or other vascular disease diagnosed more than 20 years ago, current symptomatic gallbladder disease, hypertension, ischemic heart disease, known thrombogenic mutations, hepatocellular adenoma, malignant hepatoma, multiple risk factors for atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease, multiple sclerosis with prolonged immobility, history of peripartum cardiomyopathy, cigarette smoking and =35yo, history of complicated solid organ transplant, history of stroke, history of superficial venous thrombosis not associated with catheter, systemic lupus erythematosus with positive antiphospholipid antibodies, valvular heart disease complicated by pulmonary hypertension or atrial fibrillation or bacterial endocarditis, and acute viral hepatitis\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nHealthy, women ages 18 to 39yo [AND] with BMI <30\nRegular menstrual cycles [AND] with duration between 24-35 days\nCompletion of screening visit where ovulation will be assessed [AND] with blood draw for progesterone level (must be 5ng/mL or greater)\n [NOT] Not seeking pregnancy during the study period\nUse of a [NOT] non-hormonal form of contraception, such as: sterilization (tubal ligation, [OR] Essure), copper IUD (intrauterine device), [OR] barrier methods [OR] or abstinence\nMust speak English [OR] or Spanish\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nCurrently pregnant [OR] or breastfeeding\nSevere pelvic organ prolapse [OR] or prolapse to any degree that may [NOT] prevent retention of the vaginal ring after insertion\nUse of oral contraceptive pills, [OR] patches, [OR] implants [OR] or hormonal intrauterine contraception in the month prior to screening\nUse of depo medroxyprogesterone within 6 months of screening\nUse of medications that interact with contraceptive steroid hormones: anti-epileptic medications, [OR] rifampin, [OR] rifabutin, [OR] fosamprenavir, etc\nMedical condition [AND] with safety deemed to be category 3 or 4 when using a combined hormonal contraceptive, as determined by the Center for Disease Control Medical Eligibility Criteria: current [OR] or past history of breast cancer, severe decompensated cirrhosis, history of deep vein thrombosis [OR] or pulmonary embolus, diabetes [AND] with nephropathy/ [OR] retinopathy/ [OR] neuropathy [OR] or other vascular disease diagnosed more than 20 years ago, current symptomatic gallbladder disease, hypertension, [OR] ischemic heart disease, known thrombogenic mutations, [OR] hepatocellular adenoma, [OR] malignant hepatoma, multiple risk factors for atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease, multiple sclerosis [AND] with prolonged immobility, history of peripartum cardiomyopathy, cigarette smoking [AND] and =35yo, history of complicated solid organ transplant, history of stroke, history of superficial venous thrombosis [NOT] not associated with catheter, systemic lupus erythematosus [AND] with positive antiphospholipid antibodies, valvular heart disease complicated by pulmonary hypertension [OR] or atrial fibrillation [OR] or bacterial endocarditis, [OR] and acute viral hepatitis<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Healthy, women ages 18 to 39yo [AND] with BMI <30
Regular menstrual cycles [AND] with duration between 24-35 days
Completion of screening visit where ovulation will be assessed [AND] with blood draw for progesterone level (must be 5ng/mL or greater)
 [NOT] Not seeking pregnancy during the study period
Use of a [NOT] non-hormonal form of contraception, such as: sterilization (tubal ligation, [OR] Essure), copper IUD (intrauterine device), [OR] barrier methods [OR] or abstinence
Must speak English [OR] or Spanish

Exclusion Criteria:
Currently pregnant [OR] or breastfeeding
Severe pelvic organ prolapse [OR] or prolapse to any degree that may [NOT] prevent retention of the vaginal ring after insertion
Use of oral contraceptive pills, [OR] patches, [OR] implants [OR] or hormonal intrauterine contraception in the month prior to screening
Use of depo medroxyprogesterone within 6 months of screening
Use of medications that interact with contraceptive steroid hormones: anti-epileptic medications, [OR] rifampin, [OR] rifabutin, [OR] fosamprenavir, etc
Medical condition [AND] with safety deemed to be category 3 or 4 when using a combined hormonal contraceptive, as determined by the Center for Disease Control Medical Eligibility Criteria: current [OR] or past history of breast cancer, severe decompensated cirrhosis, history of deep vein thrombosis [OR] or pulmonary embolus, diabetes [AND] with nephropathy/ [OR] retinopathy/ [OR] neuropathy [OR] or other vascular disease diagnosed more than 20 years ago, current symptomatic gallbladder disease, hypertension, [OR] ischemic heart disease, known thrombogenic mutations, [OR] hepatocellular adenoma, [OR] malignant hepatoma, multiple risk factors for atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease, multiple sclerosis [AND] with prolonged immobility, history of peripartum cardiomyopathy, cigarette smoking [AND] and =35yo, history of complicated solid organ transplant, history of stroke, history of superficial venous thrombosis [NOT] not associated with catheter, systemic lupus erythematosus [AND] with positive antiphospholipid antibodies, valvular heart disease complicated by pulmonary hypertension [OR] or atrial fibrillation [OR] or bacterial endocarditis, [OR] and acute viral hepatitis
