Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nMale and female individuals between ages of 18 to 70 years old \nMultiple contiguous gingival recession defects on a minimum of two adjacent teeth, exhibiting 3mm or more recession on at least one of those teeth \nNo prior surgical treatment in the sites planned for therapy \nMinimum of 2 mm of keratinized gingiva \nAbsence of cervical restorations extending to the CEJ \nMiller class 1, 2 and 3 recession defects will be included \nAvailability to undergo treatment and return for follow up visits at specified post-operative intervals \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nMolar teeth \nMilller Class 4 recession defects \nPregnancy (Self-reported) \nSmoking \nUncontrolled local or systemic diseases that affects wound healing (diabetes, autoimmune or inflammatory disorders) \nPast history of systemic steroid use over 2 weeks within the last 2 years \nPoor oral hygiene on a non-compliant individual \nIbuprofen Allergy/interlerance \nAnticoagulant therapy (e.g. Warfarin, Plavix, etc.), will not be automatic exclusion but patients will be required to have INR test performed and have values between 2.0 to 3. Physician consultation will be requested to determine whether anticoagulant therapy can be discontinued for 3 days prior to surgery. \nObjection to blood draw or application of blood products \nStudents and staff from USC Ostrow school of Dentistry will not be recruited for this study       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nMale [OR] and female individuals between ages of 18 to 70 years old \nMultiple contiguous gingival recession defects on a minimum of two adjacent teeth, exhibiting 3mm or more recession on at least one of those teeth \n [NOT] No prior surgical treatment in the sites planned for therapy \nMinimum of 2 mm of keratinized gingiva \n [NOT] Absence of cervical restorations extending to the CEJ \nMiller class 1, 2 and 3 recession defects will be included \nAvailability to undergo treatment and return for follow up visits at specified post-operative intervals \n\nExclusion Criteria:\nMolar teeth \n Milller Class 4 recession defects \nPregnancy (Self-reported) \nSmoking \nUncontrolled local [OR] or systemic diseases that affects wound healing (diabetes, [OR] autoimmune [OR] or inflammatory disorders) \nPast history of systemic steroid use over 2 weeks within the last 2 years \nPoor oral hygiene on a [NOT] non-compliant individual \nIbuprofen Allergy/ [OR] interlerance \nAnticoagulant therapy (e.g. Warfarin, [OR] Plavix, etc.), will [NOT] not be automatic exclusion but patients will be required to have INR test performed and have values between 2.0 to 3. Physician consultation will be requested to determine whether anticoagulant therapy can be [NOT] discontinued for 3 days prior to surgery. \nObjection to blood draw [OR] or application of blood products \nStudents and staff from USC Ostrow school of Dentistry will [NOT] not be recruited for this study<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Male [OR] and female individuals between ages of 18 to 70 years old 
Multiple contiguous gingival recession defects on a minimum of two adjacent teeth, exhibiting 3mm or more recession on at least one of those teeth 
 [NOT] No prior surgical treatment in the sites planned for therapy 
Minimum of 2 mm of keratinized gingiva 
 [NOT] Absence of cervical restorations extending to the CEJ 
Miller class 1, 2 and 3 recession defects will be included 
Availability to undergo treatment and return for follow up visits at specified post-operative intervals 

Exclusion Criteria:
Molar teeth 
 Milller Class 4 recession defects 
Pregnancy (Self-reported) 
Smoking 
Uncontrolled local [OR] or systemic diseases that affects wound healing (diabetes, [OR] autoimmune [OR] or inflammatory disorders) 
Past history of systemic steroid use over 2 weeks within the last 2 years 
Poor oral hygiene on a [NOT] non-compliant individual 
Ibuprofen Allergy/ [OR] interlerance 
Anticoagulant therapy (e.g. Warfarin, [OR] Plavix, etc.), will [NOT] not be automatic exclusion but patients will be required to have INR test performed and have values between 2.0 to 3. Physician consultation will be requested to determine whether anticoagulant therapy can be [NOT] discontinued for 3 days prior to surgery. 
Objection to blood draw [OR] or application of blood products 
Students and staff from USC Ostrow school of Dentistry will [NOT] not be recruited for this study
