Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAge = 65 years with one additional stroke risk factor (hypertension, diabetes, heart failure history of or left ventricular ejection fraction <0.40), previous stroke or transient ischemic attack).\nAtrial fibrillation and not on oral anticoagulation (OAC) therapy but eligible\nAtrial fibrillation on sub-optimal OAC\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nUncontrolled hypertension (defined as average SBP = 160 mmHg [2 readings taken at time of screening]).\nEnd stage renal disease (CrCl < 15 ml/min)\nValvular Heart Disease including those with prosthetic valve, mitral stenosis (moderate to severe) or valve repair.\nExcess alcohol intake (males: = 28 units/week, females: = 21 units/week. One unit of alcohol = 8 oz beer, 1 oz hard liquor or 4 oz wine).\nIntracranial bleed at any point.\nHistory of "Major Bleeding" at any point (defined as overt bleeding at a critical site including intracranial, intraspinal, intraocular, pericardial, or retroperitoneal; or bleed requiring hospitalization).\nForeshortened life-expectancy or severe comorbidities precluding study follow-up period\nUnable to read/understand English\nSevere cognitive impairment (defined as score = 5 on the Short Portable Mental Status Questionnaire)\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAge = 65 years [AND] with one additional stroke risk factor (hypertension, [OR] diabetes, [OR] heart failure history [OR] of or left ventricular ejection fraction <0.40), previous stroke [OR] or transient ischemic attack).\nAtrial fibrillation [AND] and [NOT] not on oral anticoagulation (OAC) therapy [AND] but eligible\nAtrial fibrillation on sub-optimal OAC\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nUncontrolled hypertension (defined as average SBP = 160 mmHg [2 readings taken at time of screening]).\nEnd stage renal disease (CrCl < 15 ml/min)\nValvular Heart Disease including those with prosthetic valve, [OR] mitral stenosis (moderate to severe) [OR] or valve repair.\nExcess alcohol intake (males: = 28 units/week, females: = 21 units/week. One unit of alcohol = 8 oz beer, 1 oz hard liquor [OR] or 4 oz wine).\nIntracranial bleed at any point.\nHistory of "Major Bleeding" at any point (defined as overt bleeding at a critical site including intracranial, [OR] intraspinal, [OR] intraocular, [OR] pericardial, [OR] or retroperitoneal; [OR] or bleed requiring hospitalization).\nForeshortened life-expectancy [OR] or severe comorbidities [NOT] precluding study follow-up period\nUnable to read/understand English\nSevere cognitive impairment (defined as score = 5 on the Short Portable Mental Status Questionnaire)<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Age = 65 years [AND] with one additional stroke risk factor (hypertension, [OR] diabetes, [OR] heart failure history [OR] of or left ventricular ejection fraction <0.40), previous stroke [OR] or transient ischemic attack).
Atrial fibrillation [AND] and [NOT] not on oral anticoagulation (OAC) therapy [AND] but eligible
Atrial fibrillation on sub-optimal OAC

Exclusion Criteria:
Uncontrolled hypertension (defined as average SBP = 160 mmHg [2 readings taken at time of screening]).
End stage renal disease (CrCl < 15 ml/min)
Valvular Heart Disease including those with prosthetic valve, [OR] mitral stenosis (moderate to severe) [OR] or valve repair.
Excess alcohol intake (males: = 28 units/week, females: = 21 units/week. One unit of alcohol = 8 oz beer, 1 oz hard liquor [OR] or 4 oz wine).
Intracranial bleed at any point.
History of "Major Bleeding" at any point (defined as overt bleeding at a critical site including intracranial, [OR] intraspinal, [OR] intraocular, [OR] pericardial, [OR] or retroperitoneal; [OR] or bleed requiring hospitalization).
Foreshortened life-expectancy [OR] or severe comorbidities [NOT] precluding study follow-up period
Unable to read/understand English
Severe cognitive impairment (defined as score = 5 on the Short Portable Mental Status Questionnaire)
