Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\n18 years or older patients who are proven to be infected by Helicobacter pylori based on positive in Urea Breath Test or positive in histopathologic examination of biopsy in antrum and corpus of gaster through esophagoduodenoscopy.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPatients refuse to follow the research\nPatient has had previous eradication therapy of Helicobacter pylori infection.\nThe patient is pregnant or breastfeeding\nPatients have a history of allergy to one component of triple therapy regimen (proton pump inhibitor, penicillin, and / or macrolide) before.\nPatients are known to have impaired liver function, evidenced by ALT values within normal limits, and no previous liver disease.\nPatients were found to have arrhythmias or obtained QT wave elongation on electrocardiographic\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n18 years or older patients [AND] who are proven to be infected by Helicobacter pylori based on positive in Urea Breath Test [OR] or positive in histopathologic examination of biopsy in antrum [OR] and corpus of gaster through esophagoduodenoscopy.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nPatients refuse to follow the research\nPatient has had previous eradication therapy of Helicobacter pylori infection.\nThe patient is pregnant [OR] or breastfeeding\nPatients have a history of allergy to one component of triple therapy regimen (proton pump inhibitor, [OR] penicillin, [OR] and / or macrolide) before.\nPatients are known to have impaired liver function, evidenced by ALT values within normal limits, [AND] and [NOT] no previous liver disease.\nPatients were found to have arrhythmias [OR] or obtained QT wave elongation on electrocardiographic<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
18 years or older patients [AND] who are proven to be infected by Helicobacter pylori based on positive in Urea Breath Test [OR] or positive in histopathologic examination of biopsy in antrum [OR] and corpus of gaster through esophagoduodenoscopy.

Exclusion Criteria:
Patients refuse to follow the research
Patient has had previous eradication therapy of Helicobacter pylori infection.
The patient is pregnant [OR] or breastfeeding
Patients have a history of allergy to one component of triple therapy regimen (proton pump inhibitor, [OR] penicillin, [OR] and / or macrolide) before.
Patients are known to have impaired liver function, evidenced by ALT values within normal limits, [AND] and [NOT] no previous liver disease.
Patients were found to have arrhythmias [OR] or obtained QT wave elongation on electrocardiographic
