Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nInclusion criteria includes all U.S. HCA hospitals with an adult ICU;\nNote: Unit of randomization is the hospital, but the participants are hospital adult ICUs\nAll patients within adult ICUs are included, including rare patients <18 years and >=12 years.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nExclusion criteria includes ICUs with an average length of stay of less than 2 days;\nHCA hospitals that are not able to transfer or merge data into the centralized data warehouse for the baseline and intervention periods of the study are also excluded.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nInclusion criteria includes all U.S. HCA hospitals with an adult ICU;\nNote: Unit of randomization is the hospital, but the participants are hospital adult ICUs\nAll patients within adult ICUs are included, including rare patients <18 years [OR] and >=12 years.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nExclusion criteria includes ICUs [AND] with an average length of stay of less than 2 days;\nHCA hospitals that are [NOT] not able to transfer [OR] or merge data into the centralized data warehouse for the baseline [AND] and intervention periods of the study are also [NOT] excluded.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Inclusion criteria includes all U.S. HCA hospitals with an adult ICU;
Note: Unit of randomization is the hospital, but the participants are hospital adult ICUs
All patients within adult ICUs are included, including rare patients <18 years [OR] and >=12 years.

Exclusion Criteria:
Exclusion criteria includes ICUs [AND] with an average length of stay of less than 2 days;
HCA hospitals that are [NOT] not able to transfer [OR] or merge data into the centralized data warehouse for the baseline [AND] and intervention periods of the study are also [NOT] excluded.
