Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nSingleton pregnancy = 37 weeks gestation\nPatient presented for induction of labor who is determined to be a candidate for oxytocin\nCephalic presentation\nReassuring fetal health assessment (no abnormal findings in fetal assessment, see below)\nMeeting one of the following BMI category:\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nNon-reassuring fetal assessment at the time of recruitment\nPrevious cervical ripening agents (cytotec, cervidil, cervical Foley Balloon)\n<18 years of age\nPrisoners\nAny patients contraindicated for vaginal delivery\nMultiple gestations\nHistory of previous cesarean delivery\nPatients with history of significant cardiac disease\nFetal demise\nEstimated fetal weight greater than 4500 grams in diabetic and 5000 grams in non-diabetic mother\nRuptured membranes\nSpontaneous labor (latent or active phase)\nAugmentation of labor (latent or active phase)\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nSingleton pregnancy = 37 weeks gestation\nPatient presented for induction of labor [AND] who is determined to be a candidate for oxytocin\nCephalic presentation\nReassuring fetal health assessment ([NOT] no abnormal findings in fetal assessment, see below)\nMeeting one of the following BMI category:\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nNon-reassuring fetal assessment at the time of recruitment\nPrevious cervical ripening agents (cytotec, [OR] cervidil, [OR] cervical Foley Balloon)\n <18 years of age\nPrisoners\nAny patients contraindicated for vaginal delivery\nMultiple gestations\nHistory of previous cesarean delivery\nPatients with history of significant cardiac disease\nFetal demise\nEstimated fetal weight greater than 4500 grams [AND] in diabetic [AND] and 5000 grams [AND] in [NOT] non-diabetic mother\nRuptured membranes\nSpontaneous labor (latent [OR] or active phase)\n Augmentation of labor (latent [OR] or active phase)<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Singleton pregnancy = 37 weeks gestation
Patient presented for induction of labor [AND] who is determined to be a candidate for oxytocin
Cephalic presentation
Reassuring fetal health assessment ([NOT] no abnormal findings in fetal assessment, see below)
Meeting one of the following BMI category:

Exclusion Criteria:
Non-reassuring fetal assessment at the time of recruitment
Previous cervical ripening agents (cytotec, [OR] cervidil, [OR] cervical Foley Balloon)
 <18 years of age
Prisoners
Any patients contraindicated for vaginal delivery
Multiple gestations
History of previous cesarean delivery
Patients with history of significant cardiac disease
Fetal demise
Estimated fetal weight greater than 4500 grams [AND] in diabetic [AND] and 5000 grams [AND] in [NOT] non-diabetic mother
Ruptured membranes
Spontaneous labor (latent [OR] or active phase)
 Augmentation of labor (latent [OR] or active phase)
