File: NCT03177811 

Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_full/NCT03177811.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInclusion Criteria:\nMale and female patients, age 18-75 yrs.\nCOPD diagnosed according to GOLD, FEV1 40-80% predicted, SpO2 =92% at 750 m.\nBorn, raised and currently living at low altitude (<800m).\nWritten informed consent.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nCOPD exacerbation, very severe COPD with hypoxemia at low altitude (FEV1/FVC <0.7, FEV1 <40% predicted, oxygen saturation on room air <92% at 750 m).\nComorbidities such as uncontrolled cardiovascular disease, i.e., unstable systemic arterial hypertension, coronary artery disease; previous stroke; OSA; pneumothorax in the last 2 months.\nInternal, neurologic, rheumatologic or psychiatric disease including current heavy smoking (>20 cigarettes per day)\nKnown renal failure or allergy to acetazolamide and other sulfonamides\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nMale [OR] and female patients, age 18-75 yrs.\nCOPD diagnosed according to GOLD, FEV1 40-80% predicted, SpO2 =92% at 750 m.\nBorn, raised and currently living at low altitude (<800m).\nWritten informed consent.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nCOPD exacerbation, very severe COPD [AND] with hypoxemia at low altitude (FEV1/ [OR] FVC <0.7, FEV1 <40% predicted, oxygen saturation on room air <92% at 750 m).\nComorbidities such as uncontrolled cardiovascular disease, i.e., unstable systemic arterial hypertension, [OR] coronary artery disease; previous stroke; [OR] OSA; [OR] pneumothorax in the last 2 months.\nInternal, [OR] neurologic, [OR] rheumatologic [OR] or psychiatric disease including current heavy smoking (>20 cigarettes per day)\nKnown renal failure [OR] or allergy to acetazolamide [OR] and other sulfonamides<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Male [OR] and female patients, age 18-75 yrs.
COPD diagnosed according to GOLD, FEV1 40-80% predicted, SpO2 =92% at 750 m.
Born, raised and currently living at low altitude (<800m).
Written informed consent.

Exclusion Criteria:
COPD exacerbation, very severe COPD [AND] with hypoxemia at low altitude (FEV1/ [OR] FVC <0.7, FEV1 <40% predicted, oxygen saturation on room air <92% at 750 m).
Comorbidities such as uncontrolled cardiovascular disease, i.e., unstable systemic arterial hypertension, [OR] coronary artery disease; previous stroke; [OR] OSA; [OR] pneumothorax in the last 2 months.
Internal, [OR] neurologic, [OR] rheumatologic [OR] or psychiatric disease including current heavy smoking (>20 cigarettes per day)
Known renal failure [OR] or allergy to acetazolamide [OR] and other sulfonamides
