tazolamide and other sulfonamides\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nMale [OR] and female patients, age 18-75 yrs.\nCOPD diagnosed according to GOLD, FEV1 40-80% predicted, SpO2 =92% at 750 m.\nBorn, raised and currently living at low altitude (<800m).\nWritten informed consent.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\nCOPD exacerbation, very severe COPD [AND] with hypoxemia at low altitude (FEV1/ [OR] FVC <0.7, FEV1 <40% predicted, oxygen saturation on room air <92% at 750 m).\nComorbidities such as uncontrolled cardiovascular disease, i.e., unstable systemic arterial hypertension, [OR] coronary artery disease; previous stroke; [OR] OSA; [OR] pneumothorax in the last 2 months.\nInternal, [OR] neurologic, [OR] rheumatologic [OR] or psychiatric disease including current heavy smoking (>20 cigarettes per day)\nKnown renal failure [OR] or allergy to acetazolamide [OR] and other sulfonamides<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Male [OR] and female patients, age 18-75 yrs.
COPD diagnosed according to GOLD, FEV1 40-80% predicted, SpO2 =92% at 750 m.
Born, raised and currently living at low altitude (<800m).
Written informed consent.

Exclusion Criteria:
COPD exacerbation, very severe COPD [AND] with hypoxemia at low altitude (FEV1/ [OR] FVC <0.7, FEV1 <40% predicted, oxygen saturation on room air <92% at 750 m).
Comorbidities such as uncontrolled cardiovascular disease, i.e., unstable systemic arterial hypertension, [OR] coronary artery disease; previous stroke; [OR] OSA; [OR] pneumothorax in the last 2 months.
Internal, [OR] neurologic, [OR] rheumatologic [OR] or psychiatric disease including current heavy smoking (>20 cigarettes per day)
Known renal failure [OR] or allergy to acetazolamide [OR] and other sulfonamides
